INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39803, '9c71cbdaeb', '', 'You know I am ginnin ear to ear w/ those compliments pimps.  Hue as for your question. \r\n[url]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=3061[/url]\r\nVery easy to do and the rubbers fit nearly perfectly (may want to do CD\'s wire insert mod, we\'ll see)  \r\n\r\nAs for this puppy, you pop off the hubs from the MT of your liking, take a dremmel or an alternative way to sand fast and shave em down to the same thickness as a Zip hub.  This is very easy due to the softness of the plasic they use.  I dremmeled out the center but you can drill to make space for the Zips pins.  Pop em on and if you drilled the correct size hole, don\'t even need to glue em on.  If I was to repete this process after learning what I did I could do it again in 15 min total.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (414, 'dbd0d4f7c7', 'wrecked lambo', 'i was working on a lambo countach body..  to be molded like my ferrari body and others that i have, but i dropped it and the dog chomped it, just like she got two of my other cars...  i decided to mold it anyway.  it will looked like a wrecked lambo..  hehe  now i just have to figure out how to paint dents and paint scratches.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39801, '0f0ced7793', '', 'Real nice Finks, those wheels are the shit. Can you put Bit tires on the Muscle Tuner wheels, or do you have to stick with the hard-ass rubber that comes on \'em?\r\n\r\nGreat start, man. I look forward to seeing more of your badass rides.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39802, '503af59aea', '', 'ahhh, EverQuest. I\'ve always wondered about that. I have a hard enough time keeping away from the games I already own. From what I\'ve read, EQ is a black hole for time. I used to be into an online WWII flight sim called "Warbirds", and occasionally still play WWII flight sims and some of the Unreal Tournament mods.\r\n\r\nAs far as other stuff I do, I have a 3 yr old (and a wife, too, hehe), so the fact that I get anything done on my bits at all is a small miracle. Almost all the modding I do happens on Friday night at hue35\'s house or weeknights between 11pm-2am. \r\n\r\nI own a small graphic design business, so the hours can get sucked up there as well.');
