INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41006, '5b7b7bf290', '', 'gta vice city is hands down the best game ever, still after over a year being released, it still out sells just about everything.\r\nit\'s become a cult-classic and a must have in any gamers collection.\r\n\r\nthe story is a billion times thicker than any other previous releases of gta.\r\nthe "world" you get to play in is monsterous in comparison to previous releases. there\'s probably 70% more game to play than previous releases.\r\n\r\nI just can\'t say enough about this game - I spent most of last winter indoors and on GTA VC.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (1534, '1b36f49129', 'Wild Char-g can\'t go any faster than it already does...', 'Meaning, I\'ve been trying to figure out how to activate the boost function on it... when in actuallity the standard controller is already transmitting at the\r\nboost freq.!  \r\n[b:1b36f49129](keep in mind that most of this is theory, as i\'m not sure I\'ve got the  skill to prove it all... but damnit I\'ll try)[/b:1b36f49129]\r\nNow since I\'ve gotten my multi-controller this is what I know;\r\n\r\nThe multi-controller has 3 settings for it\'s capable functions\r\n[list:1b36f49129]A= Standard use for non-boost chassis (setting won\'t work with boost chassis)\r\nB= Switchable Boost capabilities (setting won\'t work with standard chassis)\r\nC= Boost always on (setting won\'t work with standard chassis)[/list:u:1b36f49129]\r\nIllustrated below;\r\n[img:1b36f49129]http://homepage.mac.com/blormore/.Pictures/control/selector.jpg[/img:1b36f49129]\r\nNow I know this is all elementary, but it helps as a reference :wink:\r\n\r\nWhen running the [b:1b36f49129]Wild[/b:1b36f49129] on setting B it\'s running a 1/2 speed, painfully slow, when the boost button is pushed it now runs at \'regular\' speed (no faster), as it would with the standard controller. When on setting C it is at constant \'regular\' speed.\r\nNow these results and the settings used would be the same if running a \'Bit\' boosted chassis.\r\nAnd this why I believe the standard controller to be running at boost freq. all the time, what i will TRY to do today is to get a reading on the voltage and current on the [b:1b36f49129]Wild[/b:1b36f49129] to see if it proves my theory. As i\'ve never tried before this should be interesting.\r\nI will thank Namuna in advance for his readings on the [url=http://www.tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=8881]350z[/url] for a basis for comparison.\r\nKinda starting to make sense yet?! :idea:\r\n\r\nOn a side note; I don\'t know if anyone else has got the Wild, but if you\'ve cracked it open and seen the the kind of diff. set-up it\'s got... all this kinda starts to make sense. It would appear that the Wild in nature needs that extra \'UMF\' to get it\'s ass goin.');
