INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (2031, 'b2d0e71abb', '', 'Well, I took out my magnet to test just how strong the iron content was in the rear axle pin.\r\n\r\n- On a stock bit...Pretty weak pull, so that\'s good.\r\n- On a stock ZipZaps...Pretty STRONG pull.\r\n\r\nSo that\'s interesting.\r\n\r\nAnd if anyone cares, or needs to know; The Diameter of the rear axle pin, on a stock bit, is .048" (or 1.24mm)...I love my new Digital Caliper\r\n\r\nI measured the diameters of the front and rear wheels (on a bit) as well...I\'ll post that info tomorrow, I\'m goin to bed.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (2032, '16695549fb', '', 'I used to skate alot :twisted: then I got some dirt wheels for my deck and I was taking hills like a real mutha fukha should. I road that board day and night (are you ready) until I took a real steep hill in lincoln park and forgot about the concrete walk way 3/4 of the way down. I wound up scraped and brusied and bleeding profusely from my chin. I also had the pleasure of getting clipped in the chest on the way down by a thick ass grounding wire coming down from a pole (telephone, electric, I dunno). I still have the deck as a momento, it was the last time I ever tried to go faster than my feet could take me (without some steel reinforcement :wink: ). Anyway it\'s pretty damn cold and snowing up here  :mrgreen:');
