INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (2426, '9b2c4277f0', '', 'Yea slightly.\r\n\r\nIt seems that before the pullback mod, my bit turned fine - equally in both directions - the radius wasn\'t all that bad.\r\n\r\nWith the front pullback mod on all 4 - everything was fine - the radius was quite smaller. I likey a lot.\r\n\r\nWith the rear pullback mod on all 4 - everything was fine - the radius was only slightly smaller in comparison to the front mod.\r\n\r\nWhat I haven\'t had a chance to test yet is what exactly are the major contributing factors. I did all this with a 2.2. There was a speed decrease with either mod, but not much. So I\'m guessing the combination of softer, wider tires and a slightly slower bit made such a dramatic increase in turning radius.\r\nAnother thing I did was slap a 3.8 up in the chassis. It flew and turning was awesome! My bit appeared much more stable and less likely to roll. On my track I have a slight incline at an odd angle that tweeks the tires in certain direction for just a nano-second. Usually the faster you took the incline, the more of a little hop the bit would do. Not with the pullback mod, I flew right over it no problems, much more stable.');
