INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (2434, '32107dfc0b', '', '[quote:32107dfc0b="Shypo"]did the rear pullback rims ever seem to catch on the gaurds Cabo?[/quote:32107dfc0b]\r\n\r\n"guards"?\r\n\r\nif you mean by the railing on the track, no not really - I imagine though driving on it without a body would be terrifying as every other turn your front wheels would get violently turned into the rail once they touched it. The tires are so soft and grippy, it\'s just be a nightmare without a body.\r\n\r\nif you mean by the wheel wells on the body, on the front yea. I sliced into the front wheel wells of the S-2000 I painted to fit the rear pullback modded front wheels while turning. Just sitting there it didn\'t touch a thing, but turning would lock up the wheel as it would hit the edge of the body. The rear wheels never had problems. Each body has a bit different style to it, so I would imagine on some bodies you may have to trim more or less. The front pullback mod on all 4 didn\'t require me to cut on my S-2000 or the GT-R 2000, haven\'t looked at it with the Gloria.');
