INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39259, '37f1511eb2', '', 'Wood is seasonal, prices will vary. Particleboard, and ply is almost always the cheapest, and is usually sold in 4\'x8\' sheets. \r\n\r\nI found that I get the best traction from a smooth slick surface, and haven\'t been getting good traction from wood. I\'ve heard of several people trying chalkboard paint, but SilentWolv said that he felt it gave him almost too much traction. So I\'m thinking about going over my track with wood filler, then block sanding to get a nice level surface, and covering it with enamel.\r\n\r\nBut the track you\'re talking about is pretty huge. I think my 4\'x8\' track takes up quite a bit of space. You might want to look into some vinyl flooring. You could find a place that lays flooring, and see if they got some left overs they\'ll sell you for cheap. Usually when they do a job for a customer they\'ll get more than they need, so they might have some mismatched left overs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (2767, 'c691b00e6a', 'Rotation on the Pimp Radio! GEt me on yo !', 'A few peeps know i finished production on my latest cd release but others are still in the dark. How can a brutha get some rotation!? Its got to be easier than it was to get rotation here in the AK - Alaska ( it was a B***H but we did it)!\r\n\r\nIm originaly from the Bay Area so your going to hear a bit of fusion of Bay Area tone/slang (with some conscious lyrical content) and some off the wall WAY original beats. NO FRUITY LOOPS HERE ( for you producers/artist out there)!\r\n\r\nIf i slide ya the cd and you approve can i get some LUVVVVVVVVV!?');
