INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3126, '5eda0bb0c2', 'you guys gots da noodles...help me out', 'aight, so a brutha switched PCBs out and it was coo, steered and drove perfect, except for the part where i mixed the steering wires up.  I figured no prob, just go in and switch the magnet around. It was glued in there pretty well, so a kinda had to use some force and bent the arm. thats no good, so i just got another one from my box and put that in. It was brand new and exactly the same. no binding, nuttin. I put it all back together and the car barely steers. Im all like...whaa? I wiggle it with ma finger and its smooth as butter, returns perfectly. \r\n\r\nany explanations?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3127, 'ea916aebaf', '', 'welcome wocket  :) \r\n\r\nI\'m with ya, I\'ve never removed or altered mine and I\'m happy... don\'t wanna mess with a good thing! lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3128, '331fb48bd1', '', 'when you\'re turning the wheels with your hand, do they turn as far as before?\r\nwhen you\'re turning the wheels with your controller, do both sides, when turning, seem equally "weak"?\r\nhow\'d you put your new magnet in?\r\n\r\nmake sure you don\'t have a glob of glue over the side of the magnet.\r\nif your steering arm isn\'t hitting on anything, and you know the arm and magnet are good to go - then I\'d start guessing at those wires coming from the steering coils to the pcb, maybe one\'s broke? or maybe the connection after re-soldering isn\'t so great?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3130, '5fce2c66be', 'Where are the Hydro mods?', 'Where are they... \r\nThere is a really good one in this video\r\n[url]www.uffschnitt.de/bit/movies/bitrenntag2_low.wmv[/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3131, '4d15881045', 'Re: you guys gots da noodles...help me out', '[quote:4d15881045="wocket"]aight, so a brutha switched PCBs out and it was coo, steered and drove perfect, except for the part where i mixed the steering wires up.  I figured no prob, just go in and switch the magnet around. It was glued in there pretty well, so a kinda had to use some force and bent the arm. thats no good, so i just got another one from my box and put that in. It was brand new and exactly the same. no binding, nuttin. I put it all back together and the car barely steers. Im all like...whaa? I wiggle it with ma finger and its smooth as butter, returns perfectly. \r\n\r\nany explanations?[/quote:4d15881045]\r\n\r\nSo did you switch the magnet around before you installed the new arm? If you did, I\'d switch it back. You could also try using the steering spring off the other bent arm you\'re not using..\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3132, '871c69f852', '', 'Welcome to the barrio... That video rocks the house. Super good editing skills..\r\n\r\nAre you part of the club over there in Germany?\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3133, '279185f579', '', 'ROFLMFAO..... No seriously, ROFLMFAO......\r\n\r\n\r\nThe already existing anger brought on by your wifes filming skills coupled with the anger of your little fire stunt going horribly wrong. (and I mean horribly wrong)  \r\n\r\nI\'m guessing that you wanted to crash through the firery napkin like "Spank Spangler", and have little bits of crap flyin through the air rather than wrapping it around your car like a wool sweater in the dead of winter...lol    Your timing was way off G... I can\'t stop laughing\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI can only imagine the yelling and panic in that little stunt gone bad..\r\n\r\nSo what happened to the car?  And how mad is your old lady over that deal?\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3134, '9cd58e91cc', 'stronger steering spring', 'hey everyone. i am looking for a stronger steering spring for my project car.  i have done a monster wheel mod to it, and need some extra help getting the wheels to re-center.  any ideas?\r\n\r\ni attached the pic of the mod so far on tiny...  and will soon have it on my webspace...  i believe its near the end of the post.\r\n\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;postid=86854#post86854');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3135, 'a380201386', '', 'It was an electrical fire on the east wall 2nd floor apartment, right above my buddies, as far as who is at fault we\'re still waiting to hear.\r\nCheck out this irony though, the apartment that the fire started in was newly renovated and the tenant only lived there for probably less than a week!\r\nNow here comes the kicker, the previous tenant was this little old lady who lived there for about 25 years, she finally moved to a retirement home, and she smoked like a Chimney! It actually got so bad that i had to complain to the landlord that the smoke was coming into my apatment, which was located on the 1st floor west side :shock:. My worst fear was that one day she\'d fall asleep with a friggin\' Pall Mall between her finger burning like a camp fire and that would be the end of it.\r\n\r\nFunny how things work huh...');
