INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37396, '51e14073de', 're:', 'While these are not being made for Bits, a similar process could be used.\r\n\r\n[url=http://www.oldweirdherald.com/scalestuff/onethreetwo/silicones/silicones.html][color=red:51e14073de]Tire Casting 101[/color:51e14073de][/url]\r\n\r\nWithout spending alot of cash to test the idea you would use plaster in place of resin and silicone in place of the RTV.  I would imagine you could use Moldbuilder [?I think that\'s the name] latex as well.  \r\n\r\nMost general purpose clear silicone\'s can be cut with mineral spirits to make it a little more flowable.  And then there\'s always flowable windshield &amp; glass sealer available in the automotive section at Wal-mart among other places [42g tube sells for a couple bucks]\r\n\r\nI may have to give this a go myself.  Those Hot wheels sourced wheels he\'s got the stubby tires on  rock!\r\n\r\nhttp://members.surfeu.de/cyberjunky/spikesb9.jpg');
