INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3389, '0b669f8a17', '', 'Does the propo make a difference? In the immortal words of Steve Austin..."OH HELL YEEE-AH!"\r\n\r\nAdd to the fact is got an actual differential in the rear...Not only is it smooth on the turns, it\'s got a hella-tight turning radius.\r\n\r\nThe thing that sucks, and I\'m not the only one who\'s suffered this...Is that the front end occasionally gets locked up (whether the jam is at the servo, gears or what...hard to say) and you\'ve gotta take that thing APART to unjam the shit.\r\n\r\nThe other who\'s had the problem, johnk from that link I posted, seems to have gotten a replacement from YoHomo so maybe things are better.\r\n\r\nWill the Nazi Rims fit? I\'d say they should, since one of the pics from the link shows the Pukey Maru with Precious (Bit Clone) rims.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know if I could handle seeing the Pukey Maru with Nazi rims...I just might shit a brickhouse man!  :shock:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3390, 'a9ad14e637', 'Ph2t\'s phatass techo register', 'Yo pimps!\r\n\r\nI\'m sick and tired of having to search the whole bloody net these days to find techo stuff about this madass little toys.  So I thought I\'d do the pimpin thing and put\'em all in one place.\r\n\r\nCheck it!\r\n\r\n[b:a9ad14e637]Bit-G schematics:[/b:a9ad14e637]\r\n\r\n[url=http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/49mhz-tx_schem.jpg]49Mhz Transmitter[/url]\r\n[url=http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/49mhz-rx_schem.jpg]49Mhz Receiver[/url]\r\n\r\n[b:a9ad14e637]OOK (On -Off Keying) TX / RX schemes used by these Bits[/b:a9ad14e637]\r\n\r\nInfo can be found [url=http://members.aol.com/rchelicam/microszr/microszr.htm]here[/url] and [url=http://www.amalgamate2000.com/radio-hobbies/radio/Super-regen.htm]here[/url].\r\n\r\n[b:a9ad14e637]Datasheets about TX/RX chipsets[/b:a9ad14e637]\r\n\r\nTX2/RX2 (revision C with turbo mode) is [url=http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/tx-2rx-2.pdf]here[/url]\r\n\r\nTX6/RX6 chipset (used in 4-chan controller, also new MS\'s? possibly?) can be found [url=http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/SCTX-6BAZ.pdf]here[/url]\r\n\r\nAlternate TX6/RX6 chipset, known as the PT8A9701 (TX) and PT8A973/973L (RX).  This is a pin-for-pin replacement for the TX6/RX6 chips, the datasheet is in english (or engrish?). I would assume that the timings and other essential info are compatible with the TX6/RX6 chips.   Get it [url=http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/PT8A9701-973-973L.pdf]here[/url].\r\n\r\nIf anyone has anything else to add that would be great!  Namuna, I\'m sure you have a shitload of data from your tests. :) \r\n\r\nph2t.');
