INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3806, 'ba94483809', '', 'Alright, I found out more info on them Dub City cars...What we want is the \'Model Kits\'...It\'s basically a car/truck with a couple extra wheel sets.\r\n\r\nCheck it:\r\nhttp://www.hobbypeople.net/gallery/642959.asp\r\n\r\nAnd they\'re rubber tires too! From what I read, they ain\'t got the center rib on the rims (for the holing the tires on, just like the German Alloys don\'t have it either)...So some modifications are required for that too.\r\n\r\nThese Muscle Machines kits could be worthy as well:\r\nhttp://www.hobbypeople.net/gallery/366156.asp\r\n\r\nThe hunt continues.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3808, 'ce6d43c18e', '', 'I didn\'t buy that dub model kit so maybe they have softer rubber tires. I bought a dub city car that was allready together. the wheels I got could have had rubber tires but they were so hard that they might as well be plastic. My work around for this was putting on the small bit tires. They slip off unless you add a couple of dots of glue on there. :wink: \r\n\r\nThat muscle machine kit is exactly what I got and they have a set of rims in there that are almost identical to the dubs (dubs seem to be more shiny).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (3809, 'c78f4e34d4', '', 'Still trying to make this POS useful, I decided the easiest way was to use some of those batteries I got from Namuna and dual cell it - I did.\r\nLeaving everything else the same - it was basically just a dual celled POS still.\r\nMoved to my next thought. The gear on the motor itself is huge (see page 1 - kinda), and putting the normal black gear wouldn\'t touch to the other gear. I decided to hack at the chassis to allow room for the motor to scoot forward - and used the tabs from the batts, wrapped in electrical tape, to push the motor forward and off the rear casing. I could now put in my motors with the normal black gear. It\'s still basically just a dual celled POS.\r\nThe only left that could be holding this thing back is the pcb, I\'m not going to transfer a pcb off a good car to shit car just so I can say the POS is somewhat useful.\r\nDid I mention I hate this OEM Thunderbold Bullet Crapper Benzo, from chassis to the body - it\'s a POS.');
