INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (4513, '6a3f043131', '', 'Sure, no sweats.\r\n\r\nThe SRM mod is based on the theory that if you boost power to the TX you _should_ be able to get greater range on the pissweak MS controllers.  The thread for this mod is at [url=http://www.tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=10226]tinyrc.com[/url] and also at [url=http://www.ausmicro.com/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=476&amp;FORUM_ID=9&amp;CAT_ID=2&amp;Topic_Title=S%2ER%2EM+%28Super+Range+Mod%29&amp;Forum_Title=BCG+%2D+Technical]ausmicro.com[/url].\r\n\r\nThe multi freq mod is still in theory, getting data stage.  I want to be able to make my TX\'s on their own freqs so not to conflict with other TX\'s when racing.  There is a thread at [url=http://www.ausmicro.com/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=254&amp;FORUM_ID=9&amp;CAT_ID=2&amp;Topic_Title=RF+mod+%2D+more+controller+channels&amp;Forum_Title=BCG+%2D+Technical]ausmicro.com[/url] about it but this mod is sorta on hiatus until i can get my hands on a CRO.  There is two possible ways I _think_ it can be done.  1) modify the RX circuit to decrease it\'s bandwdith (currenty at 8MHz, this can be seen on the TX freq\'s avail today @ 27Mhz, 35Mhz, 40Mhz, 45Mhz, 49Mhz, and 57Mhz) and make it more "selective" on what signals it recieves.  Then moving the TX osc freq to somthing in between the freqs I just listed.   2) modify the osc on the TX2C and RX2C chipsets (the 220K resistor between pins 11&amp;12 on the TX and pins 4&amp;5 on the RX) so to send the L/R/Fwd/Rev commands on a different modulated freq.  It\'s all still in brainfark stage at the \'mo and I don\'t know if it will even work.....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
