INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6097, '11f86a53a4', '', 'yes i would have to agree.. it is one of the nicest ive ever been to..  and its quite large..  1/3 of the store is R/C planes..  they even have turbine powerd R/C\'s  then a big chunk is R/C cars/trucks/boats.  and in the middle are slot cars/ trains/ models/ bobbleheads/ Painting accessorys...and other nik naks..  their website is kinda new.  its just a bunch of links right now..   anyway from what i understand they are one of the largest resalers of the Traxxas trucks.  its awesome. i want one of the T-maxx\'s  but dont have that money to spend..  they have 1 corner of the store dedicated to this truck..  you can get any part, in chrome, anadized in any color, or i think even carbon fiber...  either way they have it all.\r\n\r\nhowever their microsizers are still 36.00(first gen). and they dont have sports or pro\'s.  but they do have MS accessorys... once again at a fairly steep price..\r\n\r\nhttp://www.rccountryhobbies.com/');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39125, '69e55ccf14', 'Do NOT read this if you get pissed off by newb questions!!!!', 'Umm...I was wondering about track surfaces, and barriers. \r\nHere are the Q\'s. \r\n\r\nWhat do you use for surfaces to race on? I want something hard, smooth, and perfectly flat to race on, something similar to a hardwood floor.\r\n\r\nWhat is PVC pipe, or plastic? Is it bendable, and can it be put together/taken apart? If so, how easily?\r\n\r\nWhat is the price range? Where can I buy the cheapest effective working material?\r\n\r\nWhat about barriers? Is that what PVC pipe is for?\r\n\r\nSorry for all the newb questions, but I\'m really desperate and I can\'t race on thick carpet....That\'s why I\'m looking for "put-together and take-apart" surfaces to lay on the carpet......Again, sorry to piss peeps off.');
