INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6377, 'db9101841d', '', 'yep, i know. The bit god shined a little bit though, because after i was about to thow that POS across the room, i opened up and did a little snip snip to my  57mhz crontrollybob and bam! 30\' range. No problem till the car fell apart spontaniously &lt;sp?. In like 2 days, the axle came loose, the front wheels got all wiggly, the steering stopped and the pcb came unsoldered. I think it was telling me that after a year of having only one car, its time to get another one  :D \r\n\r\nnow i\'m looking for a 57mhz car to play "dremel" with.  :twisted:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6378, 'd10339900a', '', '[quote:d10339900a="TheFanMan"]what a minute now! There\'s no stealing involved if you [i:d10339900a]leave[/i:d10339900a] it here. You gave it to me because I didn\'t have a charger from overmodding things (I have problems with doing that). But, I took pics for ya fish, and here they are:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.kassatsu.com/antenna1.jpg\r\nhttp://www.kassatsu.com/antenna2.jpg\r\n\r\nI did the mod job, but on this one the antenna is foldable and fits perfectly in cowfish\'s case.\r\n\r\nO, and, #2: I only got better range is because I put a longer antenna on my car too, but... meh. I HAVE IT NOW! HAHAHAHAHA :twisted: [/i][/quote:d10339900a]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\noi! don\'t take all the credit there.  With me 4 band: You did the initial hackin\' and fittin\',  then it all fell apart, (we learned about hot glue and it\'s no beneficialness)  so i opened it up and did some more hackin\' and fittin, and eventually screwed the antenna in with a 2" long wood screw :P and then cut the extra 1.75" off with a hacksaw. Man, that was soo much fun. You should see the back of it, maybe TheFanMan should take a pic.  :D');
