INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6884, '3bda4634fc', '', 'ok man this is how u pull of tuners hotwheels cars take a set of pliers, be very careful u don\'t scratch the rims (put a cloth between rim (silver part) and plier. Then you see the line between black and black on the backside of the riim? get the piler on the outer black one and pull like hell. Thats what i did. I got another one and i gave up on it. I just bought a Microsizer PRO. its the bomb black bB and it came with a clear bB. I also bought the Yellow GT-R body set at toys r us. I might go back there and pick up a CELI or RX-7 body set. Just maybe. I picked up my first homie today. And i got the \'66 stang and the some thing year ford something  (purple) PHAT BOYZ. there the bomb. bling on yall.\r\n\r\nedit... you put the tires on the front rims the normal regular tomy or hobbico tires. (supposing there stock) and the front rims of the hotwheels tuners shoudl just slide on. On the back well.... either do the small rim mod, or take some CA glue and glue the to the rear. Youw ill need to shave your chassis to do this work in the rear, and in the front. BEWARE ANYTHING HERE THAT DOSE NOT WORK IS NOT MY FAULT, AND I WILL NOT TAKE COMPLAINTS FOR IT. IVE TRIED THE MOD AND IT WORKS, BUT YOU WILL NEED TO SHAVE CHASSIS AND WILL NEED TO SHAVE THE BODY. -pimpike.');
