INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6969, '12e080c86c', '', 'The prices are a rip if ya ask me. I try to stay away from any site that puts up a retail price for a clone at over $25.\r\n\r\n*edit -Damn I should read closer :twisted: \r\n2 cars for $17 aint bad but I\'m wondering what they ask for shipping.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40426, 'f9fb4c4af8', '', '[quote="TMP"]Why cant my Xmod drift like that? it looks so easy... whats the secret?[/quote)\r\n\r\n\r\ntorque. and pvc for tires.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40427, '79c121e3ab', '', 'I\'m guessing you guys haven\'t seen my videos:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.guysmily.com/files/zgdrift.wmv\r\nhttp://www.guysmily.com/files/zgstage2.wmv\r\n\r\nAll it takes to drift is the right amount of oversteer.  RWD is too much oversteer with Xmods, at least in my opinion.  However, as long as you can get your car spinning in donuts (full throttle, full steering in one direction), then drifting is simply a matter of controlling those donuts and linking different donut pieces together.\r\n\r\nXmods are really difficult to drift.  Unless you\'re on a nice floor like a classroom, you\'ll need taped tires.  A spinbrush magnet swap couldn\'t hurt either.\r\n\r\nI gave up on Xmods recently, and bought a heavily modded Micro RS4 for around $240.  It handles and performs much better, and I don\'t have to worry about breaking connections when I hit something, or drivetrain parts wearing out after only a few weeks with a barely-modified motor.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6972, 'f971e7ac80', '', 'I don\'t like it... but then again, I have very strong feelings about clones. Unless you\'re hitting them with a hammer.. then be my guest');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6973, '42d795a7b4', '', 'Stoli you give up too easy, I was like that too, but then after I got one mod to work - I was hooked again lol\r\n\r\nthis is pretty tough mod just because of the tiny soldering on the pcd - don\'t let it get ya down man.\r\nyou were complaining about prices for bits, just wait till you go 1:10 scale... and break something.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (6974, '964d4b9938', 'THANX DAGENERAL ( whoever you are )', 'Thanx to C-dub for posting DaGeneral\'s Antenna mod. As I said earlier in another thread I tried to do the crip cap mod and failed. So I was looking at on old boombox of mine and well.......\r\n\r\n[img:964d4b9938]http://stoli.lixlink.com/Images/bits/holy%20long%20enough.JPG[/img:964d4b9938]\r\n[img:964d4b9938]http://stoli.lixlink.com/Images/bits/no%20cutting%20required.JPG[/img:964d4b9938]\r\n\r\nI was able to mod it in the stock hole with a little BFI ( brut force and ignorance) Just a question though. how the Fack do you brace that thing from breaking through the plastic. My controller is literally bending because of the weight. the Antenna is about 3 ft long. It improved my distance by about 15FT. Just need to solder it in properly for it to work better. I bet I\'d get awesome distance if I didn\'t live in a concrete and steel APT building!');
