INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7568, '3892351417', '', '[quote:3892351417="cj"]Picked up a copy of Scale Auto Magazine and found two company\'s in the states that do custom machined Aluminum wheels for model cars.  I email\'d both for more detail and if they could make bit/zip sized wheels.\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.mas-parts.com/[/url]\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.xstuning.com/[/url]\r\n\r\nI\'ll let you peeps in on any info I can get from them.[/quote:3892351417]\r\n\r\nJust heard from one of them \r\n\r\n[quote:3892351417] I can do the turned aluminum rims but the photo etched centers are the problem. Business has been very slow and I just don\'t have the capital to run any new photo etched panels at this time.\r\n If you think these will be a high volume item we can look into running a panel with just your items on it. You will be looking at around $2,000 dollars for a run of ten panels plus $500 to $750 for artwork time. I know it\'s alot of money but it will get you a lot of parts and a few different styles of spokes.\r\n Let me know if you are still interested and we can work on some quotes.\r\nRegards\r\nMark A. Smakal\r\nOwner\r\nMachined Aluminum Specialties\r\nwww.mas-parts.com\r\n[/quote:3892351417]\r\n\r\nThis sounds cool but expensive.  by the way the other compamy is not making aluminum rims sorry.');
