INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7655, 'c58094629b', '', 'My bro-in-law and I ran two Compact Char-G\'s together using a fresh pair of alkalines in each controller.\r\n\r\nUnmodded 27Mhz S2000 - 0:02:45 runtime from 0:00:53 charge.\r\nModded 40 Mhz Skyline - 0:06:10 runtime from 0:02:10 charge\r\n\r\nBoth bits contain the stock 60mAh NiCd\'s.\r\n\r\nThe results make sense for the increased charge time.\r\n\r\n 8) \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7657, 'c78d515172', '', 'I\'ve already got a plan. Put the bearings in the chassis, attach the idler gear to an axle for an idler gear shaft, and let the idler gear shaft spin free in the chassis. It might create more inertia, but it would be way smooth.\r\n\r\nI am thinking of how a ball diff could be done. I just need time, and money, and more time to make money.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7658, '04dd883334', '', 'Yeah, the motors I\'ve bought from Bit Char-G Motors have been my best. I had a problem with one of my motors falling out of the package, and he sent me an extra for my trouble, so if there is a problem they will make it right.\r\n\r\nI also saw his deals on ebay. First I had seen the 5 motors, and a battery package for $30, and thought that was a good deal. Then I started seeing the same deal with a Bit included for $35, and I was like, what the hell, thats a no brainer. If I had some cash right now, I\'d being jumping on that shit.\r\n\r\nFor you guys skeptical of ebay, remember your not dealing with ebay, your dealing with bitchargmotors.com, and ebay just skims a fee for adverstising a product. So I don\'t see any reason not to go for one of his auctions if he\'s selling on ebay. Just something to consider.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7659, '2ee3f02fda', 'It\'s Alive!', 'Franken-zap lives again. Back from the dead, it\'s a more subtle, refined car now.\r\n\r\nI ended up using the PCB from the LXX booster. The steering coil wires had fried, and were a dull grey color, so I replaced the steering coils. The LXX had some kick ass steering coils in it, so my steering is better than ever. While I was at the front end, I replaced the clear plastic bulk head thing with a black Microsizer one, because the clear plastic cracks too easy. I had to shave it down here and ther to get it to fit. I also covered the holes from where I moved the steering coils back.\r\n\r\nI liked how kwikbb kept his dual cell looking stock, so I decided turn Franken-Zap into a dual cell sleeper. I painted the PCB board cover to help hide, "my little secret". I think this is going to be temporary. Anyone want to take bets on it making through the weekend before I tri-cell it again?\r\n\r\n\r\nSee, innocent enough. Just a painted PCB cover that\'s all...\r\n[img:2ee3f02fda]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/refined.jpg[/img:2ee3f02fda]\r\n\r\n...or is it? \r\n[img:2ee3f02fda]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/refined2.jpg[/img:2ee3f02fda]\r\n\r\nRight now it\'s wearing my new favorite body, but I\'m going to buy a new ZZ to put this body on, because I want to see the hubcaps with it.\r\n[img:2ee3f02fda]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/maro.jpg[/img:2ee3f02fda]');
