INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7735, '1247a34f3d', '', 'great ideas nox.\r\n\r\nI would still like to iron out some details about it though.\r\nFirst off, FTP - I like this approach, but then what enters my mind is... these people are already having trouble hosting their own images, I\'m betting we\'d spend a lot of time trouble shooting and playing tech support to tell people what programs to FTP with, how to connect, how to FTP, where to FTP, how they find the link after FTP, making sure they don\'t overwrite someone elses file by accident, etc.\r\nSo I\'m still undecided about FTP.\r\n\r\nHosting them on my server is not really an option.\r\nThe reason is because I pay a company to host me (all this stuff) - they offer packages, I can\'t just pay an extra $$$ whatever for more space - I\'d actually have to upgrade to entirely new package which the difference is about 300.00. At that point, we\'re still not  in the clear, I\'d have to setup a semi-secured section of the site for FTPing (issue above again now). Then I would think of allowing attachments, my problems there are time to program in to the forum application (biggie) - and making it "stupid" proof - so if users tried to do something not kosher (like uploading a 5MB file to share with a pal) I would have to automatically check for things like this and a bunch of other crap. Eventually I\'d moderate an "uploading" directory and my server more than I would the website.\r\n\r\nAt this point - the site makes no $$$ - so it\'s kind of a hard investment for me to make to increase the server capabilities for my users. Until I find a solution that really makes a lot sense.\r\nI am open to more suggestions so if you guys got em, let\'s hear em.\r\nI\'ll still continue to try and find a solution myself.\r\nFor now, I\'m affraid the best we can offer is giving them FTP access to a freebie site, trust them to do the right things and hope all goes well.');
