INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7803, 'b16998c717', '', 'Well, I missed that opportunity. None of the Radio Shacks around me had any of those tuner kits left. One said they did, but they had the starter sets with the F&amp;F bodies. I didn\'t want to leave my house for no reason, so I said, Ok give me that. It\'s not bad, but on the way home I kinda wished I got the 350Z, but that don\'t matter because it\'s gonna be wearing one the muscle car bodies anyways. I\'m not too bummed about the tuner set because I wasn\'t that into those bodies, and I have faster motors, just seemed like a good deal if I could find it. More just irritated that I was led on. On the plus side, both RSs right next to me have pul-lenty of the muscle cars, so I\'ll have no trouble getting a couple of those later this week.\r\n\r\nSo anyways here\'s the RX-7 that came with it. It\'s not too bad, anxious to see how it runs, but I need to clean the kitchen first, so I might not get to it right away. :wink:\r\n[img:b16998c717]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/zzrx7.jpg[/img:b16998c717]\r\n\r\nAlso when I was there he was checking out a new 1/43 scale car they got in. I don\'t know how much these are like the Vipers they had before, but this was a Vette, and it was pretty nice. I like the charging base because it looked like a nice dispay stand that comes with die-cast collectibles, and the car was pretty quick. About as fast as a dual-celled bit. He let me drive it, and I couldn\'t tell if the steering was proportional, but on that low pile carpet they have in RS it was a blast to drive, and fast enough to pitch the rear end around through corners, even with the grip from the carpet. Thing would probably go mad on tile. It also has headlights, turn signals, and hazard lights you control from the controller. The $49 kinda turned me off, but I guess I\'ve put more than that into my Franken-Zap, and it\'s cheaper than a Mini-Z, so I guess that\'s not a bad price, but I\'ll wait until after next Christmas, and see if I can get one of these for $12 like they cleared the Vipers out at.\r\n\r\n**checked it out on the website, and the steering is proportional, and they\'re calling it a limited editon. I think I want it. Check it out...[url=http://www.radioshack.com/product.asp?catalog%5Fname=CTLG&amp;category%5Fname=CTLG%5F009%5F008%5F001%5F000&amp;product%5Fid=60%2D4343]1/43 scale Corvette[/url]');
