INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40317, '552fd863ce', 'Disturbing. Funny.', 'My heart skipped a beat when I found out SpikeTV is playing all the old Ren &amp; Stimpy Classics. Holy sheee-at I remember when it first came out, NOTHING else was like it, and still today there are plenty of pretenders to the throne.\r\n\r\nWhat REALLY broke RnS apart from the others was it\'s edgy in-your-face attitude, but WITH some flair and creativity. There was 1 episode in particular that kicked me square in the nuts and forever BURNED a place in my memory...And goddamit I recorded it last night!\r\n\r\nAnd I present here for all of you to enjoy, any fans of the show should know it. it is a clip from the episode \'Stimpy\'s Fanclub\'. I\'m gonna sound like hogjowlz in a dress saying this, but the first time I saw it I got CHILLS and even now when I watch it I\'m still feelin it. John Krickfalusi (or however the hell he spells it) was a damned GENIUS and the retards at Nick fired him. \r\n\r\nDon\'t spread the link around, it\'s on my site and I\'ll be yankin it soon enough\r\n\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/lincoln/Misc/RnS/RnS.htm\r\n\r\nEnjoy.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (7968, '36f33522c0', '', '[quote:36f33522c0="Stoli"]Tthats pretty phat Pimp. \r\n\r\nhow did ya do it? Just masked and prayed?[/quote:36f33522c0]\r\nI layed the Blue fade on the White, then masked and sprayed the Charcoal\r\n\r\n[quote:36f33522c0="hogjowls"]well i commend you on the nice flame job but i see no use for a pcb cover in the first place.[/quote:36f33522c0]\r\n90% of my cars are held together with tape, I wanted to build a dual cell sleeper, and the cover is hiding the goods. \r\n\r\nSee the idea here is to trick the competition into thinking that I\'m so busy detailing, that I couldn\'t possibly have anything going on under the hood. Of course that\'s pretending I had freinds to use as competition. :wink: \r\n\r\nI decided to go ahead and paint the chassis. I\'ve got nothing else to do today, so I\'ll keep you guys updated with pics.\r\n\r\nI masked the internals, and areas where there will be moving parts making contact. I sanded it down so the paint will stick, but mostly to remove my super glue blobs. I also took out the "Made in China" while I was at it. After the time I put into it, I  say it\'s Made in USA now!\r\n\r\n[img:36f33522c0]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/chassis1.jpg[/img:36f33522c0]\r\n\r\nI\'m painting right now, so more shots soon.');
