INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40318, '24ea3121cf', '', '@Bird, I have a pair of alloys that I narrowed up for the front. The aluminum is soft enough it\'s fairly easy. I just rubbed it on 400 grit sand paper for a bit.\r\n\r\nI came real close to putting those ones there, but I\'ve been looking at a bunch of cars from the 70s, and they all have that mis-matched rim thing going, so I wanted do do something like that.\r\n\r\n@Son_Gokou, Ya know I love to paint, but I happen to like black, I dig stripes on muscle cars, and I really dig the Chevelle/SS logos. So I decided to accent what was there.\r\n\r\n@sg219, lol, Yeah dude them Dodges always look good on paper, but they\'re heavy mugs. Figure no one at the strip is completely stock, so with a little warming over a Chevy could easily take a Dodge, and personally, if you ask me, they look a hell of lot better doing it. I never cared for Dodge/Plymouths boxy designs.\r\n\r\nThe \'69/\'70 Chevelle/El Caminos where available with the 397. Based off the same block design as the 427, it has excellent power to weight ratio, and is one of Chevy\'s best motors.\r\n\r\nSo bring on your Dodges, I\'m not scared. :lol:  \r\n\r\nIn fact I think I\'m coming after Payaso\'s hoosier Challenger. Hey Payaso you got your pink slip (or RS reciept) ready?');
