INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40281, '83a19e42f9', '', 'Now see HOG....thats whats confusing me. Im no rookie to multi celling cars but heres the problem...\r\n\r\nEnvision the car facing away from you. As you know there is a battery compartment towards the front and one towards the rear.\r\n\r\n[quote:83a19e42f9]i soldered a wire to the positive end of one of the batteries.[/quote:83a19e42f9]\r\n\r\nWhich ...the first battery towards the front or the rear? OR did you simply remove them completely ..?\r\n\r\n[quote:83a19e42f9]then i soldered to the negative on the third and ran a wire from the positive end of the third cell to the terminal in the battery compartment [/quote:83a19e42f9]\r\n\r\nIm trying to folow you here...You left the 1st battery touching its battery compartment (+) terminal , soldered a wire from your (-) terminal in the same compartment to the (+) end of your second battery ( which was originally in the second battery compartment) , another wire from the (-) end of your 2nd battery to the (+) end of your 3rd battery and FINALLY (lol).\r\n\r\nconnected the 3rd batteries (-) end to the (-) terminal of the 2nd battery compartment towards the rear wheels..?\r\n\r\nMy confusion stems from the fact that i already have a few 3 cell packs wired up....but i dont know if all i have to do is place a wire from the positive end of the pacl on the 1st battery compartments positive end and then adda awire to the negative end of the 2nd battery compartment (coming from the negative end of the pack). That seems simple but i dont know if the 2 compartments are connected like that ( where all i need to do is make a "bridge between the (+) and (-) terminals on each compartment)?');
