INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40269, 'ae814c7ea2', '', 'I\'m thinkin\' old....How about....\r\n\r\nDeeper Shade of Soul--Urban Dance Squad  \r\nThe Tower--Ice T\r\nMidnight--Ice T\r\nShock of the Hour--McRen\r\nBabylon--McRen\r\nAround the way Girl--LL Cool J\r\nAlive--Pearl Jam\r\nYellow LedBetter--Pearl Jam\r\n#41--DMB\r\nThe song that LL rips Canibus a new A-hole on.  Hardest LL ever.\r\n\r\n...Ya I think thats it...\r\n\r\nI\'m not a big fan of the new rap...The reason is that no one really raps anymore, its all samples and lip service.  They want it all dancey and 5hit.  Most rappers out there are so young all they remember is P. Diddy rippin\' stuff off and Master P puttin\' out the garbage on the curb. (Where are they now? Canidate--Master P)  I want original stuff.  Ya, they made their money, if you can make it...OK, but I like good music.   I didn\'t buy the trash.\r\n\r\nI like some of it, but once I here a song I like, the damn radio kills it and I don\'t even bother to check out the rest of the album, because the of the hype.  Plus when I have its turned out to be a let down....Jay-Z, Nelly, 50 cent (should of called himself 15 minutes).  None of todays rappers have any stayin\' power!!\r\n\r\nTupac and L.L. Coll J. are the greatest that ever was and will ever be!!!!\r\n\r\n\r\nBreath now.\r\n\r\n\r\n[color=green:ae814c7ea2][size=18:ae814c7ea2]I do like the playlist, always a good mix!!!!![/size:ae814c7ea2][/color:ae814c7ea2]');
