INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (8304, '42e9aec026', 'xbox', 'The xbox has a 733mhz pentium 3 with NVidia graphics all for $180 brand new. And as for Game selection, like i stated before, after a mod chip, you can get ANY game via the internet to play on an xbox. Heres a link to a 5 part series they did on tech tv on modding the xbox. It tell/shows you about some of the many advantages of a modded xbox.\r\n\r\n [url=http://cgi.techtv.com/search?query_text=xbox+mod&amp;section=The+Screen+Savers&amp;date_range=anytime]tech tv[/url]\r\n\r\nIt seems to me everyones ps2 basis is on games and namely one game. The xbox is capable of soooo much more than just playing games. But it also play them in the best graphics and all too. And like i have stated after modded you can play almost any game thanx to the internet.\r\n \r\nHere are some other sites to check out..\r\n\r\n[url=http://www.xboxcorp.com/online.shtml]xboxcorp online[/url]\r\n[url=http://www.a2zweblinks.com/games/download.htm]emulators and free game downloads to play any game[/url]\r\n[url=http://www.xboxhacker.com]xboxhacker.com[/url]\r\n[url=http://www.xboxhacker.net]xboxhacker.net[/url]\r\n[url=http://www.xbox-emulation.co.uk/]xbox emulation site[/url]\r\n[url=http://homebrew.dcemulation.com/xboxevo/]Another site with many nice articles and emulators, MAMEX used to play real arcade games on xbox!!![/url]\r\n\r\nNot to mention that all these sites hav emany other links to great info on xbox tech and stuff.\r\n\r\nSo yo ucan spend $180 to buy a $50 vice game to play (ps2) OR\r\nspend a little more on a modded xbox and play any game from any system including arcade games all for free from the internet plus movies, divx, dvd,music and sooo much more.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (8305, '43ed49b8c4', 'why?', '[quote:43ed49b8c4="midget_man1387"]definitely PS2 man.... I lvoe that system. I came out nearly a year before XBox and the graphics ar pretty close to the same. It has more games specially Vice City. The system is outstanding\r\n\r\n\r\noh yeah, and another thing... Imagine riding your bike a few blocks away to your friend\'s house with an XBox on your back.... Now imagine doing the same with a PS2. The PS2 is much smaller and lighter, and the controller is the best out of every controller on the market\r\n\r\n\r\njuss my two pennies[/quote:43ed49b8c4]\r\n\r\nWhy lug your console anywhere, when an xbox can link to the internet and play your friend or anyone over the net for free without leaving your house. OH, and the graphics are far from being close.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (8307, 'deb1f3a7e5', 'Who have you seen LIVE in concert ?', 'Just as it says, List the bands or solo\'s you have seen in concert.\r\n\r\nI\'ll start... (no particular order)  remember, I\'m in my late 30\'s.\r\nIf you don\'t know a band...look it up on the web...\r\nI\'m sure some of you younger homies will be postin bands \r\nI\'ve never heard of either... or my list sounds like your rents.\r\n\r\n\r\nBoomtown Rats. \'82\r\nYes\r\nStevie Ray Vaughan W/ Double Trouble\r\nJ, Geils Band\r\nJohn Lee Hooker (my sister in law married bassist)\r\nCarlos Santana (meet backstage and chatted for 5 mins)\r\nTraveling Wilburys (Roy Orbison pass by me within inches)\r\nBob Dylan (2)\r\nJethro Tull (2)\r\nGenesis (w/  Phil Collins)\r\nPeter Gabriel (solo)\r\nPaul Simon (solo) (from Simon and Garfunkel)\r\nSteve Miller\r\nPink Floyd (2)\r\nPaul McCartney (wedding gift)\r\nGrateful Dead (too many times, friend worked on light crew)\r\nTodd Rundgren (many times)\r\nJohn Cafferty and the BeverBrown Band\r\nU2\r\nEDIT: the Firm (w/ Jimmy Page)\r\nEDIT: Robert Plant Solo\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nprobably some more...I\'ll have to edit when I remember.\r\n\r\nanything good in there?\r\n\r\n-nox');
