INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9416, '88d95c0c35', '', 'I bought a camouflauge one for parts, I had plans  to turn the Hummer into a Scottsdale Hummer (Scottsdale is the rich part of town just outside of Phoenix, and that\'s what I call the Hummers with the fancy paint jobs, and chrome rims, because I never see those things here on the Wess Side, anyways back to my original story...), but I had to break it to get it off the chassis, oh well. Cannonball bodies are always a snug fit, but this one was extra snug.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately Cannonballs are a tad longer than bits so the bodies are not compatible. Cannonballs also have a 7.2:1 gear ratio, that\'s why the chassis is stretched slightly, to accomodate the 10-tooth pinion.\r\n\r\nHow\'s that Hummer run? I\'ve had 2 cannonballs that were total duds, with great motors, and batteries, and I have one that actually kicks freakin\' butt, and handles good too.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9417, '9a0a8e1a1e', '', 'Dats true to dood. I fogot about that in PS\r\n\r\nHere is goes.\r\n\r\n-Create a video with your camera. ( usually AVI ) \r\n-Take the video and open it into Adobe Premier 6.0 or higher\r\n-Drag the image from the preview window to the timeline under "Video 1A\r\n-Choose File--&gt;Export Timeline --&gt; Choose Movie.\r\n-In this new window click the settings button\r\n-Choose Filmstrip from the drop down beside "file Type"\r\n-Click Okay and save the file to your desktop.\r\n\r\nNow Open Photoshop\r\n\r\n- Goto File--&gt; open--&gt; choose your filmstrip you just created.\r\n- Once it opens on the tools pallet double click the magnifne glass. Each from should now open up.\r\n- Use the Image--&gt;Adjustments to make any Colour/Brightness etc mods you want/need too.\r\n- Choose File and Save the filmstrip again.\r\n\r\nReopen premier.\r\n\r\n-Open the new filmstrip you just created in Photoshop and drag it dow to timeline video 1A again.\r\n\r\n- Choose File --&gt; Export Timeline--&gt;Choose Movie again.\r\n- In the settings box this time choose Microsoft AVI. \r\n- Click Okay and save it to your desktop again.\r\n\r\nNow open Windows Movie maker ( win XP only unless downloaded for 98SE)\r\n\r\nStart--&gt; All Progs--&gt;Accessories--&gt;Movie Maker\r\n\r\n-Click File--&gt; Import\r\n-Choose you newly created AVI.\r\n- Drag the imported movie clips starting with the first one to the box on the timeline to the left and continue down the row until done.\r\n-Click File--&gt;Save Movie\r\n- Choose Highest quality\r\n- Click Okay\r\n- Save the file on your desktop.\r\n\r\nTo add music.\r\n\r\nJust import the MP3/Wav the same way you did the movie and shorten it by dragging from the end of the timeline back to the end of your movie.\r\n\r\nIts a kinda long way around but it makes the best movies possible and I personally have taken 10MB AVI\'s and made them 900KB-1.5 MB WMV\'s\r\n\r\nCheer\'s :-D  :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9418, '7634b9d08d', 'So I got a little aggressive.', 'Went in RS today to get me an extra pair of muscle car bodies to paint, when I see one last Street Tuner set. As I was seeing it, this other guy points at it, turns to his friend and says, "Check this out.." before he turned back around I had it on the counter and was handing the cashier my cash. I told the cashier I called over the weekend they said they didn\'t have any, and he told me "We just got them in, and already there\'s only ...", he looked over my shoulder to see how many, and I said, "One, I mean, none".\r\n\r\nI would definately call that a snag. I feel a little guilty, but mostly I feel pretty damn cool.  8-)  \r\n\r\nAm I a bad person? I mean I\'ve never beat anyone down for a Tickle Me Elmo or anything like that. Well I did wait in a line for 2 hours because my wife wanted a Firby for Valentines Day, but that\'s another story.');
