INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9559, '52c9a07534', '', 'My 1st favorites were the KIT 2.2 &amp; 2.6.  These motors are fast and torquey.  Then I got my first performance motor, the EM3.2 &amp; 3.5.  These were the ultimate in performance for me, not a lot of torque but tons of speed.  But of course there\'s always gonna be a bigger/better motor that comes out.  Up popped the Perfection 3.8, then the Perfection 2.2 &amp; 3.0. Now we have the Phast motor, EM 3.8 Vanquish &amp; 3.5 Big Block plus Perfection has a 4.2 High torque &amp; race motors out now!(2 fer $4)   Now who can pick from all this?   :???:    \r\nI\'ll let you know, I have a couple of Phast, Perf 4.2, EM 3.8 coming.:smile:  \r\n I\'ll do an extensive report on them and post. \r\nStay tuned!:jam:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9560, '7f2d319057', 'Dual Cell Battery Pack', 'I made a Dual Cell Pack that can be easily installed in a ZZ and maybe in a highly modified bit. No soldering is needed ( pre soldered) All you is cut/dremel the plastic "nubs" in the bottom of the chassis tub and drop the new pack in.  \r\n Basically i just soldered a small wire from neg of one to pos of other. ( i kept the batts going same direction and parallel to each other, so this wire is a diagnal from bottom of one to top of other batt)Then taped up the pos that was soldered. Then taped the 2 batts together tighly in a little "pack". Then soldered a small wired on the other batts positive and ran it straight across and left the stripped end lie on top the first batts positive end ( which is taped up) Thus creating a new contact point. Now just install as above and push this wire down between batt and contact to make a good connection. (use a knife or small screwdriver). Voila . No solder needed to install or remove this pack. can be installed or removed quickly from a ZZ. And if a bit was "tubbed" out big enuff would work for an internal on a bit too.\r\nHeres 2 pics of the top/bottom of the pack\r\n\r\n[img:7f2d319057]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid63/p6f57c193ac3cc92c36b3dcbb8bd369c3/fc0aa512.jpg[/img:7f2d319057]\r\n\r\n[img:7f2d319057]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid63/p55205143ed1a4cd772c040eecb5779fa/fc0aa515.jpg[/img:7f2d319057]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (9561, 'f774678d72', '', '[quote:f774678d72="DarkTari"]My 1st favorites were the KIT 2.2 &amp; 2.6.  These motors are fast and torquey.  Then I got my first performance motor, the EM3.2 &amp; 3.5.  These were the ultimate in performance for me, not a lot of torque but tons of speed.  But of course there\'s always gonna be a bigger/better motor that comes out.  Up popped the Perfection 3.8, then the Perfection 2.2 &amp; 3.0. Now we have the Phast motor, EM 3.8 Vanquish &amp; 3.5 Big Block plus Perfection has a 4.2 High torque &amp; race motors out now!(2 fer $4)   Now who can pick from all this?   :???:    \r\nI\'ll let you know, I have a couple of Phast, Perf 4.2, EM 3.8 coming.:smile:  \r\n I\'ll do an extensive report on them and post. \r\nStay tuned!:jam:[/quote:f774678d72]\r\nI got my EM Big Block (3.5)runnin\' in my booster right now, it rocks! With the extra current that the booster feeds the motor, it increases the acceleration even more :-D \r\nThat and kyle\'s 3.8 are all i run in my booster for "BIG" motors, for a little more technical action it\'s Tiny\'s F-34 all the way, it\'s got sick acceleration and great speed! I run that puppy in my 86. Can\'t forget about my single cell ZZ, i gotta say that i\'m really impressed with RS\'s 3.4 nitrous express motor... that combined with the RED speed gear and a 160 mah makes for big fun. And allas my beloved dual cell bit-zap.... [sniff, sob] she\'s sitting in the OR awaiting a transplant to resurrect her fine ass, again!\r\n\r\n-word\r\n-word');
