INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40116, '36745bb7e7', '', '[quote:36745bb7e7="crazydave"]And the motor has a big ol\' fat contact on the end. I don\'t know if that makes any difference, but it does seem to be a torquey motor.\r\n\r\n[img:36745bb7e7]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/newzzm.jpg[/img:36745bb7e7]\r\n\r\nI\'m curious if the 3.4s that come in the new muscle car tuner kits will be the same.[/quote:36745bb7e7]\r\n\r\nI experienced something a bit similar. I bought a KIT racer once, and I kept the 2.6 motor that came with it. But that was like, say, 4-6 months ago. A few days ago I got bored and opened it up....and HOLY SHIT! The armature was a pint-sized version of that of an Xmod or Mini-Z motor! :shock:\r\n\r\nBack on the topic: Since the motors have a new contact, maybe the armature of the motors may be different too. If that\'s so, we can take some winds off and make higher speed motors! \r\n\r\nI have yet to get the new SE\'s, but from what I\'ve read in this thread they sound PIMPIN.\r\n\r\n[quote:36745bb7e7]Im moving into an apartment...the rest is wood and tile and waiting for my bits.[/quote:36745bb7e7]\r\n\r\nDAMN YOU!!!!  :lol: Wish I were you right now.');
