INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (38735, '10629dd836', '', '[quote:10629dd836="sessiz"][quote:10629dd836="crazydave"]Menudo is ok....[/quote:10629dd836]\r\n\r\nYou sick bastard. :hurl:[/quote:10629dd836]You live around where I live, and the stuff is everywhere. People here consider it rude if you don\'t accept food when they offer it, and they\'re always offering it. i don\'t want to be rude, so I\'m always trying the stuff they bring me. \r\n\r\nThe Menudo they make at the water mart next to my work every saturday, and it actually smells really good, so I tried some, but ate around the tripe, it\'s like a soup, it\'s pretty good, but I know what tripe looks like, and that\'s why I don\'t like it. Pozole taste the same, but pork instead of tripe. Try Pozole if you get a chance, it\'s not bad.\r\n\r\nFunny story...They\'re always bringing me things I can\'t remember the names of, like Sopas, and Tortas. A Torta is a grilled beef sandwich on a Mexican bread with guacamole, lettuce, and \'maters. The beef is grilled with onions and green chilis and it kicks ass. So I said, "This is really good, what did you say it was called?", and the co-worker that brought it to me looks me in the eye, and say in a straight voice with his heavy accent, "It a beef sandwich, Dave."\r\n\r\nThey\'re always messing with me like that. :roll:\r\n\r\n\r\nAnother quick recipe:\r\n\r\n[b:10629dd836]Quick (almost) Donuts[/b:10629dd836]\r\nGet some of those biscuits that come in a tube that goes pop. Poke a hole in the center of all of them. Fry them in a pan full of oil heated at medium heat. Flipping them once, and watching for splatters. When they turn golden brown, pull them out, and drain them on paper towels. Roll them in powder sugar, or dip in chocolate icing.\r\n\r\nIt\'s almost but not quite like a domut, but they sure do taste good. :hungry:');
