INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10677, '80fd97980f', '', '[quote:80fd97980f="hogjowlz"]i bought another one of those today here in da burgh(got the other one in ohio) and it is just as good. 49mhz = 15foot range with no adjustments. no antenna sticking out of the car. goes straight turns even both ways and is way faster than a stock bit. hobbico is dropping the ball hard.\r\n\r\nthe only thing microsizers beat them out on is quality of the bodies but these aint that bad.[/quote:80fd97980f]\r\n\r\nAnd will a standard \'sizer body fit on one of these puppy\'s?  I would think it would.\r\n\r\nAlso Havok, you live in the middle of a cornfield too?  What state?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10678, '3f46fa0d4a', '', '[quote:3f46fa0d4a="hogjowlz"]hobbico is dropping the ball hard.[/quote:3f46fa0d4a]\r\n\r\nI gotta agree with that. My BigLots isn\'t open yet, so I haven\'t tried these yet, but for the price they\'re asking for Microsizers, I would expect more. My Bit Char-G was fine, once I took the cripple cap out of the controller, it was perfect, that\'s the bar by which I judge my other cars by, and all my Microsizers have been inconsistant, each with it\'s own little issue that needed be worked out. So far my newest Zip Zap is my only car that ever worked perfect out of the box.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10679, '3a30b85c91', '', 'very nice dave. your flames are superb. after the contest you should give us a tutorial or something.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10680, '6d2d2df500', '', 'I\'ll tell you something haven\'t tried on bit tires yet, but when I raced 1/10th scale me and my partner used to call this our secret weapon.\r\n\r\nWe used to use Simple Green on our tires. It\'s a degreaser, and any degreaser will give you more traction, by way of removing oils, but for some reason Simple Green softens the tires and leaves them sticky.  It\'s organic and safe, used it for a whole racing season with no problems. \r\n\r\nI\'m going to try it on bit tires, just waiting until we need some kitchen cleaner, but my wife keeps buying some Lysol citrus crap. Looks like I\'ll have to go to the store myself one of these days.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10681, 'fd6d57bb32', '', '[quote:fd6d57bb32="hogjowlz"]very nice dave. your flames are superb. after the contest you should give us a tutorial or something.[/quote:fd6d57bb32]\r\nI\'m already working on one...but you know, gotta wait until the contest is over, don\'t want to make it too easy for anyone.');
