INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (10773, '78f57a2cf8', 'The Getaway for PS2---&gt;Hidden car----&gt;Nissan Skyline G', 'for those of ya\'all who have The Getaway, I know where you can find a Skyline. If you haven\'t already beaten the game(you have free roam mode), enter this code during the FMV sequence that plays before the main screen:\r\n\r\nTriangle(3), Left, Square, Triangle(3), Left, Circle. If Entered correctly you\'ll hear a woman scream. Free Roam mode is in The "Extra Features" Menu at the main screen.\r\n\r\nNow, for the "tutorial"\r\n\r\nwhen you start off go straight and turn left at the first street you come to. Then, turn left again at the next street. Follow this road all the way down until you are forced to go left(by the Big Arch). Now, you will curve to the left and the road will split(one way straight, the other another curve, to the right) follow the right curve. Go straight through this intersection and follow the long road until you are once again forced left. Don\'t go left, instead, go straight, through the opening in the dark gray wall. Follow the little path until you reach the front of the mansion, and you have your choice of a Skyline or a TVR, right in front of the mansion. If you go into the garage across from the TVR, you will find a Lotus and a go-kart.\r\n\r\nThis is always the first thing that I do. I love the Skyline. It even has a boost function. to do this, you must be completely stopped. Hold R1(handbrake) and gas at the same time until the car edges forward. Release R1 and the car will have a small boost forward. This also works on certain other cars.\r\n\r\nwow, I wrote a lot. Time to play with my Skyline! :smile:  :-D');
