INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (11032, '5c451aebd8', 'Preliminary review of the NKOK 1/64th RC Boats', 'Haven\'t actually run them yet (Father\'s Day gift) but I\'ve got a few thoughts already.\r\n\r\nHere\'s the breakdown.\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]Bought from: Raidentech[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nThey did a SHIT job of packing and I got different boats than what I thought I was getting (thought I\'m cool with the boats I got). I DON\'T recommend these guys at all.\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]Cost: ~$36 for 2 boats, Shipped[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nI got em for a nice cheap price, but refer to my notes above\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]About the boats[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nThe Manufacturer is NKOK, they offer 3 variations; A Red (Ocean Runner), Yellow (also Ocean Runner) and a White (Micro Sea Explorer) one. Only availabe in 27MHz or 49MHz. The boats aren\'t specifically set for a specific frequency either (so it seems) so 1 place might have the red one with 27MHz and another company might have the red in 49MHz.\r\n\r\n-[b:5c451aebd8]In the package[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\n1 x Boat\r\n1 x Charge Stand\r\n1 x Controller\r\n1 x Charge Wire (to plug the boat into the charger)\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]Batteries[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nThe boat has dual Ni-Cads (same size as Bits).\r\nThe Controller needs a 9volt\r\nThe Charger needs 4xAAs\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]How the Boat works[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nThere\'s 2 propellers, each has it\'s own Motor. Steering is like a Tank, the controller has 2 forward/reverse buttons. Press both buttons up for forward, or just 1 button forward to turn and so forth.\r\n\r\n- [b:5c451aebd8]Range[/b:5c451aebd8]\r\nUntested, but the box says it\'ll go as far as 50ft.\r\n\r\nThat\'s the hard facts, as far as my personal thoughts...1 thing i am concerned about is that there\'s 2 motors in the boat, each controlling the propellers. Even perfectly matched motors will at some point start to vary in speed, which means pressing both controller buttons for forward will eventually mean the boat won\'t be going in a straight line. Given the simplistic nature of the setup, there\'s no steering trim either. We\'ll see I suppose.\r\n\r\nI\'ll report back with more info when I race my pops on Sunday.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (11033, '901f679b35', '', '[quote:901f679b35="kwikbb"]Not at all bro, go nuts! Can\'t wait to see the results, lemme know if you want me to come up with some more lyrics.\r\n\r\n-word[/quote:901f679b35]\r\n\r\nCool, I\'ll start something this weekend. It might take a while to complete a whole song though.\r\n\r\nMore lyrics, might be cool, but that would also be more for me to do. :roll: I\'m not a singer or a rapper, so I\'m not sure I can produce, but I\'ve been meaning to try some experiments with my voice so nows my chance. I\'ll probably have to get drunker than kwikbb singin\' Tom Jones on karaoke night. :eek: .');
