INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (11804, 'e8e8b0e285', '', 'BRING EM ON!!!! :hungry: \r\n\r\nI regards to the original transistors on the PCB Cab\'s I think we can leave them on.  I\'ve done a bit of thinkin\' (heh, lol!) and have come up with the following:\r\n\r\n[b:e8e8b0e285]How the H Bridge Controls Motor Direction[/b:e8e8b0e285]\r\n[img:e8e8b0e285]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/RX_H_Bridge_original_current_flow.JPG[/img:e8e8b0e285]\r\n\r\n[b:e8e8b0e285]FORWARD[/b:e8e8b0e285]\r\nWhen the car receives the command to go forward the RX chip turns on the transistor at the end of the [i:e8e8b0e285]dashed blue line[/i:e8e8b0e285], given the way transistors work this allows current to travel through the transistor, like an electrical switch, you give the transistor a little bit of current to turn on and it can let a lot of current through it\'s gates.   The transistor in the TOP RIGHT of the picture turns on as well (although a little differently \'cause it\'s a PNP transistor, out of the scope of this thread I think).  This means the current follows the [b:e8e8b0e285]solid blue line[/b:e8e8b0e285].  The motor then turns this way.\r\n\r\n[b:e8e8b0e285]REVERSE[/b:e8e8b0e285]\r\nWhen the car receives the command to go backwards the RX chip turns on the OTHER transistor at the end of the [i:e8e8b0e285]dashed red line[/i:e8e8b0e285].  The transistor in the TOP LEFT of the picture turns on as well.  The reverse of what happens above.  The current then travels in the direction of the [b:e8e8b0e285]solid red line[/b:e8e8b0e285].   This makes the motor spin in the other direction.\r\n\r\n[b:e8e8b0e285]This is how you get forward and reverse directions for the motor[/b:e8e8b0e285].\r\n\r\nGiven all this, if you take the motor out there will be no current flow at all.  The H Bridge might as well not exist for all it matters.\r\n\r\n[b:e8e8b0e285][i:e8e8b0e285]So yes Cab\'s I think you can pull this mod off without needing to remove ANY parts from the PCB.   I\'m gonna try this now on one of my Compacts to prove this.[/b:e8e8b0e285][/i:e8e8b0e285]\r\n\r\n:geek: \r\n\r\nph2t.');
