INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (11926, 'ee9db7a39e', '', 'Heya Modjo good to see ya here man, and welcome to THE place.\r\n\r\nUPDATE:\r\n\r\nAfter some testing yesterday I\'ve found that the current design has issues.   For some reason the output of the FETs I use aren\'t getting the same oompf (technical term, lol!) as the FETs from the german version of this mod.   This is really strange because on paper the FETs I use are meant to be better than the german selected FETs.  Oh well, more testing needs to be done.  So sofar the german version of this mod is still the best one out there......\r\n\r\nAlso the other problem (too many @$#^ problems! arghhhh!) is that if I leave the original transistors in, the voltage to drive the FETs is a max 0.7V.  The FETs I\'ve used need more than that to switch on.  I\'ve done some research and found some other FETs that WILL turn on at the low 0.7V level.  Just have to wait a week for delivery.......\r\n\r\nSo turn in next week at the same battime on the same batchannel.......');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (11927, '90f04700c0', '', 'I couldn\'t wait until tomorrow, so I went back today, and got 2 more. It\'s just so cool having cheap clones walking distance from my place.\r\n\r\nHavok, if your paying me up front, then I don\'t see a problem. They have tons there. Just PM me or check my profile for my email.\r\n\r\nI noticed the cars have chrome rims and the trucks have the red rims, so I got a couple cars. The yellow one is the same good quality as the SUV, but the red one had some quality issues. Nothing major, just that the PCB cover doesn\'t stay down, and the body is majorly crooked, but ironically this one was a tad quicker, and much more powerful than the first 2. I usually take a lap or 2 around the bed, before I move to the kitchen floor. The first 2 cars were getting hung up on the wrinkles in the sheets, but this one was pulling little jumps, and I never made it to the kitchen floor, because it liked to be romped, and I was having fun romping it.\r\n\r\nAll 3 steer excellent, the best I\'ve seen.\r\n\r\nI also noticed that these have a 7-tooth pinion, I haven\'t checked the final drive ratio yet.\r\n\r\nAn absolute steal for $5. I wish I could get over the bodies, but they\'re still great for parts, and projects. I\'ve got lots of plans for these.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:90f04700c0]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/tc1.jpg[/img:90f04700c0]\r\n\r\n[img:90f04700c0]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/tc2.jpg[/img:90f04700c0]');
