INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40011, '5d2b9adfcd', '', '[quote:5d2b9adfcd="payaso"]Aside from medicine/home remedies, try to lay down, and chill, and focus all of your attetion, and energy to the pain until you can only feel the pain, and nothing else.    This works well before bed.      Then you can feel it throbbing.  It\'s like when the throbbing starts, your body starts to do internal repairs. (The throbbing and pain should stop.)     I know it sounds weird, but it does wonders.[/quote:5d2b9adfcd]You know, that\'s exactly what I try to do, but no one will give me a moments peace the last couple days. \r\n\r\n[quote:5d2b9adfcd="Superfly"]Hey Dave- \r\n\r\nDon\'t you have a 3 or so year old? I ask because I\'ve started having some back trouble this year after 36 years of not ever having a sore back. Tried to figure out why, and realized I often carry a wiggling 30 lb rugrat while doing twisting things like opening car doors, cooking, whatever. Try taking a few days off carrying the little one, or when you do, hold her with both arms in front.[/quote:5d2b9adfcd]Why yes, I do have a 3 almost 4yo. You just maybe on to something there. I\'ve been blaming it on the unseasonally wet weather we\'ve been having, pressure systems, work, and BS like that. Never considered the kid. He\'s always making me throw him around, and swing him and stuff.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWell I got my new SE, and I\'m already in a better mood, even though the RS lied when I called ahead to see if they were in stock, and I ended up walking to the next one, for total of a 5 mile round trip, pushing a stroller. I would have been miserable, but after the day I had, it was to be expected, and I\'m just glad I made it home with a Chevelle.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (12520, '99b92b6450', '', 'That\'s a really great idea using the switch between batteries. I\'m going to use that technique to rig up one charger for single, dual, and triple cells, but my one criticism, from my experience with the testing I\'ve done, 3 cells is way overkill for a single cell, and 4 cells is slight overkill for dual cells. \r\n\r\nI\'ve found you get punchier more consistant from beginning to end runs when you charge at a slower rate for a longer time, ideally until the battery is peaked. I prefer 2 cells to charge 1 cell, 3 cells tocharge 2 cells, and 5 cells to charge 3 cells. \r\n\r\nI also hate timers, and rip those right out, and use my volt meter to watch for peak, but if your using a timer, chargeing at a faster rate will get you longer run times with the same charge time, it\'s just not what I consider ideal. I get 20+ minute runtimes from the stock Tomy cells, and 45+ minute runtimes from 150mAh cells.');
