INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (12526, '4901258736', '', 'I was talking to MicroAmps the other day and he was telling me how the newer perfection motors 4.0 &amp; 4.2 have the tendency to "keep going" after leftting go of the fwd button.   These motors have bugger all inertia on the rotor so they don\'t apply any breaking abilty unlike the lower rated motors, 1.0, 2.0, 2.2,...\r\n\r\nThe most excellent Japanese Bitchar-G website [url=http://www.age.jp/~ex2/bit.html]ex.2 BirChar-G[/url] has a mod for the H-bridge which gives to motor the ability to act like a brake.   So when you didn\'t press either fwd or rev the motor was acting as a brake.\r\nIt\'s called the [url=http://www.age.jp/~ex2/bit/09_custom.html]Neutral-brake Custom[/url].\r\n\r\nThe circuit has some extra components added to the regular transistor H-bridge.\r\n\r\n[img:4901258736]http://www.age.jp/~ex2/bit/09/09_1_01.gif[/img:4901258736]\r\n\r\nIt also needs to be modded even futher to be able to use FETs, still researching that one. :???: \r\n\r\nBreaking though hey? hmm,....   What sort of affect will that have on driving?   Very interesting.');
