INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (12943, '8d4336083e', '', '@all, this was our first contest so naturally there can be improvements.\r\nthe 2 picture limit deal is a very valid point, we\'ll have to see how better to approach that issue.\r\nthanks for sharing your thoughts with us, that\'s the only way we know if we need to change something or do it different way, etc.\r\neveryone\'s feedback is totally appreciated and not taken in any negative ways. that means you should feel free to express whatever concerns you have.\r\n\r\nas far as judging for this particular contest, hog and nox pretty much hit everyone\'s criteria I believe. For me, I looked at attention to detail, originality, time and effort spent, mods, drivability, etc. I\'d have to say looks played about 70% of my decisions and 30% on the technical mods - I\'m sure those #\'s are completely different for the other judges.\r\n\r\nI wouldn\'t feel comfortable saying that you should consider this contests judging for future contests, the reason why is because we might have contests that aren\'t so "looks" oriented, maybe they will be based more on the technical mods - at that point you might feel mis-led, thinking we were going to judge on looks more heavily than functionality.\r\n\r\nWe\'ll be sure to be very specific in any of our future contests when posting rules, etc.\r\n\r\n\r\nagain, thanks for speaking up - do not feel bad - we need your input so we can improve things on our end as well.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (12944, '12fb0943ee', '', '[quote:12fb0943ee="Buzzbait"]I was a bit (pun intended) bummed out by the fact that we were supposed to post two pictures of our cars. If you\'ve pimped your Bit with a lot of detail, there\'s just no way to show off all you\'ve done in two pics. This is especially true if you’ve been playing with LED mods. Pictures in the dark aren’t good for much other than proving your skills with the lights. Blowing half of your allotted pictures on a single mod is a big bummer. A two pic limit almost makes the photographer’s skill level just as important as the pimps skill with modding his ride. \r\n\r\nHog – A movie? Wouldn’t that have been against the rules? It would have also given definite advantage to the people with enough cash to afford to flick their bit. \r\n\r\nNot that I’m bitchin’. The contest rocked. I’m just tossin’ in a little input for the next contest.[/quote:12fb0943ee]\r\n\r\nI took this into consideration, read, and re-read the rules like a lawyer, I didn\'t see where a limit was ever established, so I took it as a minimum of two pics, like you know, one pic aint going to fly.\r\n\r\nIn some cases it\'s imperative that you show more that one pic. I mean you got to show the body front, and back, and sides,  and how could I just say I have a painted PCB cover, I have to show it, and I feel if you claim to have internal dual cell, well then you better open it up, and prove it with a pic. I also feel this is important, because in 1/10 scale concours judging they look at how clean you wired it up, and the whole complete package,\r\n\r\nOf coarse if a 2 picture limit is set then you could always make a collage for your second pic, or do like Hog suggested, and make an animated gif.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I would suggest for the future, you should have 2 "official" entry pics, both with your name hand written, and then allow as many detail shots as the person feels they need.\r\n\r\nHey, since I\'m posting, thanks again, and thanks for the continued compliments. Obviously I feel that this comp was run clean and fair, and the judges did an excellent job. ;)\r\n\r\nI feel like maybe you guys are waiting for me to start boasting, but really I feel humbled by all this, because now I\'m trying to figure out how I\'m going to top myself for the next comp, because I know one these other guys will, but I\'ve got a few plans brewing, we\'ll see, maybe I can still be a contender. :smile:');
