INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13168, '37b4478906', '', '[quote:37b4478906="dabigpig"]if glass is soo smoth then why is it that you can light a strike anywhere on it. found that out when i was drunk.[/quote:37b4478906]\r\nJust a theory, but maybe because of glass\'s crystaline structure makes it microscopically sharp, even though it appears smooth to us.  What appears smooth to us is actually rough under a microscope.\r\n\r\n[quote:37b4478906="Pie"]how did you cut so well with a knife? steady hands...?[/quote:37b4478906]\r\nI wish, I lost my nerves when I was 23, and my hands shake like leaves. \r\n\r\nJust keep the knife right on the outside edge of the black line, so no tape color shows through, and your not cutting into the black. Keep your right hand moving and turning, while you turn the glass with you left hand, try to keep one continuous stroke. Stopping and starting your strokes on the tips.\r\n\r\nJust force to the tip to go where to want, but not forcing it into the glass, and keeping the sharp edge aligned in the direction you\'re going.\r\n\r\nSeriously my hands do shake bad sometimes, if I can pull this off, I\'m confident that you guys can too.');
