INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13493, '3585e4103f', '', 'Found this over at phpBB [URL=http://www.phpbb.com/phpBB/viewtopic.php?t=104463]2.2 Feature List [/url]\r\n\r\n[quote:3585e4103f][b:3585e4103f]Viewtopic[/b:3585e4103f]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAs per 2.0 plus: \r\n\r\nUpdated layout for clearer post subject viewing, etc. \r\n\r\nPost icons \r\n\r\n[b:3585e4103f][u:3585e4103f]Printer friendly output option (templated) [/u:3585e4103f][/b:3585e4103f]\r\n\r\nEmail topic title/link to friend (with note if required) \r\n\r\nJump to first unread/last post \r\n\r\nComplete seperation of variable output to template, e.g. icons, edited info, signatures, etc. \r\n\r\nReport post feature with priority levels \r\n\r\nAdditional quick mod tools; merge, copy, sticky, announce, global announce, view topic moderator log \r\n\r\nTotal number of posts output \r\n\r\nFully templated attachment output \r\n\r\nInline display of images \r\n\r\nInline display of thumbnails (server dependent) \r\n\r\nAttachment viewed counter \r\n\r\nReduction in load from parsing posts \r\n\r\nImproved highlighting filter \r\n\r\nSkipping of avatars, images, flash, sigs under user control (see UCP) \r\n\r\nImproved output of poll results \r\n\r\nAbility to change vote once cast \r\n[/quote:3585e4103f]\r\n\r\nLooks like when if Cobo updates to phpBB 2.2 from phpBB 2.0.3 we can do it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13494, '7d4c993cd2', '', '[quote:7d4c993cd2="sessiz"]\r\nI did the fronts the way (I think) they\'re supposed to be, nubless. I only did one wheel with a nub on the rear and it works well. Simple and effective. All you have to do to get a nub on the rear is to install the disk on one rim with the protrusion pointing out from the rim instead of in. \r\nI will tell ya this though, [b:7d4c993cd2]DO NOT[/b:7d4c993cd2] use super glue, or use it very sparingly. It dried up white and got all over the rim face. I gotta go in and brush the crust off of every rim now. I also found that I need to cut short the pins a lil in the front. I\'m gonna try to desolve the glue on the one rim upfront and re do it or my car is gonna keep going in circles. :sad: \r\nOver all the mounting was pretty easy, not nearly as tough as I thought it would be. I recomend patients though. I kinda rushed to get these on and will probably have to redo them in the future.[/quote:7d4c993cd2]\r\nI just assembled a set tonite using the reverse hub method you suggested for the rear, and it came out mint!\r\nI did use super-glue spatingly... actually i used a paper clip to apply it to the rim, i have not assembled the axel yet though. For the reverse hub assembly i used the tire as a mold to position the 2 pieces and hold them in place while drying *use caution if you attempt this method* a little extra glue on the ouside of the rim and the rim will be now mounted to the tire permantly!\r\nAs for the insert, i didn\'t even glue it! When removing it from the tree, i left a little extra on there and sanded it down until the insert fit inside the hub nice and snug.\r\n\r\n-word');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13495, 'a6a705cd42', '', 'That is cool, your attention to detail is amazing.\r\n\r\nHey, can we see that [i:a6a705cd42]big[/i:a6a705cd42] motor?\r\n\r\nDual cells, mosfet mod, and a big motor, that thing must be screamin\'.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13496, 'bcaaf9b72f', '', 'That\'s not actually a stable release.\r\nThe latest stable version is 2.0.4.\r\nThere\'s no real significant changes in the version I have the their latest version. I\'m kind of waiting for another, bigger release with more features, etc.\r\nSo why not just go to 2.0.4 anyways?\r\nwell besides the fact of no real significant changes, ya just gotta give me time. I can\'t just use their "updaters" - all versions will screw up parts of the boards because I\'ve actually customized many of the template files in keeping with the rest of the site as well as used past "modification add ons" that will break as soon as I update unless I go through, take them out and re-code them back in.\r\nSo when I do the update, I have to manually go through line by line of code in most all of the template files and make my own updates to the "updated" files. I just don\'t have the time to do it right now.\r\nHave you ever messed with installing, customizing, updating, etc. with any of these forum applications?\r\nNo update I\'ve used yet is quite as simple as clicking on an installer or updater and letting it go. All mods require you to do the coding yourself, they just tell you how. So it\'s time consuming in all aspects.');
