INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (13983, '16f8b299fe', '', 'Auight Pimps,\r\n\r\nI\'ve been around to the other hoods checkin out decal prices for a while and $1.00 for a 1/4 sheet of 11x8 is waaaaaay toooo low dude.  A lot of hoods are selling stickers, not decals for 3-7 times as much for about 1/4 of what you\'re offering.  I understand that there will be kids wanting these also but that can\'t be a deciding factor for price.  There are [i:16f8b299fe]some[/i:16f8b299fe] kids but the majority are teenage-adults.  Kids make up a very small portion of members/visitors.  Now what ever your guys decide is fine with me.  BitPimp logos should only go out under Cabo\'s approval period.   That doesn\'t mean shipping to him then having him ship to customer, that\'s double postage and diggin in the profits, unless you\'re talking about sending to him in bulk then I\'m way off base.  I think $5 for sponsor is okay $4 would be more attractive, but $10 for BitPimp is not gonna sell at all. Make BitPimp $6.50. I\'m looking at it as if I\'m buying and you guys know how much I like to buy so to me these prices would be more attractive/reasonable. Also we have to have the [b:16f8b299fe]Right[/b:16f8b299fe] time to advertise!  If this is going to happen, finish ironing out the details and I would suggest announcing it along with the 3rd contest. After the present contest, interrest will be so high when the 3rd one is announced, they will sell in abundance.  Timing is everything!.......along with advertising.\r\nAnd Nox you do need to be compensated for your efforts/materials!\r\n\r\nCars are another issue, like Cabo said it gets real dicey, especially when selling modded Bits.  And what is a fair price? Not what it\'s actually worth I can tell you that!  And what it\'s actually worth, are customers willing to pay?  You\'ll probably sell a very small amount. And the next thing that will happen is the question..."Can I send you mine to mod?  How much? How long will it take?  Do I have to pay postage? yada,yada,yada"  It will go there in a heartbeat!  Then there has to be some sort of limited guarantee, etc.  So now you see why Cabo\'s leary about this one.');
