INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39904, '4da19a39bb', '', '...Just a little tip when \'sharing\' files of questionable nature:\r\n\r\nChange the file extension to something a little less conspicuous, like .asp or .htm (things you EXPECT to see on a regular webpage) and then whoever downloads them can just change it back.\r\n\r\nI\'m sure the ISP probably does a nightly scan for the regular stuff (mpegs, mp3s and so on) so changing the extension will at least buy some time.\r\n\r\nIt ain\'t perfect, but it throws the dogs off a little at least.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14596, '200223f698', '', 'I love all forms of cars. I remeber in 6th grade (\'81) the big end all question was do you like lowriders or 4x4s, and I could never answer, \'cause liked them both.\r\n\r\nOld hot rods are my favorite. My uncle had a \'33 Ford w/ a blown 500+hp 350, and a chopped and channelled \'53 Pontiac, and the guy across the street from my parents house had an ongoing project with a \'34 Chevy. I used to like to watch him work on his car, and get all pissed off, and I remember the Budman, the Thrush bird with the cigar hangin\' out his mouth, and I remember spending a lot of time starin\' at the Cheryl Tiegs poster. Cool stuff on his wall.\r\n\r\nI was also big time into playing with Stompers, so I was into monster trucks, had a subscription to 4-wheel and Off Road, and attended a mud bog, or truck pull about once a month.\r\n\r\nAs a teenager I was into lowered VWs, and lowered minitrucks. I also dug old muscle cars.\r\n\r\nI got into cars like the Skyline, and Mitsubishi 3000GT from playing with 1/10th scale cars, watching GT racing on TV, and playing Gran Turismo on the Playstation, non-stop for over a year. (I just started back up again too.:roll:)\r\n\r\nI dig the current street racing thing with the imports. There\'s Neons, Focuses out there too, so it\'s not just imports. Reminds me of the attitude like the original street racers in the fifties. I just laugh at the posers with the wings and graphics, because there\'s always been posers, and you can always tell who the posers are.');
