INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39899, 'a47ecb4ac6', '.', 'you raised a great concern about the freebie 4.2 kings, mine was also a freebie when i bought two lxx char-g from toyeast, i wonder why they are free... i put one king in a lxx single speed rcand dual celled it and it does wheelies like all, but the other king seems to be a dog, i should switch the two out and see if i get the same performance, cause i am thinking that the diff cars have diff voltage to the motors ect. i will be modding tis body dark t but could only wish for a nice few bodies like yours ( the big lots charger ) hey dark t i have to look again at your blue car and see what you did with the four light in the front of the hood of this car, did you shave the two top ones off?\r\n\r\npmpn8ez\r\nJ');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14640, '877272782f', 'Re: Proportional steering', '[quote:877272782f="lovedoctor"]Someone posted above that the "viper" doesn\'t have proportional steering.  I don\'t know what viper that person was talking about, but I know RS sells a 1:43 Corvette that advertises proportional steering, plus, working directional signals and headlights from the remote!!!   :eek: \r\n\r\nIt looks like  a Kyoto Mini-Z.  A mad cool sled, but six AA bats for the charging stand alone!  Not to mention a $50 price tag.  Man, I ain\'t made of money!  See ya   :-) \r\n\r\nProps to the bigguns,   :cool: \r\n\r\nDoc[/quote:877272782f]\r\nHe was saying it\'s not true proportional, but had 8 step steering, there\'s difference between digital proportional, and just plain old proportial, and 8 steps sound more than proportional enough for me and my Zip Zaps. Let\'s just hope it\'s true. \r\n\r\nI\'m wondering if they\'re going to be taking up the extra space we use to dual cell to use a motor driven steering, or how else would they make it proportional? Maybe I should be stocking up on those batteries for the Laymans Dual cell. :???:  :lol: \r\n\r\nNamuna brings up a good point with the $30 point, but I think RS would be willing to make that mark, if they know they wont have to blow them out for $12.99 after christmas.\r\n\r\nIt\'ll be interesting to see if, and how this comes about, but if it does ,this hobby could get really serious then, for me anyways. ;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14641, '2be2ee4ef1', '', 'Damn, don\'t know how I missed this one.\r\n\r\nCrazydave, I belive the circuit is based around a PIC microcontroller.  Why I say this is that the LED\'s look like they are running on a set routine and not in sync with the music.   As to which PIC chip and how diets programmed it I have no idea.\r\n\r\nThere is a chip called the LM3915 that is a LED display bar/dot VU meter that could listen to the music around it and show the VU reponse.  You would need the chip, a microphone, a DC supply af around 5V and some misc components and it would work, it would be hard to fit it into a bit though. \r\n\r\nWhat diets has achieve is mad!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
