INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39891, 'c3d122b826', '', 'i got a couple of free "elvis" motors recently and i found them to be fairly fast but lack the torque to truly reach their top speed. although on smooth surfaces they would fly. as you\'ve found out, quality control down at the ol\' perfection plant is handled by a goldfish with cataracts which can sometimes act in your favour. my 2 prized motors are both mysteries to me, one with a flourescent yellow cap and one with a purple cap. i got them with lxx cars, and if i could find them again i\'d be buying plenty more! otherwise i\'m a fan of tomy 2.6 and perf 3.8 motors for good speed and torque (all my bits are dual cells with fets) and tomy 1.6, 2.2 2.6 motors when torque is my first priority. and has anyone noticed how the 3.8 and regular 4.2 from te are identical? :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14781, '69f441b2c1', '', 'With a 50sec charge at 1A gave me about 10 minutes with just the LEDs running.  Measuring with a multimeter has shown that the current drain is about 30mA.  This is just over 10% of the total drain the car pulls on the battery when in motion so it\'s not that bad.\r\n\r\nAlso, due to the increased efficiency of the FETs I\'ve noticed a longer runtime generally because the motor is now getting a lot more current than before, the LEDs will offset this yes, but not by much.\r\n\r\nAnyways real world results will tell once I\'ve finished this beast.   The LEDs are just a sideline to the main project of the FET pcb.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
