INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14885, '52f95c93ec', '', 'This just goes to show you how much crap you can accumulate in 6 months, spending $20-$30 a pay check.\r\n\r\nHere\'s the first thing I see when I wake up.\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit03.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]\r\n\r\nHere\'s what I gots.\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit06.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]\r\n(left to right)Back row.\r\nMicrosizer Subaru - I won it! :grin:, so it\'s stock for now ;)\r\nThunder Charger RX-7 - $5 car, LXX body, custom paint, dual 100mah cells.\r\nFront row\r\nBit char-G Skyline R32 - 150mah cell, Perfection 3.8, body drop, Crip cap mod\r\nMicrosizer Subaru - 150mah cell, pink clone motor, off road tires, blue PCB cover.\r\nMicrosizer Pro RX-7 - 150 mah cell, Perfection 3.8, Zip Zap wheels, Body and chassis detailing.\r\nMicrosizer Sport Skyline - 150 mah cell, perfection 3.0, contest winning custom body, with custom interior kit, Zip Zap rims.\r\nCannonball Peugot - Internal dual cell, off road tires, custom painted body.\r\n\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit04.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]\r\nBack row.\r\nThunder Charger - parts car, already been stripped of motor and battery\r\nThunder Charger Expedition - Stretched chassis project, coming along well, it\'s funtional, just need to do some body trimming, and get more batteries in it.\r\nFront row.\r\nThunder Charger Celica - Cannonball body w/ custom paint, Zip Zap wing, dual 150 mah cells.\r\nThunder Charger GT-2000 - Bit body w/ custom paint, dual 110 mah cells.\r\nZip Zap Civic - Custom painted body, Hot Wheels wing, full size bit rim conversion, dual 100 mah cells, 2nd generation PCB, 2.8 ZZ motor.\r\nZip Zap Camaro - Custom painted body, chassis is a mix of several cars and is custom painted too. LXX booster board, dual Tomy Ni- Cds. \r\nZip Zap Challenger - Custom painted body, NEX 3.4, 8.25 gears.\r\n\r\nExtra Zip Zap bodies\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit05.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]\r\n\r\nMy drawer full of crap.\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit01.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]\r\n\r\nMy tools (not including Dremel knife set, and soldering stuff):\r\n[img:52f95c93ec]http://www.erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/allofit02.jpg[/img:52f95c93ec]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (14886, 'fce03470ad', 'time trial/speed test crap', 'ok i was bored so i measured out 10 feet in my kitchen. this is a tight weave carpet(i hate carpet in the kitchen btw) but its a nice flat surface to do preliminary testing on. and i used a stopwatch that only goes to the 1/10th of a second so this isnt very scientific but close enough for first runs. and well i didnt bother to charge my ride up all the way cuz i figured that everything needs to be slightly inaccurate. so anyhow my first measurable run from 0 - 10feet was 2.1sec and well when it hit the railing thing it flew about another 3 feet but i wont count that extra distance.\r\n\r\ni used a microsizer chassis with thundercharger wheels(wider) and tires. dual gp100 cells.teal gear ratio. suspension springs. pink clone motor(almost a year old). steel putty epoxy(ya i didnt use jbweld) in the rear end. 57mhz cyclona pcb. most of these parts have been recycled several times from car to car.\r\n\r\nso 10/2.1 = 4.76190476 feet per second = 17,142.8571 feet per hour = 3.24675325 mph(thats an average rate from a stand still) x70 = 227.27mph\r\n\r\nso i said if my average from a stop is 227mph what kinda speed am i doing towards the end? so i measured out 5feet and gave myself a 5foot head start and timed just the last 5 feet.\r\n\r\non a dying charge i got .7 sec so \r\n5/.7 = 7.14285714 feet per second = 25,714.2857 feet per hour = 4.8mph x 70 = 340mph\r\n\r\nso my next step is to a: do this on a better surface b: use a more accurate timer c: do this in a scale 1/4mile instead of 10feet. my goal is to defeat the sound barrier. to do that i feel im gona need to build a new car. i have the blueprints in my head and most of the parts so itl happen.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39886, '1a68aa24bc', 'Re: Muscle Tuners Wheels', '[quote:1a68aa24bc="DarkTari"][quote:1a68aa24bc="Finks"]Just came back from Wally World and picked up two Muscle Tuners, one for my son, and one for me to hack to bits.  They have some great minor details that I am gonna rip off (muffler, interior, and air foil to say the leaste)  What I was really wanting tho, was the wheels.  Has anyone sucessfully put Muscle Tuners weels onto a bit?  I am gonna try either way in a few days, first need to wait for my son to forget about em cuz at the moment he likes daddies car as well. :?[/quote:1a68aa24bc]\r\n\r\n[b:1a68aa24bc]Wally World [/b:1a68aa24bc]!   :eek:  I always thought that was a fictional Amusement Park made up for the [i:1a68aa24bc]Family Vacation [/i:1a68aa24bc]Movie (Chevy Chase)[/quote:1a68aa24bc]LOL, you silly guy DT. I\'m pretty sure that is the origin of the nickname given to Walmart, but you knew that, right? :lol: \r\n[quote:1a68aa24bc]Anyways the wheels are awsome Pimp!  I usually modify them to fit ZZ hubs and mount.  They are very true and I\'ve only had to slightly modify certain body\'s on Bits.[/quote:1a68aa24bc]So are you saying that you shave the fronts off Zip Zaps wheels, and just glue the dubs to those? If so that\'s a really good idea, probably saves a lot of hassle trying to get everything spinning true.');
