INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39850, '2cc53232df', '', 'Arite, prices have dropped since I slung Digi cams for Circuit city (7years in that motherboard) so this should be to your advantage.  I personally have a 2.0 Sony Cybershot.  When I got it a year ago Sunday (my B-day) it was $230.  I would imagine by now an open boxed at this point in time would be hovering right around $130 now.  If you are buying a digital camera for more that just bit pics this is a great well rounded cam.  Bottom line, my top 2 brand recomendations are VERY solid choices, and if it means a couple more bucks, I would not hessitate.  Hands down a Sony or a Cannon digital camera "ON AVERAGE" will give you a far better: Picture, battery life, ease of use, and DURABILITY.  I am not saying other cameras are crap, but these 2 brands are heavy hitters that put out amazing products. Note:  Make sure you have macro on whatever camera you buy.  You can tell it has it because a) you see a tulip on near or on a button, b) ask the salesman and make sure he shows you that icon (god knows not all salesmen are as honest as me :? )  Hope this helps and wtf my enter buttons are both broken... bah');
