INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (15544, '8af28aece7', 'Quick Hunny cuts', '[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p1f0019acd14aa044845061fadcd3ce90/fbb94fa6.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\n\r\nFirst you gotta find yourself a fly ass hunny.\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p19de0f5ee0f159380791fa80c493e9e2/fbb95009.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\n\r\nNext you open up the pic in whatever program you\'re using, I use \r\n\r\nphotoshop 7.0. Find the lasso tool (polygon lasso works well for me) \r\n\r\nand make a rough selection around your object. Get as close to the \r\n\r\nedges as you can. You can also use the pen tool to get an even \r\n\r\ncloser outline just make sure to turn the outline into a selection.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p9fc7cff5c0d52e2c371087fc23d81e52/fbb95000.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p9fc7cff5c0d52e2c371087fc23d81e52/fbb95000.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p7c25ae04fcaf3e9f6a49df7b2369c8a3/fbb94ff3.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p7c25ae04fcaf3e9f6a49df7b2369c8a3/fbb94ff3.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n\r\nNow that you got the selection, right click on the selected object \r\n\r\nand select layer as copy. If you\'re using another program (or a mac \r\n\r\nwithout a right mouse button :P ) that doesn\'t have this option you \r\n\r\nshould still be able to drag the selected object to another canvas.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p6ab21cd9370a15c6c238f92311552b9a/fbb94fe7.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p6ab21cd9370a15c6c238f92311552b9a/fbb94fe7.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n\r\nNow take the hard edged eraser and go at the hard edged parts of \r\n\r\nthe object. \r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/pfd60927e837581741c6f9e481eb928ff/fbb94fd1.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/pfd60927e837581741c6f9e481eb928ff/fbb94fd1.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p0a8c70dbfd8ed3a4a586fccd9f4c3918/fbb94fba.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p0a8c70dbfd8ed3a4a586fccd9f4c3918/fbb94fba.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n\r\nNow take a soft edged eraser and go around the soft edges like the \r\n\r\nhair and skin.\r\n\r\n[img:8af28aece7]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p8965403848f9899ec8d03cbb0fa0b9d7/fbb94faf.jpg[/img:8af28aece7]\r\nhttp://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid69/p8965403848f9899ec8d03cbb0fa0b9d7/fbb94faf.jpg.orig.jpg\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter this you should have a nice clean image to drag over any \r\n\r\nbackground. If you have any jaggies you can play around with the \r\n\r\nchannels or blur tool, experimentation is the way I learn. There is an \r\n\r\nextraction tool in ps7, but I don\'t like to use it. There are also a few \r\n\r\nother ways to extract an image but this method seems to work well \r\n\r\nfor me and is by far the simplest in my opinion. I hope this helps some of \r\n\r\nya pimps.');
