INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (15932, 'ff384685b2', '', 'I\'ve discovered that each knuckle requires it\'s own technique, or I\'ve yet to master my techique, or whatever, but it just doesn\'t seem to get any easier.\r\n\r\nI wouldn\'t reccomend wrassling the pin out with pliers because you\'ll probably bend it like I\'ve done to so many. The soldering iron has worked great for getting my bit rims off, but I discovered Zip Zap rims melt alot faster. I\'m think Hogjowls idea of prying up with 2 screwdrivers might be the best way to go, because it would pull evenly so it doesn\'t bend, but I don\'t have 2 screwdrivers small enough to try that.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (15933, '044c7fae5f', '', 'I was talking about it with payaso last night and we\'re thinking that NKOK makes hit or miss stuff - so you\'ve got a 50% chance it\'s gonna be okay or a 50% chance it\'s gonna be crap.\r\neither way, that\'s not very inspiring or a track record to be proud of.\r\n\r\nI man-handled my yellow boats controller and finally fit the frickin antenna in with brute force. Reception isn\'t nearly as good as the 49 mhz...\r\nI will say this though - it sits in the water much nicer, still a slight keel but not enough to really effect the boats drivability (as it does big time with the red boat). Again, I think this is just a hit or miss scenario.\r\n\r\nMy red boat won\'t go straight at all, one motor way over powers the other, causing it to constantly wanna do a left or right loop. Charging stand still sucks too, the yellow charging stand is slightly better, but not by much. The red one, I have to actually hold down with my fingers or the connection won\'t be made.\r\n\r\nAnyways, after my ranting and raving, I calmed down, tested the boats a little...\r\nI\'m still pretty disappointed, especially with the red boat.\r\nI don\'t think they\'d be fun by yourself for too long, but if ya had a pal with another boat - then that might be a different story.\r\n\r\nOverall, I don\'t think I trust their products, too flukey for me to gamble on. I don\'t believe toy-island.com has anything to do with it, though I could be wrong.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (15934, 'f162cb3356', '', 'there is a technique to the muscling them out.\r\npayaso bout shiat when he saw how easily I pulled them out - without a bend.\r\ntakes 2 pairs of pliers, 1 normal pair and 1 needle nose.\r\nlately I\'ve been trying the soldering iron method - I\'d suggest you not pull on the rim to get the pin out or you\'re going to melt and deform your rim, pull from the head of the pin with needle nose pliers.\r\n\r\nhaven\'t tried the screwdriver thing because I can\'t seem to think of a way to pry on the pin without completely marring up the rim with the screwdriver.');
