INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16222, '0de269a0a8', 'clearcoat chrome', 'ok i have some dub city wheels that i\'m going to be painting the inside to match my cars body but want to keep the outside ring chrome. now if i clear coat the wheels to keep the paint from rubbing off and geting chiped n\' shit will the chrome look like ass or not?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16223, 'e7bbc4f986', '', 'no it probably won\'t man. I used Chrome panit on my Computer case and it was blining and all shiny. As soon as I put the clear coat on it went a dark silver/gray colour. Its because the metal flake in the paint floasts to the surface. When you clear coat it rewets the surface and deadins the paint colour and stops the metal flake from resurfacing.\r\n\r\nSee here sorry for the big pic\r\n\r\n[img:e7bbc4f986]http://members.rogers.com/computermod/images/Computer/03%20Big.JPG[/img:e7bbc4f986]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16224, '206f624cb8', '', 'so should i try to mask the outside or just say fuckit to the clearcoat and install dem babys?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16225, 'e62d191992', '', 'Fuck the clear mam. You could try clear nail polish instead and see if it works. Just try on something else and see. I use clear nail polish on by bits because I find if you put even the slightest too much clear coat it eats your paint.\r\n\r\nyou really don\'t need to clear coat rims though. they don\'t really get banged up like a body does.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16226, 'd9fac94004', '', 'Yeah, I\'m happy with it. With a little practice I can almost negotiate it with a 3.8. I originally had the inside set up more technical with 7" lanes, but that was nearly impossible, so I pulled it up, and redid it this way, and I see why 8" to 9" lanes work out well. It seems to fit bit\'s steering radius. \r\n\r\nAnd now I have the little pit area, before I was trying to cover every inch with track.');
