INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16655, 'c4f519d3db', '', 'I like both approaches, though badboy\'s does sound better (more customizable).\r\nYea badboy - I like the idea that you\'re taking the bits further along than they already are - major props to you.\r\n\r\npersonally, I don\'t like weighing down my bit with stuff that doesn\'t either increase its performance or it\'s looks, but that\'s just me - still like the idea - just probably wouldn\'t do it myself, I\'m sure lots of others would though.\r\n\r\nthanks for posting your procedures badboy &amp; dabigpig.\r\n\r\np.s. let us know when you get that mp3 version working badboy - that\'s steppin up to the plate! good luck and good job again pimp!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (16656, 'aa165e6962', 'Re: CLEAR COAT HELP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!', '[quote:aa165e6962="BilboBaggins"][quote:aa165e6962="warmaster259"]:-)  is it ok to clear coat a bit body? if not what else can i use?[/quote:aa165e6962]\r\n\r\nOk, you can clear coat a Bit Body (I do all the time.)\r\nBut what you use is important.\r\n\r\nI use Krylon Acrylic Clear Gloss.\r\nI\'ve also heard good things about Future Acrylic Floor Polish (wax?).\r\n\r\nDo not use Rustoleum Crystal Clear, I found out the hard way about it. It will disolve/eat the top layer of paint and the undercoat will show through. I guess it could be a cool effect if you\'re looking for it.[/quote:aa165e6962]\r\nfound out about rustoleum the hard way myself, but being the persistant ass that I am - I continued to use it - just gotta do super thin coats and it shouldn\'t eat your paint.\r\nthough I\'d prefer to be using better clear coat, and plan to when I\'m out of this rustoleum.');
