INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17035, '9ecb4d787d', 'Are you thinking of getting Verizon DSL?', 'Well, if my previous dealings with them doesn\'t make you think twice (http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=97&amp;highlight=verizon) then get your reading glasses and get ready to read a REAL horror story.\r\n\r\nI just recently moved into my new Condo and needed to get Internet hooked up. A friend of mine told me about a new Verizon offer, \'Verizon Freedom with DSL\'. You get a phone line with UNLIMITED local and long distance calls AND the upgraded DSL (they upgraded service to 1.5/128) for under $100 per month. Once bitten, twice shy...But that\'s a good deal.\r\n\r\nHere is every conversation I\'ve had with them...\r\n\r\n7/2/03 @ 5:45pm: Called 800-427-9977 and spoke with Ms. McCormick to order Verizon Freedom with DSL Service. She was only customer service and transferred me to Ms. Nicole Nevarra to actually get the order in.\r\n\r\nBeing reluctant from previous dealings, Nicole assures me that I\'m within range to get the upgraded DSL speeds, so I go ahead with the order. She gave me new number and said there\'s a turn-on cost of $42.80 and the total monthly cost (after taxes with DSL) is $98.03. She also said there\'s no need to get new DSL equipment, since I already have everything from last time. Phone service activation is set for Tuesday, July 8th (with DSL set to come soon after)\r\n\r\n7/7/03\r\n@ 11:10AM: Spoke with Tara Dye (x2198, Billing location in W.Virginia 800-567-6789). I want to make sure they DON\'T send me new DSL equipment, since I already have the stuff. She\'s unable to verify that they won\'t send the equipment just yet. She also says the DSL service can\'t be ordered until the main phone line has been in place for at least 3 business days. She promises to call-back at the new home number with an update when there\'s more info.\r\n\r\n7/9/03\r\n@ 10:30am: Spoke with Elizabeth Verneesa (name?). The install date has come and gone and I still don\'t have phone service. Elizabeth Said the account is on hold? Transferred me to Customer Service.\r\n@ 10:35am: Spoke with Barbara at Customer Service. She said everything is in order but doesn\'t know why the line wasn\'t turned on...She\'s tranferring me to the Escalation Dept (866-465-2242)\r\n@ 10:44am: On hold for the Esc. Dept.\r\n@ 10:50am: Spoke with Ms. Majors. Can\'t get solid info about why line wasn\'t installed, said it was likely that the previous tennant didn\'t disconnect the line properly. She needs to tranfer me to the Business Office. (800-427-9977)\r\n@ 10:56am: Spoke with Ms. Manny. Back to square one, she doesn\'t know why the line hasn\'t been turned on, says everything seems to be in order. She checked the order again and said the line wasn\'t turned on because the previous people didn\'t put in the disconnect. I told her the disconnect WAS put through and gave her the confirm number of the disconnect. Now she\'s transferring me to Installations (866-465-2242) and says now the next available install date is Monday, July 14th. I told her NO WAY that\'s acceptable, I want the line TODAY.\r\n@ 11:02am: on hold for Installations\r\n@ 11:03am: Spoke with someone in Installations and they said they can\'t escalate the install for today at their location, that has to come from Dispatch. Ms. Manny said that\'s an interoffice number and can\'t give it to me. I\'m on hold while she contacts them.\r\n@ 11:13am: Ms. Manny says the line will be installed today, by 7pm. If the line is not on, she said to call the repair dept at 800-275-2355. Since I had to deal with all the calling, I asked to have the install cost ($42.80) to be waved. She said okay and the fee will be waived.\r\n\r\n7/11/03\r\n@ 3:07pm: on hold for someone about DSL service. Trying to make sure everything happens properly for DSL service to be installed.\r\n@ 3:13pm: speaking with Ms. Toombs, she is checking the status of the DSL line to be installed. She threw me into the Installations queue\r\n@ 3:15pm: on hold for someone in Installations\r\n@ 3:30pm: on phone with Ken. Ken says I gotta call the Local phone company (Tuesdays and Thursdays) and make sure they send the address info update to the Verizon DSL dept (you can guess I\'m not too happy with this shit). Ken says they send updates every week on Thursday nights.  Then I gotta call Verizon (800-567-6789) and ask for Sales to get status updates about the install.\r\n\r\n7/16/03 (I let a few business days pass)\r\n@ 1:12pm: Talk briefly with Mr. Wiley. Told him I want status of DSL and he xferred me to DSL Dept.\r\n@ 1:13pm: On hold for DSL Dept.\r\n@ 1:14pm: On the phone with Mrs. Perry about install date/time. After checking some things and being on hold, she comes back on and says DSL is NOT available in my area. She gave me a number to call in NJ (800-755-1068). I tried calling the number and it says no incoming calls are allowed on that number.\r\n@ 1:30pm: on the phone with Ms. Allen at the Verizon phone dept. Told her the story about getting DICKED around with DSL and that I want the first month of phone service for FREE, otherwise I\'m cancelling phone service too. She\'s giving me the free month and has me on hold to give a call over to the DSL group for one last shot.\r\n@ 2:00pm: Spoke to Doug in DSL Sales (866-268-4630), he says because of the \'low coils\' in my area the service IS available but it would take 23 business days to get the service…And since I\'m over 16,000ft from the CO I\'d only get 768kb download (instead of the upgraded 1.5). I told him no thanks.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been DICKED by Verizon enough my friends, I share all this info with you so that you do not make my mistake.\r\n\r\nOn another note...\r\n\r\nI called Comcast Cable yesterday and ordered Digital Cable Basic (promo is it\'s $30 a month for 3 months) with Cable Internet ($20 a month for 6 months promo)...The install guy came TODAY and I now have Cable TV and Internet.');
