INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17780, '9c1e95dd7a', 'MS Pro, too much hype??', 'Any pimps who have 2 speed bits or ms\'s, feel free to chime in yo...\r\n\r\nOK, I finally broke down and picked up a MS Pro today at TRU.  At 19.99, I figured I wouldn\'t get one much cheaper.\r\n\r\nI took if for a spin and I am sitting here wondering what all the hype is or what I am missing?  First thing I noticed, is the car when not boosting and just taking off, is SLOW to take off, much like first gen ZZ\'s.  And it is NOISY as hell.....but when you hit the boost button, it is much quiter and if you hold the boost and then hit forwar, it takes off faster.  Not meaning top speed, I mean take off speed.  \r\n\r\nI understand the concept of the boost and that the current is cut back and then boost button allows full potential, but I guess I was expecting more...\r\n\r\nI haven\'t tried any other motors yet, could be the 2.2 that comes with, but man, I was kinda let down.  \r\n\r\nAny advice?  Any others notice this or may I have a jacked up ride out the box?\r\n\r\nHolla\r\nTodd');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17781, '0bfcee27ee', '', 'Yo.\r\n\r\nI feel the same as you...the poor speed, the noise, the build up to speed.\r\nGuess I just wrote it off as different.\r\n\r\nI try to run mine in booster mode all the time, and then back off when needed.\r\n\r\nI believe some different motors do cause a different noise, but the ticking is still there.\r\n\r\nDuel cell the puppy, that helps in the slow mode.\r\n\r\n-nox');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17782, 'bacf2f75dc', '', '[quote:bacf2f75dc="warmaster259"]how do u strech a chassis?[/quote:bacf2f75dc]\r\n\r\nsame way...cut the chassis in half and add plastic.\r\ndremel helps.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17783, 'b7b4bfd252', '', 'naw mang, you got it pretty much right...\r\n- yup their noisey suckers\r\n- very slow unboosted on take off (not top speed)\r\n- I\'m a firm believer that the driving situation dictates what motor is good. an example is on my track, 2.2 is great for warm-ups, actual racing a 3.0, any more and you\'ll be outta control in the technical sections (this is where the boost button really comes in to play for me and my driving preferences)\r\n\r\nmy personal preference is to run boosted all the time and unboost when I need to (in corners).\r\n\r\nI like my pro\'s - they\'re probably #2 on my list, #1 being the Tomy Nissan 350 Z (that things just bad to the bone)');
