INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17791, '26c8b88330', 'Tri cell', 'Heres the tri cell i entered in the speed contest, just wanna spread the word. Its manily fits best in Bb trucks with no bed cover.\r\n\r\nMaterials/Tools needed: \r\n3 of the some type of Bit/Zip/MS batterys \r\nWire \r\nElectrical tape \r\nSoldering iron/pen/gun \r\nSolder \r\nsomething to remove a battery (EG:Smal screwdriver,guitar pick, and so on) \r\n\r\nSee link below for diagrams \r\n\r\nhttp://pic7.picturetrail.com/VOL206/1305092/2480694/30077300.jpg \r\n\r\nStep 1: Solder a wire between the - end of cell 2 to the + end of cell 3 \r\nStep 2: Solder a wire to the + end of cell 2 \r\nStep 3: Solder a wire to the - end of cell 3 \r\nStep 4: Tape (or solder then cover with tape for extra hold) the wire from the + end of cell 2 to the - end of cell 1. Make shure the whole - end of cell 1 is covered with tape. \r\nStep 5: Slide the cell 1 into the battery campartment CAREFULLY. \r\nStep 6: Use a slim screwdriver or something real skinny and hard to push the wire coming off of the - end of cell 3 in between the tape and the - tab for the battery compartment. \r\nStep 7: Modify your remote as mentioned here http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/articles/article_postings.php?id=17&amp;catId=1 \r\nStep 8: Drive liKE a maniac!\r\n\r\nOK ABUYEBUYE');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17792, '536e931811', '', 'I can\'t believe how many people out there (other sites too) don\'t prefer the 2 speed booster...\r\n\r\nHow can 1 speed be better than 2?  I agree about the noise, but a little bit of noise is ok with me as long as the car performs well. You can also cure the noise problem by popping a CD in the stereo.\r\n\r\nIMO, it\'s all about the set up. ie. motors, gears, and batts.  Before you throw em to the side, try some different set ups.\r\n\r\nI use alloy rims, strong 2.6, and a 150 nimh batt, and it runs great. This is a Tomy 350Z chassis.\r\nCould the MS pros be funky or something???   \r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17793, '47c51a9c93', '', 'I used a razor saw to cut the chassis. Zip Zap packaging for plastic, and super glue. You have to lay the super glue really thick, and let dry for a couple hours. Epoxy might work better.');
