INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17801, '19c6915502', '', '[quote:19c6915502="Yagbols"]Whoa! its starting to look damn good mang! woohoo! I figure the cars need to be fitted with a 2.2 at least.  Have you tried using a car on that thang?  Jesus, after you\'re done, how will you take out of the door? must be heavy too? :eek:  Damn, kewl track bro!\r\n\r\nHow about lights? buildings? just like in monaco! A Bitpimp blimp! hehehe and of course stop/go lights.[/quote:19c6915502]\r\n\r\nThanks bro.   The car I tested with was a Shen Qi Wei with a 2.6, whatever that compares to.    It was about the right speed for the track.   It raced pretty good.   Almost have to coast down the slide to make the (middle of the board) corner.   Haven\'t weighed it yet, prob 35-40 lbs.   Maybe 50 when I\'m done?   Solid! baby\r\n\r\nYou mean like buildings with lights in da windows and shiat?    I\'m thinking about it.  Billboard spotlights too, but I dunno.   Pretty lofty for my first model-railroading style scenery (though I do love the BitPimp Blimp idea).   Maybe.   Guess I can always add to it.     Have to see what kind of harnesses are avail at my hobby store.    Thanks for the suggestions.\r\n\r\nWelcome to da \'hood RacerGirl!    :-)    Thanks for the comps.\r\n\r\n-Silent');
