INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17845, '82c53400df', 'What\'s up with the frequencies on the Super Bits?', 'I noticed there\'s 27A, 27B, 40B, 40C. Does that mean that I can get a 27mhz one and race it with my other 27mhz? Dark Tari you\'ll have to answer this one for us, since I know you have them.\r\n\r\nIt doesn\'t matter too much to me because I want either the Jota, or the Ferrari, and they\'re both the 40mhz, but I am curious because I have an overwhelming amout of 27mhz cars. Be nice if say I could get the 27B, and have another option.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17846, 'a3a5b2d4f1', 'mhz', 'You can race a 27A, 27B, 27C all at the same time.  In theory.  Thats what Tomy says, I dont have any so i havent tried it, but i would think that they wouldnt claim it if it didnt work.\r\n\r\nIm not for sure how it would work with an existing 27mhz.  I dunno if that voice the a,b,c and c, or if a standard 27mhz is just 1 letter.... I guess well have to wait till someone has tried it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (17847, '823e59290b', '', 'I was attracted to the idea of a 2-speed car, in my desire for something more proportional, but I\'m not very impressed with the MS Pro. I wonder if the Bit-Char-G version is better, because everyone with one of those is really happy, and Namuna, basically proved it\'s putting out slightly more power than a stock bit, but that doesn\'t seem so with my Pro. \r\n\r\nI wish the unboosted was a little faster and smoother, but it serves it\'s basic purpose. My big complaint is the awkward position of the button, and just the whole system confuses me. I\'m used 1/10 scale, where the 3rd button is a brake, and I keep forgetting to boost on the straights, and boosting into the corners. So then I just end up frustrated, and POed, and it\'s not easier for me to drive, like I had hoped.');
