INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18529, '86c7065808', '', '[quote:86c7065808="crazydave"][quote:86c7065808="hogjowlz"][quote:86c7065808="payaso"][quote:86c7065808="extrememicros"], honestly, a normal zip zap out handles a bit any day. \r\n\r\nHolla![/quote:86c7065808]\r\n\r\nNot in my neighborhood...   I will be picking up a ton of the new ZZ 2.0, but I stomp on the old ones with my bits..\r\n\r\nI\'m what you might call the "Michael Schumacher" &lt;sp? of bits...lol\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:86c7065808]\r\n\r\ni gota agree with the clown. the new zipaps are cool but the bits are easier to make fast. zipzaps are heavier. bits with a really tight jbwelded rear outaccelerate and track straighter than a zipzap with the same mods.[/quote:86c7065808]Well, in my own personal experience, and opinion, I think single cell bits handle better, but I think dual-and tri- cell ZZs handle better than a dual cell bit, and I wouldn\'t even bother tri-celling a bit. Just because the ZZ doesn\'t flip as easy.[/quote:86c7065808]\r\n\r\nim gonna go with crazydave on this one\r\nbut all my zipzaps handle better than my bits, with the same mods\r\ni also think the weight of the zip zap helps handling, and with fets, reduces the backflip effect of bits\r\ni have double fet\'d my zip zap forward, single cell, on my nuvolari and this setup is both my fastest and best handler for tracks and 1/4 miles\r\ni have 14 working bits, 10 working clones, and 3 working zips\r\nand id rather charge up my zips first to mess around with');
