INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18585, 'a3442e269e', '', 'Looks good, and that wing looks so much better that way. Nice exhaust too.\r\n\r\nI clear coat my windows, I just lay a heavy coat to level everything out after I lay a few light coats. also I\'ve notice if you paint when it\'s cooler out the paint dries slower, and levels a little better.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18586, '8ebd2ebf86', '', '[quote:8ebd2ebf86="W3rd"]damn man that some crazy stuff u got there and it musta took alotta skill to creat one of these. but theres one question i have, dose it fit on all bodies?? or just the skyline?\r\nwell neways amazing job\r\nand looks great[/quote:8ebd2ebf86]\r\n\r\nThanks man.  Any shell that has enough clearance should work.  The Skyline shell works well.  So should a gloria and bB I guess from what I\'ve seen.   Lower profile shells like an RX-7 wouldn\'t work.  Also you need space in the grill to be able to mount the lights, again the skyline is suitable for this.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18587, '05da331dcf', '', 'Sinned,\r\n\r\nYour body Mod Tuitorial is Unbelievable Pimp. You make it look so easy, no wonder you\'re crankin dem out like dat!  I would never have thought of cutting up an old credit card to use for a body mod.  You guys are really resourceful.  And I see you don\'t like clear windows either, just paint \'em, permanent ink \'em and gloss \'em!   I\'ll be hanging in Yo Hood A Lil Bit Pimp!  Pick me Up, we\'ll get some Beer &amp; Babes!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18588, 'd60aa857d8', '', 'Nice DT, looks like a rally car...how do you get your pics so crisp?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (18589, 'c1d72415a8', '', '[quote:c1d72415a8="Yagbols"]My god PH, youve done it! (thunder clapping and lightning)  I have a question...is it easy to install, or do we have to send you the car?[/quote:c1d72415a8]\r\n\r\nNo need to send me a car man, it\'s quite easy to install.  There is only two wires that you need to solder to the pcb for power, it runs off the car\'s battery no sweats.  I also didn\'t notice a reduction in runtime but I\'ll do some more tests just to make sure.\r\n\r\nYou need to dremel out the front grill to be able to mount the lights, that\'s the only real modding you have to do.\r\n\r\nAn option is to run it off a small 1.5V watch battery, like the LR44 ones.  I got one of these and it runs like a treat thanks to the 1.2V -&gt; 5V DCDC converter on the KITT PCB.  You could also run it off a 3V lithium but I think you would run out of space.\r\n\r\nThere is no switch to turn the lights off/on, it\'s on all the time.  Even when on the charger! lol!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
