INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19137, '03a9d598f3', '', '[quote:03a9d598f3="crazydave"]I only have one Bit char-G, but the quality is just a tad better than Microsizer I\'ve bought yet. It just tracks a little straighter, turn evenly in both directions, the gears are a little quieter, the tires are a little stickier, and just doesn\'t have all the little issues I\'ve had with my Microsizers.\r\n\r\nThat range on it sucks though, and mine came with a 1.0, not very fast.\r\n\r\nI know Microsizers are made by Tomy, so I wonder if I just got lucky with my bit, but I see others saying they like theirs better too, and that\'s got me thinking... :???:[/quote:03a9d598f3]\r\n\r\nI own more bit\'s than microsizers and I find that to be true. I dunno what kind of quality control they have over there in japan but it seems that they\'re doin their job better. I would think that both of the products come out of the same factory. They just get packaged different. The differances are minor.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19139, 'd00e424e7d', '', 'shaweet');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19140, 'f7ce14e302', '', 'I\'ve been playin wit my super bit and I\'m not all that happy. :( \r\nThe car has a glitch of sorts where it\'ll get stuck in the last move, like keeps going forward or turning when the buttons aren\'t bein pressed. I still don\'t know why, is it pcb related or the buttons them selves on the controller. Speakin of buttons, The 2 freakin buttons on top, wtf do they do? I remember hearing something about steering concerning those buttons but haven\'t noticed anything. The controller is a major improvement on the old one but I hate being teased with buttons that don\'t do anything. The bodies look hot, real freakin good, but the lambo rides too high and it\'s a lil tight for lowering, can be done though. I definatly love the front knuckles. This is the way all cars should be done. I opened up the chassis and found that they made it even tighter inside. The pcb cover is cool though, no more snapping the lil tabs trying to get the cover off. They\'re still knoting up the ant though even though the cover has a cool ass system built in to hold the ant. I\'m also pissed off at the coloring of the steering wires, even harder to see now that they\'re a dark color blue almost black.\r\nI\'ll definatly hold off on getting anymore of these super bits. I\'ll wait for the 2buttons on top to be explained first. I hope they don\'t try to sell me another chassis booster upgrade kit just so that I can use those buttons. That would be assy of tomy to do, especially since the zip 2.0s are supposed to be coming out in a month or so. If the 2.0 is what it\'s reported to be then I\'m saying bye bye to tomy, unless they come out with some cool body I gotta have. :-)');
