INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19156, '67f9262266', '', 'That is a pretty cool track. I could use a portable system.\r\n\r\n$45 seems a tad high, but if it comes with the bag to put it in, and considering there\'s nothing else like it on the market, then that\'s probably about right.\r\n\r\nHow long are the straights on the competition track? And also do sloppy drivers who drive on the wall have a problems getting hung up on the clips?\r\n\r\nAny idea how much shipping to America is going to run?\r\n\r\nThrow in a sticker that says, \'get high with bonser\', and I might be in for one. ;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19157, 'cd2b77a36a', '', 'iIt is sorta a tinted clear coat. Like you could get a red one, and have a red chrome body.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19158, 'f3ec3c9738', '', 'Straights are just under 2 metres (80 inches). As for shipping, not sure yet. Because of the weight we will ship to US in bulk and then despatch locally. The overall weight of the track kit is about 2.6kg (5 1/2 lb) so I guess shipping in US is going to be about $10. We are hoping that for online orders the price will be under $45 INCLUDING shipping.\r\n\r\nGet High with BonzerGear Bumper sticker - like it :-D  Might just do one 1/64th scale - Download it and join TeamBonzer. :???: \r\n\r\nHave you checked out the T shirt designs -  :lol: Trying to convey a similar subliminal message :smile: \r\n\r\nHey Mods\r\nI dont want to upset my new buddies DaPimp Mods, so if you prefer I can ask that pimps who want more info email me direct rather than using the board - your call Dudes\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTeamBonzer');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19159, 'f3216fe043', '', 'What\'s up TB,  I like the Nakamichi Racer, as I said earlier it is a 2 speed car though not On Demand.  It has a switch for turbo mode which is pretty cool cause while you\'re in Turbo mode, when you make a turn the car slows down to normal speed (like a brake) and soon as you straighten up the turbo kicks back in. Also reverse is normal mode.\r\n\r\nThe only draw back is that it\'s not upgradeable. Motor is hardwired, rear wheels are in an enclosed box attached to the chassis that is a bitch to get off.  Body is not compatable with any other Micro so you can\'t change bodies with anything but another Nakamichi. PCB board is huge!  But the car needs no mods, it runs strong, excellent range, steers sharp, tracks straight, &amp; slammin wheels. I\'d get them just for the wheels alone!  The bodies aren\'t very detailed but with a nice paint job, it\'s a contender!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19160, '7e38ce0566', '', 'Thats good enough for me :-) \r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTeamBonzer');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19161, '7ed74df166', '', 'my guess(no hardcore evidence to back it up cuz i dont have my damn countache yet) is that it they send a different modulation code. think about all the interference you get with even a 49mhz and 27mhz. i cant see how that would work with 27.1 27.2 and 27.3\r\n\r\nill try to do testing when it comes.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19162, '6ecef34a05', '', 'I\'ll try to get it done tonight.\r\n\r\nSezz, you can lower the rear of the Lambo, just slide the rear chassis tab a lil further up in the body.  There\'s another notch in there that will allow this.  Drops the rear and gives the car a whole new look.\r\n\r\nI know what you mean by the car keeps running after you let off the button. Mine does the same thing. I don\'t have that problem with my 40mhz\'s, only the 27mhz ????');
