INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19590, '5351bf052b', '', '@CheeseWarfare MS\'s come stock with the orange 9.86:1 gear.\r\n\r\n@Rx-7 sounds like only one steering coil works. When you reverse the magnet, the working coil repels. You want the magnet in so that the working coil is attracting, and then you need to find where your steering wire may have come disconnected from. that would be my best guess. If your steering wire doesn\'t appear broken, then I don\'t know what could be up.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19591, '09dd385bda', '', 'Hey Tanis, welcome, :-)  and your english is fine.\r\n\r\nYou guys from Germany do amazing stuff with your cars, it\'s a pleasure to have you here to share information.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19592, '7fc912a570', '', 'I just wanted to say, I\'ve tried to make a few websites, and my major problem was lack of content. It takes a lot of work to put together an interesting website, and Cabo\'s worked hard to put together some interesting stuff for us.\r\n\r\nNotice he\'s spend alot of time and his own money, building the track, doing the vids, making tuturials, etc. etc.\r\n\r\nJust take your time on work at it, and maybe you can come up with your own content, so you can build your own unique website, like Cabo has. Honestly, there are tons of bit, and zip sites out there reposting information from around the net, and I personally don\'t see the point in visiting a website to see the same ol\' stuff.;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19593, '34eb69c7fa', 'Think us older guys are bad?', 'Other day at my shop, a guy came in about mid to late 60\'s, and he asked what micro rc\'s I carried.  Immediate thought was, Grandkids birthday...well to my surprise, not the case, him and 3 of his older buddies play with these things!!!  They get together once a week and play Micro Pool he called it.  They take ping pong balls and number them and put them on a pool table...and play pool!!!  Your car acts as the cue ball.  You are allowed to tap, slam or push the ball into the pockets.  If you push, you are allowed to push until the ball strays from your car.  That is your shot.\r\n\r\nHe said they\'d be interested in racing so, I told him to come back monday and we\'d talk racin.  \r\n\r\nHe was sittin here telling me about buying Shen clones at Chuck Homiers sale and crappy clones at a local grocery store, as well as telling me how they tried to fix the steering/return spring on the junk clones to make them better...;o)\r\n\r\nI was loving it...so now, as I sit at 29, I don\'t feel so bad....and I may have a few new older pimps to play with once a week...!!!\r\n\r\nHolla\r\n\r\nThe DOC');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19594, '608c20a480', '', 'For me, I\'d say no.\r\nMy Dad and I used to race 1/12 scale electric cars. For trophies and prizes. Man what a blast! That was when I was 8 and all through high school. I took a break when I went to college and got a job. I got the RC bug again and almost went into 1/10 electric. I thought it was too expensive (bills got to be paid!  :sad: ).\r\n\r\nBits, MS, ZZ\'s fufill my RC craving, are much cheaper and so much fun to mod and customize!  :D \r\n\r\nI\'d agree with Dave. Sometimes I don\'t even look at my cars, but I always come back!  :grin:');
