INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19632, 'e9d36ad004', '', 'Doing my first mosfet mod today. \r\n\r\nI\'m like Hue, but I\'ve actually etched my own PCBs, and made a few distortion pedals. My only experience with these tiny boards is popping off the crip cap.\r\n\r\nMy biggest concern is the tiny size, so I\'m going to practice swapping  few transistors first.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19633, 'ca1f20791e', '', 'OK. Here\'s the first of the general tips:\r\n\r\n• MicroAmp\'s tutorial says it takes about 2 hours. This is true for the most part, but we needed an additional 2 hours for troubleshooting/fixing broken stuff.\r\n\r\n• You need 4 mosfets to do the mod. The little tabs break off very easily, so order extras. Hue35 and I each used 6, I believe.\r\n\r\n• You need a really good soldering iron with a very fine tip. I would also recommend the really fine soldering wire. \r\n\r\n• Don\'t drink too much coffee, and get up and stretch after each milestone.\r\n\r\n• Hue35 removed a couple of the mosfets while troubleshooting no reverse function. He ended up replacing some of the original transistors, and now has a car that has the mosfet boost only in the forward direction. Actually quite useful, considering one usually uses reverse for crash recovery, and you don\'t really want all that torque in reverse. Not to mention perhaps only needing 2 mosfets to do the mod. We\'re going to look into this.\r\n\r\n• Here are some really helpful diagrams from the german tutorial… \r\n\r\n[img:ca1f20791e]http://www.universalhost.de/html_bit/mosfet/1fet.jpg[/img:ca1f20791e]\r\n\r\n[img:ca1f20791e]http://www.universalhost.de/html_bit/mosfet/2schaltplanmosfet.jpg[/img:ca1f20791e]\r\n\r\n[img:ca1f20791e]http://www.universalhost.de/html_bit/mosfet/schaltplanmosfet.jpg[/img:ca1f20791e]\r\n\r\n• One last thing: it\'s not obvious from the turorials I found that you will be gluing the 2 mosfets on the back of the pcb on their backs with the tabs facing up. We used superglue, but wished we had a hot glue gun. The superglue was fine, though.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19634, '93e3b66ba9', 'powerbrutes trucks', 'picked up the "lug" from toysrus.heavy truck.slow.steers by dragging one of the rear wheels..independent front suspension.. these are just 1st impressions..it is kinda fun to climb over sh*t w/it but it aint the 2nd coming..\r\ni\'ll holla back w/more info once i\'ve played some more..');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19635, '0be467c449', '', 'Here is where I\'m at so far...\r\nI stuck the body on a chassis I already had dropped. I will do a wheel mod to this chassis. I went ahead and painted it to see what needs fixin. I will shave off a little of the side skirts and try to contour them more. I removed the hood intake, because someone had stated that Skylines don\'t use hood scoops, and all the pics I reveiwed did not show any.\r\n\r\n[img:0be467c449]http://www.rcpics.net/media/ZIP_ZAPS_040.jpg[/img:0be467c449]\r\n[img:0be467c449]http://www.rcpics.net/media/ZIP_ZAPS_038---rcp1.jpg[/img:0be467c449]');
