INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19690, 'ad1b54c92c', '', '[quote:ad1b54c92c="Ahh5hit"]The trouble I have is instead of a smooth glass finish, I get a little bumpy look. I tired doing 2-3 very light coats. Is it that I am going too light? Do I need to give it one good spray over? BTW, I use Dupli-Color Claer Coat, same company as the paint.[/quote:ad1b54c92c]\r\n\r\nAhh5hit, Give the Model Master a try!  If you don\'t like, you can go back to duplicolor.  I\'ve never had a problem with it except just before the can is empty, then I get a bumpy finish on the sides. But one good coat and it\'s done!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (19691, '005aab20fe', '', '[b:005aab20fe]We got da prize winna\'s list[/b:005aab20fe]\r\n\r\nThe Twisted Plastic Contest came and went.\r\nOnce again, da contestants stepped up to da challenge and answered like true pimps with more dope ass sleds. All contestants should consider themselves some bad mutha scratchin pimps with some wicked fly skills. There were obvious improvements in skills from a number of you pimps and that\'s what we\'re all in search of! Reaching a new level is the best prize of all.\r\n\r\nDa bitPimps wish to extend their thanks to all da pimps and homies that entered. More good things and surprises are on their way very soon! Check back for updates and da latest low down on the haps in da hood.\r\n\r\nAnd now, da prize winners:\r\n[b:005aab20fe]1st place: lefttoe[/b:005aab20fe]\r\nEntry #14\r\n[img:005aab20fe]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/contests/twisted_plastic/lefttoe_2_3.jpg[/img:005aab20fe]\r\n\r\n[b:005aab20fe]2nd place: ph2t[/b:005aab20fe]\r\nEntry #28\r\n[img:005aab20fe]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/contests/twisted_plastic/ph2t_1_1.jpg[/img:005aab20fe]\r\n\r\n[b:005aab20fe]3rd place: hue35[/b:005aab20fe]\r\nEntry #24\r\n[img:005aab20fe]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/contests/twisted_plastic/hue35_1_1.jpg[/img:005aab20fe]\r\n\r\nMad props to all you pimps!\r\n\r\n[b:005aab20fe]Prize winners:[/b:005aab20fe]\r\nTo collect your prize, send CaboWabo a Private Message wit a complete shipping address da bitPimps can send the prize to you at.\r\n\r\n\r\n[size=24:005aab20fe]Word ta BigBird![/size:005aab20fe]\r\n\r\npeace\r\nand I\'m outta herre!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (38273, '38c0060bed', '', 'Yeah I\'ve dozens of these pipes over the years. Most before I was 18. :lol: \r\nI always liked a long one with a carb. I liked the ones with the chambers too, but those always got leaks, cause sooner or later you\'d take the pliers to it.\r\n\r\nThis one has stuck with me because the combo of the square elbow, and solid 1 piece center piece makes it 100% airtight with no need for rubber seals, and\'s the perfect length, long enough, but small enough, you know how that is. ;)\r\n\r\nPlus I\'ve always had a thing for blue anodized aluminum. :-D');
