INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (38228, '12a79d290d', '', '[quote:12a79d290d="PimpIke"]\r\n\r\noh yeah, not to start a arguement( i\'m so not wanting this, but i gotta post this up ) you can go ahead, put fets, 4wd blah blah, NML fuzion, the handling just won\'t cut it...[/quote:12a79d290d]\r\n\r\nI\'ve got no problem with the handling. I\'m way over defending the xmods from mini z owners so I\'m not going to start "but i gotta post this up".\r\nThe turning isn\'t as "smooth" or tight as a mini z (granted) but from my own personal experience on mini z tracks and running with mini z racers, I aint hurting one bit. Maybe it\'s just a skill thing? :???: \r\n\r\nI don\'t own an overland so how exactly would it be cheaper for me to buy one and then hop it up to a "stock" madforce? (or even modified)\r\nBefore I dive into anymore of this let me just put this out, Miniz - xmod and all 1/2?th scale are way too big for me to enjoy running. The main thing I like about any of these cars is the tinker value.\r\n\r\n@payaso- The stock xmod is slow and takes some room to get to speed. I don\'t have a RS corvette but I do have an epoch. (which has been said to spank the RS version) The epoch isn\'t beating an xmod with a stage 2 motor. It [b:12a79d290d]WILL[/b:12a79d290d] get the jump on it though. I attribute that to the difference in scale and the weight of the heavy ass xmod body.');
