INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (20739, 'bb3e6e2bc8', '', 'mmm......thanks for the window inside tip. and all of ur glorias look hot. and payaso, i saw urs in the gallery originally and i was like Crapz0rz mcduck i need a gloria. then the funny thing was, I HAD A GLORIA!!!! I was so happy when i foudn it. It was a bootleg my mom got for 5 bucks (isnt that thoughtful!) when she was shopping. It was from when i just started getting serious and i didn\'t kno what a gloria was yet. boy im kinda pissed i painted it tho. it was originally a really nice blue with shiny clear coat. and it had a funktastic JOMO license plate sticker. If i ever see it again, i will buy all of them and sell some to u guys. Unless something really awesome comes to me, this gloria will just be solid black with gloss coat. Perhaps minor detailing on lights to be done. Any ideas for a not overly riced paint idea?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (20740, 'f3ff021cda', '', 'snaps can be repaired. for anyone familiar with zips, u know how hotness civics are, and that they are like the gloria of ZZs. anyways, i was dremeling, and apparently the rotary saw was applying too much overall tension and weakening everything. because when i was rinsing away the powdered plastic and drying it off with a towel, IT BROKE IN HALF. so i just super uber glued it back together, sanded the hoo-hah out of it, showed it who\'s  boss and painted her up. All fixed!');
