INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21180, 'b45e6af607', 'So I checked out the Mitsu EVO VIII (the real thing)...', 'I was getting my brakes done on my \'00 Xterra yesterday, in the waiting area I\'m reading some Auto Mag with a round up of some high end street rockets. Of all the cars they tested, only 1 was actually in my buying \'range\'...The EVO VIII.\r\n\r\nI\'ve been thinking of upgrading from the Xterra for a while now and the more I was reading on the EVO, the more interested I got. The fact that it\'s a Sedan meant the Wife might actually concur.\r\n\r\nI get home and jump online to find the nearest Mitsu dealer and we head out.\r\n\r\nMan, we get there and the EVO is SWEEEEEEeeet! Me and the Mrs. fit (we\'re both 5\'10") in it no problem, even in the back! The Sales guy is going on with his verbal diarrhea and it\'s all coming across as blah blah blah cause I\'m too fixated on this beauty. \r\n\r\nAlright, now for some REAL fun...I want a test drive! But wait! The guy starts giving me shit about how they CAN\'T give me a test drive! Say what? I start hearing about how these cars are EXTREMELY limited, like only 6,000 of these things are imported per year and that they\'d ONLY give me a test drive if I was SERIOUS about buying. In other words, I gotta sign up as if I\'m buying it and lay down all my info first (as the guy says; People WON\'T buy these cars with any miles on them, so we don\'t do test drives)\r\n\r\nWell, I didn\'t hang around after that. After hearing those comments, things started running through my head. Things like; low import, HIGH theft. Any replacement parts = BIG money. The EVO is considered a \'street racer\' which = HIGH insurance...Oh well, let\'s see how nice the Maxima is!');
