INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21253, '9ed0e0f287', '', '[quote:9ed0e0f287="TheEvo"]That\'s just.. No words.. \r\nAnyway...! WTF is styrene?[/quote:9ed0e0f287]\r\n\r\nStyrene is the material of opaque plastic used for the ground effects and other structual projects, usually white.  Comes in several different ticknesses. 0.20, 0.30, 0.60.  Other materials are:\r\n[b:9ed0e0f287]Butyrate [/b:9ed0e0f287]- Optically clear, easily cut, dimensionally stable. Great for model window glazing. \r\n[b:9ed0e0f287]Vivak[/b:9ed0e0f287] - Multipurpose high-strength clear plastic. Use for forming airplane canopies. \r\n[b:9ed0e0f287]Polycarbonate[/b:9ed0e0f287] - An unbreakable, high-temperature plastic. Ideal for forming engine cowls');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21254, '0a9e9e059e', '', 'Track Update!\r\n\r\n[img:0a9e9e059e]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/track9[/img:0a9e9e059e]\r\nDidn\'t get as far as I wanted to this weekend, but the cardboard "webbing" in finished.   Next week, I\'ll hang plaster cloth on this cardboard skeleton to form grassy hills, and rock cliffs.   (with rock molds)\r\n\r\n[img:0a9e9e059e]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/track11[/img:0a9e9e059e]\r\nThis extra area here beyond turn1 I figured, would be a good place for a small waterfall (runoff from the track), and pond.    The webbing photos in the railroaders magazine look sorta like this... hmmm.    :grin: \r\n\r\n[img:0a9e9e059e]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/track10[/img:0a9e9e059e]\r\nI\'ve also got to start thinking more at this point how the garages, diner, chop shop and other few buildings are going to look and be placed.   I want to use 2-D art or photo decals like the ones those guys used in Yagbol\'s post "Look at this Track".     Hey Cabo, another water runoff (behind the banked turn) into a stagnant pond littered with tires and rusted front ends behind the chop shop sound alright to you?    :lol:');
