INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21521, '0e1e3d455a', '', '[quote:0e1e3d455a="hue35"]One potentially cool thing about too much power for the weight of the car, is adding the right amount of weight exactly where it\'s needed. I wonder if you could find the magic spot (the jee spot) that would make handling perfect?[/quote:0e1e3d455a]\r\n\r\nA thin layer of lead across the bottom of the chassis (mounted internaly) would help I beleive.   This would help maintain a low centre of gravity.\r\n\r\nWith all this power and torque increase I need to get off my but and finish developing my propo emulator.  I might just focus on the speed controll.  I\'ve noticed that pulsing the fwd button from a standing start helps keep the car straight and not lose it off the mark causing inifinte spin outs.   Any acceleration that ain\'t instant would definately help handling.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
