INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21527, 'c8749c0f99', '', 'Ok here you go;\r\n\r\nI traced the copper strip from the open contact, and determined the one on the top goes to the electrolytic capacitor, and the open contact on the second one down goes to the power source. See the picture.\r\n\r\n[img:c8749c0f99]http://erinsbaby.com/davesstuff/tcmosmod.jpg[/img:c8749c0f99]\r\n\r\nNow I\'ve swapped out both steering and forward transistors for microsizer ones, and determined that those are definately the 2 to flip. That I\'m sure of, but the jumpers I\'m only 99.99999 percent sure of, because I\'m never sure of anything until I test it. I\'m still mind boggled that my boards even work after I mess with them.\r\n\r\nSo until me or someone else has tested and confirmed that it works, [b:c8749c0f99]Try it at you own risk[/b:c8749c0f99] ;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21528, '8d6daceeea', '', '[quote:8d6daceeea="ph2t"]Any acceleration that ain\'t instant would definately help handling.\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:8d6daceeea] In 1/10 scale off road they use a slipper clutch, to keep traction off the line. It just as simple as a friction pad system. Maybe something as simple as a loosly mounted gear would help. :???: \r\n\r\nI think I figured out my issue with the Thunder Charger PCB. See [b:8d6daceeea][url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?p=21527#21527]THIS[/url][/b:8d6daceeea] if anyone wants to test it and confirm it for me. I\'ll probably be testing it as soon as I get some more mosfets, the TC PCB is strong to begin with.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21529, 'e4d2bc118d', '', 'I really fuckin hate richard simmons.\r\n[img:e4d2bc118d]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid73/p86eec822ed05bb57329796db1fa7bcd8/fb6a90e0.jpg[/img:e4d2bc118d]\r\n\r\nI owned a deli in a mall up here and this fucker decides he would make an apearance. They setup the fuckin stage right in front of my store and my deli was open on the two sides (no walls, just a railing and some glass on one side) facing the stage. I got to sit there and listen to his screeching voice on some big ass speakers and I was even privaliged enough to see his gay ass shorts most of the time. We had a nice cold ice storm goin on outside and the mall would have closed if it weren\'t for queer boy rich not canceling.(so in away good ol\' rich put peoples lives in danger by making them drive on a nice thick sheet of ice) The only customers I had were big fat moo cows there to watch rich shake his thang (that was kinda good though becuase I made some money and got to stuff these hypocrites wit fatty ass pastrami  :lol: ).\r\nAnother good thing was the freakin christmas tree store was selling richard simmons gear for a whopping $.50cents. I freakin laughed my ass off as i watched these big fat hungry hippos waddle up to richard with an abdominizer to sign that had a nice big bright collored $.50cent sticker on it. :lol: \r\nI wonder if there\'s a group or some shit for people like me who have been emotionally scarred by richard simmons. :???: \r\nI\'m gonna do a lil search. :-)');
