INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21693, 'f09dfca412', '', 'Well I don\'t know about everyone else, but i love the new playlist. \r\n\r\nHell yeah that shit brings back memories. I could tell you a story about every song. Want me to? WTF, I will, I know Nox is expecting it. ;)\r\n\r\nBreadfan - I remeber that was a b-side to the out of print Damge Inc. when the re-released the song as a B-side to another song, I remeber a freind crapped his pants. It is one of their stronger tracks, and deserved better than teh b-side treatment.\r\n\r\n\r\nMeantime - I remeber dude popped up with the dropped-D tuning right after all the seatle bands, swore he never hear the Seatle bands that everyone had heard, and he was a classicly trained jazz musician, and stubmled upon the dropped D by accident. Yeah, BS we all said, but he did teach us that heavy is not what you play, it\'s knowing when not to play\r\n\r\nJesus Christ Pose - One of my all time favorite songs, powerful track showing of Chris\' amazing range, highpoint of Badmotorfinger...but then MTV banned the video, and then Outshined bacame the big hit. Oh well probably more than the mainstream was ready for anyways.\r\n\r\nJoin the Army - Suicidal\'s first album willalways be one of my favorites, but this was another strong one. Remember the Possessed To Skate video? the used to show it on Headbanger\'s Ball. Man we wanted to tear up a house and skate it like that. Natas Kapas, ans some other pros in that video. Dogtown Skates, venice beach, yeah baby, crazy homie skaters gotta love it.\r\n\r\nHarold on the rocks - my buddy is one of the best bass players you\'ll ever meet, and a huge Primus fan, he used actually figure out and play Primus songs. Mind blowing stuff, gotta love anything by Primus.\r\n\r\nWell thanks for the trip down memory lane. ;)');
