INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37884, 'ec61eef52b', '', 'I would suggest you try buying a "broken" Xmod, and fix it yourself if you have soldering skills. The only thing that could be broken with it is that the wires are desoldered, or some shit like that. The used one will cost like, oh let\'s say.....20-25 dollars. Then buy an upgrade for it, but if there are no used ones....spend it on a new Xmod. \r\n\r\nTrust me, The Xmod is worth the 50 bucks.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21837, '670f84a6b5', '', 'I have a theory, it\'s probably wrong, but it\'s my belief...\r\n\r\nI think since slot cars were huge in the 60s, and while popular during the 70s, they weren\'t as popular. Now it\'s an obscure hobby... So I\'ve always got the impression that these are left over from the 70s, and they\'re still trying to get rid of them.\r\n\r\nYah, I know that\'s probably wrong, but since you never see recent bodies styles, that\'s just the impression I get.\r\n\r\nAnother possibly more accurate guess, might be that they\'re using the same molds, because it\'s not worth their time to make new ones for a dead hobby.\r\n\r\nEither way, I see your point Sezziz, Micro RCs are happenin\' now, and they should be cashing in on it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21838, 'a2ddd3c549', '', 'they will probably make a corvette, but not necaserily an \'83\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEDUT:I just found a slot car on that you could mod [img:a2ddd3c549]http://www.slotcars.org/164auto/catalog/full/tybody027.jpg[/img:a2ddd3c549]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (21840, '976bca1f28', 'And now...The fish are intimidated by me.', 'The other night, I had to stay late at work (to deal with that MS Blaster worm shit). When I finally make my trek home, it\'s late.\r\n\r\nAlong my regular path home, I always walk by an inlet; Here\'s a picture\r\n\r\n[img:976bca1f28]http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid74/pf8b6a032dcd4b2b54753badb57d4dabb/fb63ab67.jpg[/img:976bca1f28]\r\n\r\nAt night, the water is so low that basically all there is is mud/sludge. Though the path was pretty dark, I was able to make out the form of some fish floundering around and seeming to enjoy the mud (muddy mudskippers?).\r\n\r\nWell, since I\'m not a fisherman I can\'t attest to the \'intelligence\' of fish...But I SWEAR one of them flounderers noticed me and stopped floundering to see what I was doing! I froze, staring back at him. Then the thought occured to me; I\'ll take a picture! I start reaching toward my messenger bag and start to unzip it to go for the cam...That son of a bitch KNEW what I was doing and took off out of sight!\r\n\r\nI was going to grab the cam anyway and snap one of the other fish, but when that one jumped, the rest of em did too. So I didn\'t bother.\r\n\r\n1 of these days man, I\'ll get a shot of that fish!');
