INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22043, '99804ad318', '', 'I can tell by the flood of responses that y\'all are like "yeah, whatever." But once you start charging with AC power, you\'ll never go back. I know some of you guys just mod for looks (or maybe even performance) but don\'t actually do much driving. If you do drive a lot, especially if you race with other people, you\'ve got to give this a try. All the parts cost less than a couple packs of AA batteries (which you will no longer need to buy), and the performance increase and controller range increase make this one of the better little car projects you can do.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22044, '5db9bf8db4', 'Some Current Projects', 'http://community.webshots.com/user/aquarius228\r\n\r\nIn the RC Cars are some pics of some current projects.\r\n\r\n1.)[u:5db9bf8db4]Death by Beetle[/u:5db9bf8db4]\r\nOk so far this beetle has dual exhaust in the back and a spoiler. It also has all windows blacked out for a rally type look with the eception of the front window and driver window(red tint). It also has eyelids on the front lights. It will soon have skirts and some rally mesh.\r\n\r\n2.)[u:5db9bf8db4]Art Car[/u:5db9bf8db4]\r\nI saw this show with art cars on it so I decided to do one. First it a custom drop top ZZ skyline for bit chassi. It also has a orange to hot rod red fade. Then I hand painted on a black mask over the paint job. It also has custom inside on the PCB. It also includes a custom exhaust.\r\n\r\n3.)[u:5db9bf8db4]360 Stretch[/u:5db9bf8db4]\r\nRecently I purchased a Mini Cooper at Target for $11. And I was going to asleep last night and was thinking how cool my 1/24th 360 model would look on it so today I stripped the 360 model and began stretching the chassi. tomrow I will probably finish streching it and replace the mini cooper tires with the 360 ones.\r\n\r\nComments?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22046, '7168693e4d', '', 'i usually use my boat charger. its more convenient than an ac charger to me since it fits in my pockets along with a car and controller. if im at my friends sometimes i use his variable dc power supply tho. it controls the voltage and the amps and is super reliable but i wouldnt suggest one for home use.');
