INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22325, 'c986f1b6bc', '', 'SW - many thanx for the mention in your post. Your track is looking as sweet as ever. \r\n\r\nI remember back in the old days when I used to paint (very badly mind you) metal figure for some warhammer wargame. There was a technique we used that made painting really easy with good results. You\'d paint your figure as normal then use a method called drybrushing to add details then finally run black ink into all the cracks and details - the results were pretty amazing. Made it look like you has a single hair brush and a steady hand. Reckons this might be a useful method for paiting the rocks. I suppose it depends on what they are made of of course.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand - you could use REAL rocks. Just cement/glue them in place.\r\n\r\nI\'ll keep me eyes peeled for more updates.\r\n\r\ns\'whatitismamma.\r\n\r\nBuks');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22323, 'a0e5128ba8', '', 'Thanx again Mang,  Like I said earlier, I just got the idea one night and had at it.  I got a Bug in Da Shop now getting Da Treatment!  I STill gotta give madd props to the ModGod [i:a0e5128ba8]Sinned [/i:a0e5128ba8]for the tuit! and also I gotta give props for the pointers to Ahh5hit, told ya I had a lil sumtin sumtin cookin in Da Kitchen!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22324, '8b19a7a3d3', '', 'That\'s a TC controller, is it a TC or other generic ???  What did Wal-Mart want for it?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22326, 'e7b9be7599', '', '[quote:e7b9be7599="CaboWabo"]the more I see those comparison shots at that front end, its new, how\'d you do it?\r\nputty?\r\nchopped front off another?\r\n\r\ndamn fine work[/quote:e7b9be7599]\r\n\r\nSame front end, just modified.  I got the 0.60 Styrene for the ground effects but the front was still too high so I hadda find a way to lower it first. I also ordered some 0.20 styrene which I used for the airdam. It\'s very flexible and strong. After tab &amp; suspension lowering I cut a piece of styrene and Super Glued (modders best friend) it to the front just under the bumper, filed down close the body to blend it in.  I was gonna leave it just straight down but with the other ground effects it didn\'t look complete.  So I hadda file it down enough to get the 0.60 styrene to fit without rubbing.  Once done I SG (super glued) it to the air dam, filed to shape it,  drilled two brake cooling ducts and added the intercooler and Viola!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22327, '14f7d47473', '', '[quote:14f7d47473="brendan123"]That is sweet man i like to paint job, how did u get that intercooler.[/quote:14f7d47473]\r\n\r\nThe intercooler is standard 1" staples. Break off the amount to make the intercooler the size you want, super glue them on the back, let dry, then cut the ends with dikes according to how far out you want it to stick out. I usually like mine flat or just a slight bit out according to where it is mounted.  Very easy addition. I gotta find the perfect aftermarket grill now to use. I\'ve seen some but a lil difficult to work with and I\'m all about ease of use.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22328, '9e7e327032', '', '[quote:9e7e327032="crazydave"]That is excellent work. I can hardly even tell that used to be one of those ugly ass Thunder Charger bodies.\r\n\r\nI\'ve got a buch of those bodies I\'ve been tossing aside, I need to start doing something with them.[/quote:9e7e327032]\r\n\r\nCavey, the bodies are very cheap plastic even though they are clear. I wanted to leave the glass clear and tint it but the top of the windshield separated when cutting the targa so I did the paint everything Sinned method and permanant markered the windows.');
