INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22384, 'ff9de5ab7f', 'Scalloped RX7 ZZ (also I fixed my alloys)', 'Well that hacking the body to work with the rim business wasn\'t flying with me, so I decided to go ahead and narrow the front alloys. I just rubbed them in circles on 400 grit sand paper. I knew aluminum is soft, and would sand easy, but it went so well that I went ahead and took it down to the next bevel. I narrowed them by about 2mm. I then shaved my steering knuckles, chassis, bulkhead, and steering arm, to move the wheel in another mm, for a total of 3mm on each side. The front wheels are now tucked in the body. I lowered the front tab on the chassis, and all my bodies still work with very little, if any trimming.\r\n\r\nNow the rear wheels seem too wide in comparison, and gives it a muscle car look. Looks cool with my muscle cars...\r\n[img:ff9de5ab7f]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/alloy4.jpg[/img:ff9de5ab7f]\r\n\r\n...but looks silly on the Skyline, and Lancer. I thought about doing the back ones too, but my fingers were sore from pressing on the rim, and I dug it with the muscle car bodies.\r\n\r\nThen I discovered the RX7 body was wide enough in the back to keep them meats contained.\r\n[img:ff9de5ab7f]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/alloy3.jpg[/img:ff9de5ab7f]\r\n\r\nSo I tried to redo the scallops I did on the 911 on it. they came out a little crooked, but I think the overall paint job came out better.\r\n[img:ff9de5ab7f]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/alloy1.jpg[/img:ff9de5ab7f]\r\n[img:ff9de5ab7f]http://members.cox.net/crazylittlecars/alloy2.jpg[/img:ff9de5ab7f]\r\n\r\nTook a little work, but now I\'m 100% satified with my alloys. :grin:');
