INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22648, '363e49cca6', '', '[quote:363e49cca6="payaso"][quote:363e49cca6="dmoh7"]the only thing that pisses me off is havin to hold that mofo all the time, and plus when your not holdin the turbo it goes so frickin slow.... you still think i should cop a 2 speed? \r\n\r\nCan you give me a few reasons why its better?[/quote:363e49cca6]\r\n\r\nI don\'t even drive my one speed cars anymore..\r\n\r\nI think the 2 speed is the way to go.. Why? Cause you can compensate for the slow speed by simply changing motors, and the batts..\r\n\r\nIf you run a 4.2 King motor, it\'s fast all the time, but if you want to slow it down a bit, just let off the boost..\r\n\r\n2 speed is always better than 1 IMO..  Others have different views..\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:363e49cca6]\r\n\r\nI definitely agree, 2 speed is better. I use the 4 band controller, so I can set the switch to drive it like a single speed. But, i have taken to mosfet modding many of my cars, then a 2 speed is almost a must (certainly with 4.2). The low speed is also not so slow with mosfets. I also like 2 speed for dual cell cars.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22649, 'bf87b60fd7', '', 'I prefer a two speed...same reasons as Silla Payaso.\r\nI run it always in turbo mode...then when needed...I back off.\r\n\r\nI also don\'t have any experience with the LXX series.\r\n\r\nGo Tomy.  Pay the bucks and you\'ll compain like the rest of us.\r\n\r\n-nox');
