INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22887, '04856a473b', '', 'The very interesting micro_amps, thanks for the info.\r\n\r\nI had feeling something was up besides the the different layout, because the Super bits handle the 4.2 soooo much better than my Microsizer, the chassis isn\'t that much lighter, so I had a feeling something is up in the circuit design.\r\n\r\n....but I wonder why the mosfets don\'t give that much improvement, the theory of cutting resistance is the same.\r\n\r\n...and I\'m baffled that you say they wont run on dual cells, there\'s been a couple people at TRC that have claimed to dual cell theirs, so were they just blowing smoke up my ass?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22888, 'e3ec785f02', '', 'You have to coppy and paste it, because geocities sucks.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22889, 'dd008a7c98', '', '[quote:dd008a7c98="crazydave"]\r\n...and I\'m baffled that you say they wont run on dual cells, there\'s been a couple people at TRC that have claimed to dual cell theirs, so were they just blowing smoke up my ass?[/quote:dd008a7c98]\r\n\r\npossibly,  micro is very solid in his work CD, I\'ve had many discussions with him on various electronic issue surrounding these cars.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22890, '447f7f372d', '', 'Thanks ph2t, \r\nre this...\r\n[quote:447f7f372d]so were they just blowing smoke up my ass?[/quote:447f7f372d]\r\nnot necessarily, these are just my findings at this stage. I measured the \'switch off\' voltage several times and it is spot on 2.7v every time. Initially I thought I\'d fried the pcb, but it just shuts down.\r\nId be interested to see the a \'super\' dual celled, because of the reduction in chassis space.\r\nAsk them what voltage they are charging at, and if the car works whilst on charge, and see what they say.\r\nThis is a minor issue anyway, my main concern right now is getting an SBCG fet modded, the lighter chassis fet modded WILL rock, its just a matter of getting a few things sorted out first. I have a few ideas, but until I can test them, they remain just that, ideas.\r\n :) uA');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22891, '372632cf66', '', 'Couldn\'t wait fellas,  :smile: .\r\n\r\nHere\'s my attempt at the mod using the layout Crazy detailed earlier.\r\n\r\n[img:372632cf66]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/fet1.jpg[/img:372632cf66]\r\n\r\nI played with it for a day and then said stuff it, lets stack \'em.\r\n\r\n[img:372632cf66]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/fet2.jpg[/img:372632cf66]\r\n\r\nHere\'s another view.\r\n\r\n[img:372632cf66]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/fet3.jpg[/img:372632cf66]\r\n\r\nAnd when they have all been soldered on:\r\n\r\n[img:372632cf66]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/fet4.jpg[/img:372632cf66]\r\n\r\nI have never seen a 3.8 motor go so fast, dang!\r\n\r\nThe principal behind fet stacking (mini-Z\'s are big on this) is to half the resistance of the Fet.  This gives you more juice and oompf (very technical terms here....) in the motor.....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22893, '4bf516fb30', '', 'That\'s cool to hear that FET stacking works, but now I\'m thinking, everytime I mod a car I end up with a pile of transistors left over. Since I\'m waiting for mosfets, maybe in the meantime I could stack the transistors in one of my cars, to see if that gives me a slight boost.\r\n\r\nYeah I know it wont be nothing like a mosfet mod, but my cars could use a little xtra oomph to get these 4.2s going, maybe that just might help.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (22894, 'e6cd17954f', '', '[quote:e6cd17954f="ph2t"][quote:e6cd17954f="crazydave"]\r\n...and I\'m baffled that you say they wont run on dual cells, there\'s been a couple people at TRC that have claimed to dual cell theirs, so were they just blowing smoke up my ass?[/quote:e6cd17954f]\r\n\r\npossibly,  micro is very solid in his work CD, I\'ve had many discussions with him on various electronic issue surrounding these cars.\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:e6cd17954f]Oh yeah, I trust micro_amps, he definately know his stuff. that\'s why I just wanted to clarify.\r\n\r\nI know a bunch of people at TRC charge their dual cells by just wiring the 2 cells in the controller straight to the pad, it works, just takes longer to charge, so maybe that\'s why they\'re getting away with it. Time to head over to TRC, and ask some questions. ;)\r\n\r\nThanks again micro_amps. It\'s smart that you don\'t post your findings until your 100% sure. I\'d rather do the same, but I\'m just muddling through this, so I post what I\'m up to so people like you and ph2t correct me when I\'m wrong.\r\n\r\n\r\n*** EDIT: This all got me thinking, and I just wanted to add. In organized racing, limits have to be set in order to create a level playing field. With the added frequency it would seem Tomy is aiming more at organized competition. Anyone else think that Tomy is purposely making these cars harder to mod, to prevent cheating in organized racing? \'Cause it would be too easy on the original to just slip one mosfet in, and have a cheater board that would be virtually undetectable.');
