INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (23232, 'b67a4a0dc1', '', 'Yeah no prob. I only made you guys a little tut, because some people were interested in my method. Thanks for showing interest. :grin: \r\n\r\nI only hope I didn\'t make it sound too simple. There\'s a few little complications along the way. The knurled part of the front pin can be hard to get through. Cannonball pins work best because they have no knurled part, and a larger head. Thunder Charger ones will give slight resistance, but you should be able to push it through with your fingers. Microsizer ones might need a tap from a hammer. I just line the hole up in the bushing with the hole in an old junk rim, to give it room to push through, and usually a it just takes a slight tap to get it through. Forget about using Zip Zap pins with the pen tips.\r\n\r\nAnother tricky part can be getting them the right length, especially the rear one with the spacer. It\'s best to cut them a tad long, and grind  them back to the exact lenghth with a Dremel.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (23233, '5d46c8c6b1', '', 'Ok, this is what I scored.\r\n\r\nGP01 - Skyline GTR R34 Pullback\r\nGP02 - Skyline GTR R32 Pullback * 2\r\n\r\nGM08 - Subaru Impreza WRX Shell Pack\r\nGM05 - Nissan Gloria Shell Pack\r\n\r\nGS03 - Gear &amp; Axle Set * 2\r\n\r\nG26 - BitChar-G Beetle, 45Mhz\r\nG03 - BitChar-G Skyline GT-R, 35Mhz\r\nG14 - BitChar-G Nissan Gloria, 45Mhz\r\n\r\nThe total cost for all these bits \'n pieces was $44 USD!!!!   The shipping was (as always) the killa @ $28 USD.   So the total price was $72 USD.   Now all things considering, especially the avg cost of Bit-CharG shit in Australia I believe it\'s a great deal.\r\n\r\nIt took a week to get to me and everything was cool.   I\'m offically recommending Joynpeace as a great supplier for stuff from HongKong.   The only thing is that she hasn\'t got everything in stock (ie, some pullbacks I couldn\'t get and no SBCG), but hey, it\'s still a great deal none the less.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
