INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (23819, 'ad24a2c52b', '', 'Project WRX Rally\r\n\r\nI had a Clone WRX body I bought on eBay (Notice a trend) that I wanted to try and make look like the rally car. Unfortunately I could never get a set of decals I liked for it so I made it into a street rally car.\r\n\r\nThe chassis is one of my LXX clones with an interesting history. Is was sold as is (not working) on eBay. I got it for less than $8.00 shipped to me. It came with the black rim and a blue Calsonic body. The body was peeling but I decided not to complain when I discovered that the car worked when I installed a new motor, the one that was in the car wasn\'t even a LXX motor but a MS motor. I put in a clone motor and ZOOM. The gold Perfection heat sink came in anound the same time so on it went.\r\n\r\nThe Body was slammed to the ground. I put in a exhaust pipe on the passenger side of the car (just like the pro rally car). Blue paint and some detailing and this is what emerged.\r\n\r\nI wish I had an Alps printer so I could make the decals for this car.\r\n\r\n[img:ad24a2c52b]http://www.rcpics.net/media/WRX-1.jpg[/img:ad24a2c52b]\r\n[img:ad24a2c52b]http://www.rcpics.net/media/WRX-6.jpg[/img:ad24a2c52b]\r\n[img:ad24a2c52b]http://www.rcpics.net/media/WRX-7.jpg[/img:ad24a2c52b]\r\n[img:ad24a2c52b]http://www.rcpics.net/media/WRX-8.jpg[/img:ad24a2c52b]\r\n[img:ad24a2c52b]http://www.rcpics.net/media/WRX-9.jpg[/img:ad24a2c52b]\r\n\r\nEnjoy');
