INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24003, 'ba92aa2547', '', '[quote:ba92aa2547="hogjowlz"]and your car will be slow and get no traction. why not just lower a hotwheels car?[/quote:ba92aa2547]\r\n\r\nI beg to differ. I have a Zip Zap with all small bit wheels on it, it handles like it is on rails! It has red Zip Zap gears, clone tires, Mosfet modded pcb and purple zip zap motor and the tabs are lowered. In a drag race against a bit with normal size (clone) tires, orange gears, mosfet mod and perfection 4.2, it is dead even for the entire quarter mile (20 ft.)!\r\n\r\n[img:ba92aa2547]http://mysite.verizon.net/res1aa2l/images/DSC00321.JPG[/img:ba92aa2547]\r\n\r\nAlso, my 69 Camaro rs convertible Zip Zap has all small wheels and tires on it as well. It is even faster than this one, with mosfet booster board, perfection 4.2 and red gears. It doesn\'t handle quite as well because it does not have the good tires on it (yet, just got them the other day).\r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1599[/url]\r\n\r\nAll I can say is "just do it", the look is more to scale for sure!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24004, '3af6c3015e', '', '[quote:3af6c3015e="VooDooMafia"]Nice \r\n\r\n  How does the Super bit run with the 4.2?\r\n\r\n  Hell how does it run stock?[/quote:3af6c3015e]\r\n\r\nIt was painfully slow with the stock 1.6. I didn\'t put a 4.2 in it, I put a perfection 3.8 in it. It is plenty fast now, the tires just suck bad on the floor I run on. I put some of the colored tire set tires on it (red in back, blue in front), and that seems to help quite a bit. It does still spin out once in a while.');
