INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37506, '843c498707', '', '[quote:843c498707="payaso"][quote:843c498707="SuperFly"]Just to make sure, you guys do know about rubbing alcohol and salt, right?[/quote:843c498707]\r\n\r\n\r\nNope.... Do tell though.  I\'m guessing it cleans it good?   :???: \r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:843c498707]\r\n\r\nDude, if you\'ve never tried it... you will be amazed.\r\n\r\nAs you know, the inside of a bong is one of the foulest and nearly uncleanable environments. This cleaning method is about as good as it gets, and doesnt require too much elbow grease or any scrubbing brushes.\r\n\r\nHere\'s what you do:\r\n\r\nEmpty out  the old water, take out the stem, and plug the hole with a stopper. I use the stopper from the bottom of my ash catcher and just put it in the hole that the stem goes in. I use my finger to cover the carb hole.\r\n\r\nDump a little salt (like 2 tablespoons) and some rubbing alcohol (probably about 1/4 to 1/3 the amount of water you would normally have in there). I\'m naturally cheap when it comes to using things up, so using a little more of each wouldn\'t hurt, alcohol and salt are cheap. Then, with all holes plugged, place the palm of your hand over the mouth hole and shake and swirl that bitch. About 2 minutes of thorough shaking and dump out the solvent and the abrasive (tha alcohol and salt) and rinse with water. Done. If that doesn\'t give you the cleanest bong with the least amount of work, I\'ll refund your money.\r\n\r\nI should have taken a picture of my rig after i cleaned it. It looks just like hue35\'s  :cool:');
