INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24913, '79f4dc6290', '', 'The farthest I can even go in my kitchen is about 15 feet and it does that easily. With the stock red motor in it, it is just as fast as a bit 2.2. The controller is a little akward at first, but after getting used to it, I really like it. You will develope a feel for it. With a 28k motor in it, the battery lasts about 5 minutes without the lights plugged in, and about 4 minutes with the lights plugged in.\r\n\r\nCrazydave: I don\'t like the take-off either, but IMO, I really enjoy the propo steering and being able to slow for turns, etc., and then gun it and kick the rear end around. Worth the trade off for me.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24914, 'b0dd938abb', 'Cheap tank', 'My cheap tank just came in from ebay.\r\nHere are some pics with my web cam.\r\n[img:b0dd938abb]http://www.montypics.com/pic.php?url=/T-maxximum/2003-09-05/1062811363_all.jpg[/img:b0dd938abb]\r\n[img:b0dd938abb]http://www.montypics.com/pic.php?url=/T-maxximum/2003-09-05/1062811389_tank.jpg[/img:b0dd938abb]\r\n\r\nAs you can see the controller is smal, but in even in my fairly large hands it feels pretty good. The range on this thing, well, sucs. It also stuters when it starts getting far away. It is alredy duel celled, but it uses to cells about 1/3 of the size of normal bit cells. It goes on pretty steep slopes probably around or steeper that 45. It is powered by two green end ball motors. It can go from carpet to hardwood and yo can\'t notice a differece. Al in all even with the range problems, for 8 dollars shipped from Honk Kong I think this si pretty good.\r\n\r\n\r\nEDIT: oh yeah one more thing the controller uses button cells, but they some with it, and it has an external charger.\r\n\r\nAnd another thing is that it will not interfere with other bits even though it is 49 mhz.');
