INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24966, 'b36fce93ce', '', 'I was day dreaming of getting a T-Maxx (someday), and checking out Tower Hobbies. I saw the Microsizers, and thought they were cool as hell, but 30 bucks seemed a bit pricey(for a guy on a budget), and then I was going to have to get the 9.99 2.6 motor, gears sets, and all the goodies. Added up it was too much, and I put it off.\r\n\r\nThen I saw the Zip Zaps on a TV commercial, I the price was better, and I liked the longer, more scale looks better. I had to have one, but I guess so did everybody else, and the darn things sold out as fast as Radio Shack was getting them in.\r\n\r\nSo then I got a Cannonball clone from Checker. I went down there the day they got them in, and there was only 2 left already. (So where the heck are all these people that were buying them up before Christmas?) I thought I was pretty lucky just to have found that, but being the POS that it was I got bored with it a couple days later.\r\n\r\nI would have been done had I not recieved a Zip Zap for Christmas. It was slow, but handled great, and seemed to be of some quality. So I went out on a mission for speed. That\'s when I got turned on to TRC, met up with Hogjowls, and the gang, and my life\'s never been quite the same.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (24967, '1e38a5d6b0', '', 'fredensborg indkøbscentral you say? Hmmmm :???: Nope don\'t think I\'ve seen that around here. :lol: \r\n\r\nOk, here\'s a quick explanation of spray paints. The stuff you get in the hardware section it usually Acrylic Enamel. Model paints are usually Acrylic Enamel. Automotive touch up paints are almost always Acrylic Laquer.\r\n\r\nKrylon is a brand of enamel that they sell in the hardware section, and Duplicolor is a Krylon brand of laquer that they would sell in the automotive section.\r\n\r\nSo anyways long story short, Tamiya is a model company so their paint is more than likely enamel. I wouldn\'t know what brands are Laquer over in Europe, but I heard one of the German guys mention using Opel paint, or maybe it was just an Opel color, I don\'t know, but hopefully that all made some sense.');
