interested in this promotion please email us at xmodes@gcmginc.com \r\n\r\nSubject line: XMODS girl NYC \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nJob Qualifications: \r\nPlease include: 1. full name 2. contact numbers 3. list prior promo experience 4. are you available to work 9/25 &amp; 9/26? 5. why should our client pick you to be an XMODS model? 6. resume 7. one outstanding picture (not larger than 100k) \r\n\r\nContact Information: \r\nName: Gilad Carni \r\nPhone: 000000000000 \r\nAddress: \r\n210 West 70th St. Suite 311 \r\nNew York NY, 10023 \r\nSalary: \r\n$20/hour \r\nHours: \r\nTo Be Determined [/quote:4536a576ce]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25005, '5599e59a0d', 'Judging: Middle of the Road contest', 'welp, the contest ended Friday, so I\'m sure the pimps are expecting us to use the weekend to judge. So, when you get a chance, lets get it crackin and post up our picks.\r\n\r\nalso, this is the contest we were planning on putting the crazy spin twist judging on (i.e. best, middle, worst swap) so how do we handle the picks?\r\nany suggestions?\r\n\r\nsemi side note:\r\nPimpin Body Mod tutorial contest ends this Sunday (tomorrow), looks like cj won? lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25006, '24156fa756', '', '[quote:24156fa756="CaboWabo"]Tamiya is the shizznit, that\'s all I use.[/quote:24156fa756]\r\n\r\nCabo, your paint jobs are sweet. Smooth and shiny!  :cool: \r\nDo you use Tamiya spray can or bottle and an airbrush?\r\n\r\nThe reason I ask is that I\'ve been having a problem airbrushing Tamiya. I can\'t get a consistant spray. Sometimes it\'s just right, other times it\'s too thick/thin causing "orange peel" texture. Might have to do with humidity and not the paint.  :? Don\'t know...\r\n\r\nAnyone have the same prob???');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25007, 'db73c698b1', '', 'I\'m still on spray cans man, I use the bottles too when I\'m detailing, but I still don\'t own an airbrush (by the word of the bit gods I will someday)\r\n\r\nthere\'s a slim chance you need to thin the paint down before running it through your airbrush, but Tamiya\'s bottled paint is already pretty thinned out.\r\nthere\'s a better chance that the airbrush is spraying it too thick or the humidity thing. with humidity though, usually that just increases the drying time. raised paint (orange peel) is usually the result of laying paint too thick in shot (it happens to the best of us at times).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25008, 'fd70f318c3', '', '[quote:fd70f318c3="Ahh5hit"][quote:fd70f318c3="Havok"]Hook us up dog...where\'d you get that tackle box? \r\n\r\nI have a pretty sizable collection now...but all I can find are sh*#ty loose, small tackle boxes... :([/quote:fd70f318c3]\r\n\r\nI picked it up at Dick\'s Sporting Goods for $19.99. Now I need to get another for my Bit collection which is growing just as fast.\r\n\r\nBTW, I have added about 10 more cars including my recently painted ones.[/quote:fd70f318c3]\r\n\r\nI see it\'s been awhile since this post, but....\r\n\r\n[b:fd70f318c3]Got a brand name and product # for that bad boy[/b:fd70f318c3]? I [i:fd70f318c3]needs[/i:fd70f318c3] one!\r\nNever heard of Dick\'s Sporting Goods... I\'ll scope out my local sporting goods.  :search:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25009, 'b6b14457da', '', 'Thanks for the input, Cabo. I do thin the paint when I airbrush.\r\nStrange that it only happens when I use Tamiya paint. :???:  I\'ll just have to play around with it more.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25010, 'c2dc276b5f', '', '[quote:c2dc276b5f="oxhadokenxo"]I have 2 of the "Micro Combat Vehicle" tanks and they\'re pretty good...good speed good turning they\'re also the ones with the infra red beams like the digi-q\'s but they aren\'t that accurate...At close range it\'s very very easy to hit the person..at long range it\'s accurate but it has a big "explosion" range..not like shooting a bomb and it exploding when it hits..The beams bounce of walls for ricochet shots..realistic, no..but it does call this a "feature" in the instructions lol. They were about $15 a piece shipped.[/quote:c2dc276b5f]\r\n\r\nWhere did you get them, my tank just died cause it sucks.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25011, '64c0416a32', '', 'You can get them from ebay or ToyEast has some of the cheap battle tanks(they dont have treads though) for like $35 set of 3.\r\n\r\n  IMO if you want the "Battle" type tanks then spend the money and get the Digi Q\'s');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25012, '6dd9213373', '', '[quote:6dd9213373="SuperFly"]I\'d hate to be the judge of this contest. Lately I\'ve been forgetting to post props for all the nice rides, so consider this a blanket shout out to all the entries, especially DriveWRX, Yagbols, Crazy Dave, Bilbo, too many others. \r\n\r\nYou guys are making it too hard for me to enter any of my rides. Or I should say y\'all make me feel like I need to keep working on them, hence they\'re never finished.[/quote:6dd9213373]\r\n\r\nHeck, sometimes I feel mine aren\'t that good.\r\n\r\nI\'m currently in the planning stages for at least 2 for AusMicro\'s contest. One may be a WRX and the other something a little different.');
