INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25321, 'cd266e7096', '', 'Man I like the new one\'s!  They didn\'t have those when I went on Sunday.  \r\nThat\'s even better, a great prize!  I did pick up a truck &amp; a $15.00 car cover. Damn is it too late to enter?  You need to post dat on Da HookUp!\r\n\r\nEverytime I go to Big Lots (which isn\'t that often) I find something new a reasonable to spend my money on!  Can\'t wait til they get the new Micro Speed cars in, I got a bodymod plan already!  Was that the only body style?  Thanx for steppin up Nox!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25322, '34fa8dc5fa', '', 'I understand the concept of how we\'d like to judge, I think we might all just have different opinions on who deserves what.\r\n\r\nhere\'s my picks and my explinations for each pick:\r\n- Reality = Best; Post = Best; Prize = 3rd place = bdebde\r\nI chose bdebde over DriveWRX simpley because I have my doubts that DriveWRX\'s car even rolls much less turns.\r\n\r\n- Reality = Better; Post = Better; Prize = 1st place = MaximumAttack\r\nI chose MaximumAttack over barto_85 because of improvement on skills and overall look. barto_85 has improved, but not by much, still painting single colored cars with little to no details. MaximumAttack acctually painted a design with his color scheme - much more deserved in my eyes. Personally I think barto_85 belongs in the "worst" category. ZipRC could be in this category, but his job follows existing lines, while color is original, the scheme isn\'t. So MaximumAttack gets my vote.\r\n\r\n- Reality = Worste; Post = Good; Prize = 2nd place = Brendan123\r\nI chose Brendan123 over barto_85 because well... Brendan\'s is a real piece of shit, but he went as far as he could with it, to me that\'s obvious. Again, barto_85 is clean, but very boring and even more so basic.\r\n\r\nSo there\'s my votes, there\'s my reasons.\r\nPersonally, I don\'t really have my heart set on one way or the other.\r\nI\'m leaning towards hogjowlz\'s opinion of "this is DT\'s baby".\r\nbeing that it is DT\'s baby, I\'d be willing to let DT make the final call and claim responsibility for the decision and responses when users ask how we came up with the list we have.\r\nRemember too, when this contest was posted, we posted a general note that stated something to the fact of "hey, we\'re adding a big twist on this contest when we go to judge, so be ready for it". So in theory, the users shouldn\'t be all that bent outta shape as we warned them previous to the start of the contest.\r\n\r\nSo, the way I see it, we need to announce this contests winners (whomever it may be), so if we can\'t work it out between ourselves soon, let\'s let DT make the call and get this thing out the door.\r\n\r\nWe can take this same approach with future contests if you guys want.\r\nBy that I mean - whoever comes up with the idea, whoever supports the contest by providing the prizes, can have the majority of the say.\r\nSo essentially, we would help eachother run and judge contests, but the executive decision (if one is neccessary) will fall upon the main contributor/sponsor of the contest.\r\nSeems fair, but I can also garuntee we\'ll be opening up a whole new can of worms.\r\n\r\nSo, all in all, it\'s your guys\' call.\r\nI have no clue which would work better for our situation.\r\nAnd again, I can swing whatever way is needed on this contest, I don\'t have a shitload of emotions invested in this one so whatever we decide is fine with me. I just want to announce the winners and close this thing out.\r\n\r\nand god damn it that turned out long again lol\r\nsorry');
