INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25374, '32a61cfb56', 'New Mini Cooper Just Arrived', 'Just got done playing with it for a bit...\r\n\r\nFirst thoughts\r\n\r\n- Well built, nicely detailed.\r\n\r\n- Built-in lights are a nice feature\r\n\r\n- Controller is not the greatest (typical knock-off style)\r\n\r\n- Runs for quite some time - haven\'t timed it yet, but it seems to run a lot longer on a single charge than any bit I\'ve owned.\r\n\r\n- Way over-packaged.\r\n\r\n- Antanae is not flexible. Gives it a nice solid feel out-of-the-box, but it\'s going to get crushed at some point. Difficult to fit with other bit bodies as a result.\r\n\r\n- Tires are too small up front and too hard. Tread on tires makes it bounce around.\r\n\r\n- Does not fit any of my bit rear axles!!! This is a major problem. Looks like bit wheels will fit without any mods, but I\'ll have to fit bit rims to the Mini axle. \r\n\r\n- Body fit is tight - really tight. Will need to be modified to fit other bits.\r\n\r\nOverall impression is good, especially for the price. I can\'t help but think how cheap these would have been without all the fancy-schmancy packaging. It handles well, stock motor is good (3.8?) and seems to be well-built.\r\n\r\nThat\'s what I know.\r\n\r\n :cool: Maark');
