INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25910, '9c3ec1f097', 'couldn\'t resist', 'I set up the track in my kitchen with video tapes.  My best 6 lap time was 30.48 seconds.  I used an off the shelf kb toys clone with the pink endbell.  You definately get better times after the battery is drained just a little.  Definate room for improvement on the time though.  It\'s easy to knock a tape a little off and tag it on the next lap.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25911, '52108f51c4', '', 'I appologize for the lack of updates guys.    Got busy with real work, and had a vacation in there too.   No track work = no updates.\r\n\r\nI\'m at the point now, where I could add some rock faces, or start assembling some of the buildings.    Something that Hogjowls said way back that stuck in my brain.......\r\n\r\n[quote:52108f51c4="hogjowlz"]i use a shrinkray and zap my neighbors house when they aint home.[/quote:52108f51c4]\r\n\r\nFunny comment at the time, but really not to far off of what could possibly be done..... sort of.    I have taken some photos of a real body shop, (run-down of course).    And thinking about printing the textures out on sticker-paper, and attaching to the corrugated plastic scale buildings.     I could tweak the photo some in PSP to suit my needs.   For instance change "Body Shop" to "Chop Shop"\r\n\r\nAlot of thinking, just need to get my ass in gear.    Sorry again for the lack of progress.\r\n\r\nI did have some friends over, and had 4 cars going on it.   (the wife\'s vid camera base is busted).   I only lost 1 five-lap race   :grin:     Home track advantage, and two hundred laps practice.     Its a little different (and alot of fun) with traffic.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25912, 'ddd1a40fa2', '', 'brown tape is usually paper based masking tape.\r\nscotch tape is the thin, clear, plastic based tape. you\'ve probably used it wrapping up x-mas gifts or something before.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (25913, 'edde3c75f2', '', 'on a single cell = a loose rear makes your car bank to the right usually since the right wheel is most likely to be loose.\r\n\r\non a dual cell = a loose rear makes your car bank hard to the right\r\n\r\nbrendan:  do both front wheels freely spin?');
