INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26265, '5e7e7fcdfe', '', 'My first comp was my bro\'s Macintosh LC II he let me use it when he got his Mac Performa.  And my favorite game was Space Junky where it was a purtty version of a classic aracde I forget the name...Its the one where things scroll across the top of the screen is patterns and u shoot them before they blow u up with the random shots.\r\n\r\nLC II Info:\r\n[img:5e7e7fcdfe]http://www.aceadvanced.org/computers/apple/lcii.gif[/img:5e7e7fcdfe]\r\n\r\nCostructor:  Apple    \r\nName: Macintosh LC II  Foster Farms   \r\n Origine:  USA    \r\nYear Introduced: March 1992  \r\nTerminated: March 1993    \r\nCPU  MC68030 at 16 Mhz   \r\n FPU  none (upgradable)    \r\nRAM  4 Mb (upgradable to 10Mb)   \r\n VRAM  256Kb (upgradable to 512Kb via one socket)    \r\nROM  512 Kb    Case     Keyboard    \r\n Display  4-bit (16 color) at 640x480 or 8-bit (256 color) at 640x400    Audio  Sound Output: mono 8 bit (built-in speaker)\r\nSound Input: mono 8 bit Input/Output\r\n\r\n    * Slots: 1 LC PDS\r\n    * SCSI: DB-25\r\n    * Serial Ports: 2\r\n    * ADB: 1\r\n    * Floppy: 1.44 MB SuperDrive\r\n    * HD: 40-80 MB\r\n    * Ethernet: none\r\n\r\nPeripherals none Item in Museum 2\r\n\r\nPrice:$1240\r\n( http://www.aceadvanced.org/computers/apple/lcii.htm )\r\n\r\nAnd we had a....CD-ROM DRIVE! You had to load the discs into caddys lol. We still have this lol.\r\n\r\nEDIT: And I\'ve been playing with my X11 Terminal in OS X which is basicly just a UNIX terminal Its hard to believe that was what your OSs all used to be lol! Freaky :shock:');
