INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26329, '6d823e80c3', '', 'I\'m wondering how much of a difference there\'d be between just NOT hooking up the LEDs, and direct wiring the LEDs leads to the Motor.\r\n\r\nThe SE manual says not hooking up the LEDs causes less load and therefore could make the car go faster.\r\n\r\nThat makes think that there\'d be no extra juice by direct wiring.\r\n\r\nI\'m guessing the LEDs are hooked into the main circuit (let\'s say for argument sake that the circuit is running 100mA at 2.4v). Whenever hitting forward of reverse, the LEDs takes its\' part and loads the main line (dropping either the mA or v of the main circuit). \r\n\r\nThink of it like it\'s a water hose. the LED is like a small leak in the hose. Whether you plug the leak (same as not hooking up the LEDs) or plug a smaller hose to the leak and run it back to the main line (which would be what Hog suggested for wiring the LED leads back to the main circuit)...You end up with the same result. There\'s probably a couple of people who will comment on this without reading this far, you\'re a nut tard if you do (let\'s see who does).\r\n\r\nAnd there you have it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26330, 'b8ac4126ff', '', 'hmm i dono if its hooked into the main circuit cuz when you hook an led up to the motor circuit it does not light up. when the car is under heavy load(dual cell) because the motor is drawing everything and there isnt enough power to turn the led on(edit i forgot to mention that once it revs up the light kicks on so this could be used as a crude hp meter). but in vids ive seen of ses they turn on as soon as you hit fwd so that tells me that they are not on the same circuit as the motor.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37337, '395ea37cdb', 'Micromatch, I need a response....please??', 'I realize this isn\'t the place to post this, but there weren\'t really any other sections for this.  A while back I mailed Micromatch a couple of 3.8 motors and he said the payment was on the way.  I sent the motors in good faith and I haven\'t received a payment, nor hav I received any replies from him to my private messages.  If anyone knows him, could you ask him to pm me?  I\'m not a hard ass and I\'m not going to bust his balls if he forgot to send the payment.  I cut him a deal on the motors and I\'d just like him to get the payment to me.  Thanks.  :cool:');
