INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26359, 'a92640f256', '', '[quote:a92640f256="SuperFly"]So, uh, you willing to share your vector art, Cabo? I just got this waterslide decal kit, "SuperCal". I\'m kinda skeptical. What paper type do you tell your inkjet printer you\'re using? Gloss photo paper? Does the spray really work to seal the ink? I tried one sheet the other day, and within a few hours the images totally bled and got all blurry. I hadn\'t sealed it yet, and it was kinda humid, so hopefully next time it works better. \r\n\r\nP.S. I\'m willing to trade my decal art, though it\'s not vector, it\'s 800dpi at 100%.[/quote:a92640f256]I don\'t have anything worth a crap, beside the bitPimps logo.\r\nI also printed single sheet inkjet (no special settings, just printed at 600 dpi like normal)\r\nI think laser is much, much, better than inkjet and bubblejet, there\'s no "dots" to see, and you will see them with inkjet depending on the graphic and surface its going on.\r\nwhen I did my inkjet, I clear coated the sheet after it was dried. If you do use inkjet or bubblejet, definitaly coat it or it\'s gonna bleed when you put the water slide decal in the water.\r\nlaser doesn\'t seem to bleed, at all and doesn\'t seem to need a protective coating, problem there is color laser printers can get pretty pricey.');
