INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26699, '89582b94ff', 'ph2t i have a question...', 'going back to your original design on pg 1  of this thread.\r\n\r\nyou show a picture with the two yellow square showing where you hook up the FET\'s on the auxiliary pcb. are these the FWD and BACK pulse signals that come out after the 3 volt converter? ARe these the signals that turn on the FET\'s gates in the H-Bridge?\r\n\r\nalso could you explain why there is a need to do anything with the steering. if one keeps the two steering bjt trannies on the board wouldn\'t the steering still work?\r\n\r\nthanks a lot, this mod seems like a doable one for me as there is no way i can solder on the so-23 fets.\r\n\r\njeff');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26700, 'ea3a5d949e', '', '[quote:ea3a5d949e="CaboWabo"]downloading and serving up un-copyrighted material is illegal[/quote:ea3a5d949e]\r\n\r\numm don\'t you mean copyrighted material? \r\n\r\nIf its un-copyrighted not only can you make a copy and use the item you can go as fas as to cpyright it in your name.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26701, '333a74bda5', '', 'ok i just got my hands on one of these things and it is strange. mostly a good strange but its different than any other bit ive ever seen fersure. i gota say the mechanics are top shelf. i havnt had a chance to open her up on the carpet yet but its a lot quicker than ahhshit made it out to be(in my opinion). its quicker than a stock bit with maybe a little less low end. \r\n\r\nthe controller is gona take getting used to but its not bad so far. still unbelievable that its totally propo for that size and price. the springs are just right.\r\n\r\nthe only bad ive discovered(other than the ugly body) is there is a slight twitch in the steering but i think that has something to do with the trim which i havnt had time to figure out. and actually the enifi shell isnt as ugly in person as it is on a pic i think. its about as ugly as the original fnf zz shells.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26702, 'ab18402bc3', '', 'umm no, actually I mean both now.\r\noriginally I didn\'t, but you know what I meant Mr. Smartypants\r\n\r\nand in most cases, even if its un copyrighted, there\'s a little something called "intellectual property" so no you can\'t just go copyrighting stuff that hasn\'t already been copyrighten. it\'s more complicated than that.\r\n\r\nhere\'s a link to 10 big myths of copyrights:\r\nhttp://www.templetons.com/brad/copymyths.html');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26703, '99483db5de', 'Re: ph2t i have a question...', '[quote:99483db5de="burgan"]going back to your original design on pg 1  of this thread.\r\n\r\nyou show a picture with the two yellow square showing where you hook up the FET\'s on the auxiliary pcb. are these the FWD and BACK pulse signals that come out after the 3 volt converter? ARe these the signals that turn on the FET\'s gates in the H-Bridge?[/quote:99483db5de]\r\n\r\nYes they are the signals, but they come from the RX2/6 chip not the DCDC converter.   The RX chip needs 3V to run that\'s what the DC convertor is for. :lol: \r\n\r\n[quote:99483db5de]also could you explain why there is a need to do anything with the steering. if one keeps the two steering bjt trannies on the board wouldn\'t the steering still work?[/quote:99483db5de]\r\n\r\nThere\'s no [i:99483db5de]need[/i:99483db5de] to do anything with the steering at all and yes it would still work.  Fet steering is better, but only barely so.   Works best on full wheel mods, pulbacks...\r\n\r\noh and welcome to the real deal man.... :smile: \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26704, '716adcd6da', '', 'i gota agree on the chassis. it rules hard. now off to figuring out how to make it faster.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26705, '425c8cd30a', '', 'i was guna paint a beetle and try to use modeling clay for a bodykit ill tell you how  it goes');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26706, '86e317d4fe', '', 'Been do some more dev on this.   [b:86e317d4fe]Credis to Matic for the info and [i:86e317d4fe]I think[/i:86e317d4fe] original design credits go to micro_amps for this one.[/b:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nWith the two fets that are soldered the dodgy way. ie: one leg hanging astray, there is the problem with them not being flat on the pcb and therefore it\'s tricky to be able to solder well.\r\n\r\nSo we flip the buggers,..\r\n\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/moslayout_flipped.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nIn the two pics below the left one is original and the right has it\'s pins bent upwards.  Be careful not to snap the pins on the fet whilst bending them the other way.\r\n\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/fets_flip1.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/fets_flip2.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nSo, you then flip the fets upside down and place them on the pcb.\r\n\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/fets_flip3.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nHere\'s another angle.  Note I am talking about the two fets closet to the black blob.\r\n\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/fets_flip4.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nNow we connect the fets together as per the diagram.   [b:86e317d4fe]Note that the MOSFET pin that the wire connects to must not be soldered to the pcb.   This is on the flipped fets side of the wire only.[/b:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\n[img:86e317d4fe]http://www.prahranpianos.com/bit_g/hbridge/fets_flip5.jpg[/img:86e317d4fe]\r\n\r\nshamon\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (26707, 'adf0673ada', '', 'I would not suggest using clay\r\n\r\n  Use puddy or epoxy.  Clay will be very brittle and more then licky you will need to cure it.  its good for making stationary things(pots and shit).\r\n\r\n  Here is a link to some good stuff IMO\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.gamesworkshop.com/storefront/store.ca?do=Individual&amp;code=99219999005&amp;orignav=300810[/url]');
