INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (27567, 'a0c464d63f', '', 'Well, I can tell you that the Tamiya paint went on a LOT nicer than anything else I\'ve used. If you are scared to use the gloss, the color paint itself shines like glass. I went ahead and threw the clear coat on for protection. I only used one pass/coat of the clear. This stuff goes on smooth.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (27569, '3a821c02ed', '', '[quote:3a821c02ed="Ahh5hit"]Well, I can tell you that the Tamiya paint went on a LOT nicer than anything else I\'ve used. If you are scared to use the gloss, the color paint itself shines like glass. I went ahead and threw the clear coat on for protection. I only used one pass/coat of the clear. This stuff goes on smooth.[/quote:3a821c02ed]\r\nYeah, I have used Tamiya paints on models before...\r\n :eek: They are awesome.\r\nDo you need to use a primer coat?\r\nWill Tamiya paint stick to auto touch-up spray? :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (27570, '4a55d60478', '', 'Not sure about the auto touch sticking, but I didn\'t use any primer at all. I even had dark spots on the white body from sanding and it covered and blended well. I used about 6 passes/coats of the color and followed with one good coat of gloss. I sprayed from about 12" away and didn\'t have any problems with running. I waited about 10 minutes between coats.\r\n\r\nI ran out today and bought more Tamiya colors to paint some other cars.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (27571, '7417c8b30e', '', 'Ok cool....\r\nCome Moday, I will have paint and styrene.\r\nTuesday, our houses deal closes (We are moving.). I will then put on the styrene and sand it down. Yay for CA glue!! :-D \r\nWednesday, maybe some more fine detailing to the kit and masking.\r\nThursday, I will commence painting!\r\nI\'m thinking of doing a dark blue, or a bloody red...\r\n :eek:  :D');
