INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (28132, '96aec25551', '', '[quote:96aec25551]Super-bits on the other hand are almost perfect, the bodies look great. I\'ll tell ya, I only have to paint and modify my bodies, because I\'m not that in to RX-7s, and S2000s, etc. etc., but the Countach, one of my all time favorites, the Porshe 911, another all time favorite. The Jota? stunning beauty, I\'d never touch these bodies. [/quote:96aec25551]\r\n\r\nI gotta agree Dave, especially the comment about the Euro bodies, their form is so perfect &amp; detailed, I wouldn\'t touch it at all !!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (38918, '6811db85a0', '', 'Hmmm, that\'s odd, it was my understanding that by having perfectly timed periods of light and dark, hydro buds grow denser, and that slight exposure to light during the night time periods made outdoor weed grow looser, more scraggly. At least that\'s what I gathered from High Times.\r\n\r\nAnyays around here, most of it is imported, and that means it\'s been smashed into a brick, and all the buds are flattened and hard. Once in a while, like at this moment, we get some piney stuff, that\'s fluffy. I believe that this stuff comes from up north, where we have a lot of pine trees. it\'s my understanding that it\'s outdoor grown, because we pay more than five times as much for the hydro stuff. The quality of the high is the same, there\'s just more stems and seeds in the outdoor stuff here.\r\n\r\nMy wife grew up in a hick town in the middle of here and there, and she was telling me the hippy neighbors across the street had a Christmas tree farm, kept bees, and grew weed. That\'s when it suddedly occurred to me, the bees cross pollinate the trees with the buds, and that\'s where we get the pine weed from. I love pine weed. I think it\'s my favorite.');
