INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (28525, '176afa599b', '', '[quote:176afa599b="crazydave"]A RX-7 is not a race car, unless you make it one.[/quote:176afa599b] No car is a race car unless you make it one,  unless you bring it right off the track some shit. RX-7s are damn near close to being a race car bone stock. 13b rotary engine that can shift 10,000 rpms like its nothing while a B18c5 redlines at 9,100 in a ITR. The rx-7 is also stock with a twin turbo setup.(not all some are NA) Skylines are also twin turbo stock on a 6 cyclinder RB26DETT. The Integra Type R or Honda Integra Type R for those of you over seas are meant to be raced in a manner. My friend droped a B186c5 into a 99 Si and its crazy. They arent meant for drag but courses. they have 11:1 compression pistons stock with a head that flows better than anything with no outside workdone, a header stock and throttle response like no other it can be shifted at 9 grand oevr and over and it still remains normal and it very reliable. None of these are "race" cars but i promise that they are far from normal.');
