INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (28609, '33a7ba721e', '', 'Thanks again for the compliments, guys. That\'s why I do it. That and so I can beat hue35\'s ass in style.\r\n\r\nYep, HO slot car wheels on the Gloria, painted metallic gold.\r\n\r\nHere\'s some info:\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Porsche:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nMosfet modded single speed PCB\r\nTeal gears, 4.2 King motor\r\nSpring suspension\r\nTab lowered front and rear\r\nRemoved wing, filled and sanded wing holes\r\nMask, paint (originally dark blue), detail. Model Master Light Ivory\r\nPainted wheels gloss black\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Lancer:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nSingle speed PCB\r\nTeal gears, 4.2 King motor\r\nBlack finned heatsink\r\nBody kit added front, sides, rear with pass-through cusom exhaust\r\nMask, paint, detail, clearcoat. Custom mix metallic silver-blue over Boyd\'s Hi Gloss White\r\nLXX Black wheels\r\n\r\nI\'m surprised no one commented on this one, it\'s one of my favorites. The body kit looks like it came from the factory. I may still put some decals on this one\r\n\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Mazda RX-7:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nMosfet modded single speed PCB\r\nKIT racer red gears, 3.8 perfection motor\r\nBlack finned heatsink\r\nSpring suspension\r\nBody kit added front, sides, rear\r\nReshaped wing, added custom exhaust\r\nModel Master Metallizer metallic paint (aluminum plate). You buff this stuff out right after you put it on and it looks like polished metal.\r\nTinted windows from inside\r\nClearcoat\r\nKIT racer wheels, front and rear\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Gloria:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nsingle speed Panther PCB\r\nOrange gears, 2.2 Microsizer motor (slow and low, that is the tempo)\r\nSpring suspension\r\nTab lowered front\r\nRemoved wing, filled and sanded wing holes\r\nGold chassis detail, mask, paint, detail, clearcoat. Boyd\'s Lime Gold Pearl or something like that, and Testor\'s Gold\r\nBangin\' stereo on the package shelf/motor clip device\r\nHO slot car wheels, front and rear, silicone tires\r\n\r\nI added the stereo, metal flake upholstery, gold chassis detail and clearcoat since the first time I flossed this ride.\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Esso Supra:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nMosfet modded two speed PCB\r\nteal gears, 4.2 Pro motor\r\nSpring suspension\r\nTab lowered front and rear, as low as it can go, slightly routed rear wheel wells\r\nPainted wheels gloss white \r\n\r\nI put this one in here mostly because it drives like a mofo, and Supras don\'t look half bad when you drop them. Also, the Supra used to handle like crap, but the mosfets driving a fast motor seem to make it all better. It\'s a pretty nice $4 body from Toy East\r\n\r\n[b:33a7ba721e]Skyline:[/b:33a7ba721e]\r\nMosfet modded two speed PCB\r\nOrange gears, 3.8 perfection motor\r\nBlack finned heatsink\r\nSpring suspension\r\nMask, paint, detail, clearcoat. Boyd\'s \r\nNakamichi racer wheels, front and rear\r\n\r\nHue35 and I, unknown to eachother, bought the same color of paint. He put his over white primer I think, while mine has the inside of the body painted bright yellow. They end up looking totally different in RL.\r\n\r\nSo, any advice on which 3 to enter in the contest?[/b]');
