INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29342, '0b7d31cb05', '', 'No its not a stepper ph2t, its a normal motor (green cap so a 1.6 I think) it has a feedback pot connected to the steering mechanism to confirm position. The front end is pretty much just a \'servo\', not a stepper.\r\n :) uA');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29343, '956cf7233e', '', 'mine drives well in the street if you want to give that a try\r\n\r\n(i just got mine today and love it even though its stock)\r\n\r\nit would be funny if they think your some punk noob and your xmod smokes the mini z, that would make my day to do that');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29344, '597a676cde', '', 'The steering is driven by a motor. It has a green endbell, at first I thought it was just a plain ol\' 1.6, but then I realized it is hardwired. I was considering wiring a pink clone motor to see what happens...\r\n\r\n...but now that you mention the second Hibridge being for steering (and that makes sense to me) I\'m wondering if I\'ve gone and FETed my steering.\r\n\r\nI didn\'t notice a difference, because I was focusing on the speed, and shortly after took the jumper off my steering pot, which made it super sensitive.\r\n\r\nI like the proportional steering, but proportional throttle doesn\'t help me drive much, because of my driving style. I\'m thinking I wouldn\'t mind ditching the propotonal throttle, to get power. \r\n\r\nmicro-Amps, you think it would be possible to put a mosfet at the output to the motor, and set it up to switch the juice straight from the battery when current to the motor start to flow?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37225, '582b297519', 're:', 'Just reading through some old posts and came across this one.  \r\nI couldn\'t agree more with the guys saying HO slot cars ROCK!  \r\nI\'ve been racing them for about 15 years (I\'m 31).  Strayed away from T-Jets for a long time and got into the modern magnet cars.  About 3 years ago started getting back into T-Jets.  Get hooked on Bit Racers for those times I wasn\'t at the track and then a friend showed me one of his Char-G clones and I was hooked.  I had my new \'away from the track\' time killer.\r\n\r\nI still race HO slots.  Mostly on road course style layouts but I do partake in the occasional drag race.  Something about seeing a car built in the 60\'s hit 60MPH+ on a 20ft straight that gets the blood goin\'.  I bet the Aurora engineer\'s would flip if they seen what their design was capable of some 40 years on.  Neo motor magnets, custom wound .9 ohm arms, bronze crown gears, CNC\'d idler and driven gears...fun fun fun.\r\n\r\nHere\'s one I started working on.  It was painted lime green metallic but was destroyed before I had a change to snap any pics  :(  ...  \r\n[img:582b297519]http://mywebpage.netscape.com/edpleadwell/diggers/otj_lowered.jpg[/img:582b297519]\r\n\r\nI finally convinced a friend to give me one of his old AFX Capri\'s.  Plenty wide, now I just have to shorten without making it look too weird and cast in resin.  \r\n[img:582b297519]http://mywebpage.netscape.com/edpleadwell/minirc/capri2.jpg[/img:582b297519]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29346, '9571ba178d', '', '[quote:9571ba178d="micro_Amps"]No its not a stepper ph2t, its a normal motor (green cap so a 1.6 I think) it has a feedback pot connected to the steering mechanism to confirm position. The front end is pretty much just a \'servo\', not a stepper.\r\n :) uA[/quote:9571ba178d]\r\n\r\nCool, thanks for the info dude :). Is it interchangeable with other motors?\r\nAlso, this stacked bjt intrigues me, I take it\'s the npn one of the pair?  Was that 0.9V measured with a DMM or a CRO?  Also dude was it an open circuit measurement?   Sorry, so many questions man...Is the drivetrain h-bridge the same layout as a BitG apart from this stacked transistor? \r\n:lol: \r\n\r\nph2t.');
