INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29366, 'a3f9147afd', '', '[quote:a3f9147afd="ph2t"][quote:a3f9147afd="crazydave"]The steering is driven by a motor. It has a green endbell, at first I thought it was just a plain ol\' 1.6, but then I realized it is hardwired. I was considering wiring a pink clone motor to see what happens...[/quote:a3f9147afd]\r\n\r\nHave you unsoldered it and put it in a normal bit for speed comparisons?\r\nThat would be an interesting exercise.. :???: [/quote:a3f9147afd]\r\n\r\nThe wires run directly into the endbell, I could probably modify it to work in a bit, but it would be very difficult, and probably would not go back in the SE very easy.\r\n\r\n[quote:a3f9147afd="ph2t"]So Dave, are you saying you should connect the gate pin of the mosfet to the terminal where the motor is connected on the pcb? this would imply that you are not using the output pin of the chip, yeah? interesting... \r\n[/quote:a3f9147afd]Yeah that\'s what I was talking about. I wanted the FET to essentially switch on a bypass around the PCB. i know this has been done with bit PCBs for multicell dragsters, but I wasn\'t sure if the SE\'s pulsed current would be strong enough to turn it on, and micro_Amps seems to agree, but still it\'s an option I\'m willing to look into.');
