INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41235, '1b7937fbfe', '', '[quote:1b7937fbfe="betty.k"][quote:1b7937fbfe="Son_Gokou"]I myself am indian (from India, not native american) and some bitch-fuckers like to take advantage of the fact that my background is from the east, and call me osama. I was eatin a white cocunut meringue cookie one time, (meringue cookies are basically just dry and hard), and this black guy, tall and FAT, asked me for one. I gave him one, and he crushed it into a powder in his hand, and said "Whatchoo tryin to do to me boy? Is this anthrax? You trying to poison me, indian terrorist boy???" And today he brought it up, 4-5 months after that incident, and told everyone. \r\n\r\nThese guys at my school are a perfect example of LIARS....They will slander my background, say things such as "Hey A.J., how\'s uncle osama?" and a bunch of [b:1b7937fbfe][size=24:1b7937fbfe]SHIT!!!!!!![/size:1b7937fbfe][/b:1b7937fbfe] In fact, you wanna know about my race\'s accomplishments? First off, did you know about the time they....*gets slapped in the face with hogjowlz\'s trout*......never mind....gotta stay on the topic....[/quote:1b7937fbfe]\r\n\r\n#1: tell em to be real careful when they open their locker\r\n\r\n[quote:1b7937fbfe]But, payaso....I don\'t get what you mean by the teachers at my school lying about how getting good grades can affect your career. I mean, for god sakes, a guy who has F\'s and D\'s in his math classes all the time can\'t exactly become an html designer or a code-hacker![/quote:1b7937fbfe]\r\n\r\n#2:i dropped out of school at 15 and have worked in some very priveledged positions. it\'s all down to attitude and work ethic. i get what you\'re saying, jimmy the idiot boy probably won\'t be an air traffic controller, but it\'s not a rule. einstein was told in school that he would never amount to much! the most important talent you can possess is the ability to learn, drop me in any job and i\'ll do pretty well.[/quote:1b7937fbfe]\r\n\r\n#1: LMFAO...never thought of that\r\n\r\n#2: Yeah, I guess that just because you spin out in a race on the corner from the 1st place doesn\'t mean it can\'t be swung past the finish line :smile:\r\n\r\n[quote:1b7937fbfe="payaso"]Quitter... \r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m on my 15th year at Harvard...[size=7:1b7937fbfe]I\'m the janitor.[/size:1b7937fbfe]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:1b7937fbfe]\r\n\r\nLMFAO.....2nd time :smile:\r\n\r\n[pre-edit] I just saw filelicker\'s post (was using another window to take the quotes from and paste in here, when it reloaded, saw his)\r\n\r\nThis reminds me of a question I had to ask: Sure, you can drop out of high school and all....but getting a job has some requirements, like diplomas and all that crap. So, how can dropping out let you get a GOOD job? I mean, my parents are always telling me I have potential to do great, and let me tell you....I\'m pretty damn good at math...[size=7:1b7937fbfe]Well, in my class at least.[/size:1b7937fbfe] So, can\'t I grow up to fit into a job that requires good math knowledge, say, circuit board engineering and shit like that? I mean, we\'ve seen ph2t talk about circuit board schematics in the Weird Science sections of the forums....(hey ph2t, in high school, weren\'t you a math wiz? I mean, quoting you from the SE fet thread: "Yes, my mates always thought I was a nerd and they still do!" So, you were a math wiz...doesn\'t that come in handy for your electronic stuff?)   \r\n\r\nBut, your stories are your stories....I\'ll forge my own path in life, and see how that turns out.');
