INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29488, 'df35826297', '', 'Same thoughts here.  Instal the Bearing kit first sine you have to strip the care down to just electronics.  I only ran into 1 problem so far and one of the front stock stub axles was larger in diameter than the bearing inside.\r\nThe bearing inside is .115" where the axel was .118".  Spining it and shaving off the extra .003" was easy.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29489, '0d6487277d', '', ':cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29490, '545a50df59', '', 'The bearing kit is all I need. Unfortunatly the xmod bearing kit isn\'t what I\'ll be getting. I don\'t like how they left them open faced. I\'m hoping the miniz bearings will fit, gonna haveta try em. :???: \r\nPeople say the xmods car isn\'t full propo and it "only" has 15/16 steps of steering. I really don\'t see a need for 500 more steps. Not at this scale. Unfortunatly I\'m a newb with these cars so I\'m still learning and might change my mind later, but for now I\'m liking it. Even though I gotta drive 20miles sos I can race it.\r\nGood thing I got my bits to pick up the slack inbetween track visits. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29491, '5f847a5e97', '', 'Those look to be the rims that are on my RX-7 Super-Bit. I also got a deep dish vrsion from the Porshe pullback.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29492, '446ae20b09', '', 'Same as above. Get yourself a Xacto Kit from walmart and a small roll or a piece of the finest grit sand paper you can buy. Remember when your cutting, never put too much pressure or you\'ll cause the body to crack and it will look nasty.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29493, '870dd0f26d', '', 'I know I\'ve been gone for a while, but it\'s just been school and some other stuff.   Anyway, that\'s some real nice work.  What I Want to know, is what do you usually use for the body kits and stuff, where it\'s plastic, but real real flat?  It definetly looks real nice.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29494, 'c6b33cf5a3', '', 'Project: Outback\r\nBody: Clone WRX\r\nChassis: Tomy Booster\r\n\r\nMods\r\nBody: Removed front scoop (I thought it was too large for this project) cut off rear window and truck and converted it to a wagon. Two tone paint scheme.\r\nChassis: Cat5 Antenna.\r\n\r\n[img:c6b33cf5a3]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Outback1b.jpg[/img:c6b33cf5a3]\r\n\r\nIt took me three days of cutting, glue, putty and sanding to get this ready to paint. I don\'t rush things.\r\n\r\n[img:c6b33cf5a3]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Outback2.jpg[/img:c6b33cf5a3]\r\n[img:c6b33cf5a3]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Outback3.jpg[/img:c6b33cf5a3]\r\n[img:c6b33cf5a3]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Outback4.jpg[/img:c6b33cf5a3]\r\n\r\nYes I\'m entering another Grocery Getter, and I probably will keep making them until I win a contest with one.  :lol: As I said before Hobbits think of food and ways of getting it home to prepare.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29495, 'c3303b020d', '', 'I can\'t believe it either lol\r\nI\'m just kinda sitting back and lurking on these to see how well they perform.\r\nI came from 1/10th scale so I\'m not too keen on going bigger than the micro\'s but... ya never know, I might get a hair up my ass and go get one lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29496, '787525089a', '', 'diagonal cutters or "dykes" hobbico sells some. they are quicker and easier and safer than exacto knives.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29497, '14858a07f3', '', '[quote:14858a07f3="crazydave"]Those look to be the rims that are on my RX-7 Super-Bit. I also got a deep dish vrsion from the Porshe pullback.[/quote:14858a07f3]\r\nyeah same as on the ferrari 512 too, i like the new smaller rims on the supers.\r\nDefinetly fits the the viper well too! Nice work 8)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29498, 'b3aa6ae9d7', '', 'kent = micromatch');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29499, '7ed4f9dddd', '', 'Just a little info on these boys.  The wife picked one up for me about 2 weeks ago.  Typical bullet clone style of controls as you can see.  Great little charging mechanism though as they have a small cable that actually plugs into the bottom of the car from the controller.  It takes just a hair longer than a normal bit/ZZ to charge but nothing outrageous.\r\n\r\nPerformance.  The car has some great torque to it and the giant wheels and clearance helped it crawl across the carpet pretty well.  That being said the steering is such a trip with the whole front end spinning that it is very hard to control and turn.\r\n\r\nIn all, it\'s kind of a cool micro to mess with but really nothing more than a a novelty toy.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29500, '85f442b5c2', '', '[quote:85f442b5c2="ph2t"]I love the 2000gtr, great job there dude![/quote:85f442b5c2] \r\n\r\nthanks ph2t!\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:85f442b5c2="ph2t"]   You know toyeast has now gots the 2000gtr back in stock, you might wanna order some, I did!\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:85f442b5c2]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nwell, easier said than done... hopefully today, I\'m buying an XMod, so that\'ll be the rest of my money! eh, I can wait!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29501, 'ee314f9716', '', 'okay folks, I gotta tell ya about this because if I can make it happen, I\'m going to be advertising it like it\'s gonna make me rich (though it won\'t)...\r\n\r\nremember this fucking dickhead?\r\nhttp://www.ggteks.net/david/zipzaps/ \r\nDavidBeoulve\r\n\r\nhe stole our image content and is hosting it on his own site.\r\nI\'ve:\r\n- sent him an email, and PM.\r\n- sent the "webmaster" of the site an email.\r\n- sent an email to the host "geof" at www.ggteks.net\r\n\r\nall with no response.\r\nI then:\r\n- sent an email to the hosts provider iPowerWeb.com\r\n- sent an email to the providers backbone AT&amp;T.\r\n\r\nso far, only AT&amp;T has responded saying I need to deal with iPowerWeb, if they don\'t help me, then AT&amp;T said they will help as far as they can according to DMCA.\r\n\r\nI\'ve complied with the DMCA and sent off the proper notifications, proofs, etc. so by law, I\'m hoping to:\r\n\r\n- have http://www.ggteks.net/david/zipzaps/  removed from the Internet completely.\r\n- have http://www.ggteks.net (a supposed IT consulting firm - probably 2 fat bastards sitting in an unfinished basement) removed from the Internet completely.\r\n\r\nthey have no clue how far I\'m willing to go to destroy them.\r\n\r\napparently this "David" dink has been contacted by other moderators from other sites, letting him know that he is stealing.\r\nBasically he replied back with "why would bitPimps be mad, they\'re being dumb so screw them"\r\n\r\nso with that, I now have promised myself that I\'m not only going after him and his 3 pals, but I\'m going after their host.\r\nI\'m even considering paying the fees to the government so I can actually take their asses to court and sue for legal fees, damages, time and efforts, court costs, and compensation from damages... up to $100,000.00 per image. :wink:\r\n\r\nthey fucked with the wrong pimp.\r\nthey chose to ignore the wrong pimp.\r\nI gave them many opportunities to be cool and just remove the items in question.\r\nnow I\'m going to war and I\'m not coming back until I have someone\'s decapitated head mounted on a stick.\r\n\r\nI encourage you all to make life as miserable as possible for these chumps, I know I will.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29502, 'edb2773887', '', 'Let me tell you a story about kent. He bought one of the mosfet cars hue35 and I were pimpin. It\'s gossipy, I know, but you have to read the text of the PMs to get a full appreciation:\r\n\r\nIt all started with:\r\n[quote:edb2773887]hey superfly i was thinkin of buying your white 49 mhz skyline for 30.00 if you still have it because my car from micro amps al the suddenly died and i really admire the mosfet cars please pm me back or email me at \r\nkodiakmonky1776@yahoo.com \r\nor my screenname for aol is k77562\r\n[/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\nI reply with the specifics, and the Paypal address. A couple days later I get money in Paypal, and it\'s from a female name. I think "Interesting, not too many chicks doing bits." Then I realize it\'s his mom. I package up the car and send it off.\r\n\r\nFirst message:\r\n\r\n[quote:edb2773887]"hey dudesup \r\n\r\nhey i got my car on the 25th and i drove it arond an dit was awsome but the longest wire connecting 2 fets broke..so i went and bought a soldering iron with a smaller tip and i tyed to resolder it but now i onlyhave fsat in fowwards and the back wards has a constant idletype thing how do i fix it??[/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\nThen before I had a chance to reply, he said:\r\n\r\n[quote:edb2773887]"hey wel i tryed to fixit agian and the long enamled wire broke off, i go fast forwards and i go so slowback wards that my car doesn even have enuff power to turn..isthere any way i can fix this..or get a new one or sumthing?[/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\n\r\nmy reply:\r\n"Dude, what happened? Sorry to hear it\'s not working. We try to do a really good job putting them together and test them before we ship them, so I\'m surprised it broke so soon. \r\n\r\nI can\'t just send you a new one, but if you mail me back the one you have, I\'ll fix it for you, no charge. Assuming you haven\'t damaged the PCB, anyway. \r\n\r\nMy address to send it back is.....\r\n\r\n[quote:edb2773887]"o man icant say enugh abut how good of a jb you did it was an awsoe job bu the onl reason it broke iscause of smthng stupid i did lol i accidentl broke the wir and stupidly tryed fix cause im terrible solderer any way man ill sen off the chaaassis and imma still post a good report in fo sale tho case is carrocked"[/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\nEnglish is this dude\'s first language. I don\'t think someone with that level of spelling/grammar should be using a soldering iron.\r\n\r\nThen he writes:\r\n[quote:edb2773887]hey superflyhave you received my car in the mail yet? i included a speacial gift for you[/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\nHe did send me 2 layman\'s dual cell button-type batteries along with the car, which came (chassis only) wrapped in a kleenex in a regular #10 paper envelope.\r\n\r\nI wrote, "Yeah I got it the other day, thanks for the batteries. I\'ll probably get that fixed over the weekend and mail it early next week." \r\n\r\nTo which he replies,\r\n[quote:edb2773887]"dayam thats hela long pimp! \r\n\r\nalrigt dude happy you like your bateries andthanks a bunch for fixin it" [/quote:edb2773887]\r\n\r\nSo we get his car back and hue35 fixes it, and we go to test it, only to find that he has removed the battery and motor (apparently he didn\'t trust us enough to just leave that shit in there).\r\n\r\nAt this point hue35 and I decided that we would be better off keeping the remaining mosfetted cars ourselves than deal with this crap. We build those things tough, and he broke it within a day of receiving it. And the only way to really mess up a mosfet job is to start digging around on the PCB, which he obviously had no business doing.\r\n\r\n:roll:');
