INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29602, '27585e75d6', '', 'ok my questions on these.\r\n\r\n\r\nso nominal running is 5-6v? what about running 2 lipos? 8v?????   \r\n\r\ni dont know tons about minizs but are parts swappable??\r\n\r\nwhats overall perfomance comparison between the two?\r\n\r\nso 50bucks?? the ability to put 100$$ into it? so it kicks ass for 50$???\r\n\r\ntheres a roller hockey rink up the hill from me that would totally kick ass for this i think.\r\n\r\nwhats runtimes like on 4aaas? or is it aa? they sell a charger but if i got a nicd charger already its the same right or is it a speed charger? fuk theres enough room for tons o battery options.\r\n\r\nwhere do i put jbweld on this thing?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29603, '0696eb9e68', '', '- Nominal is 4.8v to 6v (depending on NIMH or Alkalines)...I can\'t say if the XMods PCBs are the same as ZZs as far as how it passes power to the motor. I\'d think your idea of using LiPoly should be viable.\r\n\r\n- Mini-Zs are 1/24th scale, XMods are 1/28th...The sizes are VERY close, there might be some cross-compatibility for parts, don\'t know at this time what will or won\'t work.\r\n\r\n- Haven\'t done a hardline comparison yet, but so far what I have done leads me to believe the Z is still the champ (as far as steering goes)...Other than that, Stock vs. Stock I have to give it to XMods. The performance and options available, for the cost just plain KICKS ASS.\r\n\r\n- For the entry fee of $50 my impression is \'Nice\'. Add a little Body Kit and some different Motors and then you\'re in kick ass territory.\r\n\r\n- With the Starter Kit, which the Acura RSX is what I got, it comes with 8-tooth gearing (which means high top-end, so-so torque)...A nice big roller rink would be ideal for this setup.\r\n\r\n- Car uses Triple-As. I\'ve never used alkalines, always NIMH. With the Mini-Z, runtimes are up to an hour. I\'d think the X would be similar or even a little better.\r\n\r\n- JBweld not needed, the Hood, front &amp; rear bumpers, side-skirts and mirrors are all interchangable and they\'re all screwed-on.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29604, '75575f125c', '', 'sorry to bring up an old post, but i\'d really like to try this mod out.  My props to all you who did this and thanks for puttin up all the diagrams.  i do got some Q\'s though.  \r\nWhile cruzin round FRYS electronics down here in San Diego, i went lookin for mosfets.  I was lucky enough to find some, but the packaging said "Surface Mount transistor" and no where did it saye MOSFET.  I wasn\'t quite sure which one to use, they had several different ones.  My first question is, which MOSFET or "surface transistor" am i supposed to get.  $9 for 25 of them is pretty good, but i\'d like to save my $9 until i know for sure which to get.  It seems as though many, or most of you use the mosfets from digikey.com.  the mosfest from there are from the company Iternational Rectifier.  Are those the only mosfets that you can use for this mod (the one from IR)???  I remember seeing "AF" on top of one of the packets of transistors at FRY\'s, and other markings on the others.  They look VERY similar to the transistors in the bit pcb (as in size shape ect.).  If you can tell me what i should be looking for and what kind of "surface mount transistor" to use that would be awsome \r\nIn this diagram:\r\n[img:75575f125c]http://www.spedition-reinhold.de/bits/plan3a.jpg[/img:75575f125c]\r\nare all the stock transistors swtiched out with the new mosfets???  OR do you only replace 4 of them???\r\n\r\nSorry for the long post, but i just wasn;t sure with a few things.  Thanks in advance for any help.\r\n\r\nKeep Pimpin\'...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29605, '15cef561c2', '', 'So far charge time on the rs nimh bats at about 30mins gives me well over an hour, this is with the 30k (blue) motor.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29607, '84829d4d87', '', 'The irlml2502 mosfets from international rectifier are probably the lowest resistance fets you can get. If you use suface mount transistors, which are not fets, there will likely be no change (that is what is in there now), in fact it may even be a downgrade if the ones you get have higher resistance than stock.');
