INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29620, '5513a952ae', '', 'I see where you are heading ph2t, but..........\r\n\r\nI spent some time on it today, and I\'ve cracked it. Got my ZZ SE clocking  about 13 km/h (8.5 mph) it screams now and still has full proportional control in both speed and steering control.  Yee Haaaaaa.\r\nIt loves high speed motors and tall gears, has no problems pushing the red gears (on carpet) which are the ones I am using for the 13kmh speeds.\r\nIts kinda  like a fet modded BCG but because its heavier (50% heavier thankyou very much) it accelerates slower and takes nice smooth corners at speed, just before it flips or spins out, (depending on tyre choice and skill level).\r\nIt is now the utimate micro r/c, fully propo, good speed, great control, love it.\r\nIve put some stuff on my website, I\'ll post more stuff here in the morning, its getting late here.\r\nMy work for today, is done.\r\n :) uA');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29621, 'a7627393a6', '', 'Wow!  That\'s great news Micro.  I hope you find it in the goodness of your heart to share this with us lamefolk..... :grin: \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29622, 'aa88a0c103', '', 'Alright, I\'ve been waiting to see Superfly. Not quite what I imagined, but after seeing Hue, I definately can see you guys hanging together.\r\n\r\nSo what instrument did you play Superfly? I forget, I keep thinking Hue is the bass player, but I can\'t remember if I\'m correct, or just thinking that way, because he looks like a bass player. For some reason you look like a horn player to me.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29623, '146e129a62', '', 'Yeah man, I finally gots me the purple star. (I think been a few since I been around there.) Then I find out I need like 500 to get the next one. WTF, it took me while to hit 50. Why even bother trying now.\r\n\r\nPart of the reason I\'m avoiding ebay now, is because rating, feedback, and all that apparently mean nothing. I ordered some clones from a guy with over 500 feedbacks, and 0 negative comments. Seemed like a sure thing. Then I get an email from the guy saying he\'s having problems with Paypal, I could wait for him to work out the problem, or send a money order. I figured alot people are having problems with Paypal, since ebay took over, so I sent off a money order. 3 days later the negative feedbacks started rolling in. After about 25, ebay banned him. The thing that got me, is all the sales were from 3-4 months before, it\'s like, nice guys you could have warned the rest of us sooner.\r\n\r\nI think the problem is too many people are afraid of leaving a negative feedback over a small purchase like diet pills, or a cheap clone car, and risk the seller leaving them negative feedback, to get back at them.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29624, '1d2949ee98', '', '[quote:1d2949ee98="ph2t"]Wow!  That\'s great news Micro.  I hope you find it in the goodness of your heart to share this with us lamefolk..... :grin: \r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:1d2949ee98]Ditto\r\n\r\n...or maybe a hint at least.  :-D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29625, '486d348460', '', '[quote:486d348460="sessiz"][quote:486d348460="Maxximum Attack"]Can the X-speed motor from the mini-z fit the X-mod, seeing that they are the same scale and all?[/quote:486d348460]\r\n\r\nI took a look at one of them today and it looks like with a touch of resoldering (the xmods motor connector), Yes the xmods will take it, or should be able to. I still don\'t know what purpose the caps on the xmod motor have.[/quote:486d348460]\r\n\r\nIf you do give us a report.   The Caps are required in all RC cars motors to reduce RF interferance.  Don\'t want you car acting up once you run the motor do you?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29626, '72bb9ea8ed', '', 'That is one cool car.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29627, 'bb21f98c92', '', '[quote:bb21f98c92="CaboWabo"][quote:bb21f98c92="crazydave"]Very nice Bilbo. I freakin\' love that color. Very similar to Sea Foam Green, like you\'d see on an old Nomad, or \'Vette.[/quote:bb21f98c92]first off - Bilbo you\'ve done a fine job...\r\njust as with all the contestants to date\r\n\r\nnow\r\ndude, that\'s it.\r\nI\'m re-doing a sea-foam green something.\r\nthe very first bit I ever painted, my whole goal was to put in a sea-foam green design to the metallic green I had used for the base (payaso\'s got my back here, I was doing it at his pad) and I fudged up. it was my first bit paint job so kind of expected.\r\nhowever, I know what I\'m doing now and I\'ve still always had this thing in the back of my head that told me to do it again and do it right.\r\nwell crazydave, you just inspired me.\r\nI haven\'t had the desire to paint, nor have I painted, for almost a month...\r\nnot anymore.\r\nsomething sea-foam green (shade TBD = To Be Determined) coming from me in the near future.[/quote:bb21f98c92]Alright well since I got my first bit, I\'ve been planning a sea foam green something. The only sea foam green I can find is high-temp engine enamel, but it is the Chevy version. Been scared to try it, but that\'s it, I\'m trying it, and my next entry [i:bb21f98c92]will[/i:bb21f98c92] be sea foam green.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29629, 'f075910608', 'Bad Xmods reviews here', 'Please put any problems or discrepancies with your xmods here. I don\'t have one yet but am getting one. \r\nThats the first of what I hope to be very [u:f075910608]few[/u:f075910608] but please be honest.\r\n\r\nThanx guys');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29631, 'de428f20a2', '', 'Thanks fellas...I am honored to be here....now kiss my ass!!  :lol: \r\n\r\nI\'ve been away for awhile...almost ended up on the MIA list like Kwikk....adjusting to this day schedule at work has been shitty....but I am now well adjusted :-D \r\n...and I\'m at work...so even better....I\'m getting paid to pimp......... 8-) \r\n\r\nThanks guys.....and don\'t forget to [b:de428f20a2]Say Word![/b:de428f20a2]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29632, '7d9a739db1', '', 'Oddly enough, hue35 is a bass player, but I think he went to college on a music scholarship earned on a trumpet. I\'ve never really heard him play the horn much, but you can see how he\'d be good on account of that purdy mouth. :P \r\n\r\nMe, I\'m just a hack rhythm guitar player with a greasy wah pedal, and play a little shaker. I\'m getting pretty good on the turntable, though. Hue and I played in a circus of a band that had drums, bass, 2 guitars, trumpet, sax, and a "frontman" (none of them truly qualified as a "singer"). :cool:  \r\n\r\n :rockon:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29633, '7bd3dc15f8', '', '[quote:7bd3dc15f8="crazydave"]\r\n\r\nI think the problem is too many people are afraid of leaving a negative feedback over a small purchase like diet pills, or a cheap clone car, and risk the seller leaving them negative feedback, to get back at them.[/quote:7bd3dc15f8]\r\n\r\n  I agree but as a seller and buyer I have had very few problems.  If I sell something and the person doesn\'t pay I just go through the steps and fill out a nonpaying bidder form, after 3 they are kicked off.  As a buyer I have yet to not get a product or my money back for a product(knock  on wood).  There are alot of dead beats on ebay though so I see your point for sure.  And as for negative feedback if I leave feedback for someone and they leave negative to get back I will respond with a link to my comment and the date it was left.  Plus if someone leaves you feedback that offends you contact ebay they will remove it:)\r\n\r\n  Can please everyone so a few negs is fine by me :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29630, '3bb91471aa', '', '[img:3bb91471aa]http://www.lemsko.de/hinten.jpg[/img:3bb91471aa]\r\n\r\nthat was done in max?? or maya or whatever?\r\n\r\nthat dude is ill. i have a few friends who do this stuff for a job. not designing cars but architectural renderings. he musta spent weeks on that shit.\r\n\r\nive been playing some wolfenstein enemy territory lately. its free to play online and is kinda like counterstrike but its a better engine and its allies vs nazis. i still love some warcraft3 frozen throne tho.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29634, 'ae05387a72', '', 'just got home from NYC. launch event was pretty awesome. if anyone went, they showed off this awesome foam track that has potential to be sold on-line only.  i was a bit disappointed with the track. the company who was hired to do the track setup and girls of xmods did a really crappy job. track one was down for a couple hours because they used some weird tubing crap for the barriers and it wouldnt stay in place. i would have liked to see a bit more challenge. i won all 5 of my races but im not elligable to go on to the semifinals and stuff cuz i was workin and stuff. overall it was pretty kewl, the cars were great, lots of give aways, and a pretty good turn out.\r\n\r\n[quote:ae05387a72]Alright, im just plain out PISSED! The Savior* Inside has been mouthing off on how SHITTY the quality is on the MINI-Z, and I have to TOTALLY disagree. If there quality is shit, then why dosen\'t the whole world buy x-mods instead of those "shit" quality mini-z\'s? DID you notice that Tiny had a and still does have a WHOLE SITE just for the light of mini-z\'s? Are you kidding me that these are shit quality? Man you must be paied by RS to mouth off like that. Geesh, im out. and PEACE... \r\n[/quote:ae05387a72]\r\n\r\nmini-z is overpriced, scarcely available, delicate, touchy... howd ya get shitty from that?  :lol:  :-) \r\nlol they can be fun at times... these times just happen to coinside with when your wallet is empty.  and btw, a large majority of people who do rc WILL buy xmods instead of "those shit quality mini-z\'s"');
