INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29766, '790eeb7817', 'My X-Mod review...', 'I went to the RS here at the mall to get my new X-Mod, and I was looking at it in the box, when I noticed the same one already put together..\r\n\r\nI asked the guy if I could check that one out, and he said sure...\r\n\r\nIt was fully charged, so I took it for a spin in the store..\r\n\r\nMy first impressions are what a piece of SHIT..  Not trying to offend anybody that likes em, but for me, I just think they\'re a big dookie piece of doo doo..  I don\'t really drive on flat surfaces though, and  these things seem like they\'re more set up to race on a super flat shit..  And if you jumped it, you probably break some shit..\r\n\r\nI had to cut the guy off in his little sales pitch, and tell him my 1/64 car would whip this things ass up, and down...  (I actually used those words)\r\n\r\nHe just snickered, and said really?\r\n\r\nLike I said before. I\'m not trying to offend anyone with these, but I\'ll be sticking with my bits..  They\'re just not my cup of tea.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29767, '6f7c78aa3d', '', 'ya i wana drive a demo before i drop 50bucks. too bad none of the radiosnacks around here have em yet and too bad im broke as hell.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29768, '90dd423f57', '', 'what do ya mean? besides their sales pitch.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29769, '6697f749f7', '', '[quote:6697f749f7="hogjowlz"]what do ya mean? besides their sales pitch.[/quote:6697f749f7]\r\n\r\n  I amnot sure what it is torque or what not but in a normal 2 speed the car will run like  3.0 or bettter on low speed then make a big difference on high speed.\r\n\r\n\r\nWiththe king or elvis I find teh low speed moves like a 1.0 or 2.0 at most.\r\n\r\n  Then is a fetted car they both work well but with the pro I find the car will outrace a non fet on low speed were the king has trouble keeping up on low.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29770, '7fd00355aa', '', '[quote:7fd00355aa="hogjowlz"]all i got is the 4.2 elvis. how does the pro compare?[/quote:7fd00355aa]\r\n\r\nThe one with the blue end bell is nothing special.. I tested it in a 2 speed car, but the one with the E on it rocks the house.. Also tested in a 2 speed car.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29771, 'bb7e8ee910', '', '[quote:bb7e8ee910="payaso"][quote:bb7e8ee910="hogjowlz"]all i got is the 4.2 elvis. how does the pro compare?[/quote:bb7e8ee910]\r\n\r\nThe one with the blue end bell is nothing special.. I tested it in a 2 speed car, but the one with the E on it rocks the house.. Also tested in a 2 speed car.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:bb7e8ee910]\r\n\r\n  I do like the white one better :) can\'t wait till the SE can pull it');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29772, 'b5adbc79d3', '', 'Don\'t get me wrong, I\'m no big advocate, BUT you gotta be fair with this shit...You were probably running the car on carpet at RS right? XMods have like ZERO ground clearance so running on anything other than HARD, SMOOTH surfaces is gonna drag these shits down.\r\n\r\nThe other thing is you probably tested a stock setup, which has 8-tooth gearing and a 26k motor...Which means it needs ROOM to get up to speed, something else a RadioShack store lacks.\r\n\r\nI ain\'t trying to shoot you down my nubian sister, just saying you gotta even the playing field and then make the decision or comparison.\r\n\r\n...Myself, now I\'m thinking about getting the AWD and Stage-2 motor kits to see just how much more badass I can get this thing...But doing so might bring me closer to KEEPING the goddamned thing! I might just say F-it and pack the shit up and bring it back before I get hooked.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29777, 'b6d7951a2a', '', 'lmao\r\nthis reminding me of the south park episode with "mr. slave"\r\n\r\nIf nobody else has a problem with it, I think I\'ll just leave it as it is now.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29773, 'a16e506b05', '', 'Are you using it in a 2 speed chassis?   TE says these things work better in a 1 speed chassis.. Not for me.\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29774, '816472db02', '', 'I could see how one might get that impression. I do think that these things aren\'t that unlike bits in that the driving surface/area is pretty important. After having an XMod for a couple days, I really like it, but I won\'t be leaving my Bits anytime soon. They do suck down the batteries, and it will cost around $130-$150 to trick out an Xmod to my liking, but the racing is pretty intense, and I think they\'re built like a tank for $50.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29775, '10dae58749', '', '[quote:10dae58749="payaso"]Are you using it in a 2 speed chassis?   TE says these things work better in a 1 speed chassis.. Not for me.\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:10dae58749]\r\n\r\nThe ones I am using are all in fetted cars the other ones just sittin there in  there boxes (or in the mail to you).\r\n\r\n  my non fetted cars dont get much play these days unless I am on a tech track but then I use the TC pink motor :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29776, '625c1dba26', '', '[quote:625c1dba26="Namuna"]\r\nI ain\'t trying to shoot you down my nubian sister, just saying you gotta even the playing field and then make the decision or comparison..[/quote:625c1dba26]\r\n\r\n\r\nLMAO... I hear ya bro... The performance wasn\'t that bad for me, and yep it was on carpet, but that\'s where I do my racing, so I needed to test it there as well.. What gets me is the car itself. It just looks like it\'s limited on its abilities. ie. rough terrain, jumping.. Things like that are more suited for me...\r\n\r\nMy bit with alloys will run on thick carpet (not burbur) and plow over speaker wires, pencils, pens, and cigarette lighters.. It\'s like a little tank..\r\n\r\n\r\nI guess size has alot to do with it too. I\'m a true micro fan, and the size of the X-Mods are just out of the size range for me too.. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe car would be fun to drive in a huge open area if that\'s what you\'re into.\r\n\r\nI need to get off my lazy ass a show a vid clip of what my bit can do..\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29778, 'aa2a6577b6', '', '[quote:aa2a6577b6="payaso"][quote:aa2a6577b6="Namuna"]\r\nI ain\'t trying to shoot you down my nubian sister, just saying you gotta even the playing field and then make the decision or comparison..[/quote:aa2a6577b6]\r\n\r\n\r\nLMAO... I hear ya bro... The performance wasn\'t that bad for me, and yep it was on carpet, but that\'s where I do my racing, so I needed to test it there as well.. What gets me is the car itself. It just looks like it\'s limited on its abilities. ie. rough terrain, jumping.. Things like that are more suited for me...\r\n\r\nMy bit with alloys will run on thick carpet (not burbur) and plow over speaker wires, pencils, pens, and cigarette lighters.. It\'s like a little tank..\r\n\r\n\r\nI guess size has alot to do with it too. I\'m a true micro fan, and the size of the X-Mods are just out of the size range for me too.. \r\n\r\n\r\nThe car would be fun to drive in a huge open area if that\'s what you\'re into.\r\n\r\nI need to get off my lazy ass a show a vid clip of what my bit can do..\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:aa2a6577b6]\r\n\r\n  I agree with the whoe size thing, my mini z has not been out in forever(couldn\'t even tell you what box its packed in). and its easyer to race in the living room with 5 buddies and some beer :)\r\n\r\n  I would though get an xmod only cause the price and thre is a track at the mall that I go to once a month.\r\n\r\n  I also picked up an epoch indoor racer so we will see what that is like when it comes in.\r\n\r\n  But all in all Size is big factor in the matter.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29779, '0c1a731329', '', 'Yup, I\'m living in a goddamned box myself, I gotta fricken sit side-saddle to take a shit in our guest bathroom (I mean that literally) that\'s how small a Condo we got. \r\n\r\nSo the Mini-Zs and Overland I got are doing a great job of taking up space...So now, with this thread, my pratical side calls and I\'ll be bringing the X back this week.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29780, '5998e5d85c', '', 'whats funny is now that the SE\'s can be fetted to 8.5 mph, by comparison, it kicks the shit out of the x-mod as far as what I\'m reading.\r\nthat, the scale and price difference are enough for me to stay away.\r\n\r\nthere\'s a laundry list of pro\'s and con\'s on every car, guess it just matters how those weigh out for your personal preference.\r\n\r\nnow that it seems decided you need extremely flat and smooth surface for the x-mod, to you owners out there, what kind of room do you recommend for these things? do you need a rather large area?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29781, 'b538ad0d8a', '', '[quote:b538ad0d8a="hogjowlz"]ya im sure he could still make $$ even after unveiling plans. someone could pay for it and then distribute?? haha you know that wont be me. i personally think its silly but then again he did take his skills(assumable he paid a lot to goto school to learn them) and his time and resources to do this so you cant totally bag him for it but ya not spreading the wealth to those who could do it themselves is kinda crappy.[/quote:b538ad0d8a]\r\n\r\n\r\nI agree with that one hog..  Maybe we can talk Micro Amps into sharing some info with us, and our members..\r\n\r\nHe\'s not a company, but a private seller, so we can\'t say he\'s self promoting his shit, cause he\'s following the rules....\r\n\r\nBut on the other side of the coin. Why would you advertise in a forum where people are mad at you?\r\n\r\nIf he\'s a true salesman, he\'ll see his errors, and make it right... I think that he feels like he worked hard to find a solution for the problem, and doesn\'t wanna give it up too soon.. (understandable)   \r\n\r\nLets compose a letter to him... What cha think?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29782, '932556bc6f', '', 'go for it, whatever we agree upon I\'m cool with.\r\n\r\nI\'m not certain yet how we\'d approach it in the letter without coming off like "hey man, don\'t be a dick" ya know?\r\nso if ya gots some ideas, toss em out in the ring and well hammer out details till we\'re done.');
