INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (29998, '5e98b57900', '', '[quote:5e98b57900="crazydave"][quote:5e98b57900="bdebde"][quote:5e98b57900="DarkTari"]I gotta go wit Black!  Don\'t see any real cars w/anything but.\r\n[/quote:5e98b57900]\r\n\r\n[b:5e98b57900]I\'m not so sure about that. Last time I bought tires for one of my full size cars, I almost bought some that had a blue stripe tread pattern. They come in several colors, I think they are made by BF Goodrich (TA\'s). Of course that was just in the tread.[/b:5e98b57900]\r\n\r\nThanks for the comments pimps.\r\n\r\nOh, looks like it is still a toss up on color according to the poll.\r\n\r\n*edit* you don\'t like those rims DT?[/quote:5e98b57900]You could simulate that effect by cutting the tires in half, and super glueing them back together, but with 2 different colors. \r\n\r\nSuper glue bonds soft rubber excellently. The 1/10 scale buggy guys take truck tires, cut them down to make extra wide buggy tires, and they use super glue. You just have to sand the extra glue off, so the surface is smooth. I\'ve tried it to make extra wide tires for my alloys.[/quote:5e98b57900]\r\n\r\nOr you could sniff the glue and they might look whatever color you want!\r\n\r\nMy question would be: is that car a looker or a driver? If it\'s a looker, the black looks best. If it\'s a driver, whatever handles best.');
