INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30021, 'eb7c06d6e7', '', 'Well, I figured out the hard way that Xmods are not meant for outside use.  I had just assembled everything and I was testing it out in front of my condo.  The driveway is concrete so it\'s not rough terrain, but there are a few concrete joints.  I looked over the area first to make sure there wasn\'t any obstructions.  To make a long story short, I hit a rock about 1/4" in diameter.  If the tire had hit it, no problem.  If you examine the bottom of the Xmods, you will see a screw that attaches to shocks/wheel knuckle.  There is very little clearance between the bottom of this screw and the ground.  I happened to hit rock with the screw and it cracked the screw right off along with a small piece of the knuckle.  Fortunately, I had the AWD kit and I replaced the broken knuckle with the upgrade.  You have to be very careful and I found out the hard way.');
