INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30043, 'f734e2e287', '', '[quote:f734e2e287="Grunge"]Well, I figured out the hard way that Xmods are not meant for outside use.  I had just assembled everything and I was testing it out in front of my condo.  The driveway is concrete so it\'s not rough terrain, but there are a few concrete joints.  I looked over the area first to make sure there wasn\'t any obstructions.  To make a long story short, I hit a rock about 1/4" in diameter.  If the tire had hit it, no problem.  If you examine the bottom of the Xmods, you will see a screw that attaches to shocks/wheel knuckle.  There is very little clearance between the bottom of this screw and the ground.  I happened to hit rock with the screw and it cracked the screw right off along with a small piece of the knuckle.  Fortunately, I had the AWD kit and I replaced the broken knuckle with the upgrade.  You have to be very careful and I found out the hard way.[/quote:f734e2e287]\r\n\r\n\r\nI was afraid something like that might happen..  Anyway to raise them up a hair?\r\n\r\nThat sucks man.\r\n\r\nWhen you get a chance, you should come down, and race that thing in my tennis courts... I\'d like to see what it can do against my bits, and SEs.\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30044, '2d3c287fc4', '', '[quote:2d3c287fc4="Micro s2000"]i charge mine when i notice its not going full speed. it charges fast and i can race my xmod almost constantly with it.[/quote:2d3c287fc4]\r\n\r\nAlmost constantly? I doubt that, unless you have at least four sets of batteries... eventually you\'ll have to wait for the batteries to charge. 2-hour charge and 30-minute run time... even with two sets of batteries you\'ll run out of juice in an hour and wait another hour for the first set to recharge. Personally, the charge time was almost a deal breaker for me... getting the run time longer than the charge time changes everything.');
