INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30214, '29c2394c93', '', 'hog, if you get the ballbearing upgrade, the stage 2 motors and NiMH batteries (they work WAY better than alkalines), I think it will be plenty fast for you. It looks like it would be around 300 scale mph.\r\n\r\nThe stock motor is about like a 2.2 with blue gears on a bit.\r\n\r\n\r\nVDM-\r\nWe\'ll take some pictures maybe this weekend. The way we race, we basically just set up a track interior and no outer walls, kinda like how airplanes race. So if you want to go full out, you can take a larger line, or you can slow down for the corners and take it tight. Oddly enough, you can make it around the track just as quick either way.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30215, '83f0142f37', '', '[quote:83f0142f37="TheSavior*Insider"]my pics at that pic gallery of the xmods launch[/quote:83f0142f37]\r\n\r\nwell there are lots of pics in that gallery could you be more specific? post the link to that pic then :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30216, '34891f45c8', '', 'besides cost how would they be better? 4 alkalines are 6v. nimh are only 4.8v');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30217, 'fcad6af2c9', '', 'VDM, we don\'t have a "track" for the xmods yet, but a great space (SuperFly\'s office). For now we just set up phone books and 5gal. water bottles as a track. In my living room we use ZipZap barrier on the hard wood floor for a bit track.\r\n\r\nhog, for starters, rechargeable batteries make a pretty big difference in speed. The stage 2 motor with speed gears makes this thing haul ass. I\'m still surprised at the performance. Almost too fast for my current driving ability... that will change.\r\n\r\nedit: uh, ya.. what Supey said... sorry for the doubled info. Good thing we keep our "stories" straight.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30218, '7f96dcbcf3', '', 'I think it has something to do with ability to maintain steady voltage while under load. I think alkalines dip rather quickly compared to NiMH. I\'m talking out of my ass though, some scientist will have to explain it. They just perform way better.');
