INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30279, '6f087fc1a7', 'Video Editing', 'Hey fellas.   As you all know I like to make videos of this sickness as do many others.  We have seen great videos from Cabo, Crazy, Nox, Voodoo and many other pimps out there and I thought that we could probably learn from each other.\r\n\r\nSo, what hardware/software do you guys use?  What process do you go though?  What\'s your compression of choice? (to quote Yul Bruner from The King and I), etc,etc,etc......\r\n\r\n[b:6f087fc1a7]My Setup[/b:6f087fc1a7]\r\n\r\nI\'m an analogue man so I gots me a standard hi-8 analoge video camera but it has digital processing on it.   It was a good price at the time when DV was just hitting the market and I\'m still very happy with it.   \'Cause it\'s analogue I have a video capture card called the FlyVideo98SE.  I use the composite video-in for the PAL signal and the line-in on my AWE64 soundcard.\r\n\r\nI\'m on XP and I\'m a WDM man so I use FlyDS to capture.   Unlike the DV format (through the firewire interface) with analogue is all about the framerate and not dropping any frames.   So far I can achieve the capture in the following settings:\r\n\r\nCodec: HuffyUV (the best lossless cap codec)\r\nPAL 768 * 576 @ 25fps\r\n24 bit colour depth\r\n\r\nFor this I have an Athlon 1600XP and my capture drive is a RAID stripe combo of 2*60GB Seagate Barracuda\'s.  The RAID stripe gives me the speed to capture such high bandwidth video.  With the specs above it\'s grabs approx 70-80MB a second.  A 1 minute video in RAW format is about 600MB, fucken huge!\r\n\r\nI then use a combo of software to massage the video stream and filter/clean it up.  The best for this \'cause I\'m a bloody puritan is AviSynth.  It\'s like C++ for AVI files and with it I do funky shit like de-interlacing, bicubic resizes and temporal smoothing (sounds and looks cool, lol).\r\n\r\nI then use the best program in the world [b:6f087fc1a7]VirtualDub[/b:6f087fc1a7] to edit the video and compress to the end presentation codec.  I also use it the mux in the audio track that I\'ve prepared from an external source (usually a combo of [b:6f087fc1a7]Cool Edit Pro and BeSweet[/b:6f087fc1a7]).\r\n\r\nIt sounds like a lot of fucking around and it is!  But hey, that\'s half the fun.\r\n\r\nMy main codec of choice for these videos is DivX.  It like it\'s interface and the ability to do multipass encoding (this way you get the smallest size vs. best quality).  But  the windows media 9 is pretty cool as well.  The only gripe I have is that the interface (Windows Media Encoder) is still buggy and has issues interfacing with frame-serving programs (like avisynth).  Then again it\'s all about the target, who and what are you trying to reach.  I mean, hell if I wanted to view this shit on my TV (cause I sick enough to think it might be cool, lol) I would encode to SVCD format as MPEG2 and burn it to CD and watch it on my DVD player.  So really there is no "best codec".\r\n\r\nSorry, this has ended up a long (and probably confusing) thread....\r\n\r\nend rant....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
