INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30287, 'f5466d0ebe', '', 'lol drunk with the eyes shut, only way to drive\r\n\r\nI was actually trying to capture the rinky dink power-slides I was getting outta the se, but they didn\'t really show.\r\n\r\nor, my "artsy" explination...\r\n\r\nI was trying to use symbolism to express and document the struggles of an se living in a black and white world with no emotion and clearly defined social structures while maintaining its proportional outlook on the races that make up it\'s micro world.\r\n\r\n"they\'re coming to take me away haha hoho hehe - to the funny farm where life is good..."');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30288, 'd1ef7381a6', '', 'I take digital clips.\r\nTransfer to the computer and pick my clips I\'m going to be using.\r\nI import those clips into Adobe Premiere.\r\nThat\'s where I do all the video editing.\r\nI use SoundForge to edit soundtracks if needed.\r\nOnce everything is pieced together in Premiere, I either use an existing "export" profile or create my own.\r\n\r\nI can\'t express enough how much Adobe Premiere is the defacto standard for editing movies. The options you have are near limitless. Compression profiles out that wahzoo, filters, etc., etc.\r\nSoundForge is the same for audio that Premiere is for video, probably the leading audio editing software on the market. it too offers all sorts of cool bells and whistles, zoom in to the thousands of a second, etc., etc.\r\n\r\nThe compression I typically use:\r\n2 streams (audio &amp; video)\r\nAudio: 16 Kbps, Windows media 8 codec, mono 16.0 khz\r\nVideo: 80 Kbps, Windows media 7 codec, 15 fps, 8 secs. / key\r\n\r\nthat seems to work best for me when I\'m aiming to stream to a broadband audience\r\n\r\nif you had access to a windows media server, I would suggest streaming using a VBR so you can stream to multiple audiences with multiple streams using multiple compressions. so if you\'re on dial-up, you\'ll get a more compressed version than if you were on cable.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30289, '0e779a220c', '', 'brendan, the converter you use prolly doesn\'t set the compression at a good level.  I use virtualdub, it can be found here:  http://www.virtualdub.org/ \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30290, 'bd6b382427', '', '[quote:bd6b382427="CaboWabo"][quote:bd6b382427="crazydave"]Damn, 40 watts, that is dim. I\'ve been buying 75 watt bulbs so I can see what the hell I\'m doing, and it\'s still pretty dark in our place.\r\n\r\nLol @ Cabo. Maybe instead of the "Fuck You" I could just settle for one of them Yosemite Sam stickers that say "Back Off"?[/quote:bd6b382427]oh yea, you got a kid, guess ya can\'t be driving the "FU" car around the house and have him growing up like cartman lol\r\n\r\nmaybe yosemite sam can flip the bird? lol[/quote:bd6b382427]You know, actually I wasn\'t thinkin\' of the kid, he\'s already a little cornholio. I was just getting in the spirit of the 70s and trying to think of a bumper sticker that might actually have been seen on this car, but now in retrospect, I  realize that was pretty lame, and I pussed out.\r\n\r\nYes, definately Yosemite Sam is is flipping the bird, and instead of "Back Off" it would have to be, "Fuck Off".\r\n\r\nOk, gots the plan, now I need decal paper.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30291, 'c1b4b1ce77', '', '[quote:c1b4b1ce77="CaboWabo"]I take digital clips.\r\nTransfer to the computer and pick my clips I\'m going to be using.\r\nI import those clips into Adobe Premiere.\r\nThat\'s where I do all the video editing.\r\nI use SoundForge to edit soundtracks if needed.\r\nOnce everything is pieced together in Premiere, I either use an existing "export" profile or create my own.\r\n\r\nI can\'t express enough how much Adobe Premiere is the defacto standard for editing movies. The options you have are near limitless. Compression profiles out that wahzoo, filters, etc., etc.\r\nSoundForge is the same for audio that Premiere is for video, probably the leading audio editing software on the market. it too offers all sorts of cool bells and whistles, zoom in to the thousands of a second, etc., etc.\r\n\r\nThe compression I typically use:\r\n2 streams (audio &amp; video)\r\nAudio: 16 Kbps, Windows media 8 codec, mono 16.0 khz\r\nVideo: 80 Kbps, Windows media 7 codec, 15 fps, 8 secs. / key\r\n\r\nthat seems to work best for me when I\'m aiming to stream to a broadband audience\r\n\r\nif you had access to a windows media server, I would suggest streaming using a VBR so you can stream to multiple audiences with multiple streams using multiple compressions. so if you\'re on dial-up, you\'ll get a more compressed version than if you were on cable.[/quote:c1b4b1ce77]\r\n\r\nSome interesting points there man.  I hear where you are coming from with premiere, I just gotta get my hands on a copy ($$$).   I learnt my tools from doing dvd rips before a lot of script-kiddie tools flooded the market.\r\n\r\nIf you\'re gonna use WMV format you might as well goto version 9 and reap the advantages of that release of the codec.   I say this because even if users don\'t have the v9 codec, because it\'s wmplayer it will d/l that codec anyways.   This has always been good thing of WMV .vs different container formats like MPEG and AVI.  The user is online to d/l your movie so hey, that can then d/l the codec and swear at freakin MS, lol.\r\n\r\nMy only suggestion is up your frame rate to 24fps (NTSC source) or 25fps (PAL source), this will increase the quality of the video and considering that "action orientated" style most BitChar-G videos are I believe it\'s suitable.  With v9 of WMV codec use the VBR mode and set a max video stream bitrate, the compression will take a while but you\'ll get great results.   Also, do keyframes every second, for action this is a must.  Otherwise get a "scene-change aware" codec like Divx/Xvid that will insert a keyframe at every scene change independent of the keyframe rate.\r\n\r\nThe media servers are cool.  I\'ve been testing live video feeds (looking at a home-grown security system at home) using the hookup explained earlier into WMC or WMS.  It\'s amazing what you can do these days.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30292, 'd43ceae23c', '', 'excellent input.\r\nI can\'t bump up the rate with most of my clips, the "Big Pimpin Broadband" video I did had a higher frame rate because it was taken with a better camera. If I bump up the rate with clips taken with my digital camera, the video gets choppy because of the frame rate from the camera.\r\n\r\nPremiere doesn\'t garuntee you a WMV format, you can AVI, MPEG, MOV, and all other video formats.\r\nI choose not to use the 9 codec because when it was first release (6 months now maybe?) it was still very buggy with poor streams, which I\'m guessing is probably fixed by now. I do need to get the new profile.\r\n\r\nman I wish we could all get together and do some filmin, with everyones skills and know-how, it\'d stomp the matrix lol');
