INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30450, 'c0032fb60e', '', '[quote:c0032fb60e="sessiz"]Do the xmod rubbers fit well on them rims? :???:[/quote:c0032fb60e]\r\nYes, the rubber is interchangable, but the only difference is the Xmod wheels have the center ridge and the XS wheels don\'t. The next time I do this mod, I\'ll take pics and do a tutorial on how I cut the D holes out.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30451, '9f69e8ca17', '', '[quote:9f69e8ca17="SuperFly"]Very nice! Just super clean and, well, perfect. DarkTari, your cars never have even a hint that something you were trying to do didn\'t work out as planned.\r\n\r\n :eek:[/quote:9f69e8ca17]\r\nThanx SuperFly, that\'s very high praise and I appreciate it!\r\n\r\n[quote:9f69e8ca17]What\'s the brand and where did you get it. I was thinking something simular for my new truck. Metallic but not that shade of green (since you used the color already.) [/quote:9f69e8ca17] \r\n\r\nBilbo,\r\n\r\nLike I said earlier, I like Duplicolor Auto Paint best!  It\'s cheaper than Testors, Pactra, Tomika, etc.  and the colors are endless.  Check your local auto store, Wal-Mart, K-Mart, Target, etc.  This paint dries in less than 5 minutes w/adjustable nozzle.  I suggest getting a spray can handle from your local hardware store, makes painting easier than shooting a pistol!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30452, '78e4d83011', '', 'I didn\'t think I\'d like a "SeaFoam" color on a Bit but as usual, you changed my mind, very nice Pimp.\r\nThe only detail I see that you missed is if you didn\'t want the door handle body colored but they look dope just like they are!\r\nDamn you can lay some paint Cabo !\r\nCan you lay your women like that ?????? lol !');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30453, 'cd7d9da29f', '', 'thanks guys :-) \r\nI\'m not disappointed as much as I\'ve been before, by no means.\r\n\r\nwell, I was gonna paint the middle strip on the back left and right tail light lens amber to be a blinker, but I got lazy.\r\nI was also planning on painting the molding around the exhaust black, but then I decided it was too much with the windows.\r\n\r\nthese bodies wouldn\'t be bad at all if the molding on the front headlights was better, on the passenger side, the blinker sits way crooked, they need to make the mold better. actually all the lights up front suck as far as the molding goes.\r\nI love the hoods on these bodies though, nice sweeping hood with some great lines, alot like the gloria\'s hood but the accords hood slopes down more sport-like.\r\n\r\nthe wife likes how I drive too :lol: \r\n\r\nthanks for compliments pimps');
