INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30692, '0f2ad6cd0d', '', 'I read a few of his posts and he seems to offer experienced advice on things he\'s sure about that obviously has to do with his business which is good though he seem to be a bit bias towards the merchandise that he offers even thought I haven\'t visited his site.  Some posts that have been answered thoroughly, he seems to put in his 2 cents even though he\'s just repeating what was already said.  He seems to have good intentions, he does list his website so that\'s no secret. If it\'s any good, maybe we can work a BitPimp % price cut for advertising.  ?????');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30693, '30de5b799f', '', 'It\'s Finished, YEAH\r\n\r\nProject: Happy Hauler\r\nBody: Nakamichi Racer Truck\r\nChassis: Precious\r\n\r\nModifications\r\nBody: Cut off rear cap and put on bed cover. Added Rails over bed. Hidden rear slot that lowered the rear. Cut front mount to lower front end. Dupilcolor Twilight Blue (Metallic) Paint.\r\nChassis: Cat 5 Antenna\r\n\r\n[img:30de5b799f]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Haulerb.jpg[/img:30de5b799f]\r\n[img:30de5b799f]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Hauler4.jpg[/img:30de5b799f]\r\n[img:30de5b799f]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Hauler5.jpg[/img:30de5b799f]\r\n[img:30de5b799f]http://www.rcpics.net/media/Hauler6.jpg[/img:30de5b799f]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30694, 'bacb048f3d', '', '[quote:bacb048f3d="barto_85"]I disagree, I always race anti clockwise.  At least in Australia, I know Bathurst (v8\'s) and the Gold Coast (indy &amp; v8\'s) are both anti clockwise.  [b:bacb048f3d]And I thought the oval races in the U.S. in the indy series are usually anti clockwise[/b:bacb048f3d]???[/quote:bacb048f3d]\r\n\r\n[b:bacb048f3d]They do![/b:bacb048f3d]\r\n\r\nI don\'t race on a track either, guess cause I don\'t have one yet.  Got the material, just not the time or space so I\'m like hog, I run al over da place.\r\nFriday I was pickin my son up from Karate, in this mall that has only a few stores left open so I took my Office Carpet Runner (Cloudy, Z-Car) and ran that sucker balls out.  Man talking about fun, that KITT 2.6 definately runs like a 3.2 or better!  Basically no obsticle limits, only range. Flat out running for as far as your range allows (mine was over 50\') !!  Only the floors are kinda dirty, not dust bunnies, just shoe dust which make the tyres dirty quick which makes turning a bitch, especially with a high torque rotor!  A couple of passer by\'s thought the cars were too cool.  I bet if I ran there every Friday, I could get a following and get some races together for Friday evenings, maybe even get the LHS (5mi away) to get involved.  We\'ll see !!!\r\n\r\nWell I just jumped off my soapbox.........\r\n\r\nOut!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30695, '462f31ed8e', 'Getting someone\'s driving record?', 'Pardon me if I\'m overstepping boundaries by asking this question but...How does one go about getting a person\'s driving record? \r\n\r\nI\'m fairly sure it\'s not going to happen over the net, at least not for free.\r\n\r\nAny thoughts?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37203, 'e15284bc41', '', '"As Seen On TV" has a store at a mall near me.  They had a shelf full of bubble cars, some of them were broke, still sealed, but fallin\' apart, like bodies fallin\' off, and the guts spilled in the bubble.  So, I offered the the guy there $3 a peice for the broken ones, and he took it.  I bought 3 or 4 that day and then went back a day or two later and offered $2 to a different guy, and he took it, I bought 3 more.  They turned out to be Bensu brand.  Not bad parts and expeirmental cars to use.  Now their all out of busted ones and they sell for $9.99, thats too much for that junk.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30701, 'f0001b12db', '', '[quote:f0001b12db="CaboWabo"]now that\'s tight, great job bilbo\r\nwhat color is that? looks like a charcoal blue - I dig it.[/quote:f0001b12db]\r\n\r\nI used Duplicolor Twilight Blue (Metallic) number DSCC 353. I listened to DT and went to Auto Zone and picked up a can of it. It was a choice between this and Garnet for the truck, I liked this a little better for this project. The clear coat was done with Krylon Crystal Clear Acrylic (my personal favorite for clear) and the details were done with Citadel paints.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30702, '66060416d8', '', 'Thanks for the comps guys, and Superfly, it\'s funny you\'ve said that a few of my recent cars were you\'re favorite to date. I must be working in your direction, but it makes me wonder, "What could I possibly come up with that would be Supefly\'s next favorite?"  :lol: \r\n\r\n@Payaso, here ya go man.\r\n[img:66060416d8]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/cosmo3.jpg[/img:66060416d8]\r\n\r\nIt was supposed to have gold rims, that\'s one place where I went astray. It was also supposed to be a convertible, that\'s the other place I went astray.\r\n\r\nNow after putting it on this chassis I kinda wish I went with my original plan, but oh well, it looks cool. No use being hung up on the woulda, coulda, shoulda\'s.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30703, 'fbc6983cd6', '', '[quote:fbc6983cd6="CaboWabo"]looks great man, you chose a classic color too.[/quote:fbc6983cd6]You know what\'s funny about that? I\'ve been using the same can of red for the last 4-5 months, I just use different color base coats to change it\'s shade. I had been using gold under it, but this time I went with the white primer to give it a brighter sportier look.\r\n\r\nThis car was the end of that can, I barely sputtered out 2 coats.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30704, '9b91af4607', '', '[quote:9b91af4607="DarkTari"][quote:9b91af4607="barto_85"]I disagree, I always race anti clockwise.  At least in Australia, I know Bathurst (v8\'s) and the Gold Coast (indy &amp; v8\'s) are both anti clockwise.  [b:9b91af4607]And I thought the oval races in the U.S. in the indy series are usually anti clockwise[/b:9b91af4607]???[/quote:9b91af4607]\r\n\r\n[b:9b91af4607]They do![/b:9b91af4607]\r\n\r\nI don\'t race on a track either, guess cause I don\'t have one yet.  Got the material, just not the time or space so I\'m like hog, I run al over da place.\r\nFriday I was pickin my son up from Karate, in this mall that has only a few stores left open so I took my Office Carpet Runner (Cloudy, Z-Car) and ran that sucker balls out.  Man talking about fun, that KITT 2.6 definately runs like a 3.2 or better!  Basically no obsticle limits, only range. Flat out running for as far as your range allows (mine was over 50\') !!  Only the floors are kinda dirty, not dust bunnies, just shoe dust which make the tyres dirty quick which makes turning a bitch, especially with a high torque rotor!  A couple of passer by\'s thought the cars were too cool.  I bet if I ran there every Friday, I could get a following and get some races together for Friday evenings, maybe even get the LHS (5mi away) to get involved.  We\'ll see !!!\r\n\r\nWell I just jumped off my soapbox.........\r\n\r\nOut![/quote:9b91af4607]I always thought they were clockwise, \'cause you know that ol\' saying on how you race ovals, "Go fast, and turn right", or is that just dirt ovals?\r\n\r\nAnyways I usually race clockwise, but sometimes race counter-clockwise to switch it up for a challenge.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30705, 'da835aff02', '', 'hire a hacker to break into the DMV.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30706, '0a73d1eda7', '', 'I agree with Dt...his answers arn\'t bad...\r\n\r\nI\'m just make you ALL aware of him.  no harm done.\r\n\r\nhe might be a \'bennie\' to us....as DT said..\r\n\r\n-nox');
