INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30725, '1f6b01d807', '', 'Thanks Hog. You know I almost put some silver flames in my base coat, so there would be just a hint of flames showing through the red, but I decided to keep it tasteful.\r\n\r\n\r\nHere\'s the real deal...\r\n\r\n[img:1f6b01d807]http://www.s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/cosmo4.jpg[/img:1f6b01d807]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30726, '24b7022467', '', 'ya dude you dont need flames on every job you do. that thing is very tasteful.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30727, '3f7d81d4e7', '', '[quote:3f7d81d4e7="BilboBaggins"]My Krylon is Acrylic not enamel. It works on everything I\'ve tried, not a probelm yet. Now Rust-o-leum that is trouble with their clear, it eats the top coat of paint.[/quote:3f7d81d4e7]Sorry don\'t mean to correct you, but Enamel is Acrylic. Laquer can be Acrylic, or Nitro Cellulose, but Nitro is very expensive, and sprays like Duplicolor are Acrylic Laquer. \r\n\r\nThis is a guitar refinishing site, but they have great info on the paint types, http://www.reranch.com , check it out, you\'ll see I speak the truth.\r\n\r\nHey man, it\'s all cool, I was just trying to warn you, because it [i:3f7d81d4e7]is[/i:3f7d81d4e7] risky mixing brands of paint, and I really would hate to see you mess up one of your neato projects, but with good paint techique, proper surface prep anythings possible, so since you\'re doing alright I should probably shut up right about now.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30728, '5185be4b07', '', 'I think I only gave "favorite so far" props to your Porsche (or did I do that for the Beetle also?). Anyway, you just keep raising the bar. Also, I like flames as much as the next pimp, I just don\'t think they are appropriate for every body type. Your last several cars seem to have been approached like Michaelangelo with chunks of marble: that the final sculpture is already in there, you just have to chip off the extra pieces.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30729, '7dd09a521f', '', 'I normally won\'t mix brands Especially after the Rust-o-leum fiasco on a few bodies. But Krylon\'s Acrylic Crystal Clear has worked with everything I\'ve tried.\r\n\r\nI may try Futura Acrylic Floor Polish, I\'ve heard from two reliable sources (my LHS and RCmod.com) that it works very well and is self leveling so no streaks or runs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30730, 'b69bbc6851', '', '[quote:b69bbc6851="SuperFly"]I think I only gave "favorite so far" props to your Porsche (or did I do that for the Beetle also?). Anyway, you just keep raising the bar. Also, I like flames as much as the next pimp, I just don\'t think they are appropriate for every body type. Your last several cars seem to have been approached like Michaelangelo with chunks of marble: that the final sculpture is already in there, you just have to chip off the extra pieces.[/quote:b69bbc6851]I believe I got the "favorite so far" for the Porshe and the Beetle, and my stealth flamed Supra got the "favorite flames so far", but I guess that\'s a slightly different category.  :lol: \r\n\r\nBut you\'re totally right, I have been \'listening\' to the cars more, and as much as I wanted to paint it sea foam green, this little bitch just kept screaming, "I\'m a little Red sports car.", and it got to the point where it\'s like, "fine your Red now shut up."');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30731, 'e8c18ad572', '', 'I\'ve thought about trying that Future stuff too. One of them bottles would probably last forever, but I\'ve been kinda scared to, I like to play it safe, especially with the final step.\r\n\r\nLet us know how it works out if you try it.');
