INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (30931, '84f78e9dcc', '', '[quote:84f78e9dcc="oxhadokenxo"]Are the newer Zip Zaps SEs better? I\'m looking at the white RX-7 (the Savannah I think...2nd gen 1986-1992 Rx-7 anyway) but don\'t know if I want to spend $25 and then $13 for the upgrade kit when I already have a Lxx char-g with a 4.2 pro in it..does the 4.2 Pro work as good as the 34,000 RPM Zip Zap motor?  Are the newer versions (non launch...like the ones I could buy now at Radio Shack) of the Rx-7s any better than the first ones that came out?[/quote:84f78e9dcc]If your looking to get a SE, avoid the white RX-7 Savannahs. The Yellow RX-7 Enfinis are reported to be slighty improved. This Mustang I found to be an enjoyable car, but it still has the SE\'s issue with a lack of torque. Me and ph2t are trying to work out a solution to that. (micro_Amps has already figured it out) I just saw the Audi TT at Rat Shack, and it looks great, I really wish I held out for that instead of the Mustang\r\n\r\nThe 4.2 has a faster top end than the 3.4 (as evidenced by the numbers ;) ), but the 3.4 has more bottom end torque, making it better suited to the SE in it\'s current state.\r\n\r\nThe SE\'s proportional controls makes it an entirely different animal than the traditional bit. So it will not replace yor LXX, it\'ll just give you something else to play with.');
