INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31095, '66797e91c1', '', 'I\'ve now sat here and read the entire contents of this thread and I just can\'t believe what I\'ve been missing.   \r\n\r\nThe first high speed motors I got were the perfection 3.8 and then onto the 4.2 series (king and pro).  Up untill then I had mainly yellow TOMY 2.2\'s and some clone 2.3 - 2.6\'s for my bits so from that perspective the perfections kicked arse.\r\n\r\nI can get some original TOMY 3.0\'s for cheap, should I get some of these?  Are these known as the lucifer rotor?\r\n\r\nI then scored the EM 3.0, 3.5 &amp; 3.8 from the "middle of the road" comp and I noticed that the EM3.8 had a lot more torque that the perfection 3.8 but the top speed was similar between the two.\r\n\r\nPayaso, if it weren\'t you saying it homie I would say it was utter bullshit but now you\'ve got me intrigued. :???: \r\n\r\nph2t.');
