INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31487, '2c829c2af6', '', 'Hi\r\n\r\nI have one of those bit racer IR timmers. Works reasonably well upto 15-20 cm (6-8"), but beyond that forget it. They were designed for the bitracer track and the reflector would normally be fixed to the counter with a 3cm gap. It is tricky to line up the reflector with the counter over bigger distances but if you get it right they work ok.\r\n\r\nYou can see mine in the promo vid on my site.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\nTeanBonzer');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31488, 'be06ecee93', 'Extrememicros.com changes', 'At this time, we have decided to make the site strictly wholesale only site.\r\n\r\nThe change will take place on November 11th.  Until then, all orders for retail will be honored and filled.  After that, the site will sell motors only, and to resellers.\r\n\r\nOur reseller policy will be fairly lax.  IE, we won\'t have a huge application, and all that junk.  Just need to prove you sell goods, or want to begin to sell goods.\r\n\r\nMinimums will most likely be 100 motors at a time and we are strongly considering flat pricing regardless of RPM count.\r\n\r\nThe other items on the site will no longer be offered.  We will probably try to move the remaining tubes out in a different manner, and since batteries are fairly easy to come by, we will no longer stock those either.\r\n\r\nI have checked a few US sellers of motors for wholesale pricing, even directly with a couple manufacturers, and our TBA pricing will be far more competitive and hope that our potential customers can see that as well.\r\n\r\nWe do want to take the time to thank each and every customer who has supported us over the last six months or so.  We appreciate all of your support since our inception.\r\n\r\nFeel free to contact us for further details.  \r\n\r\nThanks again\r\nTodd Cuzzort\r\nExtreme Micros');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31489, 'ea75736c2b', 'I am soo glad I jumped on the Xmods band wagon.', 'See here\'s what my hang up was. In 1/10th scale there are literally thousands of dollars worth of hop ups you can put in your car. In the end the point doesn\'t seem to be how constructive you are, as much as how much money you have.\r\n\r\nWith Bits we\'re over here totally making everything ourselves. It\'s a real grassroots kinda scene. I dig that, reminds me of the early days of hotrodding, when they didn\'t have many aftermarket parts to work with either.\r\n\r\nSo when I actually had seen the Xmod in RS, with all it\'s accessories, I started getting the impression of the "how much money you got?" feeling I got from 1/10th scale.\r\n\r\nBut everyone\'s talkin\' \'bout the Xmods, and I\'m kicking myself in the behind for not getting one last payday. So I cracked, I finally broke down, and bought one.\r\n\r\nI\'m so happy I did, this is a complete package for 50 bucks, and has all the coolness of my 1/10th scale cars. It kinda remind me of a little Tamiya car with it\'s modular design. If the hobby oriented companies catch on to the popularity of these, I could totally see some light weight replacment parts coming out. It\'s also nice to know it can be precisely tuned, and not just twist this, bend that, cut here, trim there, kind of hit and miss process I go through with bits.\r\n\r\nIt will not replace my Bits for racing on my bed, while I watch TV at night, but it\'s whole \'nother toy with new possibilities. Nothin\' wrong with new toys. :grin: \r\n\r\nIf you\'re holding back like I was, then just let yourself go, be free, buy a freakin\' Xmod for christ\'s sake. They\'re worth every penny.');
