INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31639, '34a60d6a28', '', 'ok, i thought i knew how to do this mod, like in the black and white diagram. but in the color diagram the flipped mosfets are connected to different points. can someone check this out and tell me the right way to do it? thanks alot');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31640, '47bca8d2a9', '', '[quote:47bca8d2a9="vinnyg"]ok, i thought i knew how to do this mod, like in the black and white diagram. but in the color diagram the flipped mosfets are connected to different points. can someone check this out and tell me the right way to do it? thanks alot[/quote:47bca8d2a9]\r\n\r\nThe same pins are connected. The mosfets with black dots in the color diagram are flipped upside down, so it looks kinda backwards.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31641, '70de5d5cdc', '', 'The two flipped mosfets have one pin that is NOT connected to the PCB.  This pin is connected to the red and black wires in the pic that connect to the other 2 (normal side up) mosfets.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31642, '29832e0374', 'Enhance the lightkit on your ZZ SE', 'Hey fellas, being a zzse owner and all now  :rockon:  I was thinking of another fricken project to add to my list and that would enhance the functionality of the lights on the zz se.   A few things come to mind like:\r\n\r\nmake the rear lights function like a real car, dim usually, go bright when stopped.\r\n\r\nmake reverse lights (white) that come on in reverse only.\r\n\r\nfront headlights stay on all the time (or just dim usually except when going fwd, they would be at full brightness then)\r\n\r\npossibly do indicators, got a circuit for that somewhere......\r\n\r\nHas anyone noticed how crap the headlights are on the SE\'s?  I mean they point up into the air for frick\'s sake!   If you put your SE near a wall you will see that the focal point for the headlights are about 5-6cm ABOVE the top of the car.  This is the for Savannah anyways, dunno about the other models....   This "issue" needs fixing as well..\r\n\r\nYou\'re all probably going to say, "ph2t, stop fucking arond with this eye candy shit and get back to work on the fet mod..."  Oh well. I asked for it I guess, lol............');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31643, '2929ad2073', '', 'Well I just spent a few hours reading at mini-zracer.com, and I\'ve determined that it\'s gonna take me a few hundred dollars, and a couple years to see the Xmod\'s fullest potential, that\'s ok though, because I can take it slow, with many steps along the way.\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna just wait for Tiny to get his bearings in. I\'ll probably be ready to afford them by then, so that works for me. Maybe he\'ll have a hot motor by then that I can order at the same time. I\'m still gonna get the stage 2 motors, even if I get a hotter motor I\'m still gonna get the stage 2 motor set, just for the pinions, and heat sink.\r\n\r\nWhen those Mini-Z guys we\'re talking about cramming Novak electronics in one of these, man, that got my crank turning. I had Novak electronics in all my 1/10th scale cars. If I did that and replaced the radio with a nice FM Airtronics, this car would be the ultimate, but that\'s where it get\'s expensive. I might never reach that point, or I might totally get into this over the next year, and be doing that by next year. Who know? I think it mostly depends on the competition I find.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31644, '8a7a8dd256', '', '[quote:8a7a8dd256="ezenterprises"]for $40 i think i could make a nicer one from stuff from a craft store... but waayyy cool none the less[/quote:8a7a8dd256]Yeah you know I was thinking the same thing. Man, calling plastic rhinestones \'ice\'. What\'s up with that? I\'d like to see a real pimp cup with real ice, now that would be impressive.\r\n\r\nThose are cool though. I was having some fun ripping on them. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31645, '54cd5ca1bb', '', 'thanks alot guys, i knew that one pin was not connected but id didnt know that the fets in the color diagram were flipped. thanks');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31646, '2232292d04', '', 'That a good idea having the taillights dim, and go bright when stopped. Kinda opposite of how I hear the Xmod works. Those are dim all the time, and go bright when going in the coinciding direction.\r\n\r\nThe headlight in my Savannah weren\'t too bad, they pointed straight ahead, and not at the road, but that din\'t matter because most the light leaked out the bottom. My mustang the LEDs poke right out the front of the body, and they just seem brighter, more focused that way, and alot more light coming out the front instead of the bottom.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31647, '928223162e', '', 'its brighter than the se lights and it is dim when idling. it turns off after about a minute of inactivity. the headlights get bright when in fwd or reverse. the tails get brighter only when you pull back to break. they are dim in reverse. one of the leds was not as thick as the others so i had to use testors glue to keep the tail lights in and i reglued the tail light covers. thats all ive had to do with it. it plugs in just like the se does but its a longer wire. i tried plugging the se lights into the xmod chassis and nothing..\r\nplus dude its five bucks\r\n[img:928223162e]http://images.google.com/images?q=tbn:teN8o8BGgokC:earth.leeds.ac.uk/~nicholas/images/rs52.jpg[/img:928223162e]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31648, '937a791118', '', '[quote:937a791118="crazydave"]That a good idea having the taillights dim, and go bright when stopped. Kinda opposite of how I hear the Xmod works. Those are dim all the time, and go bright when going in the coinciding direction.\r\n\r\nThe headlight in my Savannah weren\'t too bad, they pointed straight ahead, and not at the road, but that din\'t matter because most the light leaked out the bottom. My mustang the LEDs poke right out the front of the body, and they just seem brighter, more focused that way, and alot more light coming out the front instead of the bottom.[/quote:937a791118]\r\n\r\nMust be a QA thing then.  Mine are clearly pointing up.   The area they sit in is pretty small (on the savannah) so I think I would need to file down the bezel on the led to enable them to point straight, possibly on a slight down angle, as real headlights are.....\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31649, 'b13f8f3e98', '', 'no shit, that is a good idea - dimming the lights, that\'d be killer\r\n\r\nyea my se\'s headlights aren\'t that great either, but whatever I don\'t know if I care - I\'ve got better lol\r\n\r\n :???: we need to be able to put on the high beams.\r\nhave em dim normally and juice em when you need to bust out the "move bitch, get out the way" lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31650, 'b5b13b04b1', 'i have jumped off the bandwagon', 'i love these xmods but i cannot accept their poor quality construction..\r\nbought my 1st one a red supra/put in suspension upgrades and even altered the rack for tighter turns..then put in stage 2 motor and bearing upgrades..experimented with awd and liked that too..\r\nthen the car started stuttering.\r\ntried fresher batt in tx tried new batts in chassis tried better soldering job on car ant lead tried cleaning contacts on xmitter ant tried pushing tx batt harder to contacts\r\nscreamed in agony as car stutters anytime it gets more than 7 feet away..\r\nripped all my hopups off+returned it..\r\nopened 2nd xmod it seemed better..put in hopups and slowly but surely range decreased..\r\nwent to ratshack again and showed them how useful a 15 mpr car can be with 5 feet of range..\r\nthey opened up a 3rd xmod case and i assembled tires+ant+batt in front of them..new controller+batts and the 3rd one also lost signal intermittantly but this time at any range..\r\nyyyeeeeeeeeaaaaaaaaaaaagggggggggggghhhhhhhhhhh\r\nat least they gave me my money back\r\nthe thing that makes me angry is i see so much potential in this chassis but the propriatary tx and rx inadequacy renders it useless and unreliable\r\n\r\ni do wish you all the best of luck with your xmods');
