INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31662, '363dca7274', '', '[quote:363dca7274="DarkTari"]A Dodge Neon ?[/quote:363dca7274]You no like?\r\n\r\nI kinda dig Neons. They\'re cheap, and kinda cool lookin, but the coolest thing is Dodge sells all the Mopar hop up parts you need to build this thing into a full on race car. I remember a Dodge representitive on TV bragging that it is possible to pick one of these up, drive off the lot and around back to the shop, and have everything you need to be competititve in rally racing, purchased and installed right there. Dodge has 2 Neons doing fairly well on the rally circuit right now. I thought that was pretty cool, and I\'ve always dug Dodge, because they understand the \'Hot Rod\' mentality.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (31663, '18c828fea1', '', 'The chassis doesnt look like a Super Bits, it just looks like a Perfection car with all the extras, but the controller is definatelty a Super Bit knock-off, and they have the 6-frequencies.\r\n\r\nI\'m disappointed, because the Super Bit\'s new chassis handles so much better, I consider that a major bonus, and the PCBs are very punchy, almost like a FETed car, but not quite. Since the chassis looks the same, I have to assume the 2-speed booster technology is the same too. It\'s a shame too, because I love my Super-Bits, but that annoying glitch makes them almost unusable. It would have been really cool if someone really made a Super Bit knock-off, but with out the anoying glitch.\r\n\r\nStill Super-Bit comparisons aside, that Super Perfection does look really cool, and comes with a lot of cool stuff for 12 bucks.');
