INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32141, '7e8cfb59d9', '', 'I use an exacto with replacable blades. I go over each cut again and again, until it cuts all the way through. You have to be very patient, because it takes a lot of time. You also don\'t want to break anything.\r\n\r\nHere\'s an example:\r\n\r\n[img:7e8cfb59d9]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/580482_4129261232787615622_vl.jpg[/img:7e8cfb59d9]\r\n\r\nIt took almost 2.5 hours just to cut this hood out. But with a lot of patience(which was the hardest part) it came out okay. Practice on some old bodies if you have them. after cutting out, take a peice of sandpaper or even a nail file, and smooth out the edges.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32142, '59695180b3', '', 'It isn\'t the easiest mod to do, but It also isn\'t the hardest. When everything is said and done, It all comes down to the wiring. When doing the internal mod, I built a wiring harness that kept everything neat and organized. After that was finished, it was just a matter of soldering it all together.\r\n\r\n\r\nProject F-14GT-R\r\n[img:59695180b3]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/580331_3316473676706312493_vl.jpg[/img:59695180b3]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32143, 'b89dbbadd0', '', '[quote:b89dbbadd0="DarkTari"]They\'re 30 bills, cheaper than the $45.92 HLJ was asking.  Now I\'m just waiting for TE to get the Enzo\'s in.  They\'re almost always cheaper than HLJ and delivery is faster.  I guess later on they\'ll offer the 4.2 King with it instead of that shitty azz Tomy 3.0 (from what I\'ve heard) !   Well, it\'ll be the 1st Tomy 3.0 I\'ll own so I can compare it to the 2.6.[/quote:b89dbbadd0]\r\n\r\n  The 3.0\'s aren\'t that bad you will notice a big difference in there performance in the SBCG\'s rather then the normal BCG\'s.\r\n\r\n\r\n  Yea that 30 bucks is a good price :)');
