INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32518, 'c3e3b17b19', '', 'Well I\'ve completed the mosfet changover to the se chassis as per microsash\'s method  and I gotta say that the car definately does perform better overall. :bs:   \r\n\r\nI\'ve experienced a healthy amount of increased torque and the top speed has increased by approx 25% .   This mod works and it does improve the performance of your car BUT it barely taps into the power of the H-Bridge mosfets unlike microamps\' version of the mod. That crafty bugger has figured it out :smile: .  \r\n\r\nStill, I gotta say that my car didn\'t spin out under full throttle before I did the mod and now it does.  I\'m running a 4.2Pro in the chassis under the(possibly misguided?) belief that these motors are best suited for pulsed applications.?  I will hopefully have a NX motor soon, I believe that\'s the best motor for zips?\r\n\r\nHey crazy &amp; hog, to what extents did you fet mod your se pcbs?\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32519, '9c29b069f4', '', 'Here\'s a little play by play for this mod.\r\n\r\nOpen up your SE, remove the screws, blah blah blah.\r\n\r\nOn the underside of the pcb (non expoxy side) you will\r\nsee a pair of transistors.  One will be two high, the other\r\nnormal height.  See below:\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s1.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nRemove these transistors.  I use a hobby knife to cut the pins \r\nto the small black package.  After you remove the old transistors\r\nclean up the solder pads by dabbling your soldering iron onto\r\nthem remove the old solder.\r\n\r\nI use a small drop of cantact glue to secure the new fets in place.\r\nThe fets to use here are [b:9c29b069f4]IRLML2502[/b:9c29b069f4].\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s2.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nThis way soldering them is piss easy!\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s3.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nNow flip the pcb over to its topside and remove the old \r\npnp transistors.  Again, clean the solder pads after removing the\r\nold transistors.\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s4.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nHere, you need to use [b:9c29b069f4]IRLML6401[/b:9c29b069f4] fets.  Again, secure them\r\nwith glue to assist soldering.\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s5.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nThat\'s it.  All done.  Enjoy your car...\r\n\r\nAlso, if you wanted to stack the [b:9c29b069f4]IRLML2502[/b:9c29b069f4] fets, well you\r\ncould do that to if you wanted :suspect: .\r\n\r\n[img:9c29b069f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/zzse/mk1/mk1_s6.JPG[/img:9c29b069f4]\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32520, 'ad40c55830', 'BitTunerz/body testfit.', 'well, i got to drive the car today. It ran for about 30 seconds and died. So I ended up tearing it all back down and re-wired everything. It ran through three charges and never quit once. The body is a problem I test fit it today and it seems that I\'ll have to cut the wheels down a bit. to clear the fenderwells. but this should give you an idea of how it will look.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:ad40c55830]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/590149_4694296113633290492_vl.jpg[/img:ad40c55830]\r\n\r\n\r\nNext month the Blue focus will get the same.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32521, 'e2d344cb09', '', '(check flossin). I got pics of the body test fitted on the chassis. I came to the conclusion that the wheels will have to have a little width cut back to clear completely. Becuase I grinded a bit of the chassis off, the front wheels turn very well. It runs straight and fast.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32522, '0847199b74', '', 'I ended up having to completely break it all back down and re-wire everything (plus two off the cells were bad). I put two new ones in and wired it all up. It has a little more left but this is much cleaner.\r\n\r\n[img:0847199b74]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/590127_4305789786098003849_v.jpg[/img:0847199b74]\r\n[img:0847199b74]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/590128_5567252299966658517_vl.jpg[/img:0847199b74]\r\n[img:0847199b74]http://www.digitalpose.com/mbr/1/32188/p/590129_3195305751714721722_vl.jpg[/img:0847199b74]');
