INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32524, '0101848b42', '', 'Well, I\'m totally impressed. I guess that Focus is a nice tall body, but still to get all that chassis under there and have it sit on there nice like that is an accomplishment. The fact that it drives well is amazing. I do think it\'s kind of funny that you will need to trim the wheels to get them to function, given that it looks like the stock HW. I guess they are just meant to go in a straight line, aren\'t they?  :wink: \r\n\r\nDid you say that was a triple cell? I imagine that can push the cast metal body fairly well.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32525, '585c2055ef', '', 'Yeah, It\'s been fun. It steers fine without the body. The bit chassis geometry pushes the wheels out so much more than stock. If I cut some width out, it should tuck them in enough to steer clearly.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32526, '17cd27c4b3', 'How being a Bit Freak improved my life!', 'Yes that\'s right, \'playing\' with the Bits IMPROVED my life.\r\n\r\nHow? It happened in steps...\r\n\r\n- First, I buy the little bastards because their cool. \r\n- Then, from hanging out at the Forums and seeing all the cool shit you can do with multi-batts and other things with the electronics...I get jazzed up about learning electronics (went so far as to buy a 700+ page book on the "Basics of Electricity")\r\n- My first Frankenstein job was swapping PCBs of a Bit (put an IR PCB in)\r\n\r\nBetween reading that book (and knowing some electricty basics), and working with TINY ASS components on Bits...I fear NOTHING now. Where I used to just throw shit out, now I\'ll crack it open to see if I can fix it first (and if I can\'t I\'ll rape that shit for parts!).\r\n\r\nSo far, around the house alone, I\'ve fixed a remote control for our ceiling fan (damned buttons wouldn\'t respond unless you pressed them HARD. I ripped that thing apart, gave the contacts a good cleaning and VOILA! all fixed). I also have an old ass 900MHz AT&amp;T cordless phone, same situation. Buttons stopped responding unless HARD pressed, RIPPED that bitch apart and cleaned the contacts and I don\'t have to shop for a new phone anymore.\r\n\r\nWho says playin with toys ain\'t no good for yur brain?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32527, 'f035714eb3', '', 'I almost lost one of those. I crapped my pants, \'cause I thought I just ruined my SE over a teeny tiny spring.\r\n\r\nThat is bummin\' Sorry I was of no help.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32528, '1fb88d04a2', '', 'I\'m totally in the same boat.\r\n\r\n- My electronic knowledge hast vastly improved, and I actually have a better understanding how a guitar amp works, from trying to understand how bits work.\r\n- I only ever wanted to make art to be appreciated. Making banner ads, I don\'t feel very appreciated. Painting bits, I feel the love.\r\n- Just sold a couple modified cars on ebay, made about as much as I do for my little graphic art side jobs. I think I just found a new side job.\r\n- I have something harmless to annoy my wife with.\r\n- I\'m happier at work, because I have something to look forward to when I get home.\r\n- I have actually cut back on smoking weed, so I can buy more cars, because when it comes down to it, my bits are actually more important to me than my weed, and that amazes me every time I realize that.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32529, '12c02e8636', '', '&amp;#305;t has been 27 mhz and loose range and loose steering but it is funny. Paint job isn\'t good may be i have a new paint for it. :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32530, '6639dd374b', '', '[quote:6639dd374b]- I have actually cut back on smoking weed, so I can buy more cars, because when it comes down to it, my bits are actually more important to me than my weed, and that amazes me every time I realize that.[/quote:6639dd374b]\r\n\r\nLOL, that is quite possibly the GREATEST thing I\'ve ever heard! I mean that literally. I\'m not laughing at you here, I just think that\'s the coolest thing that these little cars is making such a positive impact.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32531, '29a9321c0f', '', 'ya dude. i mean i took some electronics classes when i was like 19 but i fell asleep trying to memorize resistor colors. but before all this bit stuff my greatest electronics acomplishment was soldering my old atari jaguar power plug back onto the board. \r\n\r\nthen i started hanging out with my friend who fixes crap all day and for the most part i was totally lost by the stuff he does plus afraid cuz most of it is really high voltage. ive also been building computers for years but thats more like legos than electronics.  then one day i saw an article on bits on some pocket pc site and i have been a crackaddict ever since.\r\n\r\nive learned a lot about batteries, soldering skills have increased 20fold, diodes, transistors, all that crap. you also cant forget all the mechanical stuff involved. plus ive learned a lot about what glue to use when/where needed. its endless.\r\n\r\nthen theres the painting techniques that ive learned from you guys. \r\n\r\nand well i dont think i ever owned an rc car before i got into bits and now i have like 20 or 30.\r\n\r\nso the most important skill ive learned is the ability to smoke any one of your asses on any given day in any race  :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32532, 'fbe6b03ce4', '', '[quote:fbe6b03ce4="Namuna"][quote:fbe6b03ce4]- I have actually cut back on smoking weed, so I can buy more cars, because when it comes down to it, my bits are actually more important to me than my weed, and that amazes me every time I realize that.[/quote:fbe6b03ce4]\r\n\r\nLOL, that is quite possibly the GREATEST thing I\'ve ever heard! I mean that literally. I\'m not laughing at you here, I just think that\'s the coolest thing that these little cars is making such a positive impact.[/quote:fbe6b03ce4]\r\n\r\ni cant remember the last time i bought that stuff');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32533, 'db45d2b438', '', 'i originally had the accura now i got the white supra. mechanically both are/were sound other than the accura having one axle that wasnt threaded.\r\n\r\ni got the stage 2 motors and wowee. the blue gear 6:1 gave me the strangest problem. tire expansion!!! such a problem that the tires kept falling off. so i put the white gear on and its not as bad. haha');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32534, '888bb6bf87', '', '[quote:888bb6bf87="hogjowlz"]i cant remember the last time i bought that stuff[/quote:888bb6bf87]\r\n\r\nCan\'t remember eh? Sounds like it may have been very recent. :cool:\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'ve also learned a lot about electronics and mechanics through these little bastards... also a little about my addictive personality, or my hoarding, as SuperFly puts it. I never would have imagined pulling off something like a mosfet mod when I started this madness 10 months ago. I think the learning part is a big part of why I\'m still interested... and of course, the racing. \r\n\r\ncrazydave, post a link next time you have an auction going.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32535, '96d021ac52', '', '[quote:96d021ac52="hogjowlz"]i originally had the accura now i got the white supra. mechanically both are/were sound other than the accura having one axle that wasnt threaded.\r\n\r\ni got the stage 2 motors and wowee. the blue gear 6:1 gave me the strangest problem. tire expansion!!! such a problem that the tires kept falling off. so i put the white gear on and its not as bad. haha[/quote:96d021ac52]\r\n\r\nWe started gluing the tires on, and man does it make a big difference. It\'s nice to have all that torque.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32536, '623c059620', '', 'Since the completion of my Elect Eng degree several years ago, the most relative application I\'ve used it for up until now is these cars, so I think that is pretty bloody sad.  \r\n\r\nStill, I like to think that I can bring something to the scene......\r\n\r\nOtherwise it\'s been IT for me baby, all the way......\r\n\r\nph2t.');
