INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (32911, 'c49c09a890', '', '[quote:c49c09a890="ph2t"]Actually Dave the P chan fets aren\'t flipped mate, just replaced one-for-one from the old PNP transistors.   I get 2.6V across the motor terminals when it\'s an open circuit but when you put  a motor in there this drops to approx 1.6V instead.   So it\'s better than stock but not to the performance of microamps version.   I put 3V on the Gate pin of the nchan fet and I got 2.3V across the motor whilst in circuit!  The thing flew!\r\n[/quote:c49c09a890]Thanks for clarifying, I was a little confused, but I fugured I\'d just have to stick my face in there to get it, but I get it now. :lol: \r\n\r\nSo how\'d you get the 3 volts on the gate pin of the N-channel FET? DC/DC converter? \r\n\r\n...and why \'flew\' in the past tense, did something happen to it?\r\n\r\n\r\n**Edit** Ph2t,  I reviewed your PM, and saw where I got confused. You were saying something about future possibilities of useing the P-channel FETs for switching, and all Nchannel FETs in the H-bridge. That  idea had appealed to me, and that\'s why that idea had confused me. Good thing i got that straightened before my FETs got here. :lol:');
