INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33001, 'be6579a88b', '', 'I was going to put something together. Just hadn\'t got around to it.\r\n\r\nSo far I just have the standard bit PCB which covers Microsizers sport and pro\'s, Cannonballs, Cyclonas, Shens, LXX bosters, and non boosters. \r\n\r\nHere\'s that:\r\n[img:be6579a88b]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/moslayout.jpg[/img:be6579a88b]\r\n[img:be6579a88b]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/FETed2.jpg[/img:be6579a88b]\r\n\r\nSuper Bits Char-Gs are already strong out of the box, and micro_amps says FETs make no improvement. He has yet to find a fix, so I see no need to pursue that, until I know it can be done.\r\n\r\nThe info for the original Zip Zap is on the German site, and I could probably figure it out relativly quick, but I prefer to just ditch the ZZ\'s larger PCB, and put a clone board in there to make room for a second battery, and keep it under the PCB cover.\r\n\r\nThe Thunder Charger looks like the MS board, but is actually entirely backasswards, but I got it figured. Here\'s that:\r\n[img:be6579a88b]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/tcfet.gif[/img:be6579a88b]\r\n[img:be6579a88b]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/tcfet.jpg[/img:be6579a88b]\r\n\r\nThe Micro Speed is slightly different still, and I have a Mini Cooper clone that Havok sent me to do, that has the same layout. I have it in my head, but need to wait until my FETs get here before I can test it. I\'ll have this with in a week.\r\n\r\nThen there\'s ZZ SE...:roll:\r\nIt\'s possible to do, and it does improve performance, but it does not act like a FETed car. The theory is that the FETs are not being hit with enough voltage to turn them on all the way. micro_amps has figured it out, but he\'s not sharing his info, so we\'re having to fumble thrlough it ourselves. You can follow the progress on that here:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2140\r\n\r\n...and I think that about covers all my info.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33002, '2f31d74969', '', 'To whom it may concern. Is it the hobby that brings you here or just the chance to piss people off?\r\n\r\nI\'m here for the rides....not the drama :ignore:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33003, '407b60e587', '', 'Oh yeah, that is an electrolytic capacitor. I just assumed it was a diode because we used diodes on our motors in 1/10th scale, but now that I think about it, we didn\'t have reverse. You can\'t use a diode on a motor that gonna be reversed like the Xmods.\r\n\r\nSo knowing that, Hog\'s friend is more than likely correct. They\'re probaby 2 types of capacitors to filter different frequencies.\r\n\r\n...but tell us more about this first and second generation. I\'m curious too as to what you\'re talkin\' about.');
