INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33181, '8bdaf6e8fb', 'Are you \'hardcore\'?', 'Back in high school, when I was was little skate punk, there was this thing in the punk scene with calling everyone a poser. You know the real poser was that guy that wore eyeliner, and listened to Gene Loves Gezebel last week, and suddenly got a mohawk, and leather jacket, and is all about the Sex Pistols this week, but it was getting out of hand where everyone was calling everyone a poser. A few people that didn\'t know me would try to call me a poser. Well here I am 20 years later, 33 yo, and I\'m still hardcore, and all about my punk roots. So where they at now? Only a few of them turned out to be truly \'hardcore\'.\r\n\r\nSo what\'s that have to do with bits? Well when I first got on the forums there was a lot people that were like, \'I found them first, I\'m sick of all the trendies\', and I\'m over here like, \'Well gee guys it\'s not like I didn\'t know about them, my wife spent the month of September in the hospital, near death, and we spent the remainder of the year trying to get our budget in order. So sorry if I\'m not one of the cool kids that got the cool toys before Christmas.\'\r\n\r\nWell it\'s almost a year later, and where are they? Where the heck did all them trendies go? Seems bits and ZZs are last years cool present, and the Xmod boards are slammin\' while the bit ones seem to be fizzling.\r\n\r\nWell, I bought an Xmod, but bits are still my number one priorty. Like punk rock, I found something of myself in these cars, and they will be with me to the end.\r\n\r\nSo who\'s with me, who\'s \'hardcore\'? Who\'s still gonna be here in 2005?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33182, '2bd5600a96', '', 'i dont need this anymore, AND I USE THE SEARCH BUTTON!!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33183, 'b943067087', '', 'I ain\'t goin nowhere. I\'ve been into RC for about 20 years. It started off with 1/10th electric, I then moved on  to 1/8th gas cars , and finally micros. What makes these cars so cool is that you can race them anywhere, modify them without having to take out a second mortgage, and when you\'re done racing...put them in your pocket. \r\nI had to take a break from them last year to take care of family business, but I came back with a vengeance. My cars look so much better than my previous endeavors. \r\nNow I can\'t say that something won\'t come up that forces me to take a break from the hobby again, but I\'ll always come back to bits.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33184, '6e2c712105', '', 'Cabo, I was in the same situation. I went into RS and looked at Xmods, saw the ZZ\'s and bought one just to see what they were all about. I brought it home, and before I even fired it up, I lowered the body.\r\nJust think of it as doing a mod to another bit. Whatever you come up with, I\'m sure it\'ll be slammin! :cool:');
