INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33267, 'a53e5d522a', '', 'Well I finally got my P-channel FETs in. Since I had already done the N-Channels on the bottom, I didn\'t even have to remove the PCB to add the P-channel ones to the top. Took me about 5 minutes. :grin: \r\n\r\nWell again, slight improvement, but we\'re still not there. I stacked the the FETs, and that improved it just slighty still, but alas, no cookies.\r\n\r\nStill though, until we figure uA\'s technique, if you have an SE, and FETs laying around this is worth the effort, as there is an improvement over stock.\r\n\r\nI put a little video clip together, it\'s kinda messed up, for one I used the same controller for both cars to assure they started simultaneously, but since the steering trim is set by the radio, one car wanted to wander off. Then instead of hitting the button, then saying  go, my wife said go as she was hitting the button. So the modified car got about a 6 inch head start before the vid started, but I\'m showing it to you anyways, because I think the fact that it got a 6 inch jump in the time it took my wife to press the button, says something. The jump off the line is drastic, then it slowly accelerates past the stock car. The stock car is veering off to the right, so that makes it seem a tad slower.\r\n\r\nThe stock car is on the left, the modified on the right, both running the stock 2.2, and red gears.\r\n\r\n---&gt; [url=members.cox.net/strollerpusher/sefet.wmv]Video Clip (*.wmv)[/url] &lt;---\r\n\r\nI have a few experiments I\'m going to try, but I have to wait until I get my other SE working right again. I like to have a backup car. ;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33268, '44c24ccfd9', '', 'Great work there Dave.  Did you stack the nchan fets or the pchan fets?\r\n\r\nHopefully one day soon I\'ll figure this out, even if it kills me!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33269, 'a0eadfaa96', 'trying to remove these stickers!!! uhg', 'Im a long time bit owner, and i heard alot about these shen clones, so I bought a shen qui, but the stickers are all over it, i tried peeling them off, and was pretty succesful, accept on the sides and allitle on the top its still sticky, you cant see much but its still sticky.\r\n\r\n id prefer not to dip it in anything, (i put a body kit, hood scoop and special spoiler on  :grin: , which was very stupid  :-( , but i didnt realize it was sticky until i was finished.)\r\n\r\nany help would be appreciated guys.. thanks');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33270, 'b2db35d9e9', '', 'thanks dave im glad you like it, it would more like yours if i could pull of them sick flames you do.\r\n\r\ni guess it does kinda look similar.\r\n\r\n[img:b2db35d9e9]http://img.villagephotos.com/p/2003-10/435042/skylinem004.jpg[/img:b2db35d9e9]\r\n\r\n[img:b2db35d9e9]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/images/forum_images/contest_entries/pimpin_ride/crazydave_2_1.jpg[/img:b2db35d9e9][/img][/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33271, '76b3b3da4b', '', 'Can\'t we all just get along.\r\n\r\nI still can\'t figure why people out there worry so much about their post counts. I personally think the Quality of the posts is better than Quantity. I\'m not even sure what my post count here is, I know I have a higher count at RCmod.com because I\'ve been a member of their site longer.\r\n\r\nThere are a few out there that annoy me but I don\'t go ballistic on them, well maybe a few zingers as jokes.\r\n\r\nEverybody should remember the immortal words of John Lennon "Give Peace a Chance". Today is the anniversary of his death.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33272, '27e01a4d7a', '', 'I\'ve found the safest, easiest way to remove sticker gooies is with another sticker, or tape will work. I usually use packing tape. Just rub it on, peel it off, several times until you got all the gooies.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33273, 'beec2ead9f', '', 'Keep it up guys, I have faith that you will figure it out :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33274, '6b29e8c877', '', 'Well, I stacked the P-channels yesterday. I believe I had stacked the N-Channels before, but as I mentioned I didn\'t bother removing the PCB this time, so I\'m never sure unless I see it. \r\n\r\nI gotta tell ya, there a slot cut into the plastic piece that holds the PCB down, that the P-channel FETs poke out of, and it looks kinda cool with the 2 FETs poking out the top of it. Makes it look like the super modified beast, that it\'s not.  :lol: \r\n\r\nGot a few ??s for ya ph2t, I was looking at the specs for the P-channels, and noticed they have a slightly lower operating voltage. Does that mean they will turn on at a lower voltage? What were you saying, 3V? Any chance flipped P-channels in the N-channels\' position will help?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39224, 'bbb458c023', '', 'If they have fets, i guess i ment stacking them, and i really hope someones working on them, i havent even looked at the pcb yet. Whats wrong with a faster Xmod? id like to see mine top out to 20 or more. Xmods with IC-3 and blue stage 2 go about 15mph. Theres also that nice HIGH or LOW switch on the TX.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39225, 'd5b18f8aae', '', 'Dude, wait till you see it in action!   I\'m going over to betty\'s today for lunch.   And I\'ve got my video camera with me this time....... :D \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (39226, '483d9e056d', '', 'I\'m pretty satisfied with the speed of my Xmod as it is, but I could see wanting more speed if I had a bigger area to run it. From what I\'ve read, it sounds like some of those tricked out motors pull so much current, that if you don\'t FET your board you will fry it. I think sessiz is using one of those $50 motors, but I don\'t think he\'s done any FET modding.\r\n\r\nThat dude neurotechnik or something like that on TinyRC sounds like he would have done that by now.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33276, '68658d9315', '', 'You can also try vegtable oil.(or canola oil etc.) Just take some vegatable oil and dip the body in it or smear a hefty dose onto the stickers, let the oil soak in and the stickers should just slide off.');
