INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33403, '0d34b7847e', '', '[quote:0d34b7847e="SuperFly"][quote:0d34b7847e="DarkTari"]I\'m all HO baby!  Original Aurora, AFX, &amp; Tyco Pro.  Hadn\'t touched them in about 20 years or more. Then I bought my son a ZipZap and the bug hit me again.  This time around I can afford to support my habit, and I still have my track &amp; 3 cases of cars up in the attic![/quote:0d34b7847e]\r\n\r\nSo by Original Aurora are you talking Model Motoring sets? Cool! Hue35 has a stack of those sets in his basement. I had a killer Model Motoring set with about 15 Thunderjet and other 60\'s era cars that got left behind when I was in college and my mom split with my stepfather. Take a picture of your slot cars if you get a chance.\r\n\r\nIn case you missed this thread a while back, check out:\r\n\r\n[url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1088&amp;highlight=]hue35\'s Thunderjet conversion[/url][/quote:0d34b7847e]\r\n\r\nI\'m speaking of the HO scale Aurora, tracks with pins &amp; clips, power packs, screw in controllers, cars with pick-up shoes &amp; springs, motor brushes, guide pins, screw on bodies, 1/16 in. wide tyres, etc.  We had huge tracks back then. Started modding with different oils, screw-on alloys w/silicon tyres, silver pick-up shoes. etc.  Then Tyco came out with their HO scale TycoPro which blasted the standard Aurora to hell.  But then Aurora came back with the AF/X car which were fast but still couldn\'t dice with the Tyco\'s.  I\'ll see if I can locate them and post some picks.  The Ray that Hue posted was the  later version. I was racing back when Tyco &amp; AF/X first hit the market. Early 70\'s');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33404, '4cd091caa8', '', '1/24 scale slot cars. They were fun while there was a track I could get to. But that track closed and there are none that I can get to easily. I hadn\'t played with them for several years (they are still in my garage) but I\'d return to it if a track opened within a few miles from my house.\r\n\r\nBits and ZZ\'s are fun, plus I play Lord of the Rings and Warhammer at Games Workshop. I\'m lucky that my wife enjoys my hobbies also.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33405, 'dc89f044e9', '', 'yeah i came from 1/24th scale slot cars, they are so fun and so fast. we still have 3 tracks down here. i remember goen down the 1/4 mile scale drag strip. i wasnt into modding them or anything i was only bout  6 at tha time, but my first r/c was a radio shack one, that didnt last long then i moved on the better electric cars then about 2 years ago i got my first 1/10th scale nitro car and since then i have gone thru  3 of em. and then about this time last year i got my first bit.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33406, 'bb8c39d6a9', '', 'Auight Pimps, This is where it all started! When surfin after my last post and found these......\r\n \r\n[b:bb8c39d6a9]This is an [i:bb8c39d6a9]Orginal [/i:bb8c39d6a9]Aurora HO slot[/b:bb8c39d6a9] with 1/16 in wide tyres....\r\n[img:bb8c39d6a9]http://www.thunderslicks.com/charger3.jpg[/img:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n\r\n[b:bb8c39d6a9]I still have one of these:[/b:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n[img:bb8c39d6a9]http://www.thunderslicks.com/jag.jpg[/img:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n\r\n[b:bb8c39d6a9]This one brings back memories![/b:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n[img:bb8c39d6a9]http://www.thunderslicks.com/tbird.jpg[/img:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n\r\n[b:bb8c39d6a9]Here Ya Go Hog ![/b:bb8c39d6a9]\r\n[img:bb8c39d6a9]http://www.thunderslicks.com/Im001030.jpg[/img:bb8c39d6a9]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33407, '3375407a8c', '', 'I am having a real hard time getting the backwheels to fit the axle :x  I have tried  The Payaso Solution with blunt paper but it do not seem to work for me. Any other solution????  Please help me............');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33408, '19c415058f', '', 'According to my Calculator a 64th scale 1/4 mile is 20.63 feet or 6.29 meters (for the members that use the Metric system.\r\n\r\nif you are using the 70th scale its 18.86 feet or 5.75 meters.\r\n\r\nI did round the numbers to lessen the confusion.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33409, '6c245dfdc5', '', 'Them some cool cars DT!\r\n\r\nI always liked slot cars, but my experience was limited to the Tyco sets of the late 70s. It got boring, because you get one of those Magnum 440 cars, and they were just stuck to the track, especially the indy cars. So you just floored it, and watched it fly around the track. Got boring after a while.\r\n\r\nI had some friends that were into 1/24th scale slots. I really wanted to get into that, but my parents weren\'t biting, since I got bored slot cars after a week before.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33410, '5d8eaa66c5', '', 'you can try using some sort of epoxy.\r\nall you need to do is get something either around the axle or in the hole of the rim where the axle fits to make it snug.\r\nmake sure you roll the wheels a few times to make sure they\'re even and straight');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33411, '2143a4d55f', '', 'Cool more Pixies. That\'s actually one of my favorite songs.\r\n\r\n...and the Ramones too. \r\n\r\nThat\'s cool, I always dig your playlist.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33412, '6ecb488955', '', 'Daaaayum, you 2 are hardcore! :eek: \r\n\r\nI just smoke too much, and fight corporate BS from the bottom, like a true underdog.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:6ecb488955="VooDooMafia"][quote:6ecb488955="SuperFly"]I gotta find the pix of me being "hardcore" on a self-built 1/4 pipe out in front of my house, 6th grade, 1979. On a 10" wide Jim Muir "Dogtown" board. Also had a Powell/Peralta "bones" board, a Tony Alva signature board, and a Sims "Lonnie Toft" model in the quiver.[/quote:6ecb488955]\r\n\r\n  Man the good old days eh...\r\n\r\n  yea I remember when Skate vids just started getting big with "The search for Animal Chin", "Ban This" and others.  I still have them all on BETA.\r\n\r\n  One thing I dont remember is it hurting as much back then as it does now.  For some odd reason I just dont seem to bounce like I used to.[/quote:6ecb488955]I hear that. When I started back up, and fell over, I was no prob, I can handle it. Then like a week later I\'m still hurtin\' Sucks getting old.\r\n\r\nMy first deck was a Sims Snake in like \'78. I was into roller skating at the time, 8 yo, and sponsered by a local shop. They threw me a skateboard cause they weren\'t selling. They also threw me some of the original Van\'s, because they actaully didn\'t catch on at first.\r\n\r\nLater when I was 13 I got into skateboarding more seriously. I skated Big ol\' wide 11" and 12" decks, usually JFAs, cause they were the local boys, but i had a couple Skull skates too. Then I had my big ol\' wide ass Indy 215s. I went through all kinds of wheels. That was the set up for skating ditches and pools, which is what we did a lot here in Arizona.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33413, '6d3754853e', '', 'Yea it does suck getting old thats for sure.  The one thing I hate is that I feel old and get hurt alot more but still I get IDed at the beer store  :???: \r\n\r\n  Oh well Iguess its good they dont see the grey hair hehe');
