INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33417, '1ebcb826ae', '', 'im not into these things totally for looks but dude the body is there for a reason. wait til you(or a friend or your mom) accidentally step on one.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33418, '23ea7c93f9', '', '[quote:23ea7c93f9="CaboWabo"]1/10 scale\r\n\r\nstarted out on frogs, then hornets, then 1st gen rc10\'s, then turbo optima\'s, then broke lol[/quote:23ea7c93f9]\r\n\r\nI had one of those hornets then upgraded to an RC10 with gold aluminum chassis. Turned the hornet into a 1/10 scale pulling truck and the rc10 buggy into a truck.  Had a Blackfoot converted into a 15 pound pulling truck as well.  I\'ve also raced 1/24 and 1/32 slot cars had a few  Flexi\'s and Womps.  Even got my bigest trophy racing those slot cars (good spotsmanship).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33419, '077bb7b0c3', '', 'My best in 24th Slots was Track Champion in GTP12 and 2nd in Outlaw 12. I did win Concourse de Elegance in a regional in Group 10. Me and my Buddies in our team ZZzzz... Racing cared more for the Concourse than the race wins, because we refused to spend money like our competors. We each had talents we used to our best abilities. Me and Steve could paint (Steve was better). I was good and rebuilding the electric motors, I usually built the endoro cars for I could build tanks  :-D .');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33420, '96cc81bf54', '', '[quote:96cc81bf54="crazydave"]Them some cool cars DT!\r\n\r\nI always liked slot cars, but my experience was limited to the Tyco sets of the late 70s. It got boring, because you get one of those Magnum 440 cars, and they were just stuck to the track, especially the indy cars. So you just floored it, and watched it fly around the track. Got boring after a while.\r\n\r\nI had some friends that were into 1/24th scale slots. I really wanted to get into that, but my parents weren\'t biting, since I got bored slot cars after a week before.[/quote:96cc81bf54]\r\n\r\nI can dig it Cavey,\r\n\r\nNo fun or skill required. I left the sport long before the magna-traction cars came out so when we road raced it required skills and plenty of tyre cleaning pit-stops. The Tyco\'s I used for drag racing purposes only, had \'em set-up that way and they were fast as 5hit.  All that was needed was a good oil and some white silicon tyres.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33421, 'd88751cb27', '', '[quote:d88751cb27="CaboWabo"]one day payaso and I are gonna hook up with hue and SuperFly...\r\n4 peas in a pod I\'m tellin ya[/quote:d88751cb27]\r\n\r\nNo shit dude! We gots us the same story... the RC10 was my first serious RC car (I skipped the Frog \'cause I just knew the RC10 would be worth saving longer for), then I moved on to the Optima... then I was broke. That Optima was a badass mofacki. \r\n\r\nDT, I\'m gonna snap some pix of my T-Jets tonight, you got me jonesin\' to dig\'em out.');
