INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33425, '718cfa1a79', '', '[quote:718cfa1a79="hue35"]then I moved on to the Optima... then I was broke. That Optima was a badass mofacki. [/quote:718cfa1a79]\r\n\r\n\r\nI went through the 1/10 rc phase with the Grass Hopper, and the Big Bear truck..\r\n\r\nThat Optima was a badd mofo.. Wasn\'t it chain driven too?\r\n\r\nWe used to have a class in school that was just for rc cars once a year, but that all ended when a teacher got her ankle busted with one of them... :( \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33426, '8ab2ba7a21', '', '[quote:8ab2ba7a21="payaso"]\r\nI will say this though. Mission Space does such a good job syching people out that right before you get on it, it smells like a fuckin "Johnny on the spot" cause of all the people starting the early stages of pants shitting...\r\n\r\n\r\nFriggin sissies, and their weak butthole muscles...lol\r\n[/quote:8ab2ba7a21]\r\nIf I ever make it that way i\'ll remember to bring a can of air freshner! lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33427, 'b56ce880f5', '', 'Well HobbyEtc. just lost me as customer. Too bad too I was planning to buy a bunch of Mini- Z stuff there. They never sent a confirmation email. I emailed them asking for a confirmation email. I instead got one from UPS. I figured, oh well at least it\'s on the way.\r\n\r\nIt shows up today, and no Wild Char-G. Oh yeah sure they credited me back, but it would have been really nice if they could have contacted me, so I wouldn\'t be sittin\' here thinkin\' I\'m getting a Wild Char-G. \r\n\r\nIt\'s funny because I should be happy that I\'ve got  new bits to play with, but so what? I have bits, I was expecting a new toy, so I don\'t even care about the other cars. They\'ll probably just sit in the boxes for a while now.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSo you hear that HobbyEtc.?  You don\'t take a minute of your time to treat your customers right, and you lose our money, dig?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33428, '9c6396ba12', 'Lowered SE \'stang', 'I regretted taking the lights out of my first SE, so my intention here was to get it as low as possible, and keep the lights. I shaved the all the light mounts, and just glued them in, and shaved the mounts under the light\'s PCB. \r\n\r\nI did like an extreme flame type paint job on it, and it fought me every step of the way, and just when I thought I won, the clear coat melted part of it away.\r\n\r\nHere\'s the good side. The picture is especially bad, because I\'m PO\'ed, and didn\'t feel like taking a decent picture.\r\n[img:9c6396ba12]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/sestang.jpg[/img:9c6396ba12]\r\n\r\n\r\n...and here\'s the bad side. You can see where the charcoal melted into the silver, and along the botton, and behind the side window there\'s some silver peeking out where the paint melted away. Nothing major, but still far from perfect.\r\n\r\n[img:9c6396ba12]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/sestang2.jpg[/img:9c6396ba12]\r\n\r\n\r\nI know exactly where I went wrong too. I ran out of mineral spirits, so I cut a corner, and used degreaser. Laying the Duplicolor clear coat too heavy over the Plasti-Cote color coat didn\'t help either.\r\n\r\nSo that just goes to show you, you can break the rules, and sometimes you\'ll get away with it, but always remeber you\'re running a risk, and the wrong combination of circumstances, and BAM! you screwed up your paint job.');
