INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33775, '452dbe918a', '', 'Actually that\'s the opposite of what a limited slip diff does. What is happening is the wheel that lifts is unloading. Put some grease in the diff to fix that prob.\r\n\r\nThe limited slip ball diff that comes with the AWD kit should also fix the problem.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33776, '5ec13f03e1', 'Zip Zap SE Dual Cell?', '[color=blue:5ec13f03e1][/color:5ec13f03e1]  I like the new ZZ SEs.  They\'ve got me interested in the hobby again.  The proportional steering and acceleration is everything I wanted to race \'em......  except they\'re incredibly SLOOOW.    Even with the purple or yellow motor and/or gear combos there doesn\'t seem to be much difference.    With the propo acceleration, I want \'em to burn rubber.\r\n\r\nSo my questions is:  Has anyone done an internal dual-cell to the SEs?   Does it have any harm on the steering or burn out the lights?    Did some looking, but couldn\'t really find it.     A link or tut would be awesome.    To be honest, I haven\'t even cracked the lid on one of these, but wanted some comments before I get started, thanks.     :???: \r\n\r\n-Silent\r\nps, Cabo, How about a ZZ-SE CRIB Folder?');
