INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33856, 'b1a501ce77', '', '[quote:b1a501ce77="Skylineracer51"]how do i insert my image in my post??? it wont show up[/quote:b1a501ce77]It looks to me like your using the image tag right, you just have an incomplete address to the file.\r\n\r\nYour image should be on the web, so the address to it should be something like this: http://www. thedomainname.com, net, etc./maybe a subdirectory/your file extention, that should end with .jpg');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33857, '92b1cee768', 'We got him!', '[img:92b1cee768]http://i.cnn.net/cnn/2003/WORLD/meast/12/14/sprj.irq.main/story.saddam.close.jpg[/img:92b1cee768]\r\n\r\n[quote:92b1cee768]TIKRIT, Iraq (CNN) -- After nine months of scurrying from house to house, Saddam Hussein appeared to be a tired, resigned man who offered no resistance when U.S. troops extracted him from a hole in a rural farmhouse Saturday afternoon.\r\n\r\nL. Paul Bremer, head of the Coalition Provisional Authority, announced Sunday morning, "Ladies and gentlemen, we got him."\r\n\r\nThe audience responded with cheers, and Iraqis took to Baghdad streets dancing, doling out candy and firing rifles into the air. But in Tikrit -- Saddam\'s ancestral home town and a base of loyalty to him -- the streets were quiet.\r\n\r\nCoalition video showed the ventilated "spider hole" six to eight feet underground where Saddam was hiding with two other men who have not yet been identified. The video showed Saddam with graying hair and a long beard, undergoing a medical examination after his capture.\r\n\r\nA spokesman for the Iraqi Governing Council said DNA tests had confirmed Saddam\'s identity. [/quote:92b1cee768]\r\n\r\nhttp://www.cnn.com/2003/WORLD/meast/12/14/sprj.irq.main/index.html');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33858, 'ddd949da6b', '', 'so use yanks can do something right.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33859, '115f981eb9', '', 'Alright, so a T-jet body won\'t fit a bit, now we\'s just gots to figur a way to cram the MS guts in the T-Jet. ;)\r\n\r\nOk so the pcb board won\'t fit. I say we cut the PCB in half. Jumper all the copper traces that we just cut, so we can fold the board in half. We cram that in the car, and we got forward, and reverse, now how we gonna make that sucka steer?\r\n\r\nNo wait scratch that, we\'ll make a pan car chassis, and carry over a narrowed bit front end, yeah, that\'s the ticket.\r\n\r\nSorry, I was just brainstormin\' what I could do if I ever got a hold of one of them cars. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (33860, '9b9fdd834b', '', '[quote:9b9fdd834b="hue35"][quote:9b9fdd834b="gearboy"]hardcore? the pistols were lame, the damned were much better.[/quote:9b9fdd834b]\r\n\r\nDude, that\'s a bit harsh... lame? I dig everything on yer list and all, but I don\'t know about the Sex Pistols being lame. [/quote:9b9fdd834b]Yeah, that is bit extreme, The Sex Pistols totally turned everything upside down. I was just agreeing that I like the Damned better, but realistically considering the more gothic direction they took on later albums a lot of harcore fans might consider them lame.\r\n\r\nIt not so much the Sex Pistols that are lame, as much as the Sid Viscous wannabees that were at my school, beating their heads against the walls like a scene from Sid and Nancy every day of the week.');
