INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34119, 'e24b2e6ec4', '', '[quote:e24b2e6ec4="Grunge"]Well, I figured out the hard way that Xmods are not meant for outside use.  I had just assembled everything and I was testing it out in front of my condo.  The driveway is concrete so it\'s not rough terrain, but there are a few concrete joints.  I looked over the area first to make sure there wasn\'t any obstructions.  To make a long story short, I hit a rock about 1/4" in diameter.  If the tire had hit it, no problem.  If you examine the bottom of the Xmods, you will see a screw that attaches to shocks/wheel knuckle.  There is very little clearance between the bottom of this screw and the ground.  I happened to hit rock with the screw and it cracked the screw right off along with a small piece of the knuckle.  Fortunately, I had the AWD kit and I replaced the broken knuckle with the upgrade.  You have to be very careful and I found out the hard way.[/quote:e24b2e6ec4]\r\n\r\n\r\nexact same thing happened to me, cept not with a rock, with my friend\'s car :smile: ...but I figured out how to "fix" the problem. Use a damper screw. I know you have the AWD, but for anyone else this happens to. just an FYI! :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34120, '7c124a3bfe', '', 'My company had a Christmas party last night too. Only it was just for managers...\r\n\r\nMy boss won a XBox in the raffle, and went on about it all day today. I was starting to get jealous... :-(');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34121, 'e1055438ac', '', 'I totally agree, I used to have an 1/2 scale RC Pinto that ran like crap and handled like crap. I used a 1970, GM factory Corvette color, it was copper... that thing was kicking ass after the new "fast" paint. Then I spun out and hit a curb going backward, and the car blew up... the GM paint didn\'t fix that Pinto design flaw, but up until the explosion, that car was going about 30mph!! (that\'s like, 60mph scale speed!!!!!!)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34122, '85aa736387', '', 'Eliminate all that spinnin\' by using a motor with more top end and less torque. Also, try the teal gears, or better yet, use KIT racer gears. I\'ve had better luck finding the right amount of torque through motor and gear combos instead of messing with different tires. Tires are important, but use them to fine tune... get the torque where you want it, then try out tires.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34123, '137ad3ff0b', '', 'Has anybody done a TUT on the Fet Mod for the SE?  CrazyDave?  Buddy?    Ratshack part numbers?\r\n\r\nIts not the cost of the MicroAmps job, its just that it would be uneven with the rest of the competition on my track.    Do one, and have to do em all.   If I could do Dave\'s FetMod myself though, thats cool.    I\'m watching the "Fetted My SE" thread, but haven\'t heard anything in a while.   Anyone get it figured out?  ... and want to share for free?   :smile: \r\n\r\n-SilentWolv');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34125, '5840eb08f3', '', 'I\'ve just found this turkey over at MRCC selling the ZZSE fet mod:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php?showtopic=18782\r\n\r\nBasically it\'s the same as what we have done here already.  He says though that if you doublestack all four fets (2*n-chan and 2*p-chan) then you do get a great speed increase.   I\'ve only stacked the n-chan fets (irlml2502) and not the p-chan ones (irlml6401).  I\'ll give this a go this w/e and see what happens.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
