INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34217, '1f2cf5904f', '', 'Yeah it was probably the paper. It really didn\'t come out too bad. I think it\'s actually better without the stroke. :???: \r\n\r\n[img:1f2cf5904f]http://picserver.student.utwente.nl/getpicture.php?id=578691[/img:1f2cf5904f]\r\n\r\n[img:1f2cf5904f]http://picserver.student.utwente.nl/getpicture.php?id=578692[/img:1f2cf5904f]\r\n\r\nNow all I got left with the body is to put the 50 other stickers on there and make this a fully "sponsered" track car. :lol: I also need another coat of clear to cover everything up nice like.\r\nOr should I leave it as is? :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34218, '52bfebaa4d', '', 'Don\'t tell me that I\'m the only one that wants a \'71 Cadillac Fleetwood.\r\n\r\nI think if you did one of those in bit scale, you\'d still have to put it on a Zip Zap chassis, longest production car made ya know.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34219, '96d71a7c34', '', '[quote:96d71a7c34="ph2t"]I\'ve just found this turkey over at MRCC selling the ZZSE fet mod:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php?showtopic=18782\r\n\r\nBasically it\'s the same as what we have done here already.  He says though that if you doublestack all four fets (2*n-chan and 2*p-chan) then you do get a great speed increase.   I\'ve only stacked the n-chan fets (irlml2502) and not the p-chan ones (irlml6401).  I\'ll give this a go this w/e and see what happens.\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:96d71a7c34]\r\n\r\nEr, thats not ALL i do BTW. ;) I am not going to give you ALL the goodies I do to it to get the speed increase.. \r\n\r\nI had to live through my ASET, 7 years of design experience, and now a Physics degree i am currently enrolled in. Figure it out yourself, turkey. :)\r\n\r\nRob');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34220, 'c7edfc5d42', '', 'My SE already can climb a 30 degree incline at near full speed with the tires spinning with the 3.4 NOS motor. Anymore power and it will cease to have a useful runtime.\r\n\r\nBut, you ARE right.. These things aren\'t even truly ON at the gate voltages, which is why I posted my notes with the gate voltages included.\r\n\r\nBut, with an H bridge, there are OTHER tricks you can do.. ;)\r\n\r\nRob');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34223, '5b7dd8dac8', 'Re: here are my z cars', '[quote:5b7dd8dac8="THE #1 PIMP"]my zcars are in the 1st ann contest enteries post @rcmod.com\r\nthey also have an all black zcar to\r\n\r\nif you put an \r\norange zz motor\r\nred zz idler gear(the gear between the motor and rim gear)\r\nand leave the gear behind the rim stock\r\nit will be prety fast\r\n\r\nmine does a 20\' 7.5\'\' 1/4 mile in 8 seconds flat in the road\r\nwhat do you have under your zcar\'s hood\r\nnice rides your rides are so sick[/quote:5b7dd8dac8]\r\n\r\nRe-Read the post again Pimp!  It\'s all there!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34221, 'f716c7a6c9', '', 'you can make a dyno simply with another wheel or a drum and another motor being run as a generator feeding off the drum. ;)\r\n\r\nUse a voltage divider ladder to scale it so it lights up an LED meter and you can see the voltage drop across a known resistance and calculate real power. ;)\r\n\r\nJust make sure your load resistor is a .5% or something good like that and it will work just fine.\r\n\r\nI might mess around with something like this myself.\r\n\r\nRob');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34222, 'e9e378f1e0', '', 'I agree crazydave .');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34224, '2434e66e48', '', '[quote:2434e66e48]So denden, when you gonna put this on the market dude?[/quote:2434e66e48]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThese puppies are done one at a time . They don\'t always come out perfect. Filling and sanding are sometimes required . An advance \r\nmodder would have no problem . To market them I would want them\r\nto be damn near perfect ,. when I figure out how to do that ,.. then \r\nI\'ll market them .');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34225, '682c8a322b', '', '[quote:682c8a322b="cyborgzero"]My SE already can climb a 30 degree incline at near full speed with the tires spinning with the 3.4 NOS motor. Anymore power and it will cease to have a useful runtime.\r\n\r\nBut, you ARE right.. These things aren\'t even truly ON at the gate voltages, which is why I posted my notes with the gate voltages included.\r\n\r\nBut, with an H bridge, there are OTHER tricks you can do.. ;)\r\n\r\nRob[/quote:682c8a322b]\r\n  Well if you gots some idea on the mod post em up pimp :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34226, '7bcda1fece', 'Skyline R34!!!! (extended ofcourse)', 'I have a few pics of this cars creation in my extended project thread, but I figured I would post a nice lookin pic of it here, So all those not interested in the whole project may see it.... :p\r\n\r\nCurrently:\r\n-Single 200 mAh cell (adding second shortly) I am working on a "Battery Pack" method that will be charged outside the chassis, then can be inserted into the bit just like a single cell would.... So if you wanted to could switch from single to dual or even tripple cells without modin...  :???: \r\n-Custom fabricated chassis (held in to body same as original diecast chassis was. shaved to match the rest of the chassis.\r\n-Muscle Machine rims (soon to be replaces by 5mm alloys i hope  8) )\r\n\r\nFuture Mods:\r\n-Fully Custom controller, as this one clicks WAY to much when i drive (in order to drift I have to pulse my accelerator alot, so its hella noisy)\r\n-Whatever my brain can make up will go into this car  :???: \r\n-Casting body in resin mold.\r\n-Custom Paint job. I was thinking metalic blue in the front fadin to black in the back... with custom printed decals designed by me... \r\n\r\nIf you want a full pic (1280 x 960) check out:\r\n[url]http://members.shaw.ca/blinnstudios/SkylineR34_rims.jpg[/url]\r\n\r\nCheck out a pic of the under belly here:\r\n[url]http://members.shaw.ca/blinnstudios/SkylineR34_bottom.jpg[/url]\r\n\r\nOr pics of the chassis check out:\r\n[url]http://members.shaw.ca/blinnstudios/SkylineR34_chassis.jpg[/url]\r\n\r\n[img:7bcda1fece]http://members.shaw.ca/blinnstudios/SkylineR34_rims_small.jpg[/img:7bcda1fece]\r\n\r\nHope yall really like it... I am really happy with how it has turned out so far... still needs a lot of work, but so far so good :p\r\n\r\nThink I should enter it in the December Contest??\r\n\r\n :D Swavey  :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34227, '7cd1045426', '', 'very impressive denden\r\nI\'d love to hear how you do it if you ever feel like spilling the beans lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34228, '147d736474', '', 'pic won\'t load for me for some reason, server must be puking :-)');
