INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34230, '3b1cb43e89', '', 'looks good man.\r\nI liked how you panned out the inside, I saw that in the other thread.\r\nsome nice work in there.\r\ndig the battery swap idea, I started out doing that myself but kept jarring them hard enough to break free and give a poor connection.\r\n\r\nif you seriously plan on painting or customizing the shell, if it were me, I\'d probably enter once it was done.\r\nbut that\'s just me, many others have entered and gone on to mod more afterwards.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34231, 'e3051ef8f8', '', 'Denden you do some sick work, as I have told you before (i think  :? )\r\n\r\nI may still need to employ your services for my Skyline and a few other bodies...\r\n\r\nKeep up the good work man, ever thought of doin an old \'49 ford truck, or \'56 ford... they seem to be hard to come by.. but would look sweet bit size i think');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34232, '487fe56133', '', 'that\'s nice man, I dig it.\r\ngreat details up front :wink:\r\n\r\nI can see your improvements from sled to sled, keep up the good work home slice');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34233, '7d2e7a93a7', '', 'Thanx Cabo, glad you like it... The main goal through the whole thing was to keep it as clean as humanly possible, heh.... with regards to wireing, modling ect..\r\n\r\nA budy of mine told me after i get the paint done, I should send it in to like RC Car action magaxing and see if I can get it and specs in a readers ride section or somethin  :shock:  That would be soooo sick!!!\r\n\r\nDo you mind my asking how you went by the swapable batteries.. I have had a few ideas, but the only one I have tested worked amazing on the controller, but didnt even show any signs on life in its own..  :???:  Got any advice... Jaring shouldnt me an issue for me cause as soon as i get the batter pack figured out, I am going to custom make a pcb cover out of 2 part epoxy that will be capable of housing single, dual or tripple cells without lettin them budge.. :p\r\n\r\n :D Swavey  :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34234, 'c270191d4f', '', '[quote:c270191d4f="sessiz"][quote:c270191d4f="CaboWabo"]pic won\'t load for me for some reason, server must be puking :-)[/quote:c270191d4f]\r\n\r\nYou can\'t expect much when the server\'s free. :lol:[/quote:c270191d4f]\r\n\r\n  They loaded for me :) and free is the magic word lol man like I tell yea sess I have shit that I have not clue what it isbut if its free I will download it LOL.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34235, '2e093bcb29', '', 'Man you and sezzis with teh theme cars lol now I wanna bust out the good old Canadian car, not only paint job but replace the wheels with skates LOl :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34236, '12a67b0824', '', 'Sessiz, that\'s looking really nice. Expert job on the Turkish flag parts. Size and position is perfect. I can\'t wait to see it finished. If you just want numbers, go to a hobby store that sells decals for similar scales. I\'m sure you could find some cool ones.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34237, '2d25ce9803', '', 'TransGaming\'s much-anticipated release of WineX 3.2 brings the world\'s hottest games to Linux. Max Payne 2: The Fall of Max Payne, WarCraft III: The Frozen Throne, HomeWorld 2 and many others are now made available to TransGamers - through WineX 3.2.\r\n[url]http://www.transgaming.com/showthread.php?news=94[/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34238, '7455252c5d', '', 'All right! Something I\'m very familiar with.( I\'m using Red Hat right now) I am currently running a dual boot system with RH and XP. I pretty much use windows for gaming only (although I don\'t really need to since more games can be run on Linux now). Plus, my wife can barely use XP, so linux is like japanese to her. \r\nI also use linux to power my game servers.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34239, 'db83c15306', '', 'That\'s lookin better and better pimp. I had thought about converting a muscle machine to an RC, but went with the HW Tunerz instead. I am going to be doing another die cast ride, but I\'m definitely doing a different chassis layout this time around');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34240, 'f2a5d4840b', '', 'I left the inside of the chassis as is.\r\nsoldered my batteries, put electrical tape on the ends and I could just wedge 1 battery into it\'s normal position, set the other on top of the heat sink, and the wire ran back in between the taped end of the battery inside the chassis, and the battery post.\r\njust the added thickness of the wire was enough to keep the battery in place, until I took a super hard hit or fall, then it would start to work its way free and usually tear a hole in the tape and short itself or just pop out most of the way until there was no connection.');
