INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34285, '27336e3df9', '', 'The daughter, boyfriend, and I raced on my track a while back.  It was pretty fun, but I found out the track is too technical for consistent laps and close racing as intended.     \r\n\r\nFor Christmas, I\'m giving them a ZZSE car each, with a performance kit, and a Mercedes 500SL body kit.\r\n\r\nAnd I\'m going to rebuild the track to put in a wide sweeper, and chicane on the track, along with the banked turn.....  A much simpler lap overall.    Should make for some closer racing.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34286, '259d31fca7', '', '[quote:259d31fca7="cyborgzero"]Okay, first off, did anyone notice that the gate voltages for the steering is 1.2v?\r\n\r\nThere lies a hint in the steering circuits as to how to get higher gate voltages..\r\n\r\nAlso, too, there is NO ONE stopping you from running an extra FET stage run to the gate voltage of the H-bridge. ;)\r\n\r\nOh gee did I give it away?  :-D \r\n\r\nRob[/quote:259d31fca7]\r\n\r\nI may be wrong, but doesnt the steering use bjts instead of fets, unless they have been changed out. so then wouldnt that be base voltage instead of gate voltage?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34287, 'dbd5a28a12', '', 'Well here she is. I\'ll post some more pics when my ass isn\'t buzzing. :-) \r\n\r\n[img:dbd5a28a12]http://picserver.student.utwente.nl/getpicture.php?id=581293[/img:dbd5a28a12]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34288, '2576c0ebf7', '', 'thats a great looking car there sessiz, excellent work.\r\n\r\nps. I turned 18 today, can legally drink here in Aus.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34289, '8415063ca9', '', '[quote:8415063ca9="HirotoR34"]I am going to be doing another die cast ride, but I\'m definitely doing a different chassis layout this time around[/quote:8415063ca9]\r\nSounds cool man, if you ever need a hand with anything just let me know! I aint pro or nothin, but I just figured I would put out the helpin hand to fellow pimps :P\r\n\r\n*UPDATE* I had to switch back to crappy small wheel mod for the time being (traction was shitty on those others) but the car runs Amazing, I got my "plug and play" dual cell goin in there and everything is runnin solid!!! Spring Suspension added now, so it rids like a cloud...  8-) \r\n\r\nI have got the blue underlighting all planned out just need one more blue LED from RS. I decided to go with something that dosnt fade far out from under the car... to keep the real theme goin, heh...\r\n\r\nLovin this car, seriously!\r\n :D Swavey  :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34290, '144b05d384', '', '[quote:144b05d384="mad_haxor"][quote:144b05d384="cyborgzero"]Okay, first off, did anyone notice that the gate voltages for the steering is 1.2v?\r\n\r\nThere lies a hint in the steering circuits as to how to get higher gate voltages..\r\n\r\nAlso, too, there is NO ONE stopping you from running an extra FET stage run to the gate voltage of the H-bridge. ;)\r\n\r\nOh gee did I give it away?  :-D \r\n\r\nRob[/quote:144b05d384]\r\n\r\nI may be wrong, but doesnt the steering use bjts instead of fets, unless they have been changed out. so then wouldnt that be base voltage instead of gate voltage?[/quote:144b05d384]Well, since I have no degree, and I don\'t know what I\'m doing really, I had accidently FETed my steering. It seems the steering has 2 N-channels on the bottom, and 2 P-channels on the top, just like the throttle.\r\n\r\n..and the thing about runnning an extra FET stage to the gate voltage was a vague idea that I had, but since I just mess with electronics, I really have no clue how I\'d go about doing that. Maybe ph2t can help us out with that.\r\n\r\nWell, I least I have a little more to work off of. I learned a lot from this experience, so I guess I\'m gonna have to just keep learning, unless ph2t figures it for me.');
