INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34433, '4771f7aad8', 'Super bits! some questions', 'well ive been in and out of bit char-g for about 3 years, i now have 12 or so, thanks to cheap clones lol. but my little cuzin, at 6 years old loves these, and he can really whip my fast ones around the track, i already modded him a car, we call the green machine, (deep green skyline w/ gold rims) he cant stand going somewhere with a big driving space without it, so basicly he loves bits. to the point here, its christmas time... so i bought him a Super bit, the lamborgini, he saw the set online and loves it. i cant belive im giving it to him (i want a super bit lol  :sad: ) but he likes em more than i do. so...\r\n\r\n  Are these bits really anything different? like different chassis? it comes with a 1.6 if im correct, but i got the free 3.0 motor gift from toy east. So can somebody give me some insight on what they changed? or didnt?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34434, '6c064b1f6b', '', 'Ain\'t no pimps needin\' to be played in the name of science... that\'s just too damn complicated. It seems like you have a lot to offer in solving the problem at hand, and it will definitely not go unappreciated if you continue to lend your brain.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34435, '89f3998831', '', 'Well IMO\r\n\r\n  The superbits have diff chasies and PBC, but they lack in performance with the rance issue.\r\n\r\n  If its for a 6 YO then he will proly love it thats for sure but to do any real racing.... well out of 4 superbits I only have one that I can get around the track a few times without it losing range and have it just keep going.\r\n\r\n  If you are ordering from toyeast then I would say get some of them LXX cars as there newer stuff is great :)\r\n\r\n  I have had no real problems with them and they are a fraction of the price.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34436, '9c0cbb9b8f', '', '[quote:9c0cbb9b8f="hue35"]Ain\'t no pimps needin\' to be played in the name of science... that\'s just too damn complicated. It seems like you have a lot to offer in solving the problem at hand, and it will definitely not go unappreciated if you continue to lend your brain.[/quote:9c0cbb9b8f]\r\n\r\n  Wise words from a wise man.\r\n\r\n  Hell even when someone in the hood does a bad job there are people right there telling them it was a good effort then pointing/helping them improve.\r\n\r\n   This place is not one to just keep things inside all bottled up, if theres an idea out there you will see if from the regulars here and alot of the new pimps aswell.\r\n\r\n  The internet was made for the sharing of info and this is one site that you will find that is all about the free clear info :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34438, 'cb9ceef6f1', '', '[quote:cb9ceef6f1="cyborgzero"]\r\nWell, being introduced in this thread as "turkey" sorta pissed me off to begin with.. PHt doesn\'t even frikken know me and is calling names behind my back?[/quote:cb9ceef6f1]\r\n\r\nsilly nugget, like I give a shit......\r\n\r\nthis thread has gone from a great techo development thread into a pissing match.......\r\n\r\nthe next comment I make will be to do with the tech and not the bullshit, it\'s just a waste of time.\r\n\r\nFrom cyborgzero\'s suggestions:\r\n\r\n1)  Dude, I\'ve tried this already, unfortunately it\'s a no go.  The two resistors in question, when shorted out (ie: a wire bypasing them) don\'t add any extra voltage to the gate pins on the n-chan fets for fwd or rev.  Also, you read the value of the resistor incorrectly  :smile: , the resistor going to the gate pin on the reverse fet is 300 Ohm [301] not 1K Ohms [103], something easy to do, specially with surface mount.    You are right though, the gate voltage needs to be raised to at least 2V to be feasible.  (See my previous post re: Gate voltages vs. Rds(on)).   As an experiment I manually put 3V on the gate pin of the fwd fet and the car just flew!  So I now know the goal of what we are all working to.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34439, 'ac919b4176', 'do the mash, do tha monster mash!', 'http://www.ausmicro.com/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=1664&amp;FORUM_ID=9&amp;CAT_ID=2&amp;Forum_Title=BCG+%2D+Technical&amp;Topic_Title=do+the+mash%2C+the+monster+mash%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E&amp;whichpage=1&amp;tmp=1#pid21516\r\n\r\nYeah!\r\n\r\nSorry fellas, would of posted the whole thread but I gots to conserve picutre bandwidth these days.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34440, '818042a488', '', 'The Super Bits are improved. The new chassis handles better. The cars come in A,B or C frequencies, and the controller can be switched to control any of the 3 frequencies. The new PCB has more power, and the bodies, well you just have to look at them.\r\n\r\nThe range is not great on them, but no worse than the original Bit Char-Gs. The difference being, when it loses signal it remembers the last command. Which is particularly annoying when racing on a track. It really sucks when you\'re making good laps, then all of sudden you car starts beating itself into the wall repeatedly.\r\n\r\nAnother gripe people have, that doesn\'t bother me so much, but I gotta admit, it is annoying, is that the controller has 2 buttons that do nothing (yet).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34441, 'b57dd82dad', '', 'Just look at the 2 chassis, the visual diferences are obvious. Dave pretty much covered everything else.  Wheels &amp; tyres are smaller &amp; wider ala PullBacks.');
