INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34451, '3dec271e59', '', 'here\'s my entry\r\nRX-7 "Headlights Edition"\r\nfeaturing...CF hood\r\n                Painted rims\r\n                Custom made headlights\r\n                Custom spoiler\r\n                Clone 2.2 motor\r\n                2 speed chassis\r\n                Boston Acoustics decals\r\n\r\n[img:3dec271e59]http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/uploads/post-23-1072213950.jpg[/img:3dec271e59]\r\n\r\n[img:3dec271e59]http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/uploads/post-23-1072209341.jpg[/img:3dec271e59]\r\n\r\n[img:3dec271e59]http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/uploads/post-23-1072209399.jpg[/img:3dec271e59]\r\n\r\n[img:3dec271e59]http://www.microrccenter.com/forum/uploads/post-23-1072209455.jpg[/img:3dec271e59]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34452, '0ddfe67f47', '', '[quote:0ddfe67f47="ph2t"]From cyborgzero\'s suggestions:\r\n\r\n1)  Dude, I\'ve tried this already, unfortunately it\'s a no go.  The two resistors in question, when shorted out (ie: a wire bypasing them) don\'t add any extra voltage to the gate pins on the n-chan fets for fwd or rev.  Also, you read the value of the resistor incorrectly  :smile: , the resistor going to the gate pin on the reverse fet is 300 Ohm [301] not 1K Ohms [103], something easy to do, specially with surface mount.    You are right though, the gate voltage needs to be raised to at least 2V to be feasible.  (See my previous post re: Gate voltages vs. Rds(on)).   As an experiment I manually put 3V on the gate pin of the fwd fet and the car just flew!  So I now know the goal of what we are all working to.\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:0ddfe67f47]\r\n\r\nDude, im dyslexic as hell lol esp when my eyes are crossed in my microscope. ;) \r\n\r\nHrm, well, I am trying to increase the source voltage going into the driver chip on the upper left that is connected to the gate drivers... \r\n\r\nThere are two sources of power, one is 2.9 volts or so, and another is 1.67.. I am thinking the 2.9v is the source for the gate drivers, and the 1.67 is internal operation voltage.\r\n\r\nSo, what we are dealing with seems to be that we take 2.9v, knock another .7 volts or so off of it lost to the chip inner workings, and then you get a gate drive that ends up 1.5 or so pulsed peak to peak.. I am not sure about eh pulsed part, but I will verify it on a scope.\r\n\r\nSo, get more power to the drive side of the chip and you are golden. We can totally bypasss the rest of the BS.\r\n\r\nRob');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34454, 'dcd0d71be8', 'HELP! my best bit (clone) WONT CHARGE!', 'i bought a bunch of clones to mod and add to my previous bit collection, i had about 3 clones of the same kind before these and they worked fine. I bought a subaru, the rx7, and a hummer. now when i put the rx7 or the hummer on any charger, it just makes the charging light dimly glow. all the chargers have freshly bought duracell AAs and it seems to be the cars. Im no idiot with the technical side of bits, so i popped it open and looked at the contacts and the battery connection, looks ok. WHATS WRONG! that hummer rocked! thanks guys~~');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34455, '78ec13c94c', '', 'well my cuzins career in racing the cars consists of, his small kitchen floor, my living room hard wood, my grandmoms basement, and the floors in the mall, basicly, nothing requiring long range. i told him about how the cars do the "keep on going thing", he was kind of wowed, he thought it would be fun to chase it lol. i told him they were completly out of stock on the internet, and all the kids in japan bought the last bunch... so hes really down about not getting one. so i get to give it to him on christmas eve.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34456, '71cf53a90d', '', 'you\'ve got a scope?  you lucky bastard!  :D \r\n\r\nThis is an idea I was toying with as well.   The three pin chip on the pcb is a dcdc converter, prolly the ME301 chip that was made popular on the 1st gen zz, bits, etc....   So the output is 3V for a "less than 3V input".   If we could use another DCDC converter to up the voltage to say, 5V then hopefully as you said the output would be higher than the 0.9V that we are getting.   I\'m hesitant to do this \'cause I don\'t know the operating range of the IC\'s on the pcb and I\'ve only got the one zz se!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
