INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34621, 'fa009c1728', '', 'Thanks TM.   Yeah I still have a whole bag of fake trees, grass, rock and stuff, but I screwed the racing surface up and need to get that just right first.    I won\'t be able to fit as much scenery as I was originally planning, but should be able to try out all the media types.  At least, the 6X3\' board is much, much easier to handle. (narrowed 9" after the rebuild).\r\n\r\nI sanded the imperfections flat, and wanted to cover the track with a flat black primer.....  But the primer reacted with chalkboard paint and blistered, and cobwebbed.   So I\'ll need to wet-sand and feather that a couple times with a few more coats of flat black acrylic enamel.   The chalkboard paint was just way too much traction.   I need a surface that will allow the cars to push (powerslide),  a little at higher speeds, without that killer twitchy feeling.    (and still turn sharp at lower speeds.)\r\n\r\nOn a positive note though, I did fix the banked curve today, putting in a low flat lane (or rumble strip), so cars wouldn\'t get stuck there................\r\n[img:fa009c1728]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/track19.jpg[/img:fa009c1728]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34622, 'c79579b4f4', 'Monster Bit Video: Thrashin\' on concrete....', 'Ok then, took the monster for a test drive on the concrete out back and she\'s showing promise. Got a few things to fine tune but sofar so good!\r\n\r\n[img:c79579b4f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/monster/proto1.jpg[/img:c79579b4f4]\r\n\r\n[img:c79579b4f4]http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/monster/proto2.jpg[/img:c79579b4f4]\r\n\r\nSpecs:\r\n\r\nGen 1 LXX booster pcb - 57Mhz\r\nTOMY chassis\r\nDaul cell 200mAh Nimh\r\n8.25:1 Gears (green ones)\r\nEM3.8 Vanquish motor\r\nMosfet modded - single stack\r\n\r\n\r\nHere\'s some video (Divx format) of the monster in action. Note: she\'s a booster so you will notice a distinct difference in speed at times.\r\n\r\n\r\nEnjoy pimps:\r\n\r\n\r\n[url=http://www.users.bigpond.com/matt.marcos/bit_g/monster/monster_final.avi]Video (5MB)[/url]\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34623, '64477aa4de', '', 'U gotta judge that, then we\'ll judge it!\r\n\r\nLet\'s see an ass shot Pimp!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34624, '9f2f9ed42d', '', 'Here\'s one I\'ll call, "How I crammed a 8\' x 4\' track in my tiny apartment"\r\n\r\nSo the wife stole the dining room table to use as her work station, leaving a big empty space, where the Christmas tree sat the last couple months. Now Christmas is over, and I\'ve moved in.\r\n\r\n\r\nHere we see it put up, to make the wife happy.\r\n\r\n[img:9f2f9ed42d]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/track3.jpg[/img:9f2f9ed42d]\r\n\r\nSince I had the dart board set up there already, that makes this kinda of a gaming area. I just put stuff that was in the way elsewhere, and was light weight, so it would be easy to move. \r\n\r\nSo I can just flip it down, and be set to go like this,\r\n\r\n[img:9f2f9ed42d]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/track4.jpg[/img:9f2f9ed42d]\r\n\r\nDamn kid, already all up in my Kool Aid.\r\n\r\nAnyways, it\'s too bad I live in an apartment, because if I lived in a house, I\'d go \'Monster House\' on it, and hinge it to the wall, and put flip down legs on it. So I could just undo a latch, flip it down, and the legs would flop out.\r\n\r\nSomeday maybe...');
