INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34634, 'affa71e84a', '', 'My kid\'s 3 and a half. Up until this point I\'ve had to hide in the bedroom, with the door locked to enjoy my cars, because he pretty much turns into a spazz around them.\r\n\r\nThat was one my biggest fears about this track, not being able to hide from him, but it\'s worked out well, \'cause his favorite game, and my biggest problem is that he likes to play dinosaur, and try to step on my cars, but with the nails sticking out, if you accidently step on one it hurts like hell, and he must have found that out the hard way, because he absolutely will not step on this track. So now he\'ll just sit by the sidelines and watch, which is handy, \'cause I have an automatic car flipper now.  :lol: \r\n\r\nI feel for that poor Motorworks car. I tried to give my kid a Thunder Charger, but when he killed it after a couple days, I stole it back for parts.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34635, 'b6f1bfb209', '', 'So what\'s up? You know something? :???: \r\n\r\nAww man, don\'t make us wait and see, give us a clue at least. :grin: \r\n\r\nC\'mon help us out, I hate surprizes. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34636, '38323090bc', '', 'It\'s starting to sound like 40mhz sucks.\r\n\r\nBoth my super bits are 40 mhz. Stock I only got 5-10 ft, which is the way my first bit was before I removed the crip cap.\r\n\r\nI untied the knot in the antenna, and ran it out the back of the PCB, and now I get 15-20 ft, like all my other MS/Tomy cars, but it still glitches within that range, which is why I wonder about the 40mhz, but in all fairness, I think all my cars glitch slightly, and it\'s just more noticable, because the Super bits keep going when they glitch.\r\n\r\nFigure I live in a small apartment with TVs, a computer, a fan, a thermostat, flourescent lights, and a fridge, all with in a small area. It\'s no wonder my cars glitch sometimes.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34637, 'e22016769e', '', 'I hear ya, Comrade B. I\'ve been playing on a 4\'x4\' track, and while it was cool at first, I was busy FET modding all my cars, and making them all too fast for it. Now I gots me a 8\'x4\' track, and it\'s so nice being able to hold that button down for more than a sec, and hear my cars wind all the way up on that 8ft. straight. \r\n\r\nYou gots to build another track. ;)\r\n\r\nOh and relevant to the original topic, I found 1/2" vinyl tubing at my Lowes in the \'Plumping\' aisle with all the other pipes, and stuff like that. Not sure what it\'s intended for, but it\'s \'Not for icemakes\'. It was only 18 cents a foot. I spent about 9 bucks for 50\'.\r\n\r\nIt may not be the most true to scale way to make barriers, but it\'s very functional. Flexes easy for curves. It just the right height and shape to hold the cars in. The cars slide on it good, and it\'s soft enough they just bounce right off without damage.\r\n\r\nVinyl tubing gets 2 thumbs up from me.');
