INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34685, 'a70897a168', '', 'I was runing my Enzo last night trying different rotors.  The 1.6 stock is pretty decent, I\'m surprized, but my KITT 2.2 &amp; 2.6 rocks in the SBCG, very fast!  I tried those and the Perf 2.2, 3.0, 3.8, 4.2P, 4.2K, Phast, Ex1 3.2, Ex1 3.5, Ex2 2.4, Ex2 3.5, &amp; Ex2 3.8.  \r\n\r\nThese SBGC are the greatest handling Bits ever, the only rotor that consistantly flipped it was the Perf 4.2K.  But one thing I did notice, and it was obvious was the [b:a70897a168]"glitch"[/b:a70897a168]!  It seem the larger the rotor, the more it glitched!  After trying all these rotors and returning it back to the 1.6, not 1 single glitch and the range was 30\'+, no shit with a 40mhz "b"\r\nAnother strange thing that happened, out of all the rotors I ran last night, only the Phast motor squealed like hell !  It\'s the first time ever hearing that since my HO days.  A drop of oil will take care of it but why that rotor?\r\nThey\'ve all been sitting just as long and some even longer........Hmmmmmm?\r\n\r\nWhile I\'m home this week, maybe I can get around to doing the rotor comparison I promised to do back in the summer.......We\'ll see.');
