INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34699, '7197fda3d7', '', 'Hi Dave,   I would go ahead and hinge the board to the wall if you\'re going to be there another year or so at least.   With the collapsable legs and all.   Sounds like a great idea.   It\'d be easy enough to fill hte holes with spackle, and looks like a relatively small wall nook to paint.\r\n\r\nI sanded my track and put some primer on it to fill some imperfections.  The primer lifted, but when dry, I took some laps on it anyway.   Now, the car really PUSHES going around the sweeper, very unlike the traction I had with the chalkboard paint.  (I liked that the car was alot less "twichy")  I\'m going to end up using a flat acrylic enamel, which I hope is a happy median between the two.   Thought I\'d let you know since you were having some traction problems.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34700, '4dbac8c044', '', 'funny, I\'ve just been listening to the strokes lately at work.\r\nI think they\'ll find their way into the rotation soon.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48524, '7353adc692', '', 'Euro 2004 rullez!!! Yesterday was another great game. Too bad dutch team and fans are going home, coz they really are great supporters. This last week everyone was crazy here in Portugal. Everyone is waiting to see what Portugal will do and so far they haven\'t messed up. First nuestros hermanos, Spain.  :-(  Then was the turn of those hooligan brits (great game against them) and now was time for Holland to go home. Oh and the dutch goal was offered by Jorge Andrade (portuguese player). It was a bit of hospitality from the Portuguese Team.  :grin:\r\n\r\nToday we\'ll see who will be Portugal opponent in the final: Czech Republic or Greece. I want it to be Greece, coz those bastards defeat us in the first game of the championship and we\'re seeking revenge  :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34702, 'a8216ac2f6', '', 'I got an email from Brian of R/C Butlers (they are making alot of aftermarket items for the xmod on ebay).\r\n\r\n"Hi,\r\n  Not shure if we would be interested, send us information, cad drawings, cost , market  ect..  If you know hwta the chassie should be like and you can get us one, we will make one up when we gwt time and send it off to you, and you can test it out.  we really dont have a bg interest in zip zap\'s but if the ppl need the chassie and we can make it what the heck.\r\n \r\nBrian\r\nRC Butlers"\r\n\r\n\r\nI can\'t spare a chassis (only 1).  Anyone destroy theirs yet that send the chassis off (look at it this way you get a better one in return from them)?  You guys with the super fet versions would be perfect to judge just how well a better chassis would help (corner roll/etc at those high speeds).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34703, 'cf11089bfd', '', '[quote:cf11089bfd="HirotoR34"]damn sess, that is some artistic shit! Great as always. I gotta ask.. where\'d you get the dshaft and the lock nuts?[/quote:cf11089bfd]\r\n\r\nThanks man.\r\nI got the CF Dshafts from a cat called sluggbugg from over at tinyrc. He sends ya 3 shafts cut at different factory lengths for $10.\r\nHis email is  slugbugg@ameritech.net\r\nThe weight of these shafts compared to the weight of the stock shaft is extremely noticible. I think the stock was weighed at 4oz and this one didn\'t even register on a scale that starts at 1oz, or something like that. :lol: \r\nI got it more for the "cool" factor than any performance benefits it may give me.\r\nThe nylock nuts are nuts for mini Z wheels. They have a lil nylon washer dealie built into the nut that helps keep the nut on the lug. I picked them up locally but if you do a search for them on the net I\'m sure you\'ll find them.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34704, '70b52da4ef', '', '[quote:70b52da4ef="CaboWabo"]funny, I\'ve just been listening to the strokes lately at work.\r\nI think they\'ll find their way into the rotation soon.[/quote:70b52da4ef]You guys know I have a few opinions about music, well I happen to have some very strong opinions about the Strokes, so here it goes...\r\n\r\nWhen I read about these guys in the mags, they were comparing them to everything from Wire, to the Cars. They were the critic\'s darlings, and everyone loved them. On top of it, the guy that produced the album is a regular at fenderforum.com, where I used to hang out. So I had to have this album, and ran out and bought it. \r\n\r\nI hated it. Absolutly could not stand it. I had to skip throught the first song, then the second, and by the third that CD was outta there.\r\n\r\nThen one day MTV2 was on MTV, and I caught their live European performance of "Last Night". I hadn\'t made it to that song before, and I loved it. I was also blown away by their stage prescence, and to top it off, they play through the same amp that I have, which just further endeared them to me.\r\n\r\nDuring the time my wife spent in hospital, I became profoundly depressed, and that was the only album I listened to. It\'s funny how an album I hated, is now very personal to me.\r\n\r\nSo anyways, yeah the Strokes are cool, you should throw some of that on the playlist. Might be a good idea to let this second album grow on me before I run out to buy it. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34705, '26c194d3ae', '', 'yeah, once this is all done I will put up a completed diagram of what to do..\r\n\r\nIn advance, go ahead and do the mosfet mod.. Either way thats gotta be done..\r\n\r\nThen I will show how to reroute the gate of the FWD 6401 P-chan fet to get decreased resistance and increased speed.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34706, '11a6ad9313', '', '[quote:11a6ad9313="SilentWolv"]Hi Dave,   I would go ahead and hinge the board to the wall if you\'re going to be there another year or so at least.   With the collapsable legs and all.   Sounds like a great idea.   It\'d be easy enough to fill hte holes with spackle, and looks like a relatively small wall nook to paint.\r\n\r\nI sanded my track and put some primer on it to fill some imperfections.  The primer lifted, but when dry, I took some laps on it anyway.   Now, the car really PUSHES going around the sweeper, very unlike the traction I had with the chalkboard paint.  (I liked that the car was alot less "twichy")  I\'m going to end up using a flat acrylic enamel, which I hope is a happy median between the two.   Thought I\'d let you know since you were having some traction problems.[/quote:11a6ad9313]Yeah, you know it would be easy to fill the holes, only prob, we\'re not even allowed to use nails to hang pictures. We have to double stick tape everything. If they came in to do their yearly fire alarm inspection, and saw my track bolted to the wall, I\'d  be getting a fine, fer sure, they\'re fine happy here.\r\n\r\nBefore you try the flat acrylic, try sanding the primer with something like a 800 grit sandpaper, to see what a smoother surface will do for you. That\'ll also give you a smoother base surface if you do go with the enamel. Let us know how that works, \'cause I\'m still debating how to get the traction dialed on my track.\r\n\r\nI\'ve always got my best balance of traction and slip on smooth shiny surfaces. From what you\'re saying about the primer, I\'m thinking my best bet would be to get my track surface smoother, and then go over it with a couple more coats of the gloss enamel.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34707, 'f0e7ac2e3b', '', 'MRCC was the first forum I came across. I thought they were ignorant there. Then I saw someone\'s sig that said, "I got banned for mentioning t!nyrc.com"\r\n\r\nI thought, "Hey, if you get banned at the mere mention of the name, then I gotta check this place out."\r\n\r\nFirst thing I saw at TRC was Silla\'s hooptie, w/ the rag hangin\' out the gas tank, and thought, "What a cool guy, I think I\'ll hang out here."\r\n\r\nSo I just think all the stories about them are funny, \'cause I never even bothered with them in the first place.');
