INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34729, '3cc2a9fd05', '', '[quote:3cc2a9fd05="payaso"][quote:3cc2a9fd05="crazydave"]\r\nFirst thing I saw at TRC was Silla\'s hooptie, w/ the rag hangin\' out the gas tank, and thought, "What a cool guy, I think I\'ll hang out here."[/quote:3cc2a9fd05]\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks for the props Dave.. I certainly enjoy this place alot more...\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:3cc2a9fd05]Hey man, I just tell the truth.  :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso it wasn\'t fair for me to generalize MRCC as ignorant when I stumbled on it, because I do remember seeing sezziz, and a few other names around there. I just got that impression, because I was looking for info on the 3.8 I just ordered, and everything I read there denied it\'s existance, and said the Tomy 3.0 that they sold their shop was the fastest. Over at Tiny RC people were free to speak the truth even if TRC didn\'t carry it in their shop. I appreciate that about them.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34730, 'c766b51fc5', '', 'my two cents.....\r\n\r\nI first started at tiny and found the place very informative and enterprising.  This was back in Jan 03 when I first got into the hobby.  My biggest contribution over there was my propo controller emulator thread in the Science forum.  After a while though I noticed that there were a lot of dickheads just wanting to do neon body underglows \'cause they all just went and saw 2f2f and that drove me up the fucken wall.......\r\n\r\nI found ausmicro in about april 03 I think and started hanging out there, I was absolutely amazed that there was an aussie-centric forum for micro-rc given the fact that the commercial market in aus was very small (I didn\'t even realise that TOMY realeased an aussie legit version called the Compact Char-G until about may/june, doh!).  I like that place and like to hang around on it.  For some reason ausmicro doesn\'t get the "yank-glut" that the american based forums get.  What I mean by this is all the young dickhead posters that just bring the boards down.  I don\'t mean to associate this totaly with you yanks but given the structure and size of the various markets for micro rc around the world, by shear numbers (in the usa) this happens unfortunately.   Bottom line, I consider ausmicro my main home.\r\n\r\nBitpimps I came across sorta by accident.   One day tinyrc was down  and I was talking to Shypo (ex mod from ausmicro now) and he gave me a link to here detailing this issue.  Then I realised that all the mods from tinyrc hung out here.   I saw that noxorc was a member as well. (I had helped out nox a little while earlier from the tinyrc days with hosting his demo software for his Comp Controlled Bit project).   So I joined and got a great reception and found out that this was [b:c766b51fc5]the[/b:c766b51fc5] place to be.  There was no BS and and post quality was mega high.  I got to say that for all the arty stuff (painting, detailing, bodymodding, etc...) my knowledge has improved because of this site alone and for that pimps I thank you.\r\n\r\nMRCC has always been a funny one for me.  I must admit that there are some really nice guys on there that honestly do contribute to the scene.  People like MadScott, ripper77777 and Gfunk are all pretty cool.  Then there is mah local boy Oldtamiayphile who has now left MRCC as well due to recent infighting.  Man, OTP [b:c766b51fc5]was[/b:c766b51fc5] MRCC.   Generally I gots to say that there is a lot more techos per capita on MRCCC than say pimps or even ausmicro but they don\'t realy show their heads all that often.  I will admit that I\'ve had some great techo discussions on that board.  But these days I visit it more infrequently than before.\r\n\r\nSo bottom line pimps my homes are ausmicro and pimps.  The serve as great places to hang and I\'m honoured to be known as a pimp and reprezent accordingly  :D ......\r\n\r\nph2t');
