INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48441, 'b16f70b979', '', 'Enjoy the bounty my nubian sisters.\r\n\r\nIf you need bigger prints (the target freebie is for 4x6 only) then I suggest Costco...They do up to 11x20 (or something like that) and the prices are pretty damned good (their 8x10s are only $1.99 each).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48442, '7c2e0f71ce', '', 'That\'s cool, I\'ve kinda been interested in an Epoch, but at $80 it still aint cheap.\r\n\r\nI guess it\'s not that bad really, but I just love bits cause they\'re so cheap and simple. I guess that makes bits kinda "ghetto" in the hobby world. So I guess I\'m just a "ghetto hobbyist".');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34753, '14efa0d991', '', 'That is truly excellent work. I\'ve been tossing a similar idea around my head for months, but you actually implemented it. Which is cool, because it\'s easier to work from example, but I\'m still jealous you did it first. :-(');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34754, 'aad2b1ce19', '', 'Hey is that you on the end hiding your head? :-) \r\n\r\nDon\'t worry, I\'ll be safe from da fuzz...hiding under my covers trying to get some sleep so I can get up early for work tomorrow. :roll:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34755, 'ff1c0ca0b5', '', 'Not bad for your first paint job. Sounds like you have the right attitude. That\'s all any of us can do, is learn from our mistakes. I\'ve made pul-lenty of mistakes.\r\n\r\nI don\'t really reccomend using any pen for large coverage like the hood. I\'d reccomend that you mask and spray something like that. Small details it\'s best to use a detail brush, and some paint, but you could get away with a permanent marker. Black Sharpies are kinda purplish, but I\'ve found these ones called "Ink Tanks" that are nice and black, and if you use them when your clear coat is still fresh, they stay on really good.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34756, '8c877636c6', 'Atomic Toys and Z-Cars...', 'I went to atomictoys.com to see what they\'re up to with the Z-Car. \r\n\r\nIt\'s turbo now, when did that happen? That might be pretty cool.\r\n\r\nThey also have cool looking tanks, and an airplane, that I might just buy for the cool looking charger.\r\n\r\nWhere\'s a good place to get Z-cars online? I\'ve only seen them at hobbypeople.com, and their site isn\'t loading for me today.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34757, '277c573580', '', 'I\'ve got an SE on its way to MicroAmps, when it gets back, it gets a king 4.2, 3.5g Lithium polymer battery (3.7V), lightened, the steering improvement mod (did this with my other SE: it makes a HUGE difference), lowered body (as much as possible: still need to figure out how to locate the LiPoly cell), Bit Sprinter 6mm wide aluminum rims,  graphite dust lubrication, and the X2 chrome body (internally hollowed).  I\'m also looking at making a bronze bushing for the drive axel to prevent plastic from melting and to keep the floppy rear axel perfectly against the gears. \r\n\r\nLastly, I\'m putting in my red gear ball differential.  More on that:\r\nhttp://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;postid=152364#post152364\r\n\r\nFor the charging connection, A HO train 4 prong female connector mounted in the rear window: 2 pins for charging the Li Po battery, an extra as the "on", an extra as the guitar E-string antenna connection.  \r\n\r\nHow the connector will work:\r\nYou\'d plug in the "antenna connector" and it will be the resonant length (1/32 wavelength = 6.7" @27.5 MHz) antenna attached to a male 4 pin plug. A second pin will be the connection between ground and "on".  \r\nWith the antenna connector out, the battery is disconnected so I\'ll be sure to be shutting down when I put the car into its case (that\'s too short for the antenna without folding it up...).  Also, with the antenna out, you\'ll now be able to plug the peak charger in.  \r\n\r\n :blazin:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34759, 'adc0aac3a0', '', 'ditto on the excellent work comment...\r\nthat\'s awesome!\r\n\r\ngreat work betty, looks like hella fun to drive.... over just about anything lol');
