INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34885, 'fd1587d658', '', 'I\'m not into guns, but I do love to set things on fire and blow shit up. I usually make an annual trip up to this indian reservation in Washington that sells all kinds of stuff, and I keep a good box full for miscellaneous events like 4th of July, New Years Eve, Saturday, etc.\r\n\r\nMy dentist is Chinese, not that that makes much difference, except to illustrate his heritage for crafting his own. Every time I visit, he usually sends me home with a few, as well as a new toothbrush. About 2 years ago, he was pretty excited about his latest batch, and he gave me a couple. They were about the size of 2 film containers stacked together, with a fuse coming out of the middle. He made them with old brochures from the Mercedes dealership, cut and rolled, with hot glue "caps" in the end. Summer before last, after we had done all the "safe" fountains and whatnot, I thought it was time to try one out. I went out to the middle of the intersection in front of my house and lit the fuse and ran back toward the sidewalk. I was wearing soccer sandals, and one fell off about about 2/3 of the way back. I turned to go back for it and my wife was yelling "nooooo". So I stopped and just watched the fuse burn down.\r\n\r\nThen there was this blinding flash and a big boom. A really big boom. Like the kind that makes the entire neighborhood silent for a minute or two. The kind that makes the streetlights go out. The kind that brings people out on their porches after they had already gone in for the night. It quite literally knocked me back about a foot from the pressure wave. After I had a second to take stock of the situation, I realized my chest kinda hurt. There was the general pain from the blast wave, but then there was this more acute, localized pain in the center of my chest. I pulled my shirt collar down to reveal a white patch kinda shaped like Australia, with a bloody ring around the edges. I immedialtely started checking myself over for other shrapnel wounds or whatever, and then I found this chunk in the street, about halfway between where I was standing and where the bomb was. I picked it up and realized it was kinda shaped like Australia also. Basically what happened is the hot glue "plug" in the end of the bomb came shooting out like a bullet and hit me square in the chest. About 6 inches higher and I would have had a hot glue tracheotomy.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34886, '71e03b7630', '', 'Poten huh?\r\n\r\nhttp://www.brabus-online.de/prog10e.htm\r\n\r\n[b:71e03b7630]BRABUS SV 12 Biturbo [/b:71e03b7630]increased capacity engine, 640 hp / 471 kW, 1,026 Nm from 1.750 rpm, 310 km/h (electronically limited) \r\n\r\nWell 640 hp is nice. But what conserns me is the torgue.. 1026 nm from 1750 rpm? That gearbox cant be cheap!!\r\n\r\nIm definetly getting the benz!\r\n\r\n/Evo');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (34887, '632e282471', 'Re: How many fully automatic weapons are in your neighborhoo', '[quote:632e282471="hue35"]The latest Michael Moore documentary, Bowling for Columbine, is a great look at exactly that. That film made me want to move to Canada.[/quote:632e282471]I dug on that too, but ya know - maybe I was just nieve before, but this time around - I could totally see, hear, and feel his schtick.\r\nit was almost pathetic.\r\nfor instance, the part where he goes to charlton hestons house - frickin gold mine right there, he was doing awesome up until charlton left and then michael moore puts up a picture and does his routine - that\'s his schtick.\r\nI got bored with him like adam sandler - he hasn\'t grown much but in girth.\r\n\r\namericans will never give up their dumb ass kid rock, I\'m just a cowboy ways. and what sucks even more is some people are almost forced to carry depending upon what they do for a living and where they live.\r\nthat\'s disgusting, but that\'s also reality right now.\r\n\r\nthings are pretty clear.\r\ncrazydave hears automatic weapons - because he lives where he does (insert laundry list here - and add to that the fact that the state is a "right to carry" state)\r\nI hear shotguns and country boy shit - because I live where I do (insert laundry list here - and probably some jeff foxworthy)\r\n\r\nthe only mystery is...\r\nwho the hell am I anymore? lol');
