INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35031, '206651719c', '', 'Could be, i am sending my jota controller back today, because the car worked fine with the controller from my ferrari.\r\n\r\nIn my super bits i have the 3.0 from the SQW\'s - they are pretty fast, and doesnt glitch at all.\r\nI also tried with the 3.0 from the speed-set, but its god damn as fast as a 4.2! \r\n\r\n/Evo');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35032, '2247fa8337', '', 'Yea dvdshrink is the best thing (well simplest) for getting a dvd9 onto a dvd5 you just loose the extras.\r\n\r\n  DVD burners have come down in price alot and I bet they will get the the "under 100" section soon when the dvd9 burners come out.\r\n\r\n  I kinda wish I waited as I got my pioneer A05 when they first came out but oh well that just means I would have had to catch up on over 1000 dvd burns :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35034, '889868b7fb', '', '[quote:889868b7fb="soren"]sorry if this is such a dumb question... but i am a newb to these\r\n\r\nwhat is propo?[/quote:889868b7fb]\r\n\r\n  Propo is the stearing.\r\n\r\n  Normal bits and zips use a magnet for the stearing and its full on one left or right.\r\n\r\n  Propo (proportional) uses gear and motor stearing and lets you controll the distance the wheels turn(to an extent).  The propo in the se is nice but depending on your drining you might not use it.\r\n\r\n  I am also in Canada (as you know from our convo on msn) and Zips just came out here and are halping the market alot.  I can only hope to find more locals that will race with there own cars now and not mine lol, but thats ok cause I gots me the drag car from hell if they end up using my fetted cars (thanks CD :) )');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35035, '38f311c298', 'Possible ideas for future contest', 'This will be a brainstorming thread to throw out rough ideas while they\'re fresh in our heads, so we have a resource of ideas.\r\n\r\nI like the idea of battle bits, I think we\'ve all thought about, but no one\'s done it, so maybe a contest would help motivate people.\r\n\r\nI also would like to see more innovation with off road bits, and that made me think what a about a technical/engineering contest, that would be based on technical innovations, so it could include battle bits, off road cars, or whatever.\r\n\r\nAnother contest could be a \'Beat The Pimps People Choice Awards\'. Where the BP mods could compete to, because ultimately the judging will be up to the general population.\r\n\r\nMy final idea for now is the \'Ultimate Builder Showdown", they would be allowed unlimited entries, and instead of judging individual rides, w would judge by the overall quality of all the rides they enter, number of rides, versatility/well roundedness.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35036, 'f053543653', '', '[quote:f053543653="soren"]another thing i have noticed in pics is that the zipzap bodies are kinda ugly and sit very high on the chasis... does this bug anyone else? lol\r\n\r\ni think ill stick with bit char-g[/quote:f053543653]Yeah, I think that bugs quite a few people. The ZZ 350Z is not too bad, and the muscle cars are all really nice, but alot of the others do sit way too high in front. They look much better lowered.');
