INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35039, 'c4fcd49c4b', '', 'I see the Ol\' juices are flow huh Cavey ??\r\n\r\nWe had discussed a Truck Contest before which got put on the back Burner due to time constraints. We were going to call it The Truck-O-Treat Contest and end it Oct 31 of course. But having come off of 3 consecutive months of Contests it was decided to hold up on that idea and go with the present contest.  I still think we can do it for this years Halloween right guys  :???:  Any 1/64 truck can enter (converted cars, pickups, 4x4, brutes, etc)\r\n\r\nBeat The Pimps People Choice Contest sounds cool. That will have to be\r\nthoroughly discussed.\r\n\r\nUltimate Builder Showdown wouldn\'t be fair to all.  There are various types of skill levels which will always be the determining factor but when it comes to "quantity" that\'s where it gets foggy.\r\nEx: Say you enter 3 slammin rides, then #2 enters 6 lil less than slammin rides and it is determined by the overall quantity.  Now your 1 car may be the best I\'ve seen (California Bug), but I\'d have to give it to #2 cause he has 6 very well done quality rides entered, see where I\'m going with this ?\r\n\r\nThe biggest, most important thing about running any Contest is the Prizes!\r\nThis is first thing discussed after the contest idea, what, where, who ?\r\n\r\nI\'ve always liked the idea of Trivia Contests, something that won\'t take a lot of time or judging, the right answer wins, no extreme decisions have to be made. Prizes are small and available,  Quick &amp; Easy!  Got any Ideas?\r\nI suggested these be done in between our Car contests just to give the Pimps something to think on.  Nothing too extreme but not too easy either.\r\n\r\nI like your ambition Cavey, but that\'s what the BitPimps are all about.');
