INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35041, '865f9b5ffd', '', '[quote:865f9b5ffd="ph2t"]one of you pimps should do one of those evolutionary step diagrams, you know the one with the chimp on the left, ending up with the dude on the right.   Do it for these mods though, this car could be the first (nice work btw)....  \r\n\r\nNow to find that fucken soundrack, daaaa, daaaaa, Daaaaa, DA DAAAAAA!\r\n\r\nsorry couldn\'t help myself....can\'t wait for my body to arrive all the way from pimpcity... :D \r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:865f9b5ffd]\r\n\r\nMan U crack me up  :eek: \r\n\r\nCan\'t wait to see the finished product!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35042, '79cfb6f627', '', '[quote:79cfb6f627="DarkTari"]\r\nUltimate Builder Showdown wouldn\'t be fair to all.  There are various types of skill levels which will always be the determining factor but when it comes to "quantity" that\'s where it gets foggy.\r\nEx: Say you enter 3 slammin rides, then #2 enters 6 lil less than slammin rides and it is determined by the overall quantity.  Now your 1 car may be the best I\'ve seen (California Bug), but I\'d have to give it to #2 cause he has 6 very well done quality rides entered, see where I\'m going with this [/quote:79cfb6f627]Yeah, I see your point. It is just a rough idea, but here\'s my perspective on that one. Some people paint, some do electronics, body modding, etc. This contest would encourage people to try other things and become more well rounded. The quantity was probably not a good idea, but the idea there was that people with less developed skills could make up for that by knocking more rides, which would in turn build skills for later.\r\n\r\nThe main concept for all my ideas are to encourage creative thinking, and to force people to better themselves.\r\n\r\nEDIT: I just had a sudden realization. See this is the way I meant it. You brought up my Cali Beetle, which ok yeah I\'ll admit is very nice, but you produce tons of rides that are equally as nice, and the fact that you produce way more slammin\' rides that are almost as good as my one slammin\' ride deserves reconigtion, at least in this contest. \r\n\r\nThe idea here is not to judge by the individual ride but the over all quality, and when I say quantity, I should say the number of quality rides they have, in other words 20 crappy cars are not going to beat out one nice one, but 10 mostly top notch cars might beat out some one with 2 contest winning rides, and  8 so-so ones. See what I\'m saying?');
