INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35105, '452c87762a', 'I\'m starting to develop \'Pauly-isms\'', 'I started useing the phrase "I gotta tell ya" alot. I didn\'t know where I picked it up from, but I thought it was kinda catchy.\r\n\r\nThen I was watching American Chopper, when I noticed all the Tuttles do it... alot. I started making a game out of how many times they said it in an episode. Then I noticed Vinny and Cody had started doing it too. That\'s when I started calling them \'Pauly-isms\'\r\n\r\nAnother Pauly-ism is, "I gotta tell ya" is to start a sentence, but if it pops up in the middle of a sentence, you say, "...and to be honest with you"\r\n\r\nI had a few others but not currently watching it, my minds drawing a blank.\r\n\r\nOne more. Pauly Jr. seems to always need reassurance of his coolness. Watch whenever he finishes something up, or starts an engine, he can\'t just declare, "that\'s sick", he will always turn to everyone in the room, and say in a questioning tone, "that\'s sick, right?" to each one of them.\r\n\r\nI don\'t know, it cracks me up. I can\'t wait for the new season. That American Rodder should be cool too.');
