INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35256, '6cbb241a09', '', 'Well I did what you said, got bink and smack, and converted it to avi, added music, and then converted that to wmv(because the .avi was like 100 megabytes..), with windows movie maker... so, here it is, with a smaller filesize... I\'m terrible with the movie making crap, so, if anybody wants to edit the first one (the .mov) with a fade job at the beggining from like a screen that says "midget_man1387: just cruisin" or somethin like that, then fade out... you can also add different music... and if it\'s not to much, could you, at the end show my drift that\'s 15 seconds in... it goes from like 15:00 to 16 or 17... THANKS! and here\'s the link to the new one:\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.rcpics.net/view_single.php?medid=21175[/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35257, '9948ce8089', '', 'Ok, I know I\'m dragging up an old thread but I\'ve really gotten into my daul cell monster bit fet modded beast and now I\'m looking for the fastest motor possible.  \r\n\r\nSome observations:\r\n\r\nThe EM3.8 is the best motor in this beast.  At 50% speed the car runs quite fast and is comparable to a single cell 3.0-3.5.  At 100% speed (boost) this car just flies!  I cannot say it enough how fast it goes.\r\n\r\nI tried the perfection 3.8 in this same car and I found the performance comparable.  I couldn\'t really tell if it was a bit slower or not but I *think* the perfection didn\'t run as fast in 50% speed mode as the EM38 vanquish motor did.  Still in 100% boost the machine flys again!\r\n\r\nI then tried the perf 4.2 King in this beast and I noticed that the top speed was crap!  This is in 50% speed mode.  The top speed in this mode was less than 3/4 the speed of the 3.8\'s (EM and perf) in 50% mode.  When I went to 100% mode id did pick up speed but not to the same level as the 3.8\'s.\r\n\r\n[b:9948ce8089]So my question is this:  should I buy the bitchar-gmotor from tinyrc?  Is this motor the fastest motor out there?[/b:9948ce8089]\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35258, '8e5b113dec', '', 'ditto that');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35259, 'e62b098b05', '', 'no shit!\r\nI was just thinkin that same thing the other day....\r\n\r\ngood to see ya again Havok, days got ya all messed up? lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35260, 'e87ad10da7', '', 'I say yes, buy one and try it.\r\nI love EM\'s Vanquish, that baby is what I run my dual cell and it\'s the fastest car I\'ve got.\r\n\r\nnow... the bitchar-gmotors - I got from kyle way back when - before EM was around.\r\n\r\nand kyles motors were my favorite until I found the Vanquish... actually it still kinda is.\r\n\r\nI use the Vanquish for a perfect mix of power and speed.\r\nI use kyles 1.6 for straight balls to the wall torque.\r\nI use his 2.6 as a general motor, nice torque and good speed.\r\nI use his 3.8 to just fly at top speeds.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35261, 'f973e11208', '', 'Hey ph2t, what are the specs of that car? I got the Dual cell part. Is it just a straight-up mosfet mod, or are they stacked? Also, what gears? And finally, what chassis did you start with?... just curious.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35262, '881373c466', '', '[quote:881373c466="CaboWabo"]I say yes, buy one and try it.\r\nI love EM\'s Vanquish, that baby is what I run my dual cell and it\'s the fastest car I\'ve got.\r\n\r\nnow... the bitchar-gmotors - I got from kyle way back when - before EM was around.\r\n\r\nand kyles motors were my favorite until I found the Vanquish... actually it still kinda is.\r\n\r\nI use the Vanquish for a perfect mix of power and speed.\r\nI use kyles 1.6 for straight balls to the wall torque.\r\nI use his 2.6 as a general motor, nice torque and good speed.\r\nI use his 3.8 to just fly at top speeds.[/quote:881373c466]\r\n\r\nThanks for the info man.  With the bitcharg motors 3.8, have you put that in a fet modded chassis with the high speed gear set (green)?  I take it the EM3.8 gets to it\'s top speed before the the bitchargmotors 3.8 does?\r\n\r\nthanks dude,\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35263, 'e05dfcee49', '', 'Well, according to Micro_amps, my stock ZZ with a DKS 3.4 ran at 3.07 mph.  After stage 2 FETs (I thought that I might as well and pony up the extra cash), 4.74 mph.  Then, he dropped in a 4.2.  That ran at 6.67 mph.  The DKS 3.4 is actually running at 31,xxx rpms, according to Namuna.  So, a 4.2 should put out around 42k, I think.  Here\'s the math:\r\n\r\n31/4.74=6.540084388\r\n6.540084388*6.67=43.62236287\r\n\r\nThat\'s my shoddy math for \'ya, but the only way to know for sure is an RPM test.  Ahem...\r\n\r\nEdit: That\'s with 9.86 gears.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35264, '31ee8571c6', '', '[quote:31ee8571c6="hue35"]Hey ph2t, what are the specs of that car? I got the Dual cell part. Is it just a straight-up mosfet mod, or are they stacked? Also, what gears? And finally, what chassis did you start with?... just curious.[/quote:31ee8571c6]\r\n\r\nhey man, the specs are as follows:\r\n\r\nLxx 1st gen booster PCB, 57Mhz\r\nfet modded drivetrain (single stack) and fet modded steering\r\ndaul 200mah batts\r\nTOMY chassis\r\ntriple steering spring\r\nfrontend spring suspension\r\nTOMY high speed gear set (green ones)\r\n\r\nyou can see pics and the full developement thread at ausmicro:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.ausmicro.com/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=1664&amp;FORUM_ID=9&amp;CAT_ID=2&amp;Topic_Title=do+the+mash%2C+the+monster+mash%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E&amp;Forum_Title=BCG+%2D+Technical\r\n\r\nbasically this is the most fun car I have and I want to make it fast as hell!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35265, '50a9ff1562', '', '[quote:50a9ff1562="viperdout"]Well, according to Micro_amps, my stock ZZ with a DKS 3.4 ran at 3.07 mph.  After stage 2 FETs (I thought that I might as well and pony up the extra cash), 4.74 mph.  Then, he dropped in a 4.2.  That ran at 6.67 mph.  The DKS 3.4 is actually running at 31,xxx rpms, according to Namuna.  So, a 4.2 should put out around 42k, I think.  Here\'s the math:\r\n\r\n31/4.74=6.540084388\r\n6.540084388*6.67=43.62236287\r\n\r\nThat\'s my shoddy math for \'ya, but the only way to know for sure is an RPM test.  Ahem...\r\n\r\nEdit: That\'s with 9.86 gears.[/quote:50a9ff1562]\r\n\r\nthanks for that info dude, it\'s always good to get greater awareness of what\'s happening out there.   \r\n\r\nFor me though you can do all the tests you want, the bottom line is [b:50a9ff1562]landspeed[/b:50a9ff1562].  What speed does the car go when it\'s actually in use.  At the moment without any equipment to be able to ascertain exact land speeds one can only go on the visual "perception" of how fast the car is traveling.\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35266, '91e897112a', '', 'Exactly.  It\'s all about the power to weight ratio.  Once I get my car back (it got shipped a couple of days ago), it\'s getting a dual cell.  The goal with the car is to outrun an X-Mod.  I dunno if it can be done, but I sure as hell will try!\r\n\r\nEdit: Arrggghhh, I keep on forgetting to write stuff.  Anyway, ph2t, how do you make bit rear suspension?');
