INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35276, 'a95873cf02', '', '[size=18:a95873cf02]Ferrari Set review\r\n\r\nPart One[/size:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nYesterday i say goodbye to 300 polish zloty (80$).  :-? I got red box in return. :)\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo01.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nInside the box are:\r\n\r\n- red remote controller\r\n- red wrist strip\r\n- super Bit Char-G chassis with 2.2 motor\r\n- 3 Ferrari bodies; Testarossa, 512BB and F40\r\n- extra golden wheel set\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo02.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nYou dont fotrget to turn off your controller because there is ON led (instead of GO).\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo03.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nAntenna is the same as in some clones.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo04.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nChannel selection, useless because there is no cars without controller on the market. :?\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo05.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTwo mysterious black buttons are conncted to pcb. Hmmm... :???: Left one is connected to F2 and F2-, right one to the GND1 and VCC. Any ideas what it could be?\r\n\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo06.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nNew charging plate\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo07.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nPCB with cutted edges, pcb cover with antenna loop.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo08.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nNew chassis is more compact and made of different plastic with particles of metal (i think). Antimagnetic? Here with golden rims.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo09.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nBottom view\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo10.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nYou can change front wheels fast and without screwdriver.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo11.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nNew rear wheels are the size of old front wheels.\r\nRear\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo12.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\nFront\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo13.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTires are made of soft rubber similiar to Scala43 tires but a bit softer in my opinion.\r\n\r\nWrist strip. Well... :-? \r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo14.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\n\r\n[size=18:a95873cf02]Part Two - Bodies[/size:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nFront view\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo15.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nRear view\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo16.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTop view\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo17.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nSide view\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo18.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo19.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo20.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nBodies are very detailed and well (but not perfect) painted.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo21.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo22.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nBodies sits on the chassis to high, especially Testarossa. New zipzaps style? They have to be lowered.\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo24.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo25.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n[img:a95873cf02]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva/mrc/Ferrari/Photo26.jpg[/img:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t set white balance properly and ferrari red became a bit too orange.\r\n\r\n[size=18:a95873cf02]Part Three - Performance[/size:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nFrequncy - 40A\r\nMotor -      2.2\r\nBattery -   60 mAh\r\n\r\nI performed some tests using F40 body:\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]1. Charginig[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nCharging time is 50s.\r\nSelf discharging is very low. You can drive a car after 10h.\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]2. Driving time [/b:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTest one - car upside down on the desk\r\n\r\n- single charged, forward only -       4m40s\r\n- single charged, forward and left -  3m40s*\r\n\r\n- double charged, forward only -      10m46s\r\n- double charged, forward and left - 6m55s*\r\n\r\n- triple charged, forward only -        15m02s\r\n- triple charged, forward and left -   8m41s*\r\n[size=9:a95873cf02]*After this time there is not enough power for both motor and magnet.[/size:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTest two - driving on the carpet\r\n\r\n- single charged - ~2m40s\r\n\r\nAfter this time car is still driving but steering problems appear even at close ( ~50 cm) range.\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]Steering[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nTurning diameter on the carpet is 24 cm left and 20 cm right.\r\nTurning on wooden floor is difficult because car slips on it, but when i made nice 180\' turn, diameter was 16 cm.\r\nTires are quite sticky and get dust from the floor very fast and become skates. You can make rubber burning while trying to turn. :)\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]Speed[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nI tested speed on wooden floor (start from sheet of paper) and carpet. Distance was 2 m. In both cases time was 1.8 s. So speed is 1,11 m/s or 3,996 km/h. Scale speed is 256 km/h but should be 324 km/h with F40 body  :grin:\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]Range[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nThere is a "bug". :( After loosing a range car doesn\'t stop and continues its ride. :(\r\nFully charged (single) car range is 4,20 m\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]Pros:[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n- nice bodies and rims\r\n- smaller wheels\r\n- changing front wheels is fast and easy\r\n- good driving time\r\n- good range till it drops :)\r\n\r\n[b:a95873cf02]Cons:[/b:a95873cf02]\r\n- BUG!\r\n- price (in Poland)\r\n- bodies sitting to high on the chassis\r\n- lack of different tires\r\n- mysterious buttons\r\n\r\n[size=18:a95873cf02][b:a95873cf02]SCORE 8/10[/b:a95873cf02][/size:a95873cf02]\r\n\r\nMiva');
