INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35355, '6394022312', '', 'Thanks Sezziz,\r\nYou are taking on a great cause that will benefit each and every one of us.\r\n\r\nI did my small part and sent those artists at Road Race Replica\'s ( http://www.ho-slotcars.com/) my request:\r\n\r\n[b:6394022312]"Hi there Phil, Josh,\r\nI\'m one of the many who\'ve been bit by the micro RC thing.  Do you know if any of your bodies fit radio shack\'s Zip Zaps cars?\r\n \r\nLike many of the enthusiasts, I\'m in my 30\'s and its been fun racing others in my department at work in the cafeteria on the linoleum floor.  Your cars are works of art befitting the engineering and modifications we\'ve put in to make the cars operate unlike anything you\'d trust a kid with...\r\n \r\nThis link will show some of the extent to which the enthusiasts are going:\r\nhttp://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/index.php\r\n \r\nLet me know, and also let me know if there\'s any chance for a Miata slot car body (top down...).  I\'ve got one in 1:1 scale in red and I\'d love to get a body for my modified Zip Zap.  I\'ve read the Miata is the world\'s best selling sports car, I can\'t be the only one who\'d want one, I\'d bet!\r\n \r\nThanks, and again, excellent work!\r\nBrett"[/b:6394022312]\r\n\r\nMy favourite response to your question of interest  when reading the slot car forum was:\r\n[b:6394022312]"Re: Any interest...\r\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n How much fun can it be without a slot and pin? "[/b:6394022312]\r\n\r\nPoor, poor person. Please take a moment to feel pity for the uninitiated.\r\n :(');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35356, '09c6dbc335', '', 'http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2479&amp;highlight=jbweld\r\nis a good link for more on the epoxy axel.  I\'ve held off since I want a removeable rear gear until I figure out the best set up for the linoleum race course at my work...\r\n\r\nAny idea where I can buy Kit/Bit gears?  Never seen these at my LHS or anywhere else.  \r\n\r\nI\'m seriously thinking about experimenting with a resistor/capacitor on the motor to allow the voltage to ramp up at a reasonable level.  Ever heard of anyone trying this? This could be one amazing performance enhancer.  Otherwize, I\'ve just got to keep waiting for my uA SE...');
