INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35525, '4e2a75666d', '', '[quote:4e2a75666d="ph2t"][quote:4e2a75666d="CaboWabo"]I say yes, buy one and try it.\r\nI love EM\'s Vanquish, that baby is what I run my dual cell and it\'s the fastest car I\'ve got.\r\n\r\nnow... the bitchar-gmotors - I got from kyle way back when - before EM was around.\r\n\r\nand kyles motors were my favorite until I found the Vanquish... actually it still kinda is.\r\n\r\nI use the Vanquish for a perfect mix of power and speed.\r\nI use kyles 1.6 for straight balls to the wall torque.\r\nI use his 2.6 as a general motor, nice torque and good speed.\r\nI use his 3.8 to just fly at top speeds.[/quote:4e2a75666d]\r\n\r\nThanks for the info man.  With the bitcharg motors 3.8, have you put that in a fet modded chassis with the high speed gear set (green)?  I take it the EM3.8 gets to it\'s top speed before the the bitchargmotors 3.8 does?\r\n\r\nthanks dude,\r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:4e2a75666d]sorry man, not sure how I missed this one - anywho...\r\nnope, haven\'t put it (either) in a zz at all (no fet to make it worth while).\r\nI\'d have to say, for sure the Vanquish gets to top speed before the BCGMotors 3.8\r\nhowever, the Vanquish is just a pussy hair slower than the BCGMotors 3.8 in top end\r\nbut, the Vanquish is a more powerful motor (torque), and for the trade offs, I like the Vanquish better - especially for my typical driving habits\r\n\r\nI hope Todd (extrememicros.com) sticks around at least as a wholesaler because the vanquish is either 1st or 2nd on my list of best motors');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35526, 'bd88a57037', '', 'you aint kiddin\r\n\r\nI kind of got the feeling ph2t was feelin the same as me when I first got it...\r\nthe best I could say was "it was like a fish out of water"\r\nit just flips, flops, and goes nuts\r\n\r\nbut after playing with it for awhile, I\'m totally digging it\'s durability.\r\nI\'ve gone off my kitchen counter top (gotta be about 4 feet) on to the kitchen floor, and it was asking for more - I like that.\r\n\r\nI really like the fact that my lazy ass doesn\'t have to get up and flip it back on it\'s wheels if it happens to land on it\'s top - I can just go into "fish out of water mode" and I\'m back going.\r\n\r\nmy only complaint is that it doesn\'t turn left and right straight out.\r\nif it were a 6 way device - it would stomp all other micro r/c\'s lol\r\n\r\n[b:bd88a57037]edit:[/b:bd88a57037]\r\np.s.\r\ndid you check the tiny 3 wheel motion? lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35527, '4c0dc69fad', '', 'Bummer dude! Am I reading that correctly that you basically blew your weed off the coffee table and on to the floor in a fit of coughing. Hehe, the kind where your friends roll their eyes and mutter, "amateur."\r\n\r\nNot getting into the sorid details, but I was at a party once at my best friend in High School older brother\'s house. Classic. Anyway, a friend of his was the biggest coke dealer in town, and they were [i:4c0dc69fad]partying[/i:4c0dc69fad]. So he\'s got this mirror with a couple lines raked up, and a tennis ball sized pile off to the side that was probably worth about $2-3k. He (the dealer dude) was hot for this coulda-been-a-model-type girl with big hair (this was like 1984), and she was drunk as hell. He hands her the mirror so she could do the coke. She sets it down on the table, does a line and proceeds to sweep this guy\'s pile on to the floor (shag carpet) with her hair. It was pretty funny seeing a bunch of drunk, coked-out party people realizing that the rest of their party was awash in dog hair, dirt and lint. Oh the humanity!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35528, '71f075b674', 'Epoch indoor racer', 'Wow, just freakin wow. I just got my car today and all I can say is, Wow. Maybe I\'ll say a bit more. :???: \r\nThe car, for those that don\'t know, is 1/43rd scale and full propo.(put 2 bits head to tail and you got the size of the car)  You got spring suspension upfront and a tbar suspension in the back. The motors are hardwired, no poping in motors like bits/zips. I\'m also not finding to many hopups, but so far I don\'t see a need for them. I\'m thoroughly impressed with this car and if it weren\'t for the price I\'ld have many. :-)  :lol: \r\n\r\nPretty concise review by namuna over at tinyrc....\r\nhttp://www.tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=643');
