INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35633, '267682ec7f', '', 'hi.\r\nthanks for your help. yes I have tried the black pinion gear, and I was wondering if the white would be better, because it comes with the tomy bit racer 3.0 motor. I have seen some japanese instructions where you are told not to use the white gear with 2.2 or 2.6 motors, only with 3.0, but I have received a 2.6 motor a few days ago and it comes with a white gear. I got questioned about this and decided to ask for help to some experts in the business  :grin: \r\n\r\nThanks for your help once again\r\n\r\n\r\n:greenblob:\r\n\r\nmekinhux');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35634, '5df0f6af78', 'COLD Weather  (talking -40 F)', 'I know some of you are outside the USA.\r\nand some of you are in warmer temp areas....(AZ)\r\n\r\nbut it is swearword cold here in New England.\r\n			\r\n[quote:5df0f6af78]\r\nSunrise: 7:17 am    UV Index: 1, Minimal   Sunset: 4:35 pm\r\nMoonrise: 12:15 am     Phase: Last Quarter    Moonset: 11:26 am\r\nAverages and Records for Jan 15\r\n \r\nThursday:\r\nContinued bitterly cold. Windy with a mix of clouds and sun. Dangerous wind chills approaching -30F. High around 0F. Winds NW at 25 to 35 mph.\r\nThursday night:\r\nPartly cloudy skies. Cold. Dangerous wind chills approaching -45F. Low -21F. Winds NW at 10 to 20 mph.[/quote:5df0f6af78]\r\n\r\nI know homies from upstate NY should have colder if not the same temps as I have in middle New Hampshire.\r\nI\'m sure Stoli in Canada might report even colder temps..\r\n\r\nHaving a beard and mustash....it freezes instantly when I walk outside.\r\nLiving on the side of a mtn..(north facing) the winds are kicking up...\r\n\r\nanyone else liking this weather?  if ya dress right for it...it\'s great.\r\n\r\nat -40, you can take a glass of water, throw it in the air, and Ice will land on the ground.\r\n\r\n\r\n-nox');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35635, '5335eec354', '', 'The 7 tooth white pinion is not used on Bit Char-G cars.... It\'s intended for the "Bit Racers" they\'re the same, but non r/c. \r\n\r\nthe white will not mesh correctly with standard gearing.  Unless you do some tweeking to it.\r\n\r\n\r\nIf you use the red gearing from the bit reacer, you could pull it off. (make it work)\r\n\r\nThat\'s the reason the 3.0 "Lucifer Rotor" comes with the white, and black pinions. That motor will work in either car.\r\n\r\n\r\nHope that helps.\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
