INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35679, '7eb4f1227d', 'some new shiat from downunder', 'hey fellas,\r\n\r\ni got one of my old bodys out today thought i would have a little play around with putty see what i could do, i stuffed the back off it up but i got it as good as i could have. tell me watcha think?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:7eb4f1227d]http://pic10.picturetrail.com/VOL343/1801617/3470030/42979180.jpg[/img:7eb4f1227d]\r\n\r\n[img:7eb4f1227d]http://pic10.picturetrail.com/VOL343/1801617/3470030/42979179.jpg[/img:7eb4f1227d]\r\n\r\n[img:7eb4f1227d]http://pic10.picturetrail.com/VOL343/1801617/3470030/42979177.jpg[/img:7eb4f1227d]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35680, 'bd25be56cb', '', '[quote:bd25be56cb="payaso"]I\'d love to make a hard pack clay track for my bits and ZZs so I can get busy....[/quote:bd25be56cb]Yeah i forgot to tell you guys about the track. I made the track by taking a 4" wide paint brush, and using that to to brush away all the loose dirst and rocks, and get down to the hard stuff. In doing so I also happened to form my barriers. I then dumped a gallon of water over the whole thing, and got it good and flooded. Went away for a few hours to let it soak in. Then when I came back I brushed it off again, and sprayed it with a spray bottle.\r\n\r\n[img:bd25be56cb]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/dttrack2.jpg[/img:bd25be56cb]\r\n[img:bd25be56cb]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/dttrack1.jpg[/img:bd25be56cb]\r\n\r\nThe track was actually a partial success. It worked because the bits could run on it with out getting hardly any dust in them, as long as I sprayed it down every 15 minutes or so. It was a little too much for the cars though. The monster hill made it more a hill climb than a race track, and there was too many rocks in that area, that made it difficult to get the surface smooth enough for the bit to pass through cleanly. I think if I find an area with more clay, and less rocks, I should be able to make the perfect track. I\'m already planning the sequel...\r\n\r\n[quote:bd25be56cb="brenden123"]I also use ulead and i havnt figured out to do the slow mo bit\'s! how do u do it?[/quote:bd25be56cb]I don\'t use Ulead for that. I use Quicktime Pro to export as a image sequence, then I load the image sequence at 2 frames per sec. The original is 29 frames per sec.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nWell thanks guys. Glad you guys like it, that definately gives me incentive to do more.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35681, 'b2a464ff13', '', 'Hells yeah it\'s cold.  Up here in Maine (Southern bah haha makes it sound warmer) it\'s Balls cold as well.  Hey Nox I heard that on the top of Mt. Washington day before last it was -100 w/ windchill.  That is like 2 degrees off of coldest temp ever.  Totally fizukin sick.  I love this state, but DAMN this is pushing it.  Cars are broken down all over the place on the local and highways.  School is being called off here Bilbo due just to the cold.  My kid sister is lovin it, snow day and she can still go to the mall. :eek:   OK now where is the freezin mah arse off smiley. :x');
