INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35723, '767b0ca71a', '', 'Here in toronto, ontario, we\'ve been getting quite a chill. Windchill down to -45 celsius, (about -49,-50 f). All the homeless have been cleared off the street, and they are saying 20 minutes for exposed skin to get frostbitten. Right now, we\'re having our first break in temperature in the last 2 weeks, only -19 celsius (-2 f)! \r\n\r\nLast night, my friends handbrake got frozen in place, when he tried to put it down, the handle was actually bending and trying to spring back up.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35724, '68f1ee7954', '', '[quote:68f1ee7954="Cheesehead"]Go easy on him. You never know-his little brother might be a 1ee7 Haxor, and shut down this server for a looooooong time.\r\nThere\'s also the fact that I can make fun of  you for using NiMh batteries-as soon as I re-solder half the leads in my car back together, I\'m going Lithium! And I intend to RFFS a bitcharger, which will make both the throttle and steering PROPORTIONAL! and a RFFS can use up to 6 CELLS!\r\nRC airplanes leave you in the dust as far as technology goes.\r\nP.S. does anyone know what the 4.2 stands for? More windings=higher torque=lower speed, so that can\'t be right...\r\nPPS: does anyone want to try a Didel Coreless in one of these things? They run WAAAY faster than the stock stuff. A replacement LPS motor would work, or maybe an IPS if you drilled out the spot for it and use 3 cells.[/quote:68f1ee7954]\r\n\r\nI don\'t have any little sibs, or any brothers, just one older sister who can be so nasty.....makes hogjowlz look like a Buddhist!\r\n\r\nI use Nimh myself....not as advanced, but not as complicated to charge either.\r\n\r\nWhat\'s RFFS? I\'m guessing the big cheese ph2t invented that, knowing the bigshot he is  :???: \r\n\r\nmore torque can apply for higher RPM\'s, too. When you send out more current/voltage, torque increases-so do RPM\'s, you just need a mixture of high amperage and high voltage.\r\n\r\nThe airplanes do kick ass.....more speed, no resistance, no load, and don\'t worry what surface there is, but sometimes rain and winds can get in the way...then go inside, clean the area, and race away! Do airplanes even do 180\'s, or drifts, or whatever? Hmmm....');
