INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35785, '6f824b2f68', '', 'Hi!\r\n\r\nI like testing :) So i couldn\'t resist and did one.\r\n\r\nBoth pictures are saved with compression factor = 80  :???: \r\n\r\nFirst picture is  640*480.\r\n[img:6f824b2f68]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva//mrc/SizeS.jpg[/img:6f824b2f68]\r\n\r\nSecond picture is 2560*1980 resized to 640*480 with Bi-Linera (2 pass) method.\r\n[img:6f824b2f68]http://www.gdynia.mm.pl/~miva//mrc/SizeB.jpg[/img:6f824b2f68]\r\n\r\nThere is no difference (almost). So for internet pictures megapixels are not so important. Important is optics, CCD and electronic quality. But usually cameras with higher megapixels are better quality. :)\r\n\r\nCheers\r\nMiva');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35786, 'ac3ce29193', '', '[quote:ac3ce29193="crazydave"]I do use the macro setting, and get about 6 inches away. In the macro setting it cuts light. If put a light near it to compensate, the yellow light makes it look like crap, so I have to get up close to hit it hard with the flash, \'cause I\'m really just trying to get the colors accurate.\r\n\r\nI knew lighting was my biggest issue, in order to move back, but I thought I needed a flood, I never considered a flourescent desk lamp, I\'m gonna have to try that.\r\n\r\nYou might have noticed that I\'ve been taking some pics in the sun, to help with the lighting issue, but the sunlight is too harsh and contrasting, and again i have to hit it hard with the flash to get the colors balanced, but now I\'m wondering what would happen in the sun if I shut off the macro, and moved back.  :???:[/quote:ac3ce29193]\r\n\r\nFlourescent light will make the color worse than incandescent (it will turn green)... use a halogen desk lamp. They\'re a cheap and decent light investment. You can still use the macro setting even if you back up a bit. Try shooting 12 inches from the car, then crop in on the car.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35787, '022c629cd0', '', 'i opened it up and there was so much dog hair wrapped around that it came out like coils, big ass coils. well i basicly surgically disected the entire car, and removed all the dog hair. my dog sheds, now i no longer race in the house. i put it back together and drove it again, but even with the stage 2, white 8 tooth gear it still accels REALLY SLOW. im somewhat satisfied with the top speed even with this gear. but theres definatly something wrong with my car.');
