INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35810, '6c538526af', 'epoxy on the pcb?', 'Stupid motorworks pcbs. I swear the factory soldering job was done with bubble gum. After only a minute or two of working on the car, the wires just start to fall right out of the pcb. \r\n\r\nI was wondering if epoxy conducted electricity? I would like to dab a small amount on some of the pcb contact points to help keep them in place when I am working on the chassis. \r\n\r\nAnyone have any positives or negatives about this idea? \r\n\r\nThanks!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35812, 'a0a42f931a', 'Ichat AV+rendesvous', 'Apple makes 2 1ee7 apps called Rendesvous and Ichat AV. Rendesvous is sort of like netstumbler, in that it allows networks to be set up between 802.11x  cards and base stations. It\'s really easy to use, and, best of all, you do\'nt need a base station-just a few wifi cards. This means that, using ichat AV, which is some great software, two people in a biulding with Ibooks, small webcams, and WiFi cards, can talk to each other via WiFi.\r\nI recall that one clever student used it to relay a copy of a test (taken with the REALLY small digital camera he used as a webcam) to another student-even as math class went on!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35813, '7547d9e559', 'Pimps doing it down under!', 'Hey felllas, yes that\'s right.   Some Melbourne (AU) based pimps got together for the day and had some serious fun.  Check out the pics and video(soon) here:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.ausmicro.com/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=1743&amp;FORUM_ID=1&amp;CAT_ID=1&amp;Forum_Title=GENERAL+CHAT&amp;Topic_Title=melbourne+meetup%2C+the+aftermath%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E%2E&amp;whichpage=1&amp;tmp=1#pid22342\r\n\r\nA great day had by all.......\r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35814, '2259076baa', '', 'I dont think epoxy will conduct electricity. If you want them to stay in place, solder them back in and then put the epoxy over it to protect the connections');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35815, 'f18ce8cee0', '', 'I have a bunch of 35mm SLR gear, and I love it, but it\'s a different thing. I wouldn\'t use that camera for anything that was going to end up online. Like Miva said, the cool thing about digital is that it\'s free to use after the initial investment. I\'ve had my digital camera for almost 2.5 years, and I\'ve taken over 7,500 shots with it. I\'m damn happy I didn\'t have to pay for film processing for all those shots. Also... snap a pic, download it and post it is way faster than... shoot a roll of film, have it processed, make a scan.');
