INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35846, '78ef71f75a', '', 'Well I\'ve learned a lot since last time I had a MotorWorks.\r\n\r\nWhen I took it apart I saw every reason for it to steer stronger to the left. The coil was offset to the right. There was some flashing left on the right side of the coil holding part of the steering arm. The left magnet was crooked. There was a glob of glue hanging off the left magnet and the left front sat a tad higher.\r\n\r\nI fixed all that (not as bad as it sounds), and now it steers equally to the right as the left, but not super tight in either direction.\r\n\r\nNow I got to try to figure out get FETs in this thing, to see how that hardwired motor likes them.\r\n\r\nIt\'s not a dirt truck any more...\r\n[img:78ef71f75a]http://s2k-kidz.com/crazycars/bugmw.jpg[/img:78ef71f75a]\r\n\r\n...but I always have that body if I need it. \r\n\r\nNotice I put blue dots in the center of the rims to give them that authentic Centerline look.\r\n\r\nThis is gonna be another offroad car, but this will tide me over while I experiment with FETs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35847, '45415336dd', '', 'My cars generally take around a month to complete. Taking your time is the key to quality, and to have a good plan before you start. The best way for me is to have 2 or 3 going at once. That way, if I feel impatient there\'s something else to work on while I\'m waiting for something to dry.');
