INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35983, '7f1e3e2de5', 'Re: ?\'s about  microsizer hop up kit', 'I have been using the red hard suspension and it\'s clean and nice but you need a bigger place to "play"... About the springs I can tell anything about them, expect... damn they look really great...  :eek: Guess you got the picture  :grin:\r\n\r\nmekinhux');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35984, '2a75e2ef86', '', 'Now this is starting to get interesting. If we get the other forums involved, this could get huge.\r\n\r\nThe biggest problem I see is arranging an impartial panel of judges. I don\'t think peoples choice would be a good idea in this situation.\r\n\r\nI wonder if we had enough forums involved if Tomy, or Hobbico would take interest.  :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35985, '69c7e05237', '', 'sounds like a super fun and great idea (as everyone is saying... as long as the intentions are right and planning is in place)\r\n\r\nI love the idea, but I too can see how this could easily blow up in our faces and cause weird tensions.\r\n\r\nI haven\'t thought about it a whole lot, but I also like the idea of hold a "world" comp. though a world comp would be harder to get organized and actually kick off, it\'d still be cool.\r\n\r\nwith that said, if the "world" comp just can\'t happen for one reason or another, I\'d be down with the ausmicro vs bitpimps - all only for fun of course.\r\nafterall, most of us hang on both boards - we should do this purely out of fun and that\'s it.\r\n\r\nalso, let\'s touch on judging - who\'s the judges? who picks the judges? how will judging work? etc. etc.\r\n\r\nthat\'s gonna be a biggy, you know no matter who wins, looses, or doesn\'t even show up - there\'s gonna be some users questioning about favoritism.\r\n\r\nthere\'s not many options available to us for judging so I\'m wondering if it wouldn\'t be a good idea to take 1 judge or 2 from each site.\r\n\r\nanyways, it\'s an awesome idea and I\'m willing to help out however I can.\r\ngood to see others thinking in detail about this kind of stuff - it only makes things more fun, entertaining, interesting, etc. for everyone involved.\r\n\r\nlet\'s keep the convo going and try to work out some details and see how far we get.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35986, '2cc1a10ea0', 'Re: ?\'s about  microsizer hop up kit', '[quote:2cc1a10ea0="mekinhux"]I have been using the red hard suspension and it\'s clean and nice but you need a bigger place to "play"... About the springs I can tell anything about them, expect... damn they look really great...  :eek: Guess you got the picture  :grin:\r\n\r\nmekinhux[/quote:2cc1a10ea0]\r\n\r\nacctually they help quite a bit...they reduce flipping,and when you hit a small bumb you dont take a sharp turn to the right or left like you do with the non independent tomy sway bars...and they also offer independent sspension. check out www.rcmod.com they sell sme damn good springs');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35987, 'c3c7ad38f0', '', 'nope, never received any PMs about it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35988, '01d5ef75e5', '', 'The teal gear is about the most useful thing in that kit for speed, but it aint worth the price of admission. I found the hard ribbed tires useless for anything other than simulating driving on ice. The 2.2 motor is hardly impressive either. \r\n\r\nThe red sway bars are kinda cool. They press down on the steering knuckles, and have a spring like effect on the front end. Still though being such a tiny little piece of plastic they again hardly make it worth the price.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35989, 'f5f82a7759', 'What to do, what to do!?', 'First some background info (I\'ll try to keep it brief)...\r\n\r\nI bought a 25pack of blank DVDs from Meritline.com, price was steep for the pack but I saw a 128mb Memory Stick pop into my cart for free so I bit. Later that night I get email confirm of the order with the free mem stick. Cool! Nice deal!\r\n\r\nFew days later I get email confirm that they shipped the order...But WITHOUT the free mem stick and claimed they NEVER offered such a thing! But I have the proof and email it to them, they still won\'t give me the free mem stick and the damned package already shipped! Instead they offer free shipping to make up for the mistake (yeah right! $6 saved for free ship vs. $35+ value for mem stick?). I think NOT, I cancel.\r\n\r\nThey\'re supposed to send a shipping label (pre-paid shipping, since it was THEIR mistake) but I waited even an extra week (was supposed to have the label by 1/9/04) and didn\'t get it.\r\n\r\nYesterday I called my Credit Card company and dispute the charge, they take all the info and credit me the money (a form is on the way for me to sign and send back and it\'s all said and done)...But here\'s the thing, when I got home last night I FINALLY received the shipping label!\r\n\r\nSo, what do I do? I want to say SCREW THEM and keep the shit and have them duke it out with the CC company...But the Wife brought up a good point; What if they start hassling me about the package because they DID finally send the damned shipping label.\r\n\r\nHelp me out my Brothers, what\'s a guy to do?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35991, '0afe9b46de', '', '[quote:0afe9b46de="DarkTari"][quote:0afe9b46de="payaso"]not me....  I\'ve also got somehting up me sleeve....  \r\n\r\nWas it from denden?  \r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:0afe9b46de]\r\n\r\nWhy Yes It Was ![/quote:0afe9b46de]I remeber seeing his work at Tiny RC and being pretty impressed with it.\r\n\r\nI think he\'s a cool guy. In my opinion I think he was just trying to be cool, you know, he\'s kinda new here, and wants to be one of the hot shots, you know what I mean? I think we all do that.\r\n\r\nI\'d say make no promise about any contest, but try to get that body off him. (As you\'ve basically done) Cause I know I\'d sure like to get a body off him. ;)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35992, 'fcfd13f32b', 'Re: ?\'s about  microsizer hop up kit', '[quote:fcfd13f32b="micromatch"][quote:fcfd13f32b="mekinhux"]I have been using the red hard suspension and it\'s clean and nice but you need a bigger place to "play"... About the springs I can tell anything about them, expect... damn they look really great...  :eek: Guess you got the picture  :grin:\r\n\r\nmekinhux[/quote:fcfd13f32b]\r\n\r\nacctually they help quite a bit...they reduce flipping,and when you hit a small bumb you dont take a sharp turn to the right or left like you do with the non independent tomy sway bars...and they also offer independent sspension. check out www.rcmod.com they sell sme damn good springs[/quote:fcfd13f32b]\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks for the tip about rcmods.com!!! I have bought the TOMY suspension set and the most disappointing thing are the tyres. You really can\'t do any sharp turn with them because you slip even before starting to turn  :( The small red suspensions are a bit better than the original, at least I kinda like that "spring effect" they almost give ya  :-D \r\nNow I gotta look for a spring suspension to test it out and throw away those small red bars... just kidding   :smile: \r\n\r\nmekinhux');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (35993, 'f2a55f5362', '', 'I can totally understand your desire to screw them, but I\'m just the kind of guy that like to cover my ass, to avoid hassles later, because I can\'t stand hassles. So I would send it back.\r\n\r\n...after I spit and pissed on it.  :lol:');
