INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (40733, '351f976cd3', '', 'On the one hand if there is any country that will come out w/ a robot like that, it would have to be British (or Japanese)  They are retarded obsessed w/ robots.  I wish it was true, but being the Tech TV addict I am, I would have definatly seen somthing about this on the TV.  Either way Damn that is some great work for a hoax.  The thing that did it for me was the catch the car demonstration, the skidding the robot did on impact was more like gliding.  The spinning car wheels... if you are gonna build a robot that revolutionary, you don\'t give two craps that the wheels do that cool, movie-esq spinning, just that the damn thing works.  Ahh well, some day I\'ll hop in my Optimusprime Honda s2040 to pick up milk and non-detrimental government regulated cigs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36088, 'd5c777ba2e', '', 'You can get 2100 Nimh\'s pretty cheaply. They\'re AAA though.\r\nTry using 2 Li-Ion cells. Each one will deliver about 3.7 volts, and 7.2 volts is plenty for an Xmods. They\'re common in old Qualcomms and other cell phone batts. A warning: NEVER LET THE VOLTAGE GO BELOW 3 VOLTS!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36089, 'b1b2c98546', '', 'I don\'t think the voltage regulator will regulate "up". From my understanding it\'s more of a defense against frying the electronics. Putting in laymans cells will reduce the runtime and the weight, unfortunatly the weight reduction you get from this isn\'t going to be worth the reduction of runtime in my opinion.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36090, 'a3f4df179d', '', 'I second what ph2t said. :-)');
