INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36215, '46ff76d730', '', 'You got to be careful with that Ad-Aware.\r\n\r\nWhen I ran it, it told me we had over a 1000 possible spyware elements on our system, did I want it to remove them? Well that was too much to go through manually, so just I said yes, and it crashed our system. We were running in safe mode after that. Started backing things up when it crashed completely, and we had to reformat and lose everything.\r\n\r\nApparently it was some of those *.dll kernels that are shared by the system. I\'d be especially careful about removing any of those.\r\n\r\nSo now I avoid spyware removal programs, and I\'m just very careful about what I install. I don\'t use any Real products after Real Jukebox 8, because when you install that one you can uncheck the box, "send system requirement to Real network". Later products, the Real One Jukebox, don\'t give that option. Avoid Comet Curser at all cost, and AOL are some evil manipulative bastards. I avoid them, but my wife uses AIM, so she runs a program simply called, "AOL Spyware Protection", not sure where she got it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36216, 'fb1bf6a167', '', 'The hobby has definately slowed down out there in the real world. Target has dropped Microsizers, because they will only sell popular items they know they can unload quickly.\r\n\r\n...but the hobby is still alive and well in da hood. We aint going no where!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36217, 'ceccb1f9c8', 'Keep the dust out', 'Outside:\r\n[img:ceccb1f9c8]http://groups.msn.com/_Secure/0SwD**3QWZlNeAUGEkBQ9tOJMQgHmdBpDRyiRkkj3fFwf0!3le0GrgrK2NUOV4P4v*6Tej9T2Qo9OUfuHN7Klh3oRgw0A8DQ7*FvTGzGmwlOPgG*6wGINTg/wrxmod%20013.jpg?dc=4675457937021757540[/img:ceccb1f9c8]\r\n\r\nBut I added some mudflaps.\r\n[img:ceccb1f9c8]http://groups.msn.com/_Secure/0SwALA3UWpFNeAUGEkBQ9tHYmidFKvVz!QOXl3a6erNU1acvROhXKBtjurvQM!p8peg8BO3yEeSmIV2tuipjhqlmt8NXSIPvT6nnvGr93aSeAPXh9AqeoKA/wrxmod%20014.jpg?dc=4675457937055708461[/img:ceccb1f9c8]\r\n\r\n\r\nSo I tested it in the road outside my house its filled with construction dust,\r\n[img:ceccb1f9c8]http://groups.msn.com/_Secure/0SwDnAncWIFReAUGEkBQ9tP*Y!eewwhmMZQvtUJqn9B26e2sYSVHmA42bSxRtNtGsw0iKgqQAMLiXS!hctINC43g635O9MIBoqlmqY7CpRrPyU*O1lx4Xbg/wrxmod%20016.jpg?dc=4675457937095206253[/img:ceccb1f9c8]\r\n\r\nAnd it works :grin: If you notice, the front of the body is still clean and the back is filled with mud (no flaps behind there)\r\n\r\n[img:ceccb1f9c8]http://groups.msn.com/_Secure/0SwAQA3gWXlReAUGEkBQ9tB3KoSydGSTVJIsLWBPlVtp3wpOmu06OBwxO1s0ygsRr8!L5AmKaCq!yg*zpBp0qwguQOEIqr3eD!mgEdJ99IpAbtDCUpshx8g/wrxmod%20017.jpg?dc=4675457937128536790[/img:ceccb1f9c8]\r\n\r\nSo now we can go rallying on very flat hard-packed dirt (at least)\r\n\r\nSome one please make a lift kit for these.\r\n\r\nI hope this benifits people.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36218, '7f60f1078b', '', 'Before I forget,\r\n\r\nMake sure the top of the mudflaps dont rub the wheels. And fold it like an L so that there is piece infront of the batterypacks. This is to stop the dust from moving at an angle into the body section. Make sure the top of the flap is as wide as the wheel to ensure efficiency. You may have to trim a little to allow bady to fit.');
