INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48150, '79c5214764', '', 'Don\'t sweat it, arch. It\'s water under the bridge. I too was disappointed in the way the iWaver threads degenerated and unraveled over there(and I guess they still do, huh? I still drop in and read a lot... I love some of the stuff those overland guys are doing)... I only posted the things I did because it seemed to me that these cars were being unfairly categorized as a waste of money... I also feel the need to apologize to you for coming and acting up the way I did... although I felt it was justified at the time I realized it was not my place to be doing so(not to mention that I felt like I was arguing with my four year old)... anyways, I\'m sorry for acting like I did. \r\n\r\nAfter 3 months of owning my iWaver, I am still satisfied with it... A few of my friends have recieved problematic ones, and I feel really bad for that, but I still think that they are worth the price(I just say that because if those were mine, I\'d have fixed the problems by now lol)...\r\n\r\nI too have some custom things in mind... a few of us have been toying with the idea of making boats with iWaver or xmod electronics lol... We shall see where that leads us   :???:....  budget Palm Cruiser? Well, maybe not that style(at least for me... I have my eye on this Tyco that has an "unlimited" race lookin\' hull...)\r\n\r\nLike you, there are a lot of people, myself included, that would love to see an iWaver overland.... I\'m not holding my breath, though, as I have heard that there will be an MR02 iWaver before that...\r\n\r\nOh, damn, I almost forgot... Welcome to the hood! :cool:');
