INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36321, '8c31584ec9', 'The jam thread', 'Ok, so what we\'re talking about here is trying to get a long distance jam going. I\'m not the greatest player, so nothing fancy, just for fun. \r\n\r\nHue said he\'s down, now we\'re waiting for Superfly to check in. Just to update, here where we\'re at.\r\n\r\nWhen we last left our heroes, they were figuring how this could be done. Hue had said:\r\n\r\n[quote:8c31584ec9]There would have been separate Mac and PC editions, so that won\'t work. What we could do is just swap cds back and forth... for example, we could build a groove in stereo and send it to you on a cd, which you could load into your software and build on. Back and forth a few times and we\'d be rockin\'... not the most ideal way to do it, but it would be fun. \r\n\r\nThe other thing is that Pro Tools Free is a free download on their website, and comes in both Mac and PC editions. It\'s limited to 8 tracks and doesn\'t have all the features, but it would be plenty of recording power for our purposes. [/quote:8c31584ec9]To which I\'m about reply:\r\n\r\nYeah, I was kinda figuring that there was separate versions. So I was already looking for a freeware multi-track recorder. I couldn\'t find one for the Mac. So it looks like Pro Tools Free is the way to go. \r\n\r\nI let you guys know when I get that downloaded, and I\'m settled in with it.');
