INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36459, '9ee9ee66c8', '', 'Here I\'ll try to interprete.\r\n\r\nHe want to buy a Microsizer body set for his friend\'s Motorworks. So it doesn\'t look dumb.\r\n\r\nHe\'s asking if they will fit.\r\n\r\nThey will just snap on, but the front end sits low, and the wheel base is like maybe a milimeter longer. So you might have to do a little trimming, but the Beetle body snaps right on, no trimming, and looks cool. See my dirt truck thread.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36460, '478f28cae7', '', 'Really what I am talking about is the hop up kits you can get in the respective stores.  So not bits persay but MS.  Another Zip plus is range stock seems better.  On the neg, I find my zip chassies tuff to get off and can break the front slot if not carefull.  All in all though I am new to this gig, so it\'s a full on noob opinion.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36461, '3e0ee9ba8c', '', 'Thanks, glad you guys like it. :smile: \r\n\r\nI have to tell you guys though, part of the reason I decided against a classic baja bug, is because the rear mounted engine would have created body mounting issues, and this was just easier. It\'s really kinda surprising how easy it is to bring the classic bug influences to the new Beetle. I think alot of it has to do with chopping that roof. It\'s too much like a perfect dome. Lacks the character of the original Beetle.');
