INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36755, 'd66c94499b', '', 'REVISED EDITION!!!!!!!!!!\r\n[quote:d66c94499b]Can a two wheel drive remote controlled car be made into a four wheel drive remote \r\n\r\ncontrolled car? In this report, I will tell you how to turn a two wheel drive remote \r\n\r\ncontrolled car into a four wheel drive remote controlled car. It is quite simple, actualy. It \r\n\r\njust takes time.\r\n\r\n	First off, lets get some backround on the mini rc car. The first mini remote \r\n\r\ncontrolled car first appeared around September 2001. There are many brands out there, but \r\n\r\nsome are better than others. I would say that the Bit char-g is the best brand out there. There \r\n\r\nare many different frequencies that a mini remote controlled car can receive. They are 27 \r\n\r\nmegahertz, 35 megahertz, 45 megahertz, 49 megahertz, and 57 megahertz. The Zip Zap \r\n\r\nSpecial Edition is the only one that runs only on 27 megahertz. There can be up to six ZZSE \r\n\r\ncars running at once because the manufacturer fine tuned every ZZSE so that there are six \r\n\r\ndifferent frequencies that can be ran at the same time. The best quality has to be given to the \r\n\r\nBit char-g because it is the best of them all.\r\n\r\n	For the actual project, I needed a box cutter, some plastic glue, and some electrical \r\n\r\ntape. For the project, I needed to spare chassis. After those were found, I had to cut the \r\n\r\nmotor mount off of chassis one. This was the hardest part. It took me an hour just to cut off \r\n\r\none motor mount. I then had to cut the steering mount off of chassis two. This was as hard \r\n\r\nas the first one. From there, I used the plastic glue to glue the motor mount from chassis \r\n\r\none, onto chassis two, where the steering mount used to be. I now had to get my dad to re-\r\n\r\nsolder wires so that the printed circuit boards would fit. I kept the charging tabs in there \r\n\r\nstock place, I just moved the battery to the back of the chassis. I also had to solder the \r\n\r\ncharging tabs from circuit board one to circuit board two. I tried it, and it didnt work. It had \r\n\r\nshort-circuited somewhere. I found it, and put electrical tape on it. It now works, and is the \r\n\r\nonly four wheel drive micro remote controlled car out there that I know of.[/quote:d66c94499b]');
