INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36798, 'a2d3f33707', '', 'A couple things to check:\r\n\r\n1. You have to take the batteries out in order to use the AC adaptor.\r\n\r\n2. Is the voltage, polarity and mAh of the adaptor correct? It has to be 3V for single cell and/or 4.5V for dual cells. mAh should be between 500 and 1000. Polarity is critical. There should be a little diagram on the adaptor that shows the positive and negative arrangement of the jack coming off the adaptor, make sure you have wired the socket accordingly. If your adaptor has a hard-wired male end (  :shock: ), just switch the wires from the female socket to the circuit board.\r\n\r\n3. The problem I describe in the tutorial with Radio Shack adaptors has the same symtom. I think it has something to do with short-circuit protection. Someone corrrect me if I\'m wrong, but charging a battery with an adaptor is more or less shorting it out. The RS adaptors don\'t work for this reason, maybe Philips has the same issue. Try a different adaptor if you can. \r\n\r\nHope this helps.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36799, '8097097612', '', 'so, how\'s this idea going cabo?\r\ni think the idea of a joint comp is the way to go rather than the "vs" idea. some people might take it too far. some people expressed concern about mailing things across the globe to different team members, but i think that\'s what could make this comp unique. and 3 members per team would be ideal i think, body, chassis, electronics.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36800, '6e07159a76', '', 'Good point hue35.  I ended up buying a peak flow charger.  I was actually just interested if anybody had a quick and easy, yet safe, way to charge a quad.  It\'s not a good idea to just throw 4 AAs together for this job.  It could/and did fry the board.  I\'m not a genious about electronics, but what I know, I know as facts.  I actually had to send this to MA.  HE is the real genious.  My knowledge is basic when compared to him, although I\'m not a newb.  I do my own fet mods and dual cells.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (36801, 'c584857bb1', '', 'I\'m waiting on response from Aaron (ausmicro).\r\n\r\nI\'m with you betty - I\'m probably not going to be part of a "VS" competition, but I would be part of a "joint" competition (the word is better in itself lol)\r\n\r\nIf I had my way, I\'d probably just run this as a normal competition, teams allowed - users pick their own teams of 3 (doesn\'t matter if they\'re in Brazil or South Dakota - it\'s up to you and your team-mates)\r\n\r\n2 entries per team.\r\n\r\njudging would basically pit teams against teams, prize winners would work out their own "who gets what" issues.\r\n\r\nI feel like the key to the success of this contest is simplicity, not to over complicate it.\r\nWhile I love the idea of running things jointly, especially with ausmicro - I just honestly haven\'t heard of a good solution that wouldn\'t cause riffs yet.\r\nThat\'s not to say it\'s not out there.\r\n\r\nAs we get more information, we\'ll pass it along.');
