INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37053, '69c881cc66', 'Putty', 'A hobby shop without Squadron putty?  \r\nAre you sure it you weren\'t in the beer store?\r\nLOL  I don\'t think I\'ve ever been in a hobby store that doesn\'t sell Squadron.  \r\n\r\nIf you are having a hard time locating Squadron try finding Testors Red Putty.  Very similar to Squadron except it has less tendency to shrink over time.  Because it shrinks less you can cover bigger gaps with it.\r\n\r\nA trick used by 1/24 modellers is to take some plastic sprue [the framework model parts come on] and shave it down.  Then take those shavings and mix with some liquid cement like Tenex 7R [personal favorite].  What you end up with is a goo that is fairly easy to apply and bonds to mosts plastics really well.  It is also quite easy to sand and doesn\'t shrink.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37054, '1e25aa5633', '', 'excellent tip canabits, thanks :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37055, '59787762ca', '', 'ha - that\'s pretty cool...\r\n\r\nand so it was written... on stone tablets... a long time ago...\r\nhttp://www.kokogiak.com/webtools/orgulator.asp?ur=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com&amp;f=filter5');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37056, '392fa89813', '', 'nice wheels, now ya gotta paint the shell - the rims deserve it lol\r\n\r\ndid you make the gears?\r\ngot pics? :smile:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37057, 'c602360043', 're:gears', 'I\'ll try to snap some pics tomorrow.\r\n\r\nI took the gears from the Tomy gear set , the handfull of clones I have and the Bit Racers I have,  made RTV molds, and cast them in resin so I wouldn\'t have to buy multiple sets for specific gears.  Now I\'ve got an endless supply.  They work pretty good on the basically stock bit\'s we race the most.  Hoping to pick up a micro amps fet modded pcb on my trip to Oz.  Will see if they hold up to the extra power.  I may need to start casting them in a tougher resin, maybe even epoxy.\r\n\r\nOn my personal cars I cast them in basic white.  Ones I make for the guys I race with get cast in colour.  Makes it easy for me to see the ratio they are running while mine all look the same   8-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37058, '4c45b7ad1e', '', '[quote:4c45b7ad1e="CaboWabo"]ha - that\'s pretty cool...\r\n\r\nand so it was written... on stone tablets... a long time ago...\r\nhttp://www.kokogiak.com/webtools/orgulator.asp?ur=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com&amp;f=filter5[/quote:4c45b7ad1e]That\'s a crack up, because when I first got my computer, and wanted to make my silly little Homestead site, I got carried away with the embossing tool in Corel, and the second or third draft of my site looked exactly like that.\r\n\r\nI thought it was neato, because it looked I made a website out of clay.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (37059, '27b0d3cfea', '', '[quote:27b0d3cfea="payaso"][quote:27b0d3cfea="cj"]\r\n\r\n60-7037 STARTSKY &amp; HUTCH SE\r\n[/quote:27b0d3cfea]\r\n\r\n\r\nAre you shittin me? Starter, and Clutch were the shit with that big ass Ford Torino.....\r\n\r\nCan\'t wait for the pics....\r\n\r\nThanks cj..   I saw you @ banned.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:27b0d3cfea]\r\n\r\nbanned is pretty cool first week I was there I won the RC Driver shirt.  That group reminds me of this one but for the larger scale cars and trucks.');
