INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41375, 'dd9ba3e9e9', '', '"Net Transport" is another great app.\r\n\r\nIt\'s a Download Manager that basically intercepts any file links you click on (be it audio or video or programs) and downloads it. But what\'s especially nice is its\' ability to save streaming content too.\r\n\r\n...I yoinked all the Triumph \'The Insult Comic Dog\' from the NBC site with it (all are ASX streaming vids). But, as C-Dub mentioned, you might have to do some work in getting to the direct URL.\r\n\r\nGood luck.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41376, '1510f38b7a', '', '[quote:1510f38b7a="Bird"]I have never seen a Camaro do an ollie before. Awesome car. Great vid. Damn.[/quote:1510f38b7a]LOL, yeah, no shit, huh? It didn\'t occur to me that is like an ollie. Funny.\r\n\r\n[quote:1510f38b7a="CaboWabo"]I loved seeing the thing tip up on a side and drive on 2 wheels.[/quote:1510f38b7a]I\'ll tell ya, I loved that too when I was editing, but the more I watch, the more I realize the power loss. I need get the rear end exactly precise if this things gonna stay on the ground. Hog\'s JB Weld just might be coming into play here.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:1510f38b7a="sg219"]What about a small amount of weight in the front plus the wheelie bar to keep it level on the drag strip. Like a truck pull kind of thing maybe.[/quote:1510f38b7a]Well, if you watch the drags, they always pull the front end up off the line too. The idea is to center the weight around the rear axle, to lay the horse power. You don\'t need the front wheels off the line if you\'re pointed in the right direction, and the rear end hooks evenly. (I still need to work on that last part.) If I work some kind of shock absorbtion into the wheelie bar, it should take up some of that impact, and bring the front end down without lifting the rear, in theory, we\'ll see.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41377, 'f0b4f6d89a', '', 'man that thing is ANGRY!!! :eek: it\'s doing what a real drag car would do! once you got a shock absorbing wheelie bar happening that thing will put indentations in your fridge door!! :shock:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41378, '8d92326f2c', '', '[quote:8d92326f2c="crazydave"]Nice work! I would have never even have thought to move the idler.\r\n\r\nWhacha got planned for the body?[/quote:8d92326f2c]\r\n\r\nthanks.. .yeah, I really didn\'t think of it until last minutes lol.... The body? well, I\'m jus going to paint, I think I\'ve done enough body kitting on my recent projects. I may just leave this with the stock stuff as far as skirts are concerned. Later today, I\'ll snap a few more pics of the basically finished product, except the body. i\'ve done a few fills with just small piece of plastic and glue... it should look good when I\'m done!!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nas far as turning is concerned, it turns fine. I actually did have to move the front up a little because the stabilizer bar was hitting the body, and it wouldn\'t turn, but now, it\'s fixed!!');
