INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41419, '2792111809', '', '[quote:2792111809="sg219"]Its a sweet ride, I\'ve driven it a little bit and checked it out over Birds.  I like the handling and the get-up of it alot.  The steering is the best I\'ve driven. The only thing I don\'t like about it is the H-plate.  I know this design has been around the hobby forever, but I think its a really shitty way of puttin\' suspension on a car. Have you ever seen a real car like that?  There is no reason for it, besides costs and ease of manufacturing.(I\'ve grown really fond of the Xmod set-up!!)\r\n\r\n I will still probably pick one up, because of price, and to open a can of whoop ass on Birds iWaver. But I still don\'t like the H-plate idea. Give me some shocks on 4 wheels any day.  \r\n\r\n\r\nOverall I\'ll give it a 192.....on a scale of 1 to 219. \r\n\r\nI\'ll take away points for the H-plate and the cheesy chassis.\r\n\r\nI\'ll give it many points for price, steering, get-up, and the great controller. And for comin\' straight out of the box it is a great ride for a mear $25 US greenbacks.\r\n\r\nAs for aftermarket parts, just thank ITS clone Mini-Z for them.   :???:[/quote:2792111809]\r\n\r\n\r\nWell put man, i think the H-plate is absolute crap too. Why just make the ass end pivot when you can have independant springs. H-plates are outdated.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41420, '7e834cf832', '', 'your fortune is: you will die a terrible death.\r\nyour gear ratio is: 8.4488:1.\r\n\r\nratio is easy to figure out;\r\n\r\ncount the teeth on the gears of the first \'gear down\', in your case;\r\n18, 7. divide them to calculate the ratio.\r\n18 / 7 = 2.5714.\r\n\r\ndo the same with the other 2 gear wheels.\r\n\r\n23 / 7 = 3.2857.\r\n\r\nmultiply these two figures to find the ratio :1\r\n\r\n2.5714 x 3.2857 = 8.4488\r\n= 8.4488:1that just refers to revolutions, 1 revolution of the rear wheel = 8.4488 revs of the motor. different wheel diameters make a difference overall to the final speed and torque.\r\n\r\n(i know most of you know this little formula already,  just schoolin\' tha new kids)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41421, '7b41fac7d9', '', 'I saw a set of 3 different thickness GPM graphite h-plates somewhere online for like 9 bucks or so, I\'ll be getting them eventually. Yeah, mini-z\'s are a lot like pan cars, where xmods are more touring car-ish. But there is something about the simplicity of that h-plate/direct drive set-up. It makes for an efficient drivetrain. And it has withstood the test of time, there have been cars running similar set-ups since the late 70\'s with great success. If you really need shocks and whatnot, the aftermarket has all that stuff covered and then some.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41422, 'e99c97b9eb', 'decals', 'i went to radical decals and i liked what i saw, its just that i am looking for rallye type decal with sponsers from the 70\'s era, i did find a place and ordered some, i will let you all know what i came up with, i am trying to get the ride of the week with this puppy when its ready for show...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41423, 'ebcc989130', 'Oah! Oah! Oah!  Can\'t Touch Dis !', 'This one was done in record time!  7-8 hrs.!  The wif is headin to da Windy City, her neice\'s husband\'s B-Day is this week.  When they were down around Xmas, he luv\'d my Custom Micro\'s, so I thought I\'d make one for him.  But before he gets it, this will be my 2nd entry.............................. \r\n[b:ebcc989130]It\'s [/b:ebcc989130]\r\n[img:ebcc989130]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/AMG01.jpg[/img:ebcc989130]\r\n\r\n[b:ebcc989130]* Full AMG Style Ground Effects\r\n* Custom DUB CITY Wheels fitted to ZipZap Hubs\r\n* Lowered Front &amp; Rear\r\n* Dual Aluminum Exhaust\r\n* Serious Detailing\r\n* German Silver Paint\r\n* Blood Interior[/b:ebcc989130]\r\n\r\n[img:ebcc989130]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/AMG%20Hammer02.jpg[/img:ebcc989130]\r\n[img:ebcc989130]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10005/AMG%20Hammer1.jpg[/img:ebcc989130]');
