INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48181, '1c4d7da1d6', 'Concert Tickets...They just keep comin\'!!!', 'Thought I would drop my little story of how I go to concerts for free.\r\n\r\nFirst thing this year was "X-fest" a big show with a bunch of bands sponsered by the local Clear Channel Alt. Rock Station.  Last year I got my hat signed by Amy Lee from Evanesencse by reachin\' over some really short people.  This year there was Switchfoot, Finger 11, Story of the Year, Cypress Hill, New Found Glory, and The Offspring.  There were a couple more, but not important.  I bought my ticket for that show for $32 total, includes all those damn service charges.  The day before the Big show every year the station drives around all day doing big ticket drops, where they pull up and the first 25 people in line get a pair of tickets to X-fest.  Well I grabbed my sister and got 2 pair.  Now I had 5 tickets.  Day of show...it was raining that morning, I started gettin\' calls sayin\' people aren\'t going now, so I went solo and stood in front of the venues ticket window sellin\' (4)tickets for $10 each.  Now Parking is free and some $6 beers too.\r\n\r\nSo far 1 big show for $32.  While at the concerts I always play this Football game where you have to throw a Nerf Football thru a hole to win a pair of concert tickets to an upcoming show, it costs $1 for 2 throws.  I spent $5 and won tickets to Primus!!!\r\n\r\nOn my way to pick-up Hog to go to Primus I stopped to get gas, while there I played this stupid game by spinning a wheel to win stuff.  It was sponsered by yet another Clear Channel Station, a Hip-Hop one.  I spun the wheel, the lady tried sayin\' I won some gay ass movie, but I said I want the tickets, she gave them to me!!!  The tickets were for Styx/Peter Frampton show. I sorta wanted to go see Framton, but I was pretty broke and couldn\'t afford beer, so I sold them for $20 and a buzz.\r\n\r\nI took that $20 and got my Dave Matthews Band ticket, regularly $43, but I only spent $23!!\r\n\r\nThe DMB show is tomarrow night the 27th, and I\'m sure I\'ll have more tickets coming to me from the football game!!!!\r\n\r\nAnd the summer concert season rolls on!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\nPlus, there is a ton of free show around here, especially if you can get into a little bit of oldies or doo-wop.  If you\'ve seen any of the Doo-Wop/R&amp;B/Oldie shows on PBS filmed in Pittsburgh, I was at it!!\r\n\r\nThere\'s usually a bunch of free rock shows all summer at various festivals and Rib Cook-Offs too!!\r\n\r\nThe local band "The Clarks" played a free Semi-Acoustic show in front of the Best Buy by my work for their new release. I recorded it, it came out pretty good, and I got my CD signed by the whole band.  They will be on Letterman August 31st!!!!  The local boys are going big time!! :cool: :cool:');
