INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41879, 'c1b59e7cfd', '', 'You are one truly talented cat, dave. That is beautiful. One of a kind.\r\n\r\nMy older brother has played bass since I was a little kid, and one of the first ones he got was an old Fender music master. It had a short neck and a strat body and basically looked like a strat... Anyways, our dad is into refinishing wood, has been forever, and is always looking for something to do. He usually hits thrift stores and garage sales looking for projects(he usually gives his stuff as gifts, too), but he took one look at that old bass, with its worn and weathered  cream-colored paint, and said "I gotta take that thing to the basement." He ended up buying my bro another bass to play while he took the next 3 months totally redoing that Fender. It wound up clear coated natural wood, with a black pick-guard, a new pickup, tuners, the works... a thing of beauty. My bro has had many basses since then, but none have been nearly as nice. He still has it and keeps it locked away and rarely plays it. Personally, if I had it, it\'d be hanging on my living room wall, as a piece of art.\r\n\r\nDid you know that the guitar Jimi Hendrix burned up in that famous footage was later bought by Frank Zappa, who sent it to Fender where it was totally refit, and clearcoated right over the fire damage, and then was given as a gift to his son, Dweezil(who I believe still has it, not sure)? I saw pics of it once, and it stands today as one of the most beautiful guitars I have ever seen.\r\n\r\nSorry for the epic, but I truly appreciate a beautiful guitar, and seeing yours stirred up a bunch of memories or beautiful guitars.');
