INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41899, '9a3ef1142e', '', 'It\'s funny, I know what you guys look like from the mug shots, but I still have this image of crazydave in my head when I read his posts... I picture this tattooed up Mike Ness Social Distortion type guy, who drives a shaved up black suede primered ride with red steelies and baby moon hubcaps.... and the tele fits right in with that image... Filelicker, I just picture every cool biker guy I\'ve ever known when I read your stuff...\r\n\r\nAnyhow, did you check out the info on that Hendrix/Zappa guitar?\r\n\r\n[quote:9a3ef1142e="Bird"]OK, got it.... and all without even talking to my bro.... Miami Pop Festival, \'68. Check this out, I found a pic and everything...\r\n\r\nhttp://www.petersen.org/default.cfm?DocID=502&amp;ArticleID=12[/quote:9a3ef1142e]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41900, 'ff75eaeb9e', '', 'Hmmm....Well... \r\n\r\n-"Dragula" by Rob Zombie\r\n-"Dragula" (The Matrix Remix) by Rob Zombie\r\n-"Push it" by Static X\r\n\r\nI recommend listening to the original Dragula first, THEN the matrix version, because then you feel the step up and difference, and appreciate them better. \r\n\r\nJust my 2% of a dollar....');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41901, 'dc5d0ddfa5', '', '[quote:dc5d0ddfa5="crazydave"]So you\'ve determined, what I\'ve been coming around to slowly realize. FETs give you enough power to pull you\'re fastest gear ratio. \r\n\r\nI like running higher gear ratios now, because it actually helps keep the front wheels on the ground, but I don\'t have anything as high as the bit-racer gears yet.\r\n\r\n\r\nAre you really seeing much improvement with the triple stacked FETs? I was comparing stacked FETs, by stacking the forward FETs, and leaving the reverse. Double stacking seems like a slight improvement, but nothing like just putting FETs in there to begin with. Triple stacking seems to make the motor whine louder off the ground like there was more speed, but I didn\'t see any improvement on the ground.\r\n\r\n...but honestly, every time I run low on FETs, I steal the FETs off the cars that have stacked FET, so I haven\'t played with stacked FETs that much, that\'s why I\'m asking about your experience with them.[/quote:dc5d0ddfa5]\r\n\r\nDude, the improvement in stacked fets is there.   But you\'re right, that first jump from the normal BJT transistors to fets is still the gratest jump performance wise.   What took me to appreciate the increase in torque a double/triple stack provides was this simple test:\r\n\r\nPut on your rear wheels the standard orange gear ratio.  Now (as a sinlge fet stack) hold the rear wheels in you fingers (with the front of the car facing the ground, vertically)  and press forward.  You will noticed that the car swings a bit but prolly not much more than a 10-15 degrees angle.   Now make it a double stack.  Do the same test.  I now get about 30-50 degrees spin, more torque is definately evident.   No do a triple stack.  The car spins the full 360 degrees, no Bullshit.......\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\nph2t.');
