INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41941, '2f1316548d', '', 'ok bruce pm\'d me on ausmicro last week. i didnt notice until today\r\n\r\nQuick word mr. Jowlz,\r\n\r\nThough you may not realise it, your never ending crap about australia etc. is beginning to annoy some people, including moderators, and aaron himself. We aren\'t sheep shaggin\' farmers or whatever, if you came over here you would realise that...shock horror we do have cities, and our country is similar to yours in many ways (though we are smaller).\r\n\r\nI\'m not having a go at you, just be a bit more wise about your views. We do appreciate some enthusiasm, but just chill it a bit!\r\n\r\nCheers\r\n\r\n\r\n**the official jowlz(tm) reply**\r\ngday bruce!!\r\n\r\nconsidering you are all ancestors of brittish criminals, i dont believe you. you can call a mudhut a city as long as you want. we know better about you outback nomads.\r\n\r\ncheers,\r\n\r\ndad');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (41942, '5319066ed1', '', '[quote:5319066ed1="hogjowlz"]for a few months i was running a turntbable through a mu-tron. then i had to give it back to the dude.\r\n\r\nwhat sequencers you got dave? ive used most of em and find fruityloops to be the best for what i do. software synths are great but my korg polysix sounds 100billion times better. i have to get a midi retro kit for it i guess. lately ive been more into the percussion end of things tho just making funk patterns and shit.[/quote:5319066ed1]That\'s cool, I really want a Mu-Tron. One of the original Haz Laboratories ones?\r\n\r\n\r\nFor sequencers, I\'ve played with Acid, Rebirth, and Reason, but Fruity Loops 3 is by far my favorite, and the only one I use.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:5319066ed1="Hue35"]Beautiful Tele, crazydave. That thing will be sweet when you get it done. You are the most resourceful dude... that foil looks like a million bucks. [/quote:5319066ed1]Thanks man, I try to be inventive.\r\n...and I\'ll tell ya, the back of the guitar is painted silver, and it really offsets the silver in the foil\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:5319066ed1="filelicker"]I don\'t hate any guitar , I would own them all...[/quote:5319066ed1]I only hate Les Pauls, and guitars with locking trems. Oh, and guitars with really wide necks. If your a big guy, I can see why you like Les Pauls, the necks always seem too wide for my hand. Except for my buddy\'s Voodoo Les Paul, that has a nice skinny neck.\r\n\r\nOther than that I love just about every guitar I see, and that\'s why I had to start building them, it\'s the only way I could afford everythig I wanted.\r\n\r\nI also have an affection for cheapie guitars from the 60s. After I get this done, I want to get one of those Silvertones, that were essentially Danelectros, and refurbish that.');
