INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42258, '8c1e2e406d', '', '[quote:8c1e2e406d="ph2t"]dude, I don\'t have an sg, I wish I did!   what bodypart goes for around $2-$3K these days?[/quote:8c1e2e406d]Oh  :lol: \r\nThe way you spoke of them, I thought you were currently in love with your own baby.\r\n\r\n2-3k? Maybe for the upper end ones. A SG standard runs about 1200, you could\'ve picked up one of the USA made faded series on clearance for 500, that was a great deal for a Gibson.\r\n\r\n[quote:8c1e2e406d]that was some cool playin\' man, very satriani, i lived it!  I can just see you sitting there, on the edge of your bed, amp like 2-3 meters away and a sea of pedals and cables in between...\r\n\r\nrock on!\r\n\r\n :D \r\n\r\nph2t.[/quote:8c1e2e406d]Thanks man, I\'ll take a comparison to Satriani as a compliment any day. :grin: \r\n\r\nActually I prefer not to use too many effects. I like to just use a distortion box in front of my amp, but I do sit on the edge of my bed with my amp blasting in my face. :lol: \r\n\r\nI recorded that with a Digitech RP100, which is a great toy/practice tool for 80 bucks, but I hate the sound. No matter what guitar I plug into it, the same sound comes out. Totally kills the character.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42259, 'ce42084d83', '', 'I was using a dremel cut-off wheel to cut through an exhaust clamp on a hooptie Cutlass Supreme I used to have, and it self destructed and one of the pieces of schrapnel came about an inch from taking out one of my eyes. I always protect my eyes when using the cut-off wheels now.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42260, 'd7a8401eb7', '', '[quote:d7a8401eb7="filelicker"]all mine are dremel and I blow discs apart all the time it\'s a fact of life![/quote:d7a8401eb7]Yup, I wear safty glasses. I learned the hard way after a trip to the emergency room.\r\n\r\nThe sell re-inforced cut off wheels. They are a lot thicker, but they don\'t fly apart as bad, and are what you should be using for bigger jobs.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42261, 'ced98e7341', 'So ummm, what exactly is Cabo developing?', 'This aint pot related, but I\'m posting it here, because i figured you guys would appreciate this.\r\n\r\nIt\'s a funny story about Cabo\'s name...\r\n\r\nSee when I first came to bitPimps I always wondered what lixlink.com was. I thought it sounded like a porn sight, like a thumbnail gallery post or something, so I didn\'t want to check while my wife was around. So it was a couple months before I got around to checking. \r\n\r\nWhen I did, it was just "Scott D. Lix - Web Developer", and I thought, "oh is that all..."\r\n\r\nThen I was like, "...wait a minute, \'Scott D. Lix\' that sounds like a porn star."  :lol: \r\n\r\nSo what\'s up cabo, you developing porn? :cool: \r\n\r\nAt any rate, I just think that\'s funny, and you gots a cool name, my name has no ring to it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42262, 'd47bb3aa43', '', 'why yes dave i concur.\r\n\r\n**hogs dremel comentary**\r\n\r\nwhile the rotary cutting tool brought to you by the dremel corporation is an imensly handy utensil for modifying bits and crap, I believe that the bit community is a little "dremel happy".  sometimes a smaller cutting tool like an exacto knife or a file will do a better job and you dont even have to plug anything in.\r\n\r\nalways ask yourself "what is the best tool for the job" or "what the hell would bob vila\'s producer tell him to use".\r\n\r\n\r\nthen again you can cut yourself bad pulling a fucking cd burner out of a case. [img:d47bb3aa43]http://mywebpages.comcast.net/myaaiko/thumbscar.jpg[/img:d47bb3aa43]');
