INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42271, '57b9e48c66', 'C Swens Is back baby', '[img:57b9e48c66]http://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/Images/xback_t2.jpg[/img:57b9e48c66]\r\n[img:57b9e48c66]http://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/Images/xfro_t2.jpg[/img:57b9e48c66]\r\n[img:57b9e48c66]http://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/Images/xleft_t2.jpg[/img:57b9e48c66]\r\n[img:57b9e48c66]http://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/Images/xright2_t2.jpg[/img:57b9e48c66]\r\n[img:57b9e48c66]http://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/Images/xright_t2.jpg[/img:57b9e48c66]\r\nhttp://www.cswens.rchomepage.com/xmod.html\r\nThis is my xmod. I am proud of It. Need to update the url because i purchased the sterring suspension kit recently.  I have the stiff in back and the soft up front. and the 1.5 tie rod.  The only mods i need are lights, and bearings.  Enjoy :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42272, 'a0b05fa0cd', 'Dixmont - 142 yr old Insane Asylum', 'Yesterday Hogjowlz, Bird, 2 of Hogs friends and myself went on a small excursion to a place called Dixmont.  Its an Old Insane Asylum that was built and opened in 1862 and closed its doors in 1984.\r\n\r\nHeres a link to one of the many pages that I have found about it.\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.dixmontstatehospital.com/[/url]\r\n\r\nI didn\'t go to sleep last night after the trip till about 5am, because I was mezmorized by the history of this place and other Asylums like it all over the country.  It turns out that the same guy designed many of these kind of places around the turn of the century, his name was Dr. Kirkbride, and most of them had very similar layouts.\r\n\r\nHeres a couple of pics from the trip.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0008.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nMorgue\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0011.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nLarge Courtyard between buildings.\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0019.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nNote to Wal-Mart left by someone.  It will be torn down for a damn Wal-Mart.  Thru-out the whole place there were many FU Wal-Marts on the walls.\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0021.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nLarge ballroom, there were 2 of these, on on each end of the building, they were huge gathering areas.\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0024.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nA cool pic of the area between the main building and the smaller building behind it.  One of my favorite pics of the day.\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0032.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n\r\nThis pic has that downtown Beruit feeling to it.\r\n\r\n[img:a0b05fa0cd]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Dixmont/PCDV0067.jpg[/img:a0b05fa0cd]\r\n \r\nThis was taken as we were leaving around dusk.  It of the main building up on the hill.\r\n\r\n(@ Finks--I wish my car pics came out this good.)\r\n\r\nI took about 70 pics this day and most of them came out great, I just wish I had a flash on my camera.  There was so much great stuff to see, but it was in the dark.  To mention one, there was an underground tunnel anywhere from about 1/2 - 3/4 of a mile long downhill with some great artwork the whole way leading to a powerplant for the facilities.  Pitch Black too.\r\n\r\nThis place was totally self sustaining, farm, power, water, laundry, postoffice, everything in a small community.  407 acres worth!!\r\n\r\n@ Hog-- Thanks for a great day, I\'m hooked on findin\' out as much as possible about this place.  I can\'t believe the set up this place had going for it for about 122 years then it closes mainly because of politics!!! \r\n\r\nThanks again....');
