INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42460, 'aa16a898e7', '', 'alright i asked him bout this crap yesterday. he says the magellin sport track pro is pretty slick for about 200bucks.  \r\n\r\n[quote:aa16a898e7]Magellan\'s new Sportrak Pro Combines all the most popular GPS features and a huge onboard map memory into a pocket sized marvel. The waterproof 12 Channel WAAS receiver tracks in any outdoor environment and updates your position once per second, and when receiving the WAAS GPS signal the Sportrak Pro will provide up to 10 foot accuracy*. The built-in basemap provides highway maps for the entire US along with Marine navigation aids, such as Buoys, lighthouses, wrecks and more. By purchasing one of Magellan optional MapSend CD-ROMs you can add even more detail to the map display such as secondary road and topographic information including detailed waterway and lake outlines. The Sportrak Pro can store up to 23 megabytes of additional maps in its onboard memory from the MapSend CD\'s. The screen on the Sportrak Pro is clear and easy to read and both the display and keys are backlit for nighttime use. Seven customizable "pages" of information are available to clearly show information such as map detail, speed, heading, trip log and much more. Other features include memory for 500 waypoints and 20 routes, sunrise/sunset and best fish&amp;hunt calculator, audible alarms, built-in help information, 9 languages and save track-to-route function. 1 Year Warranty. Size: 5.6"H x 2.2"W x 1.3"D. Weight 6.1 oz. \r\n*The WAAS signal is currently available in the US only in open areas or on the water. Standard GPS accuracy is 50 feet. [/quote:aa16a898e7]\r\n\r\nor you could get a pocket pc and something like this.\r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;category=29848&amp;item=3091879124&amp;rd=1\r\n\r\nthen you got gps and every old console game you played as a kid and a bunch of other crap.');
