INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42431, 'b452d50c63', '', 'You can try the search feature also, its been gettin\' great reveiws from people that can\'t or need to find out info on things.\r\n\r\n\r\nBut here is some info for ya....\r\nI use this stuff.  It works pretty good.  Put it where you need it, then let it dry most of the way and then soak it with some cheap superglue.  It\'ll dry really, really strong.\r\n\r\n[img:b452d50c63]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/putty.jpg[/img:b452d50c63]\r\n\r\n\r\nEveryone uses different stuff.  Just find out what works best for you.\r\n\r\nThis putty called Squadron was suggested to me too, people use it alot on model planes....\r\n\r\nCheck out this thread...I asked the sort of the same question. \r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2334&amp;start=0[/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42432, '8216cf1c68', '', 'The short version of my story is that a couple friends and I decided we didn\'t want to have real summer jobs, and we all had restaurant experience. We borrowed a Suburban, and had a big gas grill on a trailer. Two big woks, and a United Grocer\'s membership and we were in business. We made stir-fried veggies served in pita bread. Our first couple gigs were the early county fairs in late May, and then we went to the Dead show in Eugene and did 4x the business. We were heads anyway, so we just followed the tour for the rest of the summer and early fall. Almost every show, someone would invite us to their house to crash. We didn\'t actually make much money that summer because we blew it all on tickets and drugs. We had this following of regulars who would bring their own mushrooms for us to throw in their sandwiches. Spent a week in the parking lot of the Oakland Coluseum between Christmas and New Year\'s that year (like 87 or so). Amazing I lived through it.');
