INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42442, 'd0e824339c', '', 'ok this is my first entry. I think this car was my favorite so far.\r\n\r\n[img:d0e824339c]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10003/normal_bnw.jpg[/img:d0e824339c]\r\n\r\nThis ride was slapped together about a year and a half ago.  She had a lot of first time mods for me. They all seemed to come together just perfect. Being one of my first dual cells, I thought i had to cut out the rear window to fit the extra battery. Two GP 100mah(og zipzap) cells were used in this model.  I finally stepped up from clone chassis to microsizer ones. The pcb was a 57mhz cyclona. most cyclona pcbs didnt have the output of this one.  It also sported like 30foot range indoors.  I ordered the pullback from ebay for like 9bucks after shipping. As soon as i opened the package i was cutting the rear window out and a crack developed down the middle.  The plastic is different than most Tomy shells. So i cut some gaffers tape straight and put a racing stripe down the center and man that added a 30% horsepower increase right there. \r\n\r\nI decided to put the pullback wheels together and hold them on the axle with jbweld. With the pullback wheels(probably one of the first attempts at this. I know C-dub did it first). And the rear battery weight, I had created a wheelie monster. But the muffler was catching and it fell over. So i cut the muffler off and it did wheelies pretty good.  Then later on the GODDAM chassis started slipping and the gear wouldnt hold(we all have encountered this im sure). I had experimented with plastic and metal tubing held in the chassis with jbweld but that never worked right.  I was pissed!! I had just put together a wheelie monster and didnt wana redo the work. So i said fuckit and cut the cassis out a little and laid the axle in with a piece of tape over the gears and poured epoxy all inside the rear covering the axle in hard steel goo. Jbweld takes six hours to dry so id fiddle with it every hour or so so it wouldnt cement the axle in but there would be no slop. \r\n\r\nheres the final result.\r\n[url]http://mywebpages.comcast.net/myaaiko/noload.avi[/url]\r\n\r\nThis thing was absolutly badass. It rode wheelies for several feet.  Too bad she only survived maybe a few weeks.\r\n\r\nhere is her demise.\r\n[url]http://hogjowlz.lixlink.com/thud.wmv[/url]\r\n\r\nthank you drive thru');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42443, '5e4b8d06c9', '', '[quote:5e4b8d06c9="hogjowlz"]thank you drive thru[/quote:5e4b8d06c9]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nI\'m Rick James Bitch...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42444, '5725a61ffa', '', 'I never got the Dead\'s music, but the scene in the parking lot was the coolest, nothing like the smell of burning sage and BO. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnyways, if 4:20 is that time, I\'ve been stuck at 4:00 all day, and it just hit 4:20\r\n\r\nSeriously my buddy was supposed to be on the way over, and disappeared, turned out his 3 month old Maxima got side swiped by a drunk driver. He\'s ok, but his cars fucked, so I suppose that\'s adequate excuse for leaving me hanging.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42445, 'f8e0c1788c', '', 'Thanks, you know the roof reminded me of something else too, but I\'m not sure I\'m familiar with a Cheetah, but I\'m imagining one of them swooshy 60s cars with the round roofs.\r\n\r\n...and Finks thanks, I appreciate the compliment, but I gotta tell ya, it\'s not quite seemless. If you look at the door, you can see a slight seem. That\'s just because there was no putty involved, I just used super glue as usual, super glue dries pourous, and soaks the paint up, causing that line. I was trying to hurry, so I only laid 2 coats, if I had laid another coat, it probably would have covered it.\r\n\r\njoez2872, yep them rims come with the tires. I carved out the little holes with my exacto, so they\'d be black, but otherwise, they\'re just like that. It\'s a pretty cool set, I\'d definately go grab one if I was you, I\'m getting some more for spares.');
