INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42659, '14b2c401b9', '', '[quote:14b2c401b9="micromatch"]is  it just me oris the rear left  rim (gear side) stick out mor than the other with pullbacks? minedoes andit pisses me off[/quote:14b2c401b9]\r\n\r\n\r\nYes it does....... (gear is thicker than wheel nub)  But the important thing is that when you install them, you should sand down the gear so it matches the nub on the wheel opposite drive wheel.\r\n\r\nMy first attempt went like this, but now they\'re as even as it gets.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42660, '7ef9be7dab', '', 'Awwwww Shit....\r\n\r\nJust sticking with bodies huh? LOL...if I had a dime for every time I thought that, I could support this bit habit of mine and not go broke!  :o \r\n\r\nOk...so you all pretty much got me beat...now I feel the need to buy more. I\'ve got just about 20 complete kits, a whole shitload of bodies, motors, wheels, batts, heatsinks, etc. If I had to guess...I\'d say I have a good $400 or so wrapped up in these damn things since December. Went out and got myself a nice big tacklebox to store it all and now I\'m pretty much out of room.....time to buy a display case I guess...\r\n\r\nHmmmm...I\'m thinking plexiglass, mirrored back, lighted on top....\r\n\r\nI\'ve been trying hard to stay away from those Ferrari and Lambo Sets because I hate the thought of dropping like $80 bucks all at once, but its getting to me and I might brake down and do it when I get that Vdub bus...Ugh!');
