INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42694, '181c7bfaa7', 'Need info on mosfet mod for Precious clones...', 'Anyone have ANY info on a mosfet mod for Precious clones? I know I can pay MicroAmps to do it, but I want to do this myself. I\'m having a hell of a time finding out info about the Precious PCB/schematic. Any info, pics, whatever would be appreciated. Thanks!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42695, '995ae3ff4f', 'casting', 'well i finally got the casting stuff today, and did some more work on the bus, this body is real light and i lose little power from the weight, it amazing that the chassis is a clone that i picked up at a conveinance store for 4.99 and did some minor tweaking like super glueing the magnet on the steering and making sure it was center and then i resoildered the antenna wire to the pot which gives me hella range, i am calling the screw thingie that you turn on the pcb for frequency tweaking a pot i dunno what its called but i was messing around one day and was testing differant locations on the pot or diff, pins and if it would make a difference in range and it does, this chassis did not have the crip cap so i did nothing really just relocated the antenna. it\'s pretty slow movin and i kinda like it that way, its a cruiser, and with a light mod and neon it will be kickin, i was thinking about adding a roof rack on the cab, westfalia made a rack for these busses once just to carry a spare tire and a gas tank and such when you were out in the safari or something , i bet i could easily make a rack from a paperclip, i wonder if you can soldier a paper clip :???:  u guys watch it gonna be slamin!!!\r\n\r\njmays');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42696, 'afbfa3e390', '', 'wow, I can\'t believe I missed this thread... looks like you guys had a great day. Thanks for sharing the pics sg219, they look great.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42697, '33cac8e776', '', 'bloody hell!! i can\'t even remember what this thread was all about!! :eek: \r\nhe he, well i fergit who asked what but i mainly wanted the pb\'s for looks! but i find they are super grippy which i like. it flips a little with turns but if you think about the scale of things i\'d like to see an f1 car turn that tight at that speed and stay upright! i\'m using a booster pcb and that helps to control things much better. i took it for a run outside on the concrete and the lack of suspension prevents it from really staying on the ground but it was turning at full speed most of the time without flipping. after i fuck with the center of gravity it should handle much better. i\'m thinking of moving the battery forward and cutting out some chassis so it sits lower, similar to hachi ryoku\'s mods http://community.webshots.com/album/135656737qEtQbh\r\ni\'m thinking foamies all round will help this baby out on concrete.\r\nas for the front wheels, whoever suggested the wd40 tubing was right on the money! i like to widen the front wheels anyway and they rub if you don\'t put a spacer in. for the rear i just ground down some plastic from the inside of the left wheel so the tyre goes over the smooth part of the gear. still a ways to go as you can imagine but as it is this thing\'s a heap of trouble juz waitin\'to happen!! :cool: \r\n\r\n[img:33cac8e776]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10012/normal_skylinepbbottom.JPG[/img:33cac8e776]\r\n[img:33cac8e776]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10012/normal_pbgearset.JPG[/img:33cac8e776]');
