INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42854, 'f6c60690ae', '', 'i don\'t really understand that mentality either. i mean how much propo do we need to have before we\'re having the official amount of fun? crikey!! here\'s me thinking i was into micro rc but oh no, i\'m not worthy of that title yet!\r\nif i rolled all my rc\'s into one i\'d be lucky to crack 30 steps of propo between them! i think it goes down like this; anal purists that were spoilt as children or had their asses wiped for them their whole lives choose to be propo purists. " lookit me, i just bought a titanium overhead damping pillow ball mounting screw, part number WANK937326554936300001, and installed it following the instructions!!" nice, predictable, bland.\r\nor there\'s people that never had enough lego to make those cool things we really wanted to build, but we got them built anyway! we CAN polish a turd, we get people telling us we\'re wasting our time persisting with restoring or converting junk with soul when we could just buy an off the rack mass produced item that everyone else has. (man, if i had a dollar.....).\r\ndon\'t get me wrong, i recently went to a real rc track and got to watch some hardcore 1/10\'s being driven well and i was damn impressed! they really are a fascinating piece of equipment, but i like my little fellers! and not all full on rc heads are purists, i was asking questions about their cars and showing them mine and most of them were kinda surprised to see bits at a track, but they were cool with us using the track so long as we followed the general rules. (there were a couple of turds there, but they were bigger than me!)\r\nbasically i\'m saying "who\'s fun is greater?"  kids in some african countries wet their pants when their dad comes home with a bit of wire for them to bend into the shape of a car! and they make some damn impressive shit those kids do!! :-) nuff said.');
