INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42996, 'd9fa49da55', '', 'I hated that while I\'m barely able to afford keeping my cars running, you got the guys at the track and the magazine saying you need all this graphite, titanium, and anodized aluminum stuff. I hated that attitude, that\'s what drove me away from hobby level RCs.\r\n\r\nBasically, in that circle, anything of "toy store" quality is scoffed at. It\'s been tradition to laugh at the guys with the big Nikkos, or RS cars, that could barely get around the track. So it\'s no wonder our bits are seen as mere "Toys". Whatever, as long as we know we\'re having fun.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42997, 'b1893c2111', '', 'Oh yeah, well I\'m gonna build an off road car with a 1/64th scale gas powered V-8...someday. I might even take some pics...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42998, '92c48810f7', '', '[quote:92c48810f7="brendan123"]wow, never thought i would get this much GOOD feedback. [/quote:92c48810f7]Cause it looks clean!  :cool: \r\n\r\n\r\nNice work man, your paint jobs have become top notch, I dig that color, and the Super-Bit rims look really cool with that body.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (42999, '703c145b9d', 'armchair rc\'ing!', 'just got me the coolest tank accesory yet..... the wireless cam mod! :smile: \r\n[img:703c145b9d]http://www.geocities.com/bettyk3332003/tankcamside640.JPG[/img:703c145b9d]\r\nmore pics here http://community.webshots.com/album/138036297rgTmjE\r\nthe range on the cam and tank are good enough for me to drive out the back door and do laps of the house, from the comfort of my lounge room! and the slower speed of the tank makes it easy to drive by screen, just like a reality video game! of course i\'m planning on a remotely controlled tilt feature so\'s i can park this baby under a chick and peek where the sun don\'t shine!! :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43000, '9c772eba3c', '', 'Those are really cool, I want one, but I can\'t have one, \'cause if I had one, I\'d have to get another to do battle with. The problem with that, is it would be a stretch of the budget just to get one, then when I get 2 I\'d wonder if my friends are imaginary, \'cause they never come over to play with me. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43001, '5c3a33d1cd', '', 'After my first rc car(Firefox, baby) died back in like \'84 or \'85, the only thing my dad could afford was "toy store" quality and price... I already had a lot of friends with Nikko Rhinos and their 380 motored little bro(can\'t recall what it was called)... I went with the Monogram Lightning... solid axle, grasshopper-based design, rs540... that thing held its own against Tamiya Hornets, Frogs, and Blackfoots, Kyosho Javelins and Icarus, and one guy l used to know with a heavily invested in Marui Big Bear.... It held together for a few years which was long enough for me to scrape together enough money for the RC10 clone Traxxas Bullet in \'87... I never had access to any real racing scene, but no one I ran with in the hood could come near that thing once I put  a cheap esc and a decent Trinity motor in it. I still have the rolling chassis, and someday I will resurrect it with modern electronics and continue to run the shit out of it... ALL IN MY QUEST FOR FUN. I will also do the same with my long neglected first generation(pre-slipper clutch) Rustler, which also holds a special place in my heart, as every car I\'ve ever been lucky enough to own does.\r\n\r\nFuck all of the people who live to suck the fun out of the hobby I have loved for almost as long as I can remember.');
