INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43387, 'e62e07440a', '', 'Damn Payaso, that looks straight up evil. I\'m glad you decided to redo it. Can\'t believe those flames I cut worked out so well for that body. You made excellent use of them.\r\n\r\nDT, what can I say? I\'ve got piles of Thunder Charger bodies, and I see nothing in them, but you seem to turn them into masterpieces over and over.\r\n\r\nCabo, That Beetle is too cool, but I can wait to see what else you gots up your sleeve.\r\n\r\nSG219, I had my entry in before your deadline, I thinks you\'s owes me a dumpster dinner. Then we can kick it in the ally drinking Mad Dog.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43388, 'f5350f1994', 'Re: Round 2', '[quote:f5350f1994="payaso"]This is the car that DEATH rides around in when he\'s not kickin asses....\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:f5350f1994]\r\n\r\nI had that repeating in my head when I was looking at the car, and then I actually saw it...... DEATH, pimpin around the hood, chain smoking non-filters, bumpin\' "Don\'t fear the Reaper", and laughing his ass off.\r\n\r\nAwesome ride, payaso.\r\n\r\n@DT &amp; c dubya.... I couldn\'t tell you guys the amount of time I\'ve spent going through your galleries, drooling on your rides.... These cars are perfect examples of why.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43389, '40f3de20ac', '', 'Well good, I\'m glad it\'s not like that. I feel better now, and Payaso, your new entry looks great, so I think you made right move.\r\n\r\nWell I\'ll tell ya guys,  I go through boughts of depression, and just feel like a POS, that\'s usually when I do an extra special project to build myself back up. I\'ve been real moody lately, so that really has a lot to do with why I tried so hard this time. Any rate, I dig where ya\'ll coming from.\r\n\r\n[quote:40f3de20ac="Cabo"]I\'m happy with my first (and only so far) entry to the contest, I actually did that one because I wanted to and didn\'t try to force it out. sure it didn\'t get the "oh my god" responses, but I\'m cool with that - I\'d much rather have honesty than pity. [/quote:40f3de20ac]I said oh my god. I was like, "Oh my god he modded a Jota". I was so inspired by such a ballsy move, I started masking off my Jota, but I just couldn\'t do it. I didn\'t want to cover the little lambo logo on the hood.  :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43391, 'e972fdb83c', 'Re: Round 2', '[quote:e972fdb83c="payaso"]Well, I just wasn\'t happy with my first shot at the Cuda, so I re did that son of a biatch different all the way up..\r\n\r\nThis one is now on top of a fetted SE chassis, with hand painted alloys from the german site. (the ones that started the whole alloy wheel thing) They are as precise as it gets, and in combonation with the red ZZ gears, it\'s smokin fast.\r\n\r\nI was working out some pent up hostility on this beast, and the colors show it.\r\n\r\nThis is the car that DEATH rides around in when he\'s not kickin asses....\r\n\r\nEnjoy\r\n\r\n[img:e972fdb83c]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10004/normal_Cuda%204.JPG[/img:e972fdb83c]\r\n\r\nCD sent me some flame masks about a year ago, for a Beetle, and they just been sittin so I thought now\'s a good a time as ever. Thanks CD.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:e972fdb83c]\r\n\r\nOK here is the god\'s honest truth, I personally never liked the look of the Cuda Zip.  Don\'t know why, but it never jived.  But Peyaso, you turned that mother into one crazy nice ride!  It looks mean like a serial killer bro.  Amazing job for a pimp that has kept his moddin on the DL for quite a while.  What a Fearsome return.  Great work.');
