INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43534, '559bc2d596', '', 'i have wood floors that are nice and smooth. lately ses are what i play with the most except for the xmod. they aint the fastest but i like the propo.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43535, '2ad7cab1ab', 'you fuckers!!', 'ok now i want to design bits left and right again. dam you all!!\r\n\r\nheres what im working on next. this dude i know in wv has been putting one of these together for years and its almost totally done.\r\n\r\n[img:2ad7cab1ab]http://www.magiccitymustangs.com/pictures/huntsville02/69-70/70RedFastback.jpg[/img:2ad7cab1ab]\r\n\r\nhis was under a cloth today so i didnt snap any pics of it but its the same deal as this one but its totally red with only the racing stripe on the hood. none of the black stuff on the side but hes got chrome running strips. the fucker just got a 65 falcon that is the same red and is almost totally pristine. not all people in wv are total hee haw rednecks.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43536, '9bdcb382dd', '', ':)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43537, 'acb78d7f33', '', 'oh shit hahahahahaha');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43538, 'f4190081d9', '', 'I;m liking the Challenger, but to me, my real prize is my Cuda I just did. There\'s so much passion in it, that it\'s my new favorite..\r\n\r\nAnything they give me will be cool.  That hummer is real dope too, bu tnow that I think about it, I could really use the SE "Starter and Clutch" set\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43539, '2442b6066c', '', 'Well I\'ll tell ya, I really don\'t care.\r\n\r\nI\'m probably favoring superfly\'s car, because I want to see if handles as well on my track. Betty\'s car is really cool, and I\'m really curious how it handles, but ultimately I\'d rather build my own off road car, cause I got plans. I\'d really like to check out ph2t\'s Biff turbo, but I\'ve played with tri-stacked FETs, so its shouldn\'t be any big surprize. I\'d kinda like that SE cause I\'ve killed three SEs trying to figure out that PCB, so I kinda feel like the world owes me a SE. Hue\'s car is really cool, but probably the least desirable to me, because I have a bunch of dual cell Zips, and stretched TCs.\r\n\r\nHow can you pick from such cool stuff? :? \r\n\r\nI hope they just give me last since I\'m the newest mod, so I can just take whatever you guys leave behind. (I\'m serious!)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43540, '1fa34e274f', '', '[quote:1fa34e274f="hogjowlz"]bit props to cabo wabo in the first place, if it werent for him there wouldnt be none of this.[/quote:1fa34e274f]\r\n\r\nyep... thanks, cw.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43541, '3871e0cb92', '', 'Downhill mod is nice, but the slingshot mod adds flight.  Best part is it needs no solder. 8-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43542, '14cf5bf837', 'My old Traxxas Rustler', 'Seeing payasos newly acquired Bandit lurking in the background of his latest T-Maxx pic made me nostalgic for 1/10th scale today, and I had to go diggin\' in my closet and pull out the old Rustler... I bought this truck back in like \'96 or so when they were pretty new(mine is so early, it doesn\'t even have a slipper, which they added soon after they came out), and proceeded to drive the snot out of it. The body is an older Andys(I think) Toyota SR5 that I had bought back in like \'89 when people were first starting to convert buggies into stadium trucks. It was originally mounted on my TRX10 Bullet(waaaaay old school Traxxas buggy), which also sits dormant in my closet, as a rolling chassis waiting for me to get around to resurrecting it. \r\n\r\nThis truck survived several summers of hard back alley bashing, until they repaved the alley and I bought the Pro-Line speed hawg tires to adapt to my newly smooth bashing spot, and soon after, the electronics gave out. It has been sitting ever since, but I think that once I cross a few more smaller scale cars off of my gotta-get list, I will resurrect it with a modern esc and motor. Oh, and this body was only my second attempt at painting, ever... Here are the pics I just snapped earlier tonight, when 219 was up my cribby with his cam...\r\n\r\n[img:14cf5bf837]http://img23.photobucket.com/albums/v70/jaybirdy/rustla2.jpg[/img:14cf5bf837]\r\n\r\n[img:14cf5bf837]http://img23.photobucket.com/albums/v70/jaybirdy/rustla1.jpg[/img:14cf5bf837]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43543, 'b468245aa3', '', 'Dude.... That thing looks kick ass.  You kept it well.\r\n\r\nNow I\'m gonna have to convert the Bandit to the Rusty. Thats what I wanted in the first place, but couldn\'t pass on a new in the box Bandit for 25 beans.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43544, 'b7db937423', '', '[quote:b7db937423="crazydave"]I hope they just give me last since I\'m the newest mod, so I can just take whatever you guys leave behind. (I\'m serious!)[/quote:b7db937423]\r\n\r\nI don\'t think that\'s gonna happen my friend. You put out some awesome cars.\r\n\r\nHow long you think it\'ll take em to get it judged? I mean we always have this forum to deliberate on contests, but they have to do it all through PMs and emails I\'m guessing. :???:  It\'s gonna be difficult for em no doubt.\r\n\r\ni\'m pretty stoked on it, but I\'ve never won anything cool in a contest in my life...lol (won a coolio cd on the radio, but that\'s not cool)\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43545, '5546598713', '', '[quote:5546598713="hogjowlz"]i have wood floors that are nice and smooth. lately ses are what i play with the most except for the xmod. they aint the fastest but i like the propo.[/quote:5546598713]\r\n\r\nSame here. I can\'t get over how well the racer quality is.  I will straight up kick the shit out of anybody in the world on a track.\r\n\r\nMy bits still rule when I wanna go off road, but the SE in my control will kick the shit out of anyboy in the world on a track. There, I said it again. Who wants some?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43546, '7bcda1fece', '', '[quote:7bcda1fece="payaso"]You kept it well.[/quote:7bcda1fece]\r\n\r\nYou wouldn\'t say that if you saw the stock body lol.\r\n\r\n[quote:7bcda1fece="payaso"]Now I\'m gonna have to convert the Bandit to the Rusty.[/quote:7bcda1fece]\r\n\r\nShouldn\'t cost you too much. I went through a thing last fall just before the micros grabbed me where I was planning on converting the Rustla into a \'Pede... It worked out to be like $55 and you figure most of that was the tires, plus the Stampede chassis had a bunch of different parts... Wouldn\'t take nearly as much to go from a Bandit to a Rustler... pretty much the front body mount, rims and tires(I\'d go aftermarket), and a body(I\'d go aftermarket here, too) and you\'d be set, I think... I have a whole folder of Traxxas parts lists and exploded views saved... I\'ll check to make sure nothing else is needed...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43547, 'd6a32f0fcf', '', 'If you could get me a list of parts I need, that would be kick ass.  Get that damn thing runnin dude..lol\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43548, '12c813d759', '', 'dave if you dont win i will protest. hands down that tops anything sinned or anyone  has ever done. true sickness in and out. its probably your least flashy but its true to your original plan which is sickeningly admirable.\r\n\r\ndt your goldenrod really shows that you can polish a turd and make it iller than just about anything.\r\n\r\ncabo i really like that chopped bug. if zz top had a bit that would be it. and the accordia. those angles are perfect.\r\n\r\npayaso i really like your porsche. those lines are insanly clean and i know that chassis is the perfect short track ride.\r\n\r\nmy transam i was just happy to have learned painting skills from watching all of you guys\'s sickness. \r\n\r\nand uh i want that offroad thing or biff. if i get the torino it will end up being an el camino. i have one already but have been hesitant to do anything with it. zipzap shells totally kick ass now. and i should goto bed');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43549, 'b26c31fc98', 'my monsters on fire!', '[img:b26c31fc98]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10027/bitp.10.jpg[/img:b26c31fc98]\r\n\r\n[img:b26c31fc98]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10027/bitp.4.jpg[/img:b26c31fc98]\r\n\r\n[img:b26c31fc98]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10027/bitp.2.jpg[/img:b26c31fc98]\r\n\r\n[img:b26c31fc98]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10027/bitp.5.jpg[/img:b26c31fc98]\r\n\r\n\r\n super bcg chassis, neon green headlights, stadium flags, ute mod with detailed sunk tray, step boards, dual spring suspension (front),  rear suspension is for show, 4.2 motor, 12:1 gears, antenna extension mod, front sun visor and jacked waaaaay up.\r\n\r\n[img:b26c31fc98]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10027/bitp.6.jpg[/img:b26c31fc98]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43550, '24cdd4a3ed', '', 'Damn ...that is just flat out cool. A lot of detail. How does it run?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43551, '7b2d6a914e', '', 'fuckin\' beautiful man.....  talk about a beast......\r\n\r\npre tell how did you do the flame work bitch?\r\n\r\n\r\n :D \r\n\r\nph2t.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43552, 'f7690375b3', '', '[quote:f7690375b3="crazydave"]RS is making me so mad. :mad:\r\n\r\nI\'m already having problems with the idea of coughing up 20 just to get a Jeep body, don\'t need the chassis, then they pull this with the F-150. Now I either have to decide, or buy both.  :sad: \r\n\r\nThank god the TA is just a body set.[/quote:f7690375b3]\r\n\r\n\r\nCD...there is a ZZ Wrangler up for auction on Ebay....99 cents NR.\r\n\r\nThe bidding is up to like $2.25. Check it out: \r\nhttp://cgi.ebay.com/ws/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&amp;item=3190832025&amp;category=34063&amp;sspagename=STRK%3AMEBWA%3AIT&amp;rd=1');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43553, 'fd1d31bd8d', '', 'looking forward to seeing some of your stuff take shape!  :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43554, 'c23d63e73a', '', '[quote:c23d63e73a="payaso"][quote:c23d63e73a="crazydave"]I hope they just give me last since I\'m the newest mod, so I can just take whatever you guys leave behind. (I\'m serious!)[/quote:c23d63e73a]\r\n\r\nI don\'t think that\'s gonna happen my friend. You put out some awesome cars.[/quote:c23d63e73a]...and you know, that was really awkward for me. I felt guilty, because I have the unique honor of being eligible for a ll the bP contest, and this one too. I originally planned to sit it out, and let you guys have your deserved glory, for all the hard work you\'ve done in the past putting up contest. No other site was running back to back contest like you guys.\r\n\r\nSo anyways, when I realized no matter what we did we\'re getting a cool prize, I had to do something. \r\n\r\n[quote:c23d63e73a]How long you think it\'ll take em to get it judged? I mean we always have this forum to deliberate on contests, but they have to do it all through PMs and emails I\'m guessing. :???:  It\'s gonna be difficult for em no doubt.[/quote:c23d63e73a]If they were smart they\'d set up a chat room.\r\n\r\n[quote:c23d63e73a]i\'m pretty stoked on it, but I\'ve never won anything cool in a contest in my life...lol (won a coolio cd on the radio, but that\'s not cool)[/quote:c23d63e73a]I could tell your having fun with this. That cool, becaus emy firts impression of you was that beat up bB. I could tell just by looking at that, that you were really having fun with that. So it was cool to see you having some fun again. Seems like you had been taking a break from modding. Hope this gets you back in the saddle again.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:c23d63e73a="hogjowlz"]its probably your least flashy but its true to your original plan which is sickeningly admirable. [/quote:c23d63e73a]Yeah, I know, that\'s what amazes the hell out of me. I\'ve never stretched a project out over 2 months, and any project that lasted more than a day never stuck to the original plan. So the fact I held onto a vision for 2 months straight, is just freakin\' amazing.\r\n\r\n\r\n....and hey DT, since th contest is over, you gonna let us in on that special project you didn\'t finish? I\'m curious, because I have a feeling the rest of us are lucky you didn\'t try to top your previous efforts, that would be hard to beat.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43555, 'b8bc045081', '', 'HOw does that thing turn correctly? I made one and it didnt turn well.  :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43556, '6f6dcebca1', '', '[quote:6f6dcebca1="payaso"]If you could get me a list of parts I need, that would be kick ass.  Get that damn thing runnin dude..lol\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D[/quote:6f6dcebca1] You should just need front supension arms, shock tower,  medium sized shocks, front body mount, and of coarse truck wheels and tires. \r\n\r\nTraxxas stuff is really interchangable, even my Stampede shared about 90% of it\'s parts with the Bandit.\r\n\r\n\r\nCool Rustler, Bird, if I still had that in my closet, I\'d be running it.  :-D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43557, 'f023d87625', '', 'screw you guys - this was gonna be my personal homepage with poetry and pictures of my wife\'s cat until you guys showed up  :razz: \r\n\r\nbut seriously, thanks for the props - you know we all deserve them, each member lends their own sense of style, fun, and education to this community making it what it is.\r\nwhich is nothing short of amazing.\r\nso big props back to all of you!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43558, '1fca82118e', '', 'well like you guys have eluded to, I\'d be happy with no prize.\r\nbut like I\'m gonna turn one down? ya right.\r\n\r\nso with that, since I\'ll probably never be able to build an off-roader - I\'d like to see what betty\'s bits do. (if not I\'ll just make crazydave build me one like I do for everything else lol)\r\n\r\nhue\'s challenger should be a mean bitch, if I know hue - that thing is gonna be perfect in everyway possible. that\'d be a killer score.\r\nfor that matter, so would superfly\'s sled. those two dudes do some great work and seem to be on the finest details.\r\n\r\nthe starter and clutch se would be cool for several reasons, but mainly because I only have that savanah se.\r\n\r\nsessiz\'s poster would be cool too - the way that dude produces graphics, it\'s sure to be an art piece.\r\n\r\nph2t\'s biff thing would be cool, but I\'m with crazydave on that one - plus just from past experiences, I prefer crazydave\'s fetting to ph2t\'s.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nas for the entries in the contest - you guys rocked, each of you.\r\ncrazydave took the friggin cake, it\'s just insane what he built. I\'m jealous and proud all at the same time. I love it. after having so many of my chassis mods (fets, dual cells, anti-boost) through you - just as in real life - I\'ve found my mechanic, I never take my bits to anyone else but you. you consistantly prove you have it all. you can mod the hell out of a chassis to compete with anyone... and you can mod the hell out of a shell to compete with anyone... you\'re like the evander holyfield of bits - you kick all sorts of asses.\r\n\r\nDT, you stepped in to a new realm of modding awhile ago and haven\'t looked back since. I honestly think we\'re seeing some of the cleanest modding from around the globe when we see your whips. You make the factories jealous, they can\'t mold perfection, but you can make it.\r\nyou\'re the smoothest pimp around and probably have the best head on your shoulders out of all of us. you\'re a diamond - a truely amazing find and something you just can\'t stop watching.\r\n\r\nhog - you\'re like my hero. you\'re a fuckin nut and what you produce, is exactly what everyone expects from you... crazy.\r\nthere is not 1 other member here or any where else that has come up with the stuff you have - you\'re truely unique.\r\nfrom the butt char-g to your last entry - they make me laugh and they make me impressed because of your slightly off kilter approach to everything, but still making it a bad ass - that\'s a real gift dude.\r\npeople try to search for that, hang on to it, whatever. that\'s what I believe we have in our youth and loose as we age - you haven\'t and you\'re a golden child for it. finishing up your last entry in the time you did was awesome to watch too. I got to witness it via chat and I could tell you were crankin and in the hogjowlz mode. you\'re a bigger influence than I think you know.\r\n\r\npayaso - man it was good to see you getting back in to pumping something out for the other pimps to see. I\'ve gotten to see so many of your works that nobody else ever has. you got me started in this whole mess so it\'s good to see you having fun and actually showing some one all the cool shit I\'ve gotten to see.\r\nI could tell that you really did have fun with your entries and again - you came up with something original. that\'s amazing - I\'m always stuck thinking everything has already been done and then you come up out with something to make our jaws drop.\r\n\r\n\r\nhope I didn\'t miss anyone, if I did - forgive me, I\'m still seepy lol');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43559, 'e0cacade5e', '', 'Aaaaaight... I pulled up all of the parts lists and exploded views, and heres what I got so far... I\'ll double check later to be sure I didn\'t miss anything...\r\n\r\nThe shocks, towers, bulkheads, steering blocks, and rear carriers are all the same throughout the three vehicles... but the Bandit does have some different stuff than the other two... you would need:\r\n\r\n3655- suspension arms,long, rear...     $10\r\n3631- front suspension arms...              $8\r\n3641- f&amp;r non adjustable camber links...$3\r\n3139- 62mm turnbuckles...                   $2\r\n(I would just reuse the Bandit ends on those, but #2742 is 6 for $4)\r\n3632- 30 degree caster blocks...            $4\r\n(the description is the same between the 2, but the part# is different)\r\n1951- half shafts, inner and outer...         $6\r\n(they also sell a six pack of these #1953 for $10)\r\n1914- front body mount...                      $5\r\n\r\nI didn\'t get the part numbers for wheels, tires or body because, honestly, Pro-Line has much nicer looking rims and bodies readily available, and waaaay better tires in a bunch of styles and compounds, all for not much more than the Traxxas stuff.\r\n\r\nDon\'t worry, fellas... I will be getting to mine soon, installing a decent esc and hotter motor, along with bearings, a slipper clutch, and one of those Pro-Line F-150 bodies, too.\r\n\r\nEDIT... Oh, yeah, thanks for the props on my truck, fellas! :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43560, '602c7b028c', '', '[quote:602c7b028c="payaso"]..the SE in my control will kick the shit out of anyboy in the world on a track. There, I said it again. Who wants some?[/quote:602c7b028c]\r\n\r\nYou know I want some.  8-)  \r\n\r\nI\'ll be drivin\' a $3.50 TC with another $5 of fets and motor into it (at 1/64th scale, that\'s huge money)... bring it on!  :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43561, '21b5e86872', '', 'As usual Cabo comes through with the perfect thing to say. \r\nDitto all of that, I couldn\'t have said it better.\r\n\r\nThat\'s your gift. You\'re a unique, creative, and entertaining character. That comes through in your cars, you\'ve inspired others with your creativity, but your real gift is the way you relate to people. You\'re genuine cool guy, and that comes through. I think that\'s the major reason why people keep coming back to bitPimps.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43562, '3e60d2e194', 'Someday, when I hit the lottery...', 'I would throw down for airfare and lodging for all the clicksters to have an international pimp get together, where we can all party and race and have show &amp; tell with all of our toys.... There would be a pimp elimination race series, where long standing long distance rivalries would be handled... complete with an audience of other pimps throwin\' loot down on their picks.\r\nThere would also be other comps like "who\'s the best hammered bit driver?", where drunken pimps would be timed on a set obstacle course, and the "too busy laughing to care" races, where it would be judged on how much weight could be smoked before cars started to lose their charge...\r\n\r\nIf any of you other guys share my dream... feel free to come up with fun shit we could all do at the shindig...');
