INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43592, '00ebbd0528', '', 'been having a ball with this little baby! a friend lent me his old nikko buggy (about 15 years old!!) which i\'ve been bashing around the yard. rollovers look cool on screen and getting air off jumps and bumps is pretty funny! on a side note, this electric buggy is bullet proof! never been serviced in it\'s life and probably sitting in a shed for the last few years, charged the batt and bang! kicked over first time! lotsa fun, i hope to get some footage digified so\'s we can put it up for all to enjoy!\r\n\r\n[img:00ebbd0528]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10012/normal_nikkocam1.JPG[/img:00ebbd0528]\r\n[img:00ebbd0528]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10012/normal_nikkocam3.JPG[/img:00ebbd0528]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43593, '5ee8b608f9', 'Some Mod\'s Challenger', 'Well, I\'m glad I wasn\'t on the same schedule as the mods,\r\n\'cuz I was runnin\' behind on this one. Anyway, she\'s done and\r\nI\'m pretty damn happy with it... it may be my favorite, of the \r\ncars I\'ve built. It\'ll be fun to ship it off to one of the pimp mods...\r\nI wonder who? :???: \r\n\r\nSpecs:\r\n- stretched Thunder Charger chassis (aluminum tubing) \r\n- tab-lowered \r\n- shaved/sculpted rear tires, so they tuck up into the rear fenders \r\n- shaved inside of body to make room for rear tires and steering \r\n- custom paint (custom-mixed color) \r\n- custom decals\r\n- custom painted controller\r\n- mosfets \r\n- custom pcb cover \r\n- kick-ass mystery 3.8 \r\n\r\nPics:\r\n\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_package.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]\r\n\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_front.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]\r\n\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_back.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]\r\n\r\nthe chassis:\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_chassis_top.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]\r\n\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_chassis_side.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]\r\n\r\nthe mosfet mod... I routed the wires more neatly\r\nthan normal on this one (I ran the shortest wire \r\nunder the tilted fet). I think I\'m gonna make this \r\nstyle my norm from now on.\r\n[img:5ee8b608f9]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/pc_pcb.jpg[/img:5ee8b608f9]');
