INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43777, 'ab8c075fdc', '', '[quote:ab8c075fdc="cj"]Great job guys I love the new 4x4.  Now all you need is a truck body and you are set.[/quote:ab8c075fdc]\r\n\r\nThats gonna be hard!!!  I have to find a body that can be chopped for one.  Since Radio Shack\'s R&amp;D department has been jerkin\' off for soooooo long.  Not a single new item in months for the Xmod!!!  Plenty for ZZ\'s which is nice, but it is not the only thing they sell!!  \r\n\r\n\r\n@ CJ--  If the opportunity presents itself, please kick someone from RS corperate in the nads for me.  Thanks and tell them I sent ya!! :lol:  \r\n\r\n[size=18:ab8c075fdc][color=green:ab8c075fdc]Thanks for the props again pimps!![/color:ab8c075fdc]  :-) [/size:ab8c075fdc]\r\n\r\n\r\nI got some shots of the body shots.  Some serious dremeling went into it!!\r\n\r\n\r\nHere are the new pics.........\r\n\r\n[img:ab8c075fdc]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Xmod%20Stuff/Xmodtires_033_5.jpg[/img:ab8c075fdc]\r\nThe smaller tires I mentioned earlier.  The car moves alot better, because of less weight, but it loses in clearance.  Big.\r\n\r\n[img:ab8c075fdc]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Xmod%20Stuff/Xmodtires_033_3.jpg[/img:ab8c075fdc]\r\nThe rear wheel wells.  Comparision of new body vs. 4x4 body mod.  Serious difference!!\r\n\r\n[img:ab8c075fdc]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Xmod%20Stuff/Xmodtires_033_2.jpg[/img:ab8c075fdc]\r\nFront wheel wells.  Same situation, major dremeling needed!!\r\n\r\n[img:ab8c075fdc]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Xmod%20Stuff/Xmodtires_033_4.jpg[/img:ab8c075fdc]\r\nNew vs. modded body.  All unneeded mounts and screws were removed.\r\n\r\n[img:ab8c075fdc]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/Xmod%20Stuff/Xmodtires_033_1.jpg[/img:ab8c075fdc]\r\nAnother pic.\r\n\r\nHope this helps with anyone interested in doing this to their Xmod.  it involves alot of plastic grinding to a perfectly good body!!!!  \r\n\r\n(insert Dr. Frankenstein laugh/cackle)\r\n\r\nI have a couple of ideas about increasing ground clearance, but it seems like its going to be very, very, very difficult!!  :???:');
