INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43825, 'b158a5d1e0', 'Xmods Racing is ON! w/ Rules', 'I saw this on their XmodsRC site about the rules.\r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]DISCLAIMER: Void in the states of CT, MD, VT, and where prohibited by law. Open only to legal residents of the 50 states of the U.S. and D.C. who are 13 years of age or older prior to registering and who have or own a RadioShack XMODS Custom RC car prior to registering. You may pre-register online or register at an event location. Entrance fee for event is $30.00. Upon check-in, each registered driver will receive a competitor\'s gift pack valued at $40. Ends 9/19. Travel and/or prize restrictions apply. First prize winners must be available for travel during September 2004. For full Official Rules send a self-addressed, stamped envelope (by 11/19/04) to: 2004 XRL National Tournament "Rules", P.O. Box 6375, Burbank, CA 91510.[/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\n\r\nnow I want to break this down a bit.\r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]DISCLAIMER: Void in the states of CT, MD, VT, and where prohibited by law. [/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\nDoes that mean that those states my not see races?\r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]Open only to legal residents of the 50 states of the U.S. and D.C. who are 13 years of age or older prior to registering and who have or own a RadioShack XMODS Custom RC car prior to registering. [/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\n\r\nThe package for the car saw recommend for ages 12 and up? :???: \r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]You may pre-register online or register at an event location. [/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\nWhat registering online where is the link to register?\r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]Entrance fee for event is $30.00. Upon check-in, each registered driver will receive a competitor\'s gift pack valued at $40.[/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\n\r\n$30 for entry fee and $40 worth of stuff doesn\'t sound bad.  But Still a 13 year old with $30 come on now get real!! \r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]Ends 9/19. Travel and/or prize restrictions apply. First prize winners must be available for travel during September 2004.[/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\n\r\nWe have an end date when will the start date be?  And winner must travel in September after the contest is over?\r\n\r\n[quote:b158a5d1e0]For full Official Rules send a self-addressed, stamped envelope (by 11/19/04) to: 2004 XRL National Tournament "Rules", P.O. Box 6375, Burbank, CA 91510.[/quote:b158a5d1e0]\r\n\r\nCalifornia what about Texas were RS is based can\'t anyone there write up the rules for the contest?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (43826, 'ddee4af293', 'Damn Computer!!!', 'Hey guys, don\'t think I\'ve been dissing on you guys because I haven\'t joined up with you guys in the AIM chatroom.\r\n\r\nAs I\'ve been saying, we had problems with our cable, my wife installed AOL, it crashed our system. for the last 2 weeks we were booting in safe mode half the time, we have to re-install AOL evertime we turn our computer on, just to keep our system working.\r\n\r\nWe had a bunch of stuff to back up, and we were being lazy about it, \'cause our CD burner is flaking out, and only burns at 4x...\r\n\r\nBlah blah blah, long story short, system completely crashed last night, we got the important stuff backed up before we lost \'er, but not everything. Then to top it off, our restoration CD developed a crack in it, and was acting flaky, we had to install windows manually, which we\'ve never done, and all our drivers are on that CD.\r\n\r\nSo my wife was up half the night working on it, she got pissed and declared it broke. I\'ve been up since 4:00 this morning, managed to get us about 90% functional. I found a old 3.0 version of AOL on the win98 CD, and that\'s how I managed to get here.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDamn, sorry for the rant, but this has been frustrating.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, I think our system is stable right now, I\'m gonna be looking into an ethernet connection for our cable, but either way, I should be jumping into the chats soon, I hope.');
