INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44649, '2b83f4d4d6', '2004 NHL Playoffs', '...continuing the convo from where-ever (too lazy to go get the link for you - sorry)\r\n\r\nWe\'ve got Tampa Bay and Philly\r\nand we\'ve got San Jose and Calgary\r\n\r\nI\'m torn, I have no emotional dedication to any of the teams, only slight sentiments, favorite players, and national pride lol\r\n\r\nSan Jose vs Calgary:\r\nNot sure who I want to win here yet. Paul Korea isn\'t on SJ anymore and he was the only reason I started watching them. Calgary hasn\'t done shit since the 80\'s lol. I do like Calgary because they\'re an old team, and they haven\'t done shit - they\'ve always worked hard, but with only Theo Fluery, they only had lots of heart, but they\'re an old time team. SJ is new - but they have done shit recently - they\'re good.\r\nI guess my national pride pulls for SJ, but my love for hockey pulls for Calgary.\r\n\r\nTampa vs Philly:\r\nTampa is surprising the shit out of me. I never really watched them. These guys are pure super-stars. The moves, all of it, they\'ve got it - it\'s frickin amazing to watch. Philly is a rough team - they get their work done in the trenches and goals usually aren\'t pretty, but they\'re banged home. I like Philly\'s work ethic, they are kind of a rival (though not a huge one since Blues only play them a hand full of times).\r\nI think the only thing that stops me from fully supporting TB is the fact that they\'re a new expansion team. Philly has worked years - TB hasn\'t.');
