INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44824, '88d0e06b3b', '', 'BTW, found another site with some good FET modding info. This basically eliminates the resistance of some resistors, and does the bypass mod to the FET like cyborgzero told us to do.....\r\n\r\nhttp://members.cox.net/codesuidae/FetMod.html\r\n\r\nI\'m thinking of doing this FET mod to my SE....micro_amps, c\'mon dude, why won\'t you just share your method with us? Your goal is to do the FET mod for people who have no electronics experience, but for those of us who want to give it a try, just spill it bro!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44829, '44a96853cc', '', 'Hey thanks for keeping us updated. :-) \r\n\r\nI read it over, and I\'ll tell you what this adds to what we already got.\r\n\r\nThere are four resistors that can be removed and jumperf to open up more current to the FET\'s gate. There are also 2 more than can be removed and replced with resistors of a higher value, for a slight increase in peformance, something the author didn\'t reccomend bothering to waste your time with.\r\n\r\nI\'m gonna try to remove and jumper those four restors, and see how it works. Cyborgzero\'s bypass mod has made my SE an enjoyable little car, so I can only imagine that any more improvement, no matter how slight can only be a good thing.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44826, '0d21422f28', '', '[quote:0d21422f28="DarkTari"][quote:0d21422f28="dodgeracerguy"]wowzors, that\'s just stock buddy, you didnt\' do anything[/quote:0d21422f28]\r\nNot Hate\'n At All,  But He\'s Right, it\'s just lowered with the wheels wells modded.  Paint is stock w/ PT Cruiser Wheels, but sometimes it\'s hard to make improvements on Perfection  :???:   \r\nI find it hard to meddle with any of the SBCG\'s, well there is 1 I\'m doin soon, stay tuned!   :cool:[/quote:0d21422f28]\r\n\r\nI know you\'re not hatin\', but I just wanted to say that i don\'t think every car needs a million things done to it, to be cool. Often times, a little is enough. I think it\'s a lot easier to take a car too far than it is to show restraint and know when to stop. It\'s all a matter of taste, but i don\'t think a car needs to have a full body kit, a wing, two-tone paint and a full blown interior to be cool, nor do I think any of those things make a car "better."  It\'s the word "just" in both posts quoted, that really bothers me... why should someone get even a little bit dissed for deciding, "it\'s done, I like it just like this".. even if that means stock outta the box.');
