INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44833, '14535630f0', '', 'Found a mistake in that link. I had to go back to make sure I wasn\'t losin\' it, but here\'s the screen capture to prove it.\r\n[img:14535630f0]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/capture2.jpg[/img:14535630f0]\r\n[img:14535630f0]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/capture1.jpg[/img:14535630f0]\r\nNotice it says RDB1 should be bridged. That is wrong. That is the one that cyborgzero had told us to remove when doing his bypass mod.\r\n\r\nBridgeing that one with the voltage bypass mod, will make your car run nonstop.\r\n\r\nI bridged RDB2-4, and there is pretty decent gain in performance. So that info is good, thanks for sharing it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44834, '0d0b52f51e', '', '[quote:0d0b52f51e="hue35"][quote:0d0b52f51e="DarkTari"][quote:0d0b52f51e="dodgeracerguy"]wowzors, that\'s just stock buddy, you didnt\' do anything[/quote:0d0b52f51e]\r\nNot Hate\'n At All,  But He\'s Right, it\'s just lowered with the wheels wells modded.  Paint is stock w/ PT Cruiser Wheels, but sometimes it\'s hard to make improvements on Perfection  :???:   \r\nI find it hard to meddle with any of the SBCG\'s, well there is 1 I\'m doin soon, stay tuned!   :cool:[/quote:0d0b52f51e]\r\n\r\nI know you\'re not hatin\', but I just wanted to say that i don\'t think every car needs a million things done to it, to be cool. Often times, a little is enough. I think it\'s a lot easier to take a car too far than it is to show restraint and know when to stop. It\'s all a matter of taste, but i don\'t think a car needs to have a full body kit, a wing, two-tone paint and a full blown interior to be cool, nor do I think any of those things make a car "better."  It\'s the word "just" in both posts quoted, that really bothers me... why should someone get even a little bit dissed for deciding, "it\'s done, I like it just like this".. even if that means stock outta the box.[/quote:0d0b52f51e]\r\n\r\nI know I\'m a guy who has yet to post any mods so take this comment with a grain of salt. \r\n\r\nI agree with Hue on the "just" thing. Sometimes less is more. I like the stock look of a lot of my micros (Particularly my muscle car SE\'s and some superbits), but I also see minor things about them that I would like to change. I think Sinned took an already good looking body and made it look even better just by lowering it. Then again, I have seen some other cars that had the shit modded out of them, which are stunning works of art...many of DT\'s cars are good examples. \r\n\r\nI find all of your pimps work inspirational, but there is something about some of the "more simple" mods that gets me going. I suppose its because I feel like those mods are something that I can accomplish, being a "rookie" so to speak, and still create a nice looking ride.\r\n\r\nWith that said, I agree with CD that a little constructive criticism is a good thing. It helps some of you more experienced pimps push the envelope and provides a learning experience for the rookies.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44835, '4dea2031ed', '', 'Yeah i havent had alot of time to work on it, ive been doing alot of paintball....\r\n\r\n\r\nlose/chickin');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44836, 'f483b7842d', '', 'I think that I\'m inspired by all the cool modding DT does, and how well it all works together, that\'s a skill. On the other hand, I\'m inspired by how just straight up clean Hue\'s work is, that\'s a skill too. I\'m left in the middle thinking, how can I do all that and keep it clean, that\'s my style. We all have our own style.\r\n\r\nBottom line, DT, and Sinned went about the Mercedes 2 different ways, just because one has more mods into doesn\'t make it better, it\'s just 2 different interpretations, and that\'s what makes it interesting. \r\n\r\nI think once we\'ve seen what someone like Sinned has done, we expect him to produce on that level everytime. Sometimes I feel like that expectation is put on me, but it just don\'t work like that.\r\n\r\nNow if DT wants to criticize Sinned for not doing enough, that\'s his point of view, and he has the car to back up his point of view, so we really can\'t condemn him for his point of view, and making it known.');
