INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44914, 'ab4516a12d', '', 'ruh roh... (but a good ruh roh)\r\n\r\nokay, talked to both dudes today, the 2 dudes that thought of doing their own hosting.\r\n1, by the time we\'ll need it won\'t be ready.\r\nthe other, might be ready - but it\'s not something any of us would gamble on.\r\n\r\nso here\'s the latest (just FYI),\r\n\r\nI did find another host. so far, my research shows their respectable and a reliable host (this all from what I\'ve read - no personal experience)\r\nbut, thus far - they offer better things in some areas (probably the areas that matter most) and less in other (these areas are very specific).\r\nwhile I do have the desire and need for those "special" areas/attributes, the overall price vs what is offered is either comparable or beats what we have now.\r\n\r\nthe price is the same.\r\nhere\'s what is different.\r\ncurrently I have 300 MB of space, with the new plan I\'ll have 750 MB, all of that I\'ll give to bitPimps. that\'s 450 more MB, that\'s alot in web talk (or should be)\r\n\r\ncurrently I have unlimited bandwidth, with the new plan I\'ll have 15 GB/month of bandwidth, more than we\'ll need.\r\n\r\n1 database - this could be an issue - I need to check in to more details (i.e. max # of user connections / queries at once, bandwidth, etc.)\r\n\r\n\r\noverall, here\'s my thoughts.\r\nfor the last month I\'ve been less than happy with our current host.\r\nwe are in a time of need $ wise.\r\nour current plan meets our needs, but in my opinion, just barely.\r\nmy future possibilities seem to offer more at the same price, in my opinion.\r\nI feel I\'m a pretty good judge on hosting opportunities and I\'m leaning towards moving from our current host to a new one.\r\n\r\noverall, the decision is mine until $ from outside sources comes in and with that - I\'m going to do more research and try to make a decision.\r\n\r\nany thoughts you might have would be much appreciated.');
