INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (44968, 'dce23c16b8', '', '[quote:dce23c16b8="crazydave"]Found a mistake in that link. I had to go back to make sure I wasn\'t losin\' it, but here\'s the screen capture to prove it.\r\n[img:dce23c16b8]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/capture2.jpg[/img:dce23c16b8]\r\n[img:dce23c16b8]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/capture1.jpg[/img:dce23c16b8]\r\nNotice it says RDB1 should be bridged. That is wrong. That is the one that cyborgzero had told us to remove when doing his bypass mod.\r\n\r\nBridgeing that one with the voltage bypass mod, will make your car run nonstop.\r\n\r\nI bridged RDB2-4, and there is pretty decent gain in performance. So that info is good, thanks for sharing it.[/quote:dce23c16b8]\r\n\r\nNo trouble at all pimp...\r\n\r\nOh, BTW crazydave....have you tried adding an extra cell to the SE after the FET mod, and do you know exactly how many MPH that thing can go? I hear RCmart.com has a Tamiya 4WD speed checker if you look around in the Mini-Z section...here\'s a few links:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.rcmart.com/catalog/product_info.php?cPath=144_21_80&amp;products_id=399&amp;PHPSESSID=2598d76f7ed4dbf40493ff66d3426a82\r\n\r\nhttp://www.etamiya.com/catalog/product_info.php?products_id=892\r\n\r\nWhen I get enough money, I plan to buy it...I\'m adding it to my "list of things to buy when I have 1000+ dollars". :-)');
