INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45248, 'fb4b654a3e', '', 'Finks, I researched that Palm Cruiser some more, and the 8 aa\'s are for the charger. That 6 minute runtime is about sucky, though.\r\n\r\nI\'m hatin\' on boat peeps right now lol... My pops just bought a 23 foot Wellcraft the other day, and a dude I grew up with bought an 18 foot somethingoranother the same day. I am super jealous. I\'m hoping that my pops will offer his old boat up to me on the cheap tip. \r\n\r\nIf we do end up doing boats, I\'m probly gonna try to do a replica of my pops\' new one.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45249, '781684fe80', 'Contest: Summer-Time Swing &amp; Bling', 'It\'s getting nicer and nicer outside... \r\nSummer\'s coming and the bitPimps are gonna bring it in with style and of course the pimp attitude.\r\nWe\'re looking for summer themed rides\r\n(e.g. a boat, a car/truck pulling a boat, a convertable, any combo there of, etc.)\r\nWe got it swingin, so now it\'s your turn to get it blingin.\r\n\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]Contest:[/b:781684fe80]\r\nSummer-time Swing &amp; Bling\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]Start Date:[/b:781684fe80]\r\nFriday, May 21st 2004\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]End Date:[/b:781684fe80]\r\nFriday, July 16th, 2004 @ 7:00 PM (CST)\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]Prizes:[/b:781684fe80]\r\n[i:781684fe80]1st place[/i:781684fe80]\r\n- Dremel set\r\n[img:781684fe80]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/11_1st.jpg[/img:781684fe80]\r\n\r\n[i:781684fe80]2nd place[/i:781684fe80]\r\n- Air-Brush kit\r\n[img:781684fe80]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/11_2nd.jpg[/img:781684fe80]\r\n\r\n[i:781684fe80]3rd place[/i:781684fe80]\r\n- Hobby Knife set\r\n[img:781684fe80]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/11_3rd.jpg[/img:781684fe80]\r\n\r\n[i:781684fe80]4th place[/i:781684fe80]\r\n- Helping Hands w/ Magnifying Glass\r\n[img:781684fe80]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/11_4th.jpg[/img:781684fe80]\r\n\r\n[i:781684fe80]5th place[/i:781684fe80]\r\n- Micro Screw Driver set\r\n[img:781684fe80]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10001/11_5th.jpg[/img:781684fe80]\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]Rules:[/b:781684fe80]\r\n- Micro R/C\'s only (bit char-g, microsizers, zipzaps/se\'s, clones, micro boats, etc.) \r\n- No previous bitPimp contest winning car can enter.\r\n- Enter as many as you wish. \r\n- [b:781684fe80]Must have your username and "bitPimps" on a piece of paper [/b:781684fe80]in at least 1 picture of your entry. ([url=http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=654]Click here for some examples[/url])\r\n- You can post as many photos of your entry as you feel necessary. \r\n- Only registered users may enter. (bitPimps admins and moderators not eligable)\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]Judging Criteria:[/b:781684fe80] (in no specific order)\r\n- Mod content \r\n- Paint job \r\n- Functionality\r\n(if you would like to submit video to offer proof of your work, we\'ll consider that come judge time)\r\n- Sex appeal \r\n- Pimp-tude\r\n\r\n[b:781684fe80]* NOTE:[/b:781684fe80]\r\nWe require valid entry photo\'s to ensure that people don\'t \'snag\' a picture from another site, of a car that isn\'t theirs.\r\n\r\nGood luck pimps! :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45250, 'f9ad6ff7d7', '', 'I have a Xmod, And You do need a lot of space (I drive it on the driveway) and if You have enough space and enough money You can make Xmods clock out at over 40MPH, (using the right after market motors, FET\'s, carbon fiber parts, bearings, and lots of weight reduction)  If You want to go over 40MPH You need to spend at least $150.00 prob. more but You can still make this go about 20-25mph with Radioshack parts. There good but I like Bits better. I like working on bits better. :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45251, '1d20427039', '', 'Cool cars....but your avatar is smokin\'!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45252, '38c1d304d5', '', 'my porche body came in good order, but the concrete out bach took care of that! i contacted toyeast regarding the missing pinions and rear facing motor mount from my set and they got back to me in 3 days stating that they have sent me the replacements and they are very sorry. i\'m pretty happy with that and i\'m confident that the replacements will be correct.\r\nregarding spacers, i\'m told that using paper shims to fine tune the gear mesh is common, and i tried it and it\'s a goer!\r\n\r\n[size=18:38c1d304d5]IMPORTANT NOTE FOR LOGIC LIGHTSET USERS:[/size:38c1d304d5]\r\n\r\ni got one of these and tested it out by touching the terminals to confirm it worked. no probs there so i installed it, switched it on and the lights and the motor were dead. i discovered that the screw lugs for the lightset were touching a couple of neighbouring compenents on the pcb, causing a short of some description. easily fixed by trimming down the little lugs so they resemble the size and shape of the motor lugs. once installed i gotta say the headlights are really bright! cons are that they only come on when using the throttle and they dip when a lotta current is drawn by the motor or when the batteries die.\r\n\r\nand is it just me or are those h plates really flimsy when slamming headfirst into walls? :-(');
