INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45609, 'c1c08c84a2', 'hey', 'SHIT ALERT!!!!!excuse my language,but i had one,they are crap!they have a v tail and a motor that lakes it up and down.It says it is,but [b:c1c08c84a2]it is not a beginners plane.[/b:c1c08c84a2] best go with a kit from GWS and a micro system that you put together.look on ebay type in GWS.itll cost more,but its worth it.they are so slow and easy to fly.when you learn,you will lear to do some aerobatics.my dad once pulled about 20 loops in a row with his slow stick...ive pulled about 9 with mine before,but someone stopped me.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45610, 'c2e3aed344', '', 'Could you work out a special deal if I just bought it all as one package, or atleast most (like only one controller or something, and maybe just the stage 2 motor)?  Also, does the chassis set include a motor?  Thanks alot.\r\n\r\nActually, I tell ya what, for the Chassis, one controller, partial AWD kit, and the skyline body (plus any other goodies you might wish to throw in) I\'ll give ya $25 shipped.  I just need to make sure with my parents I can use the money =P.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45611, '2f61dbc2e2', '', '[quote:2f61dbc2e2="hogjowlz"]they are a really expensive type of transistor. the ones used on bits are about the size of a grain of rice so if you cant solder a dual cell i wouldnt bother trying these yet.[/quote:2f61dbc2e2]Agreed.\r\n\r\nWith that said, a MOSFET is not the type of thing you\'d find at a hobby store, you\'d have to order them from an electronics supply, like Mouser or Digikey.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45612, 'de3e4a27e2', '', 'and to add to all that...\r\n\r\nsince you\'re in the US, I\'d highly recommend procuring crazydave\'s services to do your FET mods. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45613, '7157842e2f', 'Mosfet Mod: Where, Who, How, etc.', 'There\'s been so many questions about the mosfet mod.\r\nFrom where to buy the chips or the mod, who supplies the chips or who can do the mod, etc., etc.\r\nso here\'s a post that put\'s it all into perspective.\r\n\r\n[b:7157842e2f]How hard is it to do the mod?[/b:7157842e2f]\r\nDifficult. If you can\'t read and understand the directions posted in this forum, then you shouldn\'t attempt the mod. You need solid electrical and soldering skills.\r\n\r\n[b:7157842e2f]Where can I buy the "fets" for the mod?[/b:7157842e2f]\r\nNot at your local hobby store. You\'ll find them at an electronics supply store like Mouser or Digikey.\r\n\r\n[b:7157842e2f]Who on this site can do the "fet" mod for me and where are they located?[/b:7157842e2f]\r\ncrazydave - US\r\nSuperFly or hue35 - US\r\nph2t - Australia\r\nMicro_Amps - Australia\r\n(let me know if I\'m missing someone)\r\n\r\n[b:7157842e2f]Got any information about "fets"?[/b:7157842e2f]\r\nCertainly, lots, probably the most you\'ll find.\r\nMosfet Diagrams:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=1778\r\n\r\nMosfet In ZZ SE:\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2140\r\n\r\nMosfet Improvement (biff):\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=3594');
