INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45715, 'a9af50eac9', 'Nitro Bug', 'Hi yall,  sorry I haven\'t been around much.   The Nitro addiction is still taking all of my free time, and enjoying it.    We also put a pond in during our vacation last week........\r\n\r\n[img:a9af50eac9]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/paint1.jpg[/img:a9af50eac9]\r\nThis was my first attempt with an airbrush.   Thats right, its a thumb-print behind the frt wheel. &lt;G&gt;  I drew and exacto-ed the flame mask, and its hard to see, but did the carbon-fiber trick to the rear wing.   Its got a NovaRossi 3 port, 2-speed, and a front one-way diff.    The big trophy race is this Sunday, wish me luck.     I painted another one just like it, but purple instead of blue for my HPI teammate.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:a9af50eac9]http://members.cox.net/silentwolv/Pond1.jpg[/img:a9af50eac9]\r\nLast week my wife and I installed this 100 pond in the front yard.   Its really pretty cool....  Like our own little Zen water-garden to come home to.    Fancy goldfish, waterfall, solar lights, and water plants.  ahmmmmm, ahmmmmm\r\n\r\nSorry I got bored with the track I was making.   Ah, not really.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45716, '56d8f3ea79', '', 'I thought cars have to be 2 wheel drive to drift, well in D1 Championships they usually are, but for a Xmod I guess it works, because usually awd skylines are converted into rwd so they can drift better, because awd gives them to much handling.\r\n\r\nGood job though,  Keep up the good work!');
