INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45777, '82c2275cd2', 'ZZ Jeep For Sale', 'Gold, 49 MHZ, . It has the really big Lego wheels, and has a spare tire mount. What I did was I took a long Lego axle and glued it to the pcb cover, then I popped off the old fake spare, which was ugle to begin with and left a hole. Well, the axle fit perfectly through the hole, and the wheel clips on over that, thereby holding the body on. It gives the body more than enough clearence, and it has a mean look. The reason I am selling is that I am starting work on an F-150, and don\'t need this, since the F will take up the void. There are 3 things that the wheels do that annoy me:\r\n\r\n1. they make the gearing very different, and even with the blue gears, it is slow to get up to speed.\r\n\r\n2. Even though I have dual steering springs in it, the wheels go back and forth when backing up.\r\n\r\n3. (This could be annoying or good, it matters who you are) The wheels make road noise on smooth surfaces. I think it adds realism, but some people might not like it. All the wheels\' tires are still very plyable, so they are pretty new. As I said, the thing is fairly slow, but not too bad. It will come with the Orange ZZ motor. I\'m asking 20 obo. \r\n\r\n[img:82c2275cd2]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00074.jpg[/img:82c2275cd2]\r\n[img:82c2275cd2]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00075.jpg[/img:82c2275cd2]\r\n[img:82c2275cd2]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00076.jpg[/img:82c2275cd2]  \r\nHere\'s my ingeneous way of mounting the body. \r\n\r\nEmail me at viperdout@yahoo.com if interested.\r\n\r\nWill trade for 49 mhz F-150.\r\n\r\nAlso, controller was experiment for paint.  If I cannot fix it, price will be lowered to 15, or if you are trading an F-150, then you just keep your controller.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45778, '5934a4374c', '', 'Wow, I might send a 49 mhz car to you if I get some money.\r\n\r\nEdit: Just saw the thread and that is easy enough for ME to install!  This actually outperforms a stacked ZZ (2 FETs, one on top of another)?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45779, 'fdf06853c2', '', 'You COULD drift a RWD RC car, but you\'d have to play around with the throttle, say, accelerate slowly, and when you\'re at a good speed, turn and slide out the rear, but let off the throttle...that would result in a nice drift (I think), but you\'d also have to be careful with the throttle..too much and you\'ll have wheelspin, and whip the butt around too much.\r\n\r\nOverall...cool tires....');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45780, '717a295d17', 'Re: hey', '[quote:717a295d17="stampede_dude"]if i happened to send my regular ZZ to you to install it,is there any way you could fit the pcb cover back on?a naked pcb makes me nervous....very nervous....all those steering wires...ugh.[/quote:717a295d17]\r\n\r\nSo?  I haven\'t had a cover since my car was FETTED, and have not broken a steering wire because of it (it was because I was working on it.  Hog, I wouldn\'t suggest masking tape.  Duct tape is way more sturdy. :-D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45781, '1d66977ceb', '', 'I\'ve drifted RWD, and I cannot break the tires loose unless the floor is really dusty, like at school, with AWD.  RWD is still better for drifting, but AWD is great for handling.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45782, 'b298a5e1a2', '', '[quote:b298a5e1a2="viperdout"]I\'ve drifted RWD, and I cannot break the tires loose unless the floor is really dusty, like at school, with AWD.  RWD is still better for drifting, but AWD is great for handling.[/quote:b298a5e1a2]\r\n\r\nSome people have a hard time breaking the rear tires loose, others have a hard time controlling the power sent to the rear wheels. If you can\'t break the tires loose, either your setup (gears and motor) don\'t have enough torque, or the tires are sticky and cause some resistance.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45783, '7ed9581493', 'Re: 2800mah at 1.2v', '[quote:7ed9581493="DillonM"]how many mah\'s do you think a zip zap PCB can take,\r\ncuz i found a battery that is a bit bigger then the stocker, and it puts out 2800mah at 1.2v.\r\n\r\nis this safe?[/quote:7ed9581493]\r\n\r\nYou\'re joking right...A battery THAT size has 2800 mah? That\'s like..3.5 times the capacity of an IC-3 AAA battery...show us a link?');
