INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45817, '7715ed046b', '', '[quote:7715ed046b="crazydave"]Ok see drifting as when applied to racing, you\'re talking about a car that set up to hook up through the corners, but in some tight corners a practical racing tachnique is to push the car beyond it\'s traction curve, to bring it around faster, without dropping RPMs. A drift when applied in this context is a beautiful thing, and difficult to master. It\'s a fine line between heaven and hell. One wrong move and you\'re out of the race.\r\n\r\n...but now I see these drifting exibitions, where the cars are just smoking their tires, moving in slo-mo, spinning in circles. Oh yeah sure it looks cool, but it\'s about as practical to racing as burn out contest are to drag racing. To set your car up with no traction, so you can drift makes no sense to me.[/quote:7715ed046b]\r\n\r\nFinally... dave, this has been buggin\' me for a long time but it seems there\'s no reason to even try. You said that perfectly, and this should be posted on the front page of this site. Because the exhibition shit is called \'drifting\', the kids just take it as that... I\'m not sayin\' it\'s not fun to try to make an rc car mimic that exhibition stuff, it\'s just that it gets so far from the origin. It\'s the same as the kids who give Kurt Cobain credit for, "it\'s better to burn out, than to fade away"... I don\'t even know how to begin to correct that, when I know that "Neil who?" would be the response... it just ain\'t worth it. \r\n\r\nThanks, crazydave');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45818, 'aef530ecb9', '', '[img:aef530ecb9]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00076.jpg[/img:aef530ecb9]\r\n[img:aef530ecb9]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00075.jpg[/img:aef530ecb9]\r\n[img:aef530ecb9]http://img55.photobucket.com/albums/v169/viperdout/DSC00074.jpg[/img:aef530ecb9]\r\n\r\nStang has stacked FETs, Phast motor, and some wide ass Lego wheels.  It pulls some really good wheelies!  The Jeep has a DKS 3.4, blue gears, and Lego wheels also.  Might I also point out how I mounted the body on a Lego piece.  It works like a charm.  My project is not done yet...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (45819, 'e88174a142', '', 'I one, that came in the car I won from Superfly in the Mod contest. :-) \r\n\r\nIt is about as fast as a Perfection 3.8. Maybe a tad faster like the Perfection 4.2. Either way, more speed don\'t mean it\'s gonna have more power to pull big wheels. You might be better off with something like the pink endbell motors that come in Thunder Chargers, or a Zip Zap 2.2. Have you tried running 12:1 gearing?\r\n\r\nIf you want a bigger motor, and you think you can make the modifications to accept it, you could look into a Super Slicks motor, or you could just look into getting your PCB mosfet\'ed.');
