INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46202, 'b487de8027', '', 'Wow!  When I posted, I stated a very general thing as related to the MidEast.  Here is my opinion, a little more clearly. \r\n\r\nIt doesn\'t matter which news source you care to pay attention too, it is all spun around so much that you can never beleive anyone.  \r\n\r\nBut my general opinion is similar to that of WWII, the Japenese attacked Pearl Harbor and killed 2395 people.  The 9/11 attack killed 2996 people.\r\n\r\nWhen Pearl Harbor happened it was a surprise attack and we responded by eventually using a Nuclear weapon on Japan to kill thousands of people in return and it never happened again and we rebuilt Japan to be the monster economical giant it is now. \r\n\r\nWhen 9/11 happened it was a surprise attack and we responded by turning Afaganistan into more rubble than it already was without nukes and killing civilians, we were as careful as possible. Then we went after some funding that came thru Saddam\'s hands and made up a story of WMA that never came to be.  But still trying to liberate a country and let them choose for themselves on who they want to eventually want to rule them.  To me its a chance someone had to take to help these people.\r\n\r\nThen there is the Saudi connection which is so deeply intertwined with other MidEast groups, I can\'t even follow it and keep it straight.  I feel we should of went into Saudi Arabia before Iraq, because they are so touchy on every level.  but because of our precious oil addiction, we are to chicken to do anything.\r\n\r\nSo after 9/11 killing 2996 people what did we actually do?  Who did we hurt or go after and get?  Who did we punish?  Saddam.  Osama.  That crazy guy from N. Korea.  (His name slips my mind.)\r\n\r\nNo one!!  We liberated Afaganistan, and Iraq.  We didn\'t punish anyone.  Which leads me to my prior statement that has been shortened to... "Nuke\'em all!!".  \r\n\r\nWhy not, its the the same situation, but on a larger scale as Pearl Harbor.  More people were killed on 9/11, there was more cooperation between more people than Pearl Harbor, which was just Japan.  In order for 9/11 to have been a success, which it was to the terriosts and the people who support them and harbor them, there had to be a great amount of people and money that had to help.  Not just one nation or faction.  \r\n\r\nSo that is why I said, what I said.  \r\n\r\nI hope this clears up my prior statment and opinion.');
