INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46229, '9288e0bfdd', '', 'Wandering away from the Middle East, and getting to this believing the news thing.\r\n\r\nI learned how inaccurate the news is first hand when a co-worker got murdered. It started when my parents started saying she was wearing white, and argued with me when I said she wasn\'t. I was like WTH, I was there.\r\n\r\nHere\'s the kicker, I work for Pizza Hut, one news station got confused and visited the Dominoes across the street. Being more than happy to make a TV appearance, the Dominoes drivers stood there lying their asses off about how they new her well, and she worked there the last 2 months, and just regugitating the story they heard on TV.\r\n\r\nI tellin ya, you had to be there, it was crack up.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:9288e0bfdd]a teacher, would give an A to the student who can include all of these in the shortest answer: \r\nReligion, sex and mystery. [/quote:9288e0bfdd]I tried, couldn\'t do it. :lol:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46230, '73bce98a83', '', '[quote:73bce98a83="betty.k"]...when it does go out of range it just dies like a bit, as opposed to a kyosho that runs uncontrollably.[/quote:73bce98a83]\r\n\r\nYea they do that too? you know the more I hear about the superior Kyosho electronics the less superior I think they really are. Since I\'ve seen an Iwaver beat MR-02s I\'m not at all convinced the Kyoshos have any real advantage over an Iwaver at all.\r\n\r\nWith both cars set up the same and equal drivers I just haven\'t seen the big Kyosho advantage especially when you consider the price difference. Vive le Iwaver!');
