INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46388, '97256892e3', '', 'Now aint that the shiz.  Gotta love a robot with beat.  Every couple of years I rent Transformers the Movie and I don\'t know what it is, but that flick still entrtains me to this day.  \r\n\r\nOh oh just realized I had a related thing to brag about.  All you old schoolers, you remeber how when you bought a Transformer there would always be an insert of the current line they had?  Well there was always some kids playing w/ em (well thier hands) and yours trully was a hand model for the very 1st run.   That\'s right, if I remember right I had Optimus Prime.  Course this was before it all blew up and I was hella young but due to my brothers God father who still is a professional photographer, he hooked us up.  Course the fame went to my head and I became a coke head at 8 and ran off with some sluts that robbed me off all my cash (ok that\'s not true but.... :cool: )\r\n\r\nAny how, true story.  Course I have nothing to back it up on the net but this Pimp aint no liar.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46389, '6be3521bb6', '', 'The "E" True Hollywood Story: Finks... hand-model child-star gone bad lol...\r\n\r\nI had a ball with Transformers and Go-Bots and the like as a kid, but I was wondering if my favorite middle-school sport was just a local thing, or did kids in other schools do this, too?... We would have breakdance battles in the boys room with GI Joe figures lol... the one ninja "Stormshadow" was the figure to have for the best spins, but once in a while someone would bust something crazy with a tape-modded Cobra or Destro... that was the shit when I was in middle-school... was this just a local phenomenon in my hood, or have any of you guys done/heard of this?');
