INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46405, '7053b72bad', '', 'I believe that a Zip/bit could go 16 mph or so....it would just take a really good motor (4.2, 3.8, or the Phast motor from RCmod), KIT racer gearings, FETs, a paralleled layman\'s tricell, and of course, some really soft grippy tires.... :-)\r\n\r\nEDIT: a little advice on calculating speed:\r\n\r\nI calculated that, with the setup I mentioned, it would go at least 20 mph...\r\n\r\nmotor rpm= 38,000, cut in half with load, then back up to 38000 with FETs\r\nKIt gear ratio= 3.43:1\r\nRear wheel circumference= 4 cm\r\n\r\n38000 times 3 (tricell)= 114000\r\ndivided by KIT racer gear ratio= 33236.2 wheel rpm\r\ntimes wheel circumference= 132944.6 cm per minute\r\nconvert to inches by dividing by 2.5= 53177.8\r\nconvert to feet by dividing by 12= 4431.5\r\ntimes 60 to convert feet per minute to feet per hour= 265889\r\ndivided by 5280 to convert to mph= 50 mph.....well, maybe not...but you guys get the idea... :?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46406, '6570f4c48c', 'Super Street Acura body set for the SE', 'Found this at the Shack troday.\r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabs1.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n\r\nI kinda like the RSX, so I had to get it. It includes 2 bodies, 2 sets of tires, 2 sets of new hubcaps, 2 sets of spare wings in alternate colors, and 3 sheets of decals.\r\n\r\n1 set of decals is Super Street and Zip Zap logos, but the others are kinda cool, with graphics, stripes, Acura logos, numbers, and CF hoods. \r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabss.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n\r\nThe stickers are pretty nice, and fairly thin, but could be a lot more flexible. The CF hoods are cut no where near close to fitting the shape of the hood.\r\n\r\n\r\nThe bodies have separte front and rear ends to hide the slots, and look fairly long, and more true to scale than other Zip Zap bodies, when they\'re off the chassis.\r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabs2.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabs3.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n\r\nYou might notice a slight lip along the bottom edge of the side, like it\'s body kitted, and the windows are blacked out. What that is for, is what appears to be an underglow light, but I haven\'t tested it yet.\r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabs4.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the bodies sit like monster trucks because of that little underglow thingy.\r\n[img:6570f4c48c]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/acurabs5.jpg[/img:6570f4c48c]\r\n\r\nThe front tabs on these chassis are already lowered for my muscle car bodies, so you can imagine how bad it would be. On teh pluse side, since it has sparate pieces for the front and rear ends, it should be easy to cut new slots, but the underglow thingies might have to go.\r\n\r\nBottom line, pretty disappointing for $12.99. I mean 3 sheets of almost decent decals in place of 3 gear sets, and 2 fast motors. That don\'t calculate. I\'m wondering if I was mischarged. :???:');
