INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46442, 'bf9ac07164', '', 'well you got until the deadline to redo them(and the rest of you).\r\n\r\n what is the windshield made out of? i detect a green tint to it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46443, 'cb1315190b', '', '[quote:cb1315190b="hogjowlz"]well you got until the deadline to redo them(and the rest of you).\r\n\r\n what is the windshield made out of? i detect a green tint to it.[/quote:cb1315190b]\r\n\r\nThe windsheid came from an Import Tuner Die Cast that I broke down for parts.  The windsheid, dash board w/TV, center console, speaker box, and wing all came from it and a Dub City die cast truck.\r\n\r\nThe green tint is just the reflection off the green car.  Thats all, its clear with a yellow rim around it.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46444, '4a98fd100c', 'S.S.  Woody?', 'All right here is my other contest entry, but on this one I need to show off the craftsmanship!! :cool: \r\n\r\nHere it is.......from the beginning.\r\n\r\nI started with a plain plastic boat from the thrift store that I bought for 35cents.  I would have a pic of it, but I didn\'t think of doing a report till after I tore it apart.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_1.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe first setup for glueing.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_2.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nGetting the bottom complete.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_3.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe inside at the beginning.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_4.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_5.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_6.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_7.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/webboat.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_8.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe comparasion shot.  A NKOK boat and 2 bits.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_9.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_10.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe beginning of the staining process and the product that I used.  \r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_11.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_13.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe electronics installation and placement.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_14.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_12.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_15.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\n\r\nI have to take more pics of the top mounts and the inside where they are mounted.  The top is held on by three interior mounts that a Brass paper clip is passed thru to hold it in place.\r\n\r\nThe top deck is sealed with a thin gasket made from silicon spread thinnly between wax paper then cut to fit.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nA final shot.\r\n\r\n[img:4a98fd100c]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat2.jpg[/img:4a98fd100c]\r\n\r\nThe boat is coated with a gloss coat and motor compartment is sealed with super glue and silicon.\r\n\r\nThe top deck has a hatch on it.  Underneath it in the switch and chargeing plug connector.  It is not sealed, just held closed with a moving arm.  \r\n\r\nThe bottom of the top deck is reinforced with a zig-zag pattern of wood.\r\n\r\nThe wood used for the sides, mounts, and door trim, is balsa.  The bottom and top flat surfaces are basswood.  For the initial mounting of all surface covering wood, I used a wood glue.  The trim, mounts, supports, and rear motor area, I used super glue.  \r\n\r\nThe electronics are from a NKOK boat. \r\n\r\nI started this project the day after the contest was announced!!  Finished it last night. :eek: \r\n\r\nHope you enjoy. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46445, '3008e884f0', 'S.S. SG Woody  Now with Video!!  6-17-04', 'All right here is my other contest entry, but on this one I need to show off the craftsmanship!! :cool: \r\n\r\nHere it is.......from the beginning.\r\n\r\nI started with a plain plastic boat from the thrift store that I bought for 35cents.  I would have a pic of it, but I didn\'t think of doing a report till after I tore it apart.\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_1.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe first setup for glueing.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_2.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nGetting the bottom complete.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_3.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe inside at the beginning.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_4.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_5.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_6.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_7.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/webboat.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_8.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe comparasion shot.  A NKOK boat and 2 bits.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_9.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_10.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe beginning of the staining process and the product that I used.  \r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_11.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_13.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe electronics installation and placement.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_14.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_12.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/boatpost_15.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\n\r\nI have to take more pics of the top mounts and the inside where they are mounted.  The top is held on by three interior mounts that a Brass paper clip is passed thru to hold it in place.\r\n\r\nThe top deck is sealed with a thin gasket made from silicon spread thinnly between wax paper then cut to fit.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nA final shot.\r\n\r\n[img:3008e884f0]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat2.jpg[/img:3008e884f0]\r\n\r\nThe boat is coated with a gloss coat and motor compartment is sealed with super glue and silicon.\r\n\r\nThe top deck has a hatch on it.  Underneath it in the switch and chargeing plug connector.  It is not sealed, just held closed with a moving arm.  \r\n\r\nThe bottom of the top deck is reinforced with a zig-zag pattern of wood.\r\n\r\nThe wood used for the sides, mounts, and door trim, is balsa.  The bottom and top flat surfaces are basswood.  For the initial mounting of all surface covering wood, I used a wood glue.  The trim, mounts, supports, and rear motor area, I used super glue.  \r\n\r\nThe electronics are from a NKOK boat. \r\n\r\nI started this project the day after the contest was announced!!  Finished it last night. :eek: \r\n\r\nHope you enjoy. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46446, '50bf6e5461', '', 'My boat entry!   :-)   The first one! :cool: \r\n\r\nS.S. Woody\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:50bf6e5461]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat3.jpg[/img:50bf6e5461]\r\n\r\n\r\n[img:50bf6e5461]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat2.jpg[/img:50bf6e5461]\r\n\r\n[img:50bf6e5461]http://img28.photobucket.com/albums/v85/sg219/RC%20Pimp%20Stuff/contest%20land%20and%20sea/contestboat.jpg[/img:50bf6e5461]\r\n\r\n\r\nHere is the link on the building of the S.S. SG Woody....\r\n\r\n[url]http://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=3942[/url]');
