INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46496, '03b26e4119', 'Got a 4.2 that goes like stink and a 4.2K that stinks. Help?', 'I\'m a fresh fish, be gentle.  Got a couple of things:\r\nFirst, I\'ve got a light blue endcap motor, maybe a 3.8 but advertised as a 4.2 from Perfection(LXX) brand at ToyEast\'s online shop.  It goes faster than the supposed 3.8 light blue endcaps that I\'ve got(2 of them) and is so torquey that the back end of the car shakes when the motor spins without gears or axle attached.  It\'s been treated with WD40 and Singer Sewing Machine Oil.  It\'s faster than anything I\'ve got besides the Super Bit Pullbacks(those things are drag behemoths), and I got another car and some more motors from ToyEast, advertised all as 4.2\'s and a 4.2 King, with the tan cap and the E on it.  \r\nThe advertised 4.2\'s aren\'t as fast as that shaky motor of mine, and that King motor just flat out is a speed dud.  It\'s visually slower than a Microsizers 2.2 motor, and the stage I speed of my shaky motor is as fast or faster than the stage II speed of the King, even on the Perfection Phantom Racing Chassis.\r\nI think that King of mine has 1.0 potential for my street legal mode racing, and the spare 3.8\'s(advertised as 4.2\'s) will be given as gifts to two of my nephews so they can taste some real speed.\r\nIs there a way to make the 4.2K any faster (or faster than my shaky motor, the "4.2" I\'ve got) besides dismantling it or increasing my battery load to more than one 200mAh cell?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46497, '8e42ebb133', 'Problematic  gas pump outboard Charger on the wack. Help Me?', 'I hope this is where I should post this kind of thread...\r\n\r\nI\'ve got the outboard (AAA battery x3)charger of the Perfection Phantom Racer, the one that looks like a gas pump, but it doesn\'t seem to work.  The power comes on, but the thing doesn\'t charge any car I put on it, including the car that came with it.  The controller still sends a signal to the car, the car lights up its blue LED and goes like it should, and the car charges on any other onboard charger.  I tried bending the connection terminals so they would make contact with the plates on the car, and one kind of broke off, but I fixed it.  Since the chassis is transparent, you can tell if any contact of metal is happening.  But the car still doesn\'t charge.  I had to adjust the batteries so they would make the light stay on, but still nothing.  Note that a manual power switch is on the top of the charger.  Eventually, two internal wires came apart, one that connets to a metal (-) contact, and one to a non-functioning LED.  I know how to solder what to what, but I need help fixing it, actually getting the thing to charge like it should.  I\'m willing to send the thing out via mail to anyone that can fix it, but can it be fixed?\r\n\r\nHere\'s a pic of the whole kit, but mine is a ferrari 512bb with 27c frequency, purchased from ToyEast for 10$.  It was cheap, but I really wanna fix that charger.  \r\n[url]http://www.microsizer.it/html/phantomzent.shtml[/url]');
