INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46502, '34106de264', '', 'Yeah Perfection is crazy. I\'ve got a 3.5, several 3.8s, and several 4.2 pros that all have that same light blue endbell, and they all look like the motors that come in Cannoballs that are a very fast 2.6. So It\'s hard to keep my motors straight sometimes.\r\n\r\nIn general, inconsistancies aside, the 4.2 Pro (light blue endbell) seems a lot faster than the 4.2 King (Tan endbell), because it has a lot more torque, and accelerates a lot quicker, but I think they top out at about the same speed. \r\n\r\nThat of coarse is when you\'re comparing 2 good motors, the bad ones seem to come in batches.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46503, '0aeb356a98', '', 'I\'ll tell you what, all that PCB is doing timing the charge. I prefer to charge longer anyways, so I just wire the batteries straight to the charging terminals.\r\n\r\nRemember, if you do this don\'t leave you\'re car unattended, excessive charging may cause a fire. Don\'t forget the ground goes to the drive side of the car, and also I think 4.5v is a bit much for single cells , I\'d pull out one of the batteries, and wire it with 2 cells.\r\n\r\nAlso I use a volt meter to watch for voltage drop while charging. After you do this for a while you get a knack for when to pull it off.\r\n\r\nThat just my way of going about things, but it\'s worked out extremely well over the last year or so.');
