INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46556, '12d4da9cad', 'that glow from below......', 'Excess old computer parts can come in handy.  What you see below is a piece of plastic that was used by old hardrives to shine a LED indicator through a front panel.  So the good thing here is that this plastic is suited to carry light, so to speak.\r\n\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah3.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nSo what I did was get a small SMD blue led and glued it to the end of one of the pieces.   Here you can see it mounted at the end.\r\n\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah1.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nNow, putting 3V though it gets OK(but not great) results:\r\n\r\nIn semi-strong light:\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah2.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nAs you can see, not very bright.\r\n\r\nIn a darker environment:\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah4.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nIt really needs to be dark to see the effect well.\r\n\r\nBut, putting 6V through the blue led show a much stonger effect.\r\n\r\nIn semi-strong light:\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah5.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nAs you can see, there\'s still some definition in the light pattern coming from the clear plastic rod.\r\n\r\nIn a darker environment:\r\n[img:12d4da9cad]http://users.tpg.com.au/ph2t/yeah6.JPG[/img:12d4da9cad]\r\n\r\nNow it rocks!\r\n\r\nMore experimentation to continue, more to come!\r\n\r\nph2t.');
