INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46561, 'ebe23ac7cc', '', 'Zip Zaps are longer than bits and their clones, so no you will not be able to use the bodies, unless you want to stretch a custom chassis to fit, which is what I like to do, rather than buy another Zip Zap.\r\n\r\nYou can use the motors and gears, but they will not match visually. You could pull the wheels off one the axles, and do a Zip Zap wheel mod to the front. At any rate if you try to order a motor off the internet it\'ll end up costing about 12.99 after shipping anyways, so you might as well go for the spare parts.\r\n\r\nThe pink endbell clone motor comes in clones cars like the Thunder Charger, Cyclon-A, or Precious. Runs about as fast as a 3.0, but is very torquey. Since it already has a lot of torque, it doesn\'t see much gain from the FET mod, but with multiple cells this motor is really hard to beat.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46562, '5b8f7f0ba0', '', '[quote:5b8f7f0ba0]I also wonder about that whole PCB thing, because it seems to work fine charging on all my other shit, so I figure it\'s fine. [/quote:5b8f7f0ba0]Yeah, if it\'s just this one car, and all your others work fine, then it probably aint the PCB, and the direct wiring thing aint gonna help.\r\n\r\nCheck and make sure the terminal in the car is pushed all the way to the back. Sometimes the get pushed a little forwards, and the charger terminal slip behind it.\r\n\r\n[quote:5b8f7f0ba0]Anyhow, I\'ll be trying out that whole 45sec direct charge. Personally, I\'d like to adapt the whole charger for 4.5v DC operation. What milliamps and other specs does anyone here think would be closest to the output of three AAA batteries in that charger? [/quote:5b8f7f0ba0]You want something more or less around 800mA. Remember, the current from the wall varies, so with manufacturing variences, the current is not gonna be exactly the rated #. If you use less mA you\'ll have to charge longer, if you use more, you\'ll have shorter charging times. For single cells you want 3v. If you get an adapter with switchable voltages, you can use it for your multi cell cars later on.\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:5b8f7f0ba0]Also, What is a thunder charger and where can I get one for really cheap?[/quote:5b8f7f0ba0] Thunder Chargers were $5 at BigLots. Most BigLots have sold out of them, but there still a few out there.');
