INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46609, 'ece3d7d3e1', '', 'After it\'s roughed in with putty, use primer to get the surface ready for paint. Primer will get rid of scratches... you may have to use a couple coats with some fine-grit wet sanding between coats.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46610, 'bf4620830b', '', '[quote:bf4620830b="sg219"]I need to find a pimpin\' waterhole to shoot it!!  \r\n\r\nIts gotta be smooooth... :cool: \r\n\r\nCan\'t have title waves and waterspouts.[/quote:bf4620830b]\r\n\r\nIn comparison to a 1:1 boat.\r\n\r\nI know about a couple of rivers around here, but a small wave will crush the boat to peices and a water fountain is a little rough too, if it has too many spouts.   \r\n\r\nI need a pool. :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46611, '71bd136d22', '', '[quote:71bd136d22="hogjowlz"]what would be the benefits?[/quote:71bd136d22]\r\n\r\n...........*sighs*\r\n\r\nOk, everyone knows how when you do a FET mod on a bit, the power increases? well, that\'s because the internal battery\'s power is choked down through the trannies since they consume up so much of the power, or have high resistance. Grounding a zip/bit motor would bypass some of the batt\'s power directly to the motor instead of being reduced by the trannies...something similar to the no reverse mod.....');
