INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46626, 'b034661b08', '', '[quote:b034661b08]dude, you like anything that\'s smooth and easily insertable.....[/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]lol, get some lube and we can all be greek.... [/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]That yellow bannana name betty is using takes on a whole new meaning now[/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]..... you getting soft old boy? haha \r\n[/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]Yeah, I lost that picture of your moms so getting hard aint too easy anymore[/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]well it might slide in easy but it\'s a bitch to get out![/quote:b034661b08]\r\n[quote:b034661b08]Just can\'t get enough of your banana  :???:  :oops:  :innocent:  :screwed: [/quote:b034661b08]\r\n\r\nQuoting payaso, "You guys are a fucking riot...LMFAO!!!!"\r\n\r\nAnyways, betty, that "banana" looks pretty fast...just don\'t come after me with it!!  :disturbed:  \r\n\r\nI see that you painted over the rear lights...also, that woah nelly looks pretty cool under the hood.\r\n\r\nI\'d recommend installing li-poly or li-ion (what\'s the difference??  :-? ), then regulating it down to a lower voltage for the board...the woah nelly turbo would be grounded already, so just pop in the batteries and the regulator and zoom away  :shock: \r\n\r\njust a few suggestions......\r\n\r\n[size=7:b034661b08]now I need to get off my lazy ass, get some cash and do it myself[/size:b034661b08]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46627, '160d95b8d8', '', '[quote:160d95b8d8="SuperFly"]I\'m still back with hogjowlz, why would you do this? What are you trying to acheive? I take it you\'re just trying to pass more current to the motor, but it seems like there are much easier ways of doing it than what you\'re talking about.[/quote:160d95b8d8]\r\n\r\nokay, the transistors and pcb consume up some of the power sent from the battery, and very little power is left for the motor. now, if you ground the motor (meaning, link it into the reference point...in this case, the battery), then there is some unaffected current going from the battery to the motor....It\'s a similar principle to Jshwaa\'s regulator mod for his Xmod, only, I\'m thinking "how can we apply this to Zips/bits?"...\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:160d95b8d8]maybe you shouldn\'t be a fuckin\' gimp in the first place.\r\n[/quote:160d95b8d8]\r\n\r\nWhat\'s a "fuckin gimp" anyway?');
