INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46843, '25881f5ce6', '', 'Conseling 101....Next please.  The doctor will see you now. :-) \r\n\r\nI\'m still impressed with the big word ph2t used, "pontifications". \r\n \r\nWOW :shock: \r\n\r\nFor those of you that aren\'t sure what it means.  Here you go, also because I wasn\'t really sure either.\r\n\r\nMain Entry: pon·tif·i·cate\r\n \r\nPronunciation: pän-\'ti-f&amp;-"kAt\r\n\r\nFunction: intransitive verb\r\n\r\nInflected Form(s): -cat·ed; -cat·ing\r\n\r\nEtymology: Medieval Latin pontificatus, past participle of pontificare, from Latin pontific-, pontifex\r\n\r\n1 a : to officiate as a pontiff b : to celebrate pontifical mass\r\n\r\n2 : to speak or express opinions in a pompous or dogmatic way\r\n- pon·tif·i·ca·tion  /(")pän-"ti-f&amp;-\'kA-sh&amp;n/ noun\r\n- pon·tif·i·ca·tor  /-"kA-t&amp;r/ noun   \r\n\r\n\r\nFor future use and to put in your favorites.  Here is the link to the dictionary.  Use it and abuse it.\r\n\r\n[url]http://www.m-w.com/[/url]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46844, 'd222ee7721', '', 'I try not invest too much emotion and thought into any of this because it\'s like a "he said, she said" thing.\r\nboth sides have valid points.\r\nand both sides do dirty bullshit to trick their own cultures and the rest of the world into believing a lie.\r\n\r\nI don\'t mind your post. others make them - and at bitPimps - you got free speech out the asshole (&lt;--- see! :eek: )\r\n\r\nbut what I feel horrible about is that pimps here have an under-lying resentment towards each other over nothing but politics (lies for the most part)\r\nwe could have more resentment towards each other if we started talkin about aborted fetuses and god and computers and all those "taboo" subjects.\r\n\r\nit\'s too bad statistics can be made to look and say whatever. information and #\'s are easy to crunch and even easier to make look like a landslide just by purposly excluding other pieces of information or #\'s.\r\n\r\nthis is probably the most I\'ve written about this crap. why?\r\nbecause I\'m usually seeing radical or extremist points of view. why? because people are either sick of it, or very un-educated and very opiniontive. it\'s beyond most peoples comprehension. and that\'s not a negative thing. I am too when it comes to war and life in other countries. I\'m mis-informed and un-educated when it comes to "everything" - like us all in some aspects. that is to say, there\'s always something to learn - nobody knows or understands "it" all. which is why intelligent people have "conversations" about the matters at hand that are troubling them.\r\nwhich is also why I choose to talk to sessiz about this. why? because I know he\'s at least a little intelligent, more so than some others, I know he\'s got intimate knowledge of life in the middle east, and I know he has very strong opinions just like most of us. now I\'d like to learn why and how he became this way and has the thoughts that he does (no matter right or wrong in whomevers eyes - who\'s right when it comes to human beings living life?)\r\n\r\ndifferences are what makes the world great and a place for adventure and learning and evolutionary. without them, we\'d all be the same looking, same sounding, same thinking, same boring.... pop band.\r\n\r\ncrazydave couldn\'t of said it with more words :-)  :lol:');
