INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46862, 'e2f814304b', '', '[quote:e2f814304b="CaboWabo"]I\'m with ya so far man...\r\nI\'ve been to the lock-up more times than I\'d like to admit, most of my friends were what everyone calls "hood rats" and I lived like that for a long time. I know the prejudice and the double standards.\r\n\r\nnothing we can do but either join the game, cheat, lie, or loose.[/quote:e2f814304b]\r\n\r\nI\'ve only been locked up 2 times, minor stuff, but still locked up.  Both times it was over the top for what I did. But the rest of your statement is damn close to what I grew up with.  I grew up around a diverse mix of people.  Got into all kinds of bad shit.  I don\'t want to incriminate myself here, but I\'ve done worse than anyone I\'m friends with, knows about me.  We all have our skeletons, but mine is more like a graveyard.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46863, 'f2e614ca66', 'My first modding project', 'Yea This is my FD from the Auto Modelista kit and a friend of mine showed me this site and a couple others and lets just say I jumped right in hehe anywho heres a pic for the first part I cut off the roof and the side windows with a fine toothed saw.. thats why it\'s still lookin rough I couldn\'t find any sandpaper and the hardware store is closed atm... anywho the paint needs some sanding and coating and maybe a light buff to give it it\'s true chromyness.\r\n\r\n[img:f2e614ca66]http://members.shaw.ca/IronDragon/IMGP1914.jpg[/img:f2e614ca66]\r\n\r\nAny tips would be greatly appreciated');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46864, 'f21e7d5e03', '', 'hehe thanks dawg... this is my first time modding these little things and I must say it\'s hella fun... allso I have worked with many other items before case modding and such... I was bored and they messed up the supra in the modelista kit and it is lines are totally perfect for some truck action...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46865, 'b559acceae', '', 'First tip is to enter that into the contest!! :-)   That a sweet little ride dude. \r\n\r\nIf you need some sandpaper, swing past an autoparts store, they carry from rough to fine.  Everyone around here has their own little techniques, so find out what works best for you.  Go jump into the other sections and check out the many ideas you\'ll find in them.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46866, 'e98a45ff46', '', 'Well I had some really really fine sandpaper around here from my dreamcast project but it seems to have disapeared... Oh well tomorrow I\'ma head over to the store and get some sandpaper and maybe something to put on for a shiny coat hehe and then maybe swing by the hobby shop and pickup some paints for some sweet decaling...');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46867, '3aca2825e9', '', 'Nice chop job! Looks clean already, and you haven\'t even finished it up yet. That\'s pretty good.  8-) \r\n\r\nYou should enter it in the contest, but honestly, if I was you I\'d put a little more into it, some interior details, maybe a wheel mod. I mean it is a competition, you wanna represent. That\'s always been my theory anyways. ;)\r\n\r\n\r\nLook in the auto parts store for sand paper. That where you find the really fine grit wet/dry stuff. Since your just doing some finishing sanding, you want at least 800 grit, I would probably reccomend that you go no lower than 1000 grit. Use an exacto blade to clean the insides of the windows.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46868, '0a74f55ff3', '', 'allright thanks I\'ll keep that in mind... but just a question on the wheel mod I cant seem to get the damn things off the axles and being my only chassis atm(cus I am poor and it\'s gunna be about a month before I can afford serious modding) how do you get em off?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46869, 'ef09bdb077', '', 'if I may, another suggestion - fill in the holes left behind after loosing the rear wing/fin. use some putty or somethin and sand that baby down, make them holes disappear.\r\ntarga top sure says summer to me.\r\ngood work so far fella.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46870, '0ace956347', 'FAQ / Articles', 'every now and then - I keep seeing the same questions over and over again and eventually it pisses me off.\r\nusually when I get to that point I create an FAQ or an article or "borrow" one.\r\n\r\nwell this whole "how do I get the rims off the axle/pins" question is killing me.\r\nit\'s the one of the first and most basic questions.\r\nit\'s been covered a 1000 times in a 1000 different posts.\r\nbut not a one of those posts or articles has pictures, directions, or a definitive subject title to let pimps know - it\'s all about how to get the rims off existing axles or pins.\r\n\r\nso who\'s with me here?\r\nnot only with this damned question but others.\r\n\r\nwho wants to help? you know how.\r\nI wanna get rid of this "how do I get the rims off the axle/pins" question and the others as well, but this one is my new priority.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (46871, '1f096dac1f', '', '[quote:1f096dac1f]I especially hated that "do a search" thing at TRC, because you\'d read through 10 pages of an old thread, just to find out they never really had the answer.[/quote:1f096dac1f]\r\n\r\nMan, that breaks my heart...Once upon a time, when I had hogjowlz kind of time, I used to hand-slap people at TRC for responding with \'do a search\', hell if I was really annoyed with their tone I\'d go right in and edit their post.\r\n\r\nBut alas, working 12 hour days in my new postion and getting yelled at for being on the web even a minute more than I should be...I can\'t devote the kind of time it takes to weed out shit like that anymore.  :-? \r\n\r\nWell, at least I\'ve got naked pictures of some 90+ year old lady (God bless you Sez!) to console me.');
