INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47222, 'badc06ac0d', '', 'Ummm, thanks goku, but I think You missed the concept/point. (can\'t blame ya, it\'s kinda your thing)\r\n\r\nWealth has always been and probably always will be [b:badc06ac0d]THE[/b:badc06ac0d] deciding factor in society and it\'s laws. We supposedly live in a democracy run by the majority and yet special intrests groups and huge corporations are allowed to "contribute" to political races. I dunno about anyone else but that shit looks like a freakin bribe to me any way you slice it. I\'m kinda straying off the topic I wanted to pose with this thread so lets see if I can bring it back on track.\r\nThe major problem with america is it\'s blatant disregard for the importance of a "good" foreign policy. We fuck other countries the best way we can. Then we blame them for being anti west. Look at the history of the USA and you will see that at the begining of our country we were anti empire and sovreignty. Unfortunatly with the fall of the USSR we have become more and more an empirical force than anything else and we [b:badc06ac0d]DO[/b:badc06ac0d] have "royal families". We force ourselves and our ways of life on others without a second thought and if they dare dissagree with us we sanction them, embargo them or worse. We go in and open up their "markets" to our corporations. Take a long hard look at who is reconstructing iraq if you still think the war was a war of liberation. The general public is alot like cattle. As long as they have food they are happy, even if they are being milked daily or just being fattened for the slaughter. The apathy that americans have for the world is not shared by the world. When the actions of a self intrest inspired american policy starts to affect the lives of those that do not reap any benefit from those actions, isn\'t hatred justified? Don\'t get me wrong I\'m not saying that the governments of other countries are innocent, I\'m saying the people of those countries are. I\'ll use iraq as an example again. The people of iraq were "forced" to endure sadam hussein, as a dictator with military backing the general public had no choice. Any form of rebelion was squashed almost instantly and very definitaly (by death). I don\'t think that anyone can argue that america didn\'t play a major role in the prosperity that sadam enjoyed or even in the power that he aquired. So flash forward to the present time. While the people here were enjoying their mtv the iraqis were fearing that their toungue may slip and cause them to be "questioned". So in steps the "liberator" (who in fact was thought of as the originator of the problem) preaching of liberation for the iraqi people from a brutal leader and his government. Sadam\'s regime is squashed and in come the contractors from america to "help" rebuild the country after the destruction. You all should be asking yourselves "who\'s footing the bill for these contractors?" and then searching for the answers. There\'s no way you can think that these people would go into a hostile situation out of the kindness of their hearts and work for free, do you? The general public of iraq starts seeing american companies in their land building waterways and roads and constructing government buildings.\r\n-end part 2, while I go get some facts to post up- :-)');
