INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47231, '105b68397f', '', '[quote:105b68397f="sessiz"]Ummm, thanks goku, but I think You missed the concept/point. (can\'t blame ya, it\'s kinda your thing)\r\n\r\nWealth has always been and probably always will be [b:105b68397f]THE[/b:105b68397f] deciding factor in society and it\'s laws. We supposedly live in a democracy run by the majority and yet special intrests groups and huge corporations are allowed to "contribute" to political races. I dunno about anyone else but that shit looks like a freakin bribe to me any way you slice it. I\'m kinda straying off the topic I wanted to pose with this thread so lets see if I can bring it back on track.\r\nThe major problem with america is it\'s blatant disregard for the importance of a "good" foreign policy. We fuck other countries the best way we can. Then we blame them for being anti west. Look at the history of the USA and you will see that at the begining of our country we were anti empire and sovreignty. Unfortunatly with the fall of the USSR we have become more and more an empirical force than anything else and we [b:105b68397f]DO[/b:105b68397f] have "royal families". We force ourselves and our ways of life on others without a second thought and if they dare dissagree with us we sanction them, embargo them or worse.[/quote:105b68397f]\r\n\r\nOk, so basically, we are, in a way, trying to take over other countries and force them do be kinda like us. We make fun of them, some of us act racist and make fun of their culture and poor wealth/fund habits, then we rag on them for being against us and not liking us for what we did to them.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:105b68397f] We go in and open up their "markets" to our corporations. Take a long hard look at who is reconstructing iraq if you still think the war was a war of liberation. The general public is alot like cattle. As long as they have food they are happy, even if they are being milked daily or just being fattened for the slaughter. The apathy that americans have for the world is not shared by the world. When the actions of a self intrest inspired american policy starts to affect the lives of those that do not reap any benefit from those actions, isn\'t hatred justified? Don\'t get me wrong I\'m not saying that the governments of other countries are innocent, I\'m saying the people of those countries are. I\'ll use iraq as an example again. The people of iraq were "forced" to endure sadam hussein, as a dictator with military backing the general public had no choice. Any form of rebelion was squashed almost instantly and very definitaly (by death). I don\'t think that anyone can argue that america didn\'t play a major role in the prosperity that sadam enjoyed or even in the power that he aquired. So flash forward to the present time. While the people here were enjoying their mtv the iraqis were fearing that their toungue may slip and cause them to be "questioned".[/quote:105b68397f]\r\n\r\nOk, the way I take this is that, america is getting all the good stuff, but some other countries get the cons and not the pros. however, it\'s not the leaders that are justified to hate America, because they\'re the ones who attack us and kill people, like in 9/11. It\'s the people of that nation, who hate bitter feelings, but don\'t want to wage war...they only want peace. Perhaps they have bitter feelings because of us doing shit like drilling their lands for oil or whatever that shit that I was taught in the class....meh. The leaders of countries feel used by us....\r\n\r\nBut the PEOPLE of other countries are FORCED to follow suit and go against americans. They don\'t WANT to wage war or commit attacks, it\'s just that if they DON\'T, they will be killed. Am I inferring this correctly?\r\n\r\n\r\n [quote:105b68397f]So in steps the "liberator" (who in fact was thought of as the originator of the problem) preaching of liberation for the iraqi people from a brutal leader and his government. Sadam\'s regime is squashed and in come the contractors from america to "help" rebuild the country after the destruction. You all should be asking yourselves "who\'s footing the bill for these contractors?" and then searching for the answers. There\'s no way you can think that these people would go into a hostile situation out of the kindness of their hearts and work for free, do you? The general public of iraq starts seeing american companies in their land building waterways and roads and constructing government buildings.\r\n-end part 2, while I go get some facts to post up- :-)[/quote:105b68397f]\r\n\r\nSo it\'s like you and I said, people will do anything for money or fame or whatever. They do these things to hve their life spared, get cash, be looked upon as a hero. Osama and his men thought they\'d be looked at as heroes in their country for being cowards, attacking the buildings, and fleeing, demonstrating a "hit and run" technique. They thought that since America had used them in a sort of way, getting them back and saying "Screw your authority and your snobbish people"....This also goes back to when you said "I\'m not saying the leaders are justified, it\'s the people". It\'s also sad that the people have to suffer for what the leaders are looked down upon for by other countries...\r\n\r\nAm I grasping this correctly?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47232, '54cb7ab5bb', 'another custom rx7 from midget_man1387', 'aiighty folks... I\'ve been spittin out custom shit a lot here lately.... but here\'s another, and I need some input.... enter or no?? i think that its still appropraite, because at least around here, the hot rods only come out in the summer because in the winter its awful, undriveable and stuff....\r\n\r\nThe whole idea of the paint job was to make it look stock... I think I achieved this, considering my dad picked the body up and I asked if he liked my paint job, and he said "you painted that?" lol thats a good thing! anyways, it\'s also lowered if you can\'t tell lol\r\n\r\n[img:54cb7ab5bb]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10031/DCP_0093.jpg[/img:54cb7ab5bb]\r\n[img:54cb7ab5bb]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10031/DCP_0094.jpg[/img:54cb7ab5bb]\r\n[img:54cb7ab5bb]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10031/DCP_0096.jpg[/img:54cb7ab5bb]\r\n[img:54cb7ab5bb]http://www.bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpGallery/albums/userpics/10031/DCP_0098.jpg[/img:54cb7ab5bb]');
