INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47529, '14cad4587c', '', '[quote:14cad4587c] I know sometimes stuff like that gets exaggerated in photos. I\'ve had some cars that look perfect when it\'s sitting in front of you, and the pictures look I cut the masks with my fingernails. [/quote:14cad4587c]\r\n\r\nI feel ya!  Pics show things that the naked eye seems to overlook.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47530, '6ab5afa00b', '', '[quote:6ab5afa00b="sessiz"]it was cool to have either, but a status thing for the designers to have a mac. I think the whole thing boils down to price and the fact that you can actually build a pc to do what you want it to do.[/quote:6ab5afa00b]\r\n\r\nIt\'s got nothing to do with status. The whole print industry has been Mac-based since the late 80s. The money you\'d save in the initial purchase would very quickly (like, on the first job) be lost due to inefficiencies and incompatibilities with color houses and print shops, not to mention that tons of print publications still don\'t accept files from a PC. Maybe in a few more years it won\'t matter anymore, but for now, using a PC in the print world isn\'t gonna save you a penny. If it\'s what you do for a living, the cost of the computer is nothin\' compared to the money you\'ll make using it for a few years... why not buy the one that\'ll make all your jobs run smooth and save you time. In my case, a Mac is the only way to go.');
