INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47531, 'b75d993226', '', '[quote:b75d993226="hue35"][quote:b75d993226="sessiz"]it was cool to have either, but a status thing for the designers to have a mac. I think the whole thing boils down to price and the fact that you can actually build a pc to do what you want it to do.[/quote:b75d993226]\r\n\r\nIt\'s got nothing to do with status. The whole print industry has been Mac-based since the late 80s. The money you\'d save in the initial purchase would very quickly (like, on the first job) be lost due to inefficiencies and incompatibilities with color houses and print shops, not to mention that tons of print publications still don\'t accept files from a PC. Maybe in a few more years it won\'t matter anymore, but for now, using a PC in the print world isn\'t gonna save you a penny. If it\'s what you do for a living, the cost of the computer is nothin\' compared to the money you\'ll make using it for a few years... why not buy the one that\'ll make all your jobs run smooth and save you time. In my case, a Mac is the only way to go.[/quote:b75d993226]\r\n\r\nI was only speaking about the kids I knew and how I percieved them. I didn\'t hang with to many of the graphics design crews. So what you\'re telling me is that printshops/publications only accept apple formats? That don\'t sound right to me. :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47532, 'b403fa90d8', '', '[quote:b403fa90d8="sessiz"]So what you\'re telling me is that printshops/publications only accept apple formats? That don\'t sound right to me. :???:[/quote:b403fa90d8]\r\n\r\nNot [i:b403fa90d8]only[/i:b403fa90d8], just preferrably. I\'ve had publication specs this year that specify Mac-only files. That is getting more rare, but as little as two years ago that was basically standard. You could work in the print world on a PC, but all the shops are Mac-based. What I\'m saying is, I\'d spend a lot more time troubleshooting problems with my vendors if I were using a PC, so the money saved on initial investment wouldn\'t even be close to worth it. When you factor in the smoother workflow, using a Mac is way less expensive. Again, I\'m just talking about the print world, \'cuz it\'s what I know.');
