INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47743, 'b2614ae41b', '', 'Well I\'ve been there, and that is the hardest fukin thing to do.  I\'ve gone out and asked advice and none of that shit seems to work.  So now I have perfected dis shit. I\'ve bent many pins and wheels trying.\r\n\r\nIf I\'m gonna remove the pins from the hub one\'s things for sure, I\'m doin it because I want to change the wheels, therefore I won\'t need the old wheels.  See where I\'m goin?  I just take a pair of dykes or Xacto knife and cut the old wheels off the pins, take a standard pair of pliers to hold the knuckle, a pair of needle nose to pull the pin, brute strength (doen\'t take that much) and pull the pin straight out!  BAAM !!  Ready for a new set of wheels!  That\'s my technique!\r\n\r\nI did do a body mod tuit but cabo could pull it from MS Word.  It is a Damn Good Tuit.  Anyone got any suggestions ???');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47744, 'd5b3b98381', '', 'That\'s lookin\' awesome, Bird. What kind of paint is that, it\'s hard to tell what\'s goin\' on exactly... is it multicolored glitter in a dark blue paint? Anyway, it shows that you\'ve taken your time. I can\'t wait to see the finished car.\r\n\r\nSG... damn, dude. I didn\'t need to see either of those pictures. Jesus fuckin\' Christ Almighty, a lot of planning went into that projectile poop shot... that\'s fucked up.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47745, 'e014ceadbd', '', 'I think Superfly was right, with the modena.. The front end has got to be one... the rear is prolly juss custom work... but what type of car was he going for? I certainly dunno..');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47746, '80cd44091b', '', '[quote:80cd44091b="DarkTari"]Well I\'ve been there, and that is the hardest fukin thing to do.  I\'ve gone out and asked advice and none of that shit seems to work.  So now I have perfected dis shit. I\'ve bent many pins and wheels trying.\r\n\r\nIf I\'m gonna remove the pins from the hub one\'s things for sure, I\'m doin it because I want to change the wheels, therefore I won\'t need the old wheels.  See where I\'m goin?  I just take a pair of dykes or Xacto knife and cut the old wheels off the pins, take a standard pair of pliers to hold the knuckle, a pair of needle nose to pull the pin, brute strength (doen\'t take that much) and pull the pin straight out!  BAAM !!  Ready for a new set of wheels!  That\'s my technique![/quote:80cd44091b]How funny, that\'s become my technique. The only front wheels I was ever trying to save were the Zip Zap ones, and they\'re the hardest. So now I just make a new set of Zip Zap rims by buying gearsets, and ripping the wheels off those to make new front ones.\r\n\r\nI still warm the pin with a soldering iron sometimes, if I hafta.');
