INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (47813, 'a4146067ce', '', 'Thanks a ton guys.  It means a lot to get props like that from you guys.  SF to answer your question, 1st the front seat is off a ZZ S2K but the back seat and speakers (covered by the rag top) are from the insides of the Mucle Machines die casts you get at Wally world for $2.  As far as the shortening TC bodies are too long for clone chassis and the body was too long for a Cabriolet any how, they are kinda pudgy.  So I chopped a fair section out of the trunk and wheel well, used epoxy and tada!  After 3 primes and then resanding I got a seamless look.\r\n\r\n:edit:  Aww crap re read what you said and if you look in projects you will see what I did better.  I poped out and cshaved down a MM BMW front end then cut out the TCs front end, poped in epoxied and puttied to make it smoooove.');
