INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48025, '2f406f36d2', 'Another n00b question!', 'OK, I only own Zipzaps and Microworks mini rc cars.\r\nshocker, i know.\r\nAnd, after finding out how cheap bits are, \r\ni was wondering which \'one\' would you say is best?\r\nLXX perfection?\r\nBit - char g\r\nSuper bit - char g\r\nI dont know if that is all of them, but im a n00b with \r\nbit - char g and other cars like that from Toyeast\r\n\r\n\r\nAnd another question...\r\nshould i get this? its only 23 more cents than a set of 1\r\nhttp://www.toyeast.com/v2/proddetail2.asp?pdtid=AC0684');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48026, 'd49f00c07c', '', 'Oh, ok, I misinterpreted what you meant by, "you\'re other cars would do the same, but they just don\'t retain memory, which in itself says they\'re inferior." I interpreted that as saying the old cars are inferior to the Super Bits.\r\n\r\n...and I agree a Super Bit is not like a FET modded car, that\'s why I threw in the "almost", I was just trying give you an excuse for being confused. ;)\r\nReally a Super Bit is almost exactly the same as when I only do half a FET mod.\r\n\r\nI knew you had 1/10th scale cars, so being that I misinterpreted what you were saying I was confused as to why you\'d prefer an out of control car. The only reason I brought up 1/10th scale, is because when we first had this discussion when Super Bits first came out, someone had made a comment about how larger scale cars keep going, so I guess I still had that in the back of my head.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48027, 'cdc458456d', '', 'Wow, that really is a newbie question isn\'t it?\r\n\r\nWell here\'s a generalized breakdown, Bit Char-G, the original, good quality. Super Bit Char-G, second generation bit, it\'s been improved, but has an annoying glitch, I don\'t reccomend them. LXX/Perfection, bit clones. They have some unique features, but spotty quality control.\r\n\r\nThere\'s no real "best", but Tomy has better quality control, so you\'re less likely to get a lemon.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48028, '7b3c7b4ac8', '', 'You left out Microsizers, which are the US version of bit char-G. They come in 27 or 49 mhz. Worth mentioning because you can get them at Toys R Us instead of having them shipped from Hong Kong. A mosfetted single-speed 49mhz Microsizer is still my favorite chassis.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48029, 'f13c55868f', '', 'lmao im a n00b in disguise!\r\nThanks Dave for making me feel WORSE!\r\nlol jk,\r\nbut i guess i will get a bit - char g\r\n\r\nIm still waiting for an answer about the second question, though.\r\n\r\nAnd another question pops up...\r\nHow much is TE shipping?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48030, '4f923433b1', '', 'man, those coin battle sets are the best value ever! i\'d buy 2 sets, and get some cool shells. they\'re single speed, but you just won\'t get those chassis\' that cheap.');
