INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48048, 'd3a3ecfc08', '', 'Come ON Pimps!  Dis is one of Crazy Dave\'s Finest!  FET, FWM !(full wheel mod) Custom Paint!\r\n\r\n[b:d3a3ecfc08]Do I Hear 24[/b:d3a3ecfc08] meezly bucks for dis High End Pimpin Bus ?\r\n\r\nCom\'on Pimps!  Can I get [b:d3a3ecfc08][color=green:d3a3ecfc08]$24.00 [/color:d3a3ecfc08][/b:d3a3ecfc08]on Da Table ?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48049, 'f6b5d601ef', 'Re: Don\'t Forget....', '[quote:f6b5d601ef="SuperFly"]Everyone seems kinda high-strung around here the last couple days.[/quote:f6b5d601ef]\r\nEven some of the members of this secret back room. \r\n\r\nSo, I\'m gonna share some work in progress that might put \r\na smile on your face. Y\'all have seen the rest of the work in \r\nprogress on this car, but now I\'m working on the paint job\r\nand decals. I was gonna hold out on sharing paint/decal \r\nscheme until it was done, but I figured a sneak peek to the\r\nB Crew might be in order.\r\n\r\nOn this car, the fit of the decals is gonna be critical, so I\'m \r\nworking with an image of the side of the car to nail the fit. \r\nThe photo below shows the decal artwork I designed faked \r\nonto the side of the car to get the idea for the rest of the \r\npaint scheme.. mostly the top since I knew the sides would \r\nbe white. I tried a bunch of different stuff and landed on \r\nthis... it\'s gonna be vintage white on the sides with a metallic \r\ngold top... inspired by a Les Paul gold top with ivory binding.\r\nRight now, I\'m filling in all the body panel lines to simplify \r\nthe body and give it a fiberglass look. If it\'s done in time, \r\nI\'ll enter it in the contest... summer is for drag racing.  8-)\r\n\r\n[img:f6b5d601ef]http://home.earthlink.net/~hue35/images/fucker.jpg[/img:f6b5d601ef]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48050, '4fa6c16ae5', '', 'Three is a magic number,\r\nYes it is, it\'s a magic number.\r\nSomewhere in the ancient, mystic trinity\r\nYou get three as a magic number.\r\n\r\nThe past and the present and the future.\r\nFaith and Hope and Charity,\r\nThe heart and the brain and the body\r\nGive you three as a magic number.\r\n\r\nIt takes three legs to make a tri-pod\r\nOr to make a table stand.\r\nIt takes three wheels to make a ve-hicle\r\nCalled a tricycle.\r\n\r\nEvery triangle has three corners,\r\nEvery triangle has three sides,\r\nNo more, no less.\r\nYou don\'t have to guess.\r\nWhen it\'s three you can see\r\nIt\'s a magic number.\r\n\r\nA man and a woman had a little baby,\r\nYes, they did.\r\nThey had three in the family,\r\nAnd that\'s a magic number.\r\n\r\n3-6-9, 12-15-18, 21-24-27, 30.\r\n3-6-9, 12-15-18, 21-24-27, 30.\r\nMultiply backwards from three times ten:\r\n\r\nThree time ten is (30), three times nine is (27),\r\nThree times eight is $24');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48051, 'bc670da521', '', 'I think that the bottom line here is that you get what you pay for. ignoring shipping and tax, xmods are twice as much as iwavers. So why are we expecting them to be so great after all? They\'re an r/c. small scale. Real cars wouldn\'t take half of the shit that we put these r/c through, so why do we expect these things to last forever? Everything has flaws. Just like in the bit world, nothing is better than the real thing. The only difference here is that the bigger the scale, the more expensive everything gets. How much are super bit char-g\'s? We\'ll round to an easy number and say $24. so how much for a mini-z? we\'ll say $100. these iwavers are $25, so that\'s 1/4 of the real thing. now all of the BCG clones  that we get for $6 are shitty... so basically, we shouldnt expect much more out of these than we expect out of the six dollar clones.\r\n\r\n\r\nhey, I think I had something smart to say for once lol!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48052, '1c03eb1dd9', '', 'awesome stuff dude... I esp like the antennae comming out of the radio antennae spot on the truck :)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48053, '1e6c9b2764', '', '[quote:1e6c9b2764="midget_man1387"]I think that the bottom line here is that you get what you pay for. ignoring shipping and tax, xmods are twice as much as iwavers. So why are we expecting them to be so great after all? They\'re an r/c. small scale. Real cars wouldn\'t take half of the shit that we put these r/c through, so why do we expect these things to last forever? Everything has flaws. Just like in the bit world, nothing is better than the real thing. The only difference here is that the bigger the scale, the more expensive everything gets. How much are super bit char-g\'s? We\'ll round to an easy number and say $24. so how much for a mini-z? we\'ll say $100. these iwavers are $25, so that\'s 1/4 of the real thing. now all of the BCG clones  that we get for $6 are shitty... so basically, we shouldnt expect much more out of these than we expect out of the six dollar clones.\r\n\r\n\r\nhey, I think I had something smart to say for once lol![/quote:1e6c9b2764]\r\n\r\nI don\'t think you can ignore shipping and tax when comparing iWavers and Xmods, if you live in the US. The only place you can get an iWaver for $25 dollars is Hong Kong, and it will cost you almost another $25 to have it shipped here. You can probably walk to a Radio Shack and get an Xmod readyset for $50. To me they\'re the same price, and from a quality of parts/build quality, the Xmod is a little bit nicer. I really like my iWaver, but my Xmod was a better, more durable car out of the box.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48054, 'b98f6e5a7a', '', 'but if you look at it this way: What if you do live in Hong Kong? Then an XMod would cost around $75    :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48055, '0aae15916b', '', '[quote:0aae15916b="midget_man1387"]but if you look at it this way: What if you do live in Hong Kong? Then an XMod would cost around $75    :???:[/quote:0aae15916b]\r\n\r\nYes, but you live in Ohio and I live in Oregon, and we both have a Radio Shack down the street. And on Friday afternoon, when you wear out a set of tires and you need some for racing on Saturday, you can go to Radio Shack and get some. That\'s worth something to me.\r\n\r\nI see your point, midgetman, but my point is that if you\'re impatient like me, waiting a week or two for stuff to arrive from Hong Kong has a cost, even if the total dollars spent is the same.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48056, 'dae9140c2d', '', 'Can I just print out the coupon you put up and use it?  Do I need anything else? :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48057, 'd7bb86707f', '', 'I think the Clone Army just got its ass kicked by a thing called QUALITY!!\r\n\r\nI have to say that the electronics are good in an iWaver, but an Xmod will eat it alive on the endurance side of the track.  Plus, the parts are much stronger and better made.\r\n\r\nAs for the $$$ part of the cars, The iWaver is a much better value for a higher top end of a car.  You can get it for $50 and drop $100 into Mini-Z parts for it easily and have a very good car.  Then there is the Xmod in which you run out of things to buy for it.  You can only go so far, until you have to start searching for good upgrades that are avalible and quality.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAnyway my iWaver is still FUBAR!!!  :x  I do miss the fun I had with it for that one fun session with Bird and Hog.  It handled so smooth. :sad: \r\n\r\nMy first Xmod is toast, it is getting a chassis swap in the next few days to resurect it.  But I have like 10 Xmods and a shitload of parts, so its not too big of a problem. :cool:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48058, 'a7bd92d44c', '', 'I think iWaver needs to invest in a quality control department. Seems like a lot of the problems people have with them could have been caught and handled before they left the factory.\r\n\r\nAs for the xmod, I like it a lot, and I see a LOT of potential in the design, but I just don\'t see the shaq coming out with the stuff to realize that potential. Some of the xmod aftermarket is on the right track(alloy cups, etc...) but some of these guys seem to be concentrating on cosmetics instead of performance and durability. I have heard people talk about alloy knuckles, but I am yet to see them... If these were readily available and priced right(I\'d go maybe a little more than an AWD kit), I\'d be all over them...');
