INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48066, '138cefcacf', '', 'Well, if you look at the mini z platform, most of the aftermarket stuff isn\'t made by Kyosho. Likewise, we shouldn\'t neccessarily be looking to Radio Shack to come out with all future upgrades. Consider this: X-mods have only been out for 7 or 8 months, and already there are 3rd party products you can buy for them. Give it some time and there\'ll be more stuff. It appears they are made by HPI, a serious, hobby-grade R/C manufacturer, and once they start selling them in other markets, there will be enough demand for people to make money selling upgrades.\r\n\r\nAs far as quality control on iWavers goes, it already exists. It\'s called Kyosho. :wink: \r\n\r\nI think iWavers are a great way to get into Mini-z world. Adding quality control drives the price up significantly, and if that happens you might as well buy the real thing. You wouldn\'t buy a bit clone for $30 would you?');
