INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48802, '65392b8599', 'So is anybody still interested anymore?', 'Ok, so in the early days, evryone was like, if bits were proportional, that\'d be great. We all got excited over the SE before it came out, and it seems a lot of people gave up on the hobby and moved Xmods, when the SE didn\'t live up to our expectation. Many of us at bPs reverted back to our bits.\r\n\r\nBut now proportional technology is getting more practical.\r\n\r\nHere Son_Gokou turns us on to a link which points out some resistors that can be jumpered in the SE, that combined with Cyborg_Zero\'s voltage bypass mod, this opens up the potential for the SE, and makes it a very enjoyable cars. I\'m surprised more people aren\'t picking up on this. If I write a clearer tutorial in layman\'s terms, is anybody gonna use it? Do you guys think that this would help build interest in the hobby?\r\n\r\n\r\nThen you guys know the Germans are way into this stuff and we\'re always one step behind them, but they\'re apparently up to something cool over there, Sinned has recently reported of a SE clone that perfroms even without FETs, and then he\'s posting this video of a car that\'s obviously proportional, and fast, but he\'s saying it\'s a stock Panther chassis. Obviously there\'s something going on, I think he just means he got the electrics into a stock chassis. What\'s up Sinned? What the heck are you guys doing over there?\r\n\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=4080\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSo does anyone still give a damn about proportional bits by this point?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48803, 'b25f9a99c4', '', 'Ya, since I couldn\'t read anything, I just decided to drop off the rides and go.  I was afriad I would end up in a conversation about how good someones new toilet seat was or something worse.  I don\'t want to piss anyone off. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48804, '5f61945c87', '', 'if its just tweaking a few resistors and crap id probably attempt this stuff. i love the ses on my floors but they just aint all that fun cuz of the slowness. if you can make them bark dave id play with them daily.\r\n\r\nbits/zips was a fad for the most part. the few hardcore will stick around but since bitpimps is the only english forum for bits that wasnt based around making $$ the rest went to xmods to follow the trends and make their bucks. \r\n\r\n\r\ntheres a few people around dave who appreciate the little shit.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48805, '13aa72afa3', '', '[quote:13aa72afa3="grnmachnracr"] im gonna try to add an extra cell... does anyone think i would need a different charger if i added a 120 mah bit battery?[/quote:13aa72afa3]\r\n\r\ndo you mean replace the stock cell with a higher capacity one or ad a second cell??\r\n\r\n\r\n1: if thats your question then no you will get a little longer runtime\r\n\r\n2: if you run a dual cell make sure both cells are evenly matched or you wont get very good results.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48806, '0b297962d2', '', 'It would be a great thing if they wern\'t so much.  \r\n\r\nYou can go buy a Shen, or any other clone or bit for around $10-15 bucks (sometimes cheaper) and then you have the ZZSE @ $25, which puts a consierable dent in the pimp money.  If the technology got better and by better I mean smaller, so that it wasn\'t like drivin\' a hopped up 4x4 bit, I think it would be great.  The ZZSE\'s have that weird high stance and is just plain scary to work with in my opinion being so exspenive for such a little thing and hard to replace or cross-over with other cars and their parts.\r\n\r\nMaybe for some of you more expearianced people this isn\'t the case, but if you just wanna have fun and chop things up and glue and putty them back together, good ol\' Bits are still the way to go. :-) \r\n\r\nI\'d love to see a nicely biult full proportional Bit for about $15-20 or LESS in order to be able to buy and use and abuse the way I do with bits and Xmods now.  The only reason I throw the Xmod in here is because you can get them cheaper that ZZSE\'s if you know where to look.  \r\n\r\nOne last thing....If someone would make a bit like an Xmod and make it good enough, I would be willing to pay $30-40 for it because of the interchangability of it and the limitless options you could do because of the ability of total dismantlement.  Unlike bits and other 1:64th cars now, they aren\'t made to be totally dismantled like an Xmod and they are tough to work with when you do dismantle them because of size limitations and the ability to adapt other parts to them.  But in the case of Xmod type bit, I think that would be the coolest thing since CD-R\'s.\r\n\r\n :???:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48807, '8785fd4c14', '', 'I\'m sidetracked with Mini-Zs a little bit right now (I think I can speak for SuperFly too)... we tend to go in cycles. The xmod took us away from the little ones for a few months, but we came back to Bits in full force. A tutorial for FET-modding an SE is the kind of thing that pulls me back to the little ones... something new to learn. Even if I didn\'t get to it for a month or two, I\'d really appreciate the tutorial.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48808, '53475502c3', '', 'I like my SEs, too... but, yeah, they could be faster. I\'m not super-comfortable messing around with the transistors on the really tiny stuff just yet, so I\'m using the bigger cars for practice... my heart is in the smaller stuff, though.\r\n\r\nThese "pantherchassis" that Sinned keeps showing have me totally wanting one, but he never says how we can get them... but, check this post of his from the other day on MRCC out:\r\n\r\nhttp://www.microrccenter.com/forum/index.php?showtopic=26584\r\n\r\nNow, the question is, if he is willing to trade a modded Panther for a bunch of new ZZ stuff, how much cash would it take to get him to send a stock one? :???: \r\n\r\nI really would like to get my hands on one of those.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48809, '3f67aef634', '', 'These already have 2 cells in them, though, right? So, if by adding another cell you mean tri-celling it, then, yeah, you are going to want 3 of the same cells and you will need a charger... you could easily make one for a SS, though.\r\n\r\nBTW, that green is tight as hell, man. Nice job.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48810, '2c8928d754', '', '[quote:2c8928d754="ph2t"]Just to top it off he then makes this diagram for me, stating that it\'s "easier" to read.\r\n[img:2c8928d754]http://img19.photobucket.com/albums/v57/amitojbatra/woahnellydiagram.jpg[/img:2c8928d754][/quote:2c8928d754]\r\nOh man, that\'s the kind of thing that makes my blood boil... I have to say, you\'re WAY more patient than me when it comes to this kind of thing.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48811, '5fd5249528', '', 'I forgot the link.\r\nhttp://bitpimps.lixlink.com/pages/phpForum/viewtopic.php?t=2140&amp;start=135\r\n\r\nAll the info for FETing SEs is there, but I found it bit confusing and misleading in parts. I think someone needs to write a clearer tut, so if the interest is there, which it seems to be, I\'ll do it.\r\n\r\n\r\nHere\'s another thing, I understand many would be leary of experimenting on the SE, because they are more expensive than bits. I\'ve killed a couple before I got a clue what I was doing with them.\r\n\r\nBecause of the risk factor involved, and the extra cost of shipping both ways, I don\'t feel totally comfortable having everyone send me their cars.\r\n\r\nWhat do you guys think a pre-modded SE would be worth to you? Would you be willing to pay $40-$50, to make it worth my time and effort?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:5fd5249528]If the technology got better and by better I mean smaller, so that it wasn\'t like drivin\' a hopped up 4x4 bit, I think it would be great. The ZZSE\'s have that weird high stance [/quote:5fd5249528]The bodies just sit high because of the lights, it\'s pretty easy to remove the lights, and tab lower the chassis, but I\'ve found with a little ingenuity, you can get them pretty damn low with the lights.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48812, 'b632d5e31d', '', 'Ya know, I was checking my mail one night last week and he pops up on MSN messenger... "sup, Bird"(AGAIN) So, I chat with him for a bit, and he\'s tellin\' me about his schematic and all of that and askin\' why I don\'t mess with stuff like that and I told him flat-out... I don\'t understand half of that stuff and that\'s what we have guys like ph2t for... and he\'s like "Well you keep saying you\'re going to put a Nelly in your iWaver and blah blah blah, How are you going to do that if you don\'t understand the stuff?" So I\'m like "Dude... he sells them. I am confident that I can follow his installation instructions." \r\n\r\nGoku: "Oh."\r\n\r\nI almost wanted to tell him that his problem is not wanting to understand, but he seems to want SOMETHING to take credit for... even if it is his "easier"(lol) version of someone elses ideas.\r\n\r\nEDIT... Oh, yeah... I also totally deconstructed his concept of drifting as a valid racing technique, so, hopefully he won\'t be saying shit like "Surely you can\'t expect to drift..."  with that FUCKING MONSTER TRUCK!!!');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48813, '773883bb5c', '', 'Okay, except the "where are you from"-posts stupid posts, then i can say that i havent seen a negative coment yet on any of the rides.');
