INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48823, 'b49375810d', '', 'Cabo, and myself were just talking about this the other night.  I was telling him that out of all the R/C cars I have, and I have alot of just about all scales from 1/10 to 1/70.  \r\n\r\nMy absolute fav to date is my fetted SE with the Cuda body that hue inspired..\r\n\r\nI have about close to $80 in it, and it runs like it.   I don\'t mind paying extra for something I\'ll use, and have fun with, so I\'d gladly pay for one from Dave.\r\n\r\nI\'ve come to realize in the past month that I really, and truly suffer from R/C addiction, and just can\'t help myself anymore, so I might have a biased opinion...\r\n\r\n\r\nI doubt any SE will crush mine though, cause I\'ll drive circles around you guys....lol  \r\n\r\n\r\nBring it on fellas..  There goes my humbe side again :-) \r\n\r\n\r\nGreat idea Dave.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nsilla :D');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48824, 'dae9fd1590', '', 'There is a black ground loop that runs from one of the battery cases to the other. Cut that and solder it to your new cell holder in series... the end that comes from positive on the car goes to negative on the cell holder and the one coming from the positive on the cell holder goes to negative on the car... Use the s2 11 tooth to fully enjoy the added power(plus if you use the 8 tooth you\'ll eat your drive cups.)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (48825, 'b8c6c3971c', '', 'Ok thats what I\'ll do then, What does Hog mean when he said in another thread: [quote:b8c6c3971c]think daisy chain[/quote:b8c6c3971c]? Why couldn\'t You connect the new battery pack to the wires before they get to the motor? just wondering,  :cool:\r\nEDIT: so it\'s the black wire that connects both battery packs that I going to cut in half and solder both ends to the new cell holder? I got Ya, so it goes positive to negative on the cell holder, then on the other end negative to positive on the cell holder?\r\nThanks');
