INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49005, '0ebb3c3c7a', '', '[quote:0ebb3c3c7a="midget_man1387"]good points, finks. as far as keeping old pics is concerned... I like to keep the old ones so you can see the differences... I think I\'ll keep goin till i reach my limit, then I\'ll delete.. anyway... I think i\' finally got it![/quote:0ebb3c3c7a]\r\n\r\n*sigh* No Midge, you didn\'t get it...  No offence, but this will be my last post on this.  I\'ll result to PMS after if you still have problems. \r\n\r\nOK 1st problem, like I said before, the pic is too damn dark.  Take a very good look at the one I said was perfect.  You see the definition and change in color as well as the framing?  That\'s what made it good.  Also, use FLAT paper and crop to make sure you only see the white paper as the background.  You can use the curved paper effect to make it look seemless.  (As in half a sheet of paper under the car and the other half sloping up a wall or somthing, not folded mind you)  And again, GOOD lighting and focus on the car, the name is not important compared to the car.\r\n\r\nFinally, do you have access to a photo manipulation program?  I always resize my pics as stated before w/ photoshop using the "Save for Web" option and choosing 450 pixel width.  This seems to work great for all forums and screen sizes.  (Hell I use a 15" display at work to surf the Hood)\r\n\r\nAny how, take this shit to heart, cuz your tiring me out bro');
