INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49138, '62eaa67289', '', '[quote:62eaa67289="betty.k"]well done! :cool:  (NOT a typo)\r\n\r\ni have questions about the x plate. does the motor mount hit the chassis when the rear end is compressed? can you fit rear shocks with that setup?\r\n\r\nand you should be able to fit that pinion on that diff, just use the plastic spacers from the stock motor mount. i have a mount that\'s the same and i just fine tune the mesh using paper shims under the motor and screws on top, running a 10t pinion. the spur gear is the same size on stock and ball diff\'s, the only way to adjust the gear mesh is by moving the motor. this applies to all z motor mounts. you can buy aftermarket spur gears for ball diff\'s of varying size somewhereorother, but you still use those spacers under the motor (unless you got a pn racing mount).[/quote:62eaa67289]\r\n\r\nlol..with the GPM alloy motor mount, you can\'t use the spacers....there\'s nothing to hold the spacers in place...I think the only way you can adjust the height of the motor is to let the friction between the mount and the motor take care of that (that\'s what she said) and the pinion won\'t fit because of a small screw sticking out of the alloy shaft (red, in the pic), which is supposed to hold the pinion on the armature pinion shaft, makes contact with the shaft on the stock differential, in the ball diff I believe there\'s no shaft, just a small knob that you use to tighten the diff.....I believe. \r\n\r\nAs for the X plate, I think you\'d have to fuck around with the shock, but yes you can fit a rear oil shock on there...and the roll shocks would take a little fucking with too to get em to fit. I haven\'t tried though....');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49139, 'bf74c297a5', '', '[quote:bf74c297a5="Son_Gokou"]lol..with the GPM alloy motor mount, you can\'t use the spacers....there\'s nothing to hold the spacers in place...[/quote:bf74c297a5]\r\n\r\nI\'m pretty sure that it works the same as with the stock mount... the motor and the motor clip hold the spacers in place.\r\n\r\nOh, btw, Good shit, Goku... what is that 35 turn you\'re runnin\' in there?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49140, '8828487019', '', 'So you liked what I said!\r\n\r\nThe only thing is thought they left off the URLs to the sites I mentioned for aftermarket parts and my FAQ.    :sad: \r\n\r\n[quote:8828487019="original letter"]First off I love your magazine I dropped two other RC magazines for yours.  I recently received your July \'04 issue and to my surprise there was an article in the Small Talk about Xmods with quite a few errors.  I admit I sell them for RS.  Steve was calling them X-Mods when the proper spelling is Xmods no hyphen.  He also had a picture of the un-official Xmod site www.xmodrc.com instead of the site noted in the article www.xmodsrc.com.  Xmodrc the unofficial site is a great community but to find out what RadioShack is doing you must visit the official site.  Also for the web to plug my site that has been around since the start I am the keeper of the Xmods FAQ at http://www.geocities.com/cjellis/ (now if this is published it may kill by bandwidth).  He forgot all the Aftermarket parts we have Carbon Fiber chassis at www.tinyrc.com, Lithium Battery upgrades at www.atomicmods.com, Aluminum Drive axles and wheels at www.xmodworld.com, and Faster motors at xmodworld and www.XmodSpeed.com.\r\n\r\nCJ[/quote:8828487019]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49141, 'c69068136a', '', 'sg219 (on and off, no pattern yet - hidden more so lately than not)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49142, '2b0334ebb7', 'We get watched a lot more than we know', 'coincidence or not, we make the biggest waves.\r\nsites either try to replicate, or ask advice lol\r\n[quote:2b0334ebb7="RCmod.com"]We were wondering how you like your photo gallery? We need one for the new site and narrowed it down in our choices. Just wanted to get a true user experience review about it.\r\n\r\nHow are things with you guys anyway? We needed to take a break and now are getting things back in gear. By looking around...it looks like everybody left and went into Xmods. What\'s the deal there? Any news from TinyRC? We almost bought XmodRC.com but couldn\'t because of everything we already had invested in the new site.\r\n\r\nCars you guys have been posting on your site are looking superior! Keep up the good work guys!\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\nRC mod\r\nwww.RCmod.com[/quote:2b0334ebb7]');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49143, '511e66d35d', '', '[quote:511e66d35d="cj"]So you liked what I said![/quote:511e66d35d]\r\n\r\nOh hell yeah! Just the fact that those guys are aware of the following these rides have gives me hope that there is a real possibility that some heavy hitters in the industry could also be taking notice and considering developing upgrades for us!!! I know, I\'m an optimist, but daaaayum!!! Imagine the possibilities if some of those companies stepped up!\r\n\r\nOh, it also helps that this mag has a monthly micro column and in that same issue that your letter is in there is a 40th aniversary mini z monster featured in the readers rides section and a short mini z review elsewhere in there.... All of this adds up to more interest and possibly better things for the whole micro community.');
