INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49165, '3056ef737a', 'Summer \'99', 'I\'ve been reminicing (prolly this damn weed) and decided to look around the interweb for some pictures of the earthquake in turkey I lived through back in the summer of \'99. \r\nI came across this pic and it kinda brought some bad shit back to mind.\r\n\r\n[img:3056ef737a]http://www.sg.org.tr/gemeinde/erdbeben/dcp_0168.jpg[/img:3056ef737a]\r\nThese are actually a couple of guys from my neighborhood in adapazari.\r\n\r\n[img:3056ef737a]http://www.seas.ucla.edu/~wallace/Photos%20-%20Home%20Page/4%20story%20adapazari%20liq%20tilt.jpg[/img:3056ef737a]\r\nI actually walked by this building maybe a thousand times.\r\n\r\n[img:3056ef737a]http://arsiv.hurriyetim.com.tr/fix98/deprem/008101.jpg[/img:3056ef737a]\r\nBurning cat vid can\'t compare to this image.\r\n\r\nFew more pics here.\r\nhttp://cgpr.ce.vt.edu/photo_album_for_geotech/Earthquake%20hazards/Adapazari/Adapazari%20-%20Main.html#Anchor-30313\r\n\r\nSOme dude\'s write up.\r\nhttp://www.matti.co.uk/turkey/turkey5.html\r\n\r\nI have some pics that I took (didn\'t take many, wasn\'t something anyone wanted to remember really) that I could scan in if there\'s anyone that wants to be brought down some more. :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49166, 'd771af0a19', '', '[quote:d771af0a19="betty.k"]the spacers will work, i guarantee it. you need to hold them in place when you assemble it but they are the ONLY way you can adjust for different sized pinions.\r\n\r\n[img:d771af0a19]http://img78.photobucket.com/albums/v285/betty.k/spacer.jpg[/img:d771af0a19]\r\nsee the little lips under each end of the spacer? that\'s where the spacers sit. your mount will have thes lips.[/quote:d771af0a19]\r\n\r\nOh, I noticed...thanks betty.k! :-)\r\n\r\nBird...the motor consists of the following:\r\n\r\n35 turns, 30 ga wire, not pattern wound (takes up quite a bit of space actually! But I don\'t want to take any big risks yet, I just got these FETs, soldering them in was a pain in the ass, and I don\'t wanna fry them too soon! :-) )\r\n\r\nCrest Spinbrush magnets\r\n\r\nMotor can (ripped it off a motor that comes in a hand held mini-breeze fan)\r\n\r\nEscalation/stock Iwaver mini-z motor brushes....\r\n\r\n\r\nEDIT: thanks again betty, I shoved a 1.0 thick spacer in there, I just need a little putty to hold the pinion on the shaft, and DEFINITELY a ball diff tightened to the max, and I\'m set! Gave this thing a test run, it can scream pretty well, but since it\'s 1:04 AM over here and I can\'t go out on the driveway, I\'m gonna have to wait till tomorrow....Man, now I can\'t sleep....');
