INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49206, 'c9106149ac', '', 'Can\'t remember what it was called, but Havok sent me one of those to FET up. He said Yagbols hooked him up with it. It had a rectangle controller with a dome top, and otherwise was very similar to a Precious or similar clone.\r\n\r\nPretty cool car, I want one. You got the hook up on those, Chrome? :-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49207, '2ede09136b', '', 'Man, I wish I had the hook up on these.  This was the only one they had left with the Mini body.  The other one I got was a WRX with weird three spoke wheels.  \r\n\r\nLater,\r\nChrome...\r\n\r\n*Edit, I don\'t know if you guys think it\'s worth it or not, but I\'d like to own one of these: http://tinyrc.com/forums/showthread.php?s=&amp;threadid=19458\r\n\r\nI can get the body, but my lowering skills aren\'t great and I have a hard time getting Dub City cars.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49208, '492b2d2fb1', '', 'I got one of those mini cooper clones from ebay. It looks pretty cheesy and of poor quality. Then again, it is a clone. The wheels look like crap and the tires are thin and are cupped on the rim. It doesn\'t really look all that much like a mini cooper either. Here are some pics for you DT:\r\n\r\n[img:492b2d2fb1]http://img67.photobucket.com/albums/v205/sdog70/DSC00623.jpg[/img:492b2d2fb1]\r\n\r\n[img:492b2d2fb1]http://img67.photobucket.com/albums/v205/sdog70/DSC00622.jpg[/img:492b2d2fb1]\r\n\r\nNotice the cheap cupped tires:\r\n[img:492b2d2fb1]http://img67.photobucket.com/albums/v205/sdog70/DSC00624.jpg[/img:492b2d2fb1]\r\n\r\nNot really sure what brand it is:\r\n[img:492b2d2fb1]http://img67.photobucket.com/albums/v205/sdog70/DSC00627.jpg[/img:492b2d2fb1]\r\n\r\nBut it comes from noveltyinc.com\r\n[img:492b2d2fb1]http://img67.photobucket.com/albums/v205/sdog70/DSC00626.jpg[/img:492b2d2fb1]\r\n\r\nDidn\'t jmays make a convertible out of one of these a while back?');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49209, 'ea14ea4137', '', '[quote:ea14ea4137="betty.k"]that\'s where the paper comes in. in my pic you can see the yellow paper under the motor. this fine tunes the gear mesh. you can use paper, alfoil, thin plastic, anything.\r\n\r\nwith the ball diff, i was advised to tighten it up so it slips just a little with hard throttle. i have mine set up like that and it works well, the ball diff usually slips before the tyres break traction, i feel this gives me more control.[/quote:ea14ea4137]\r\n\r\nI\'m guessing that with a ball diff, the tighter it is the less slip there is in the gears, but the looser, the more slip. Too loose won\'t give it enough power through the turns, too tight will cause understeer or oversteer depending on the torque or traction of the tires. \r\n\r\nAnyway, I think I may have already fried my FETs.....The motor hookup wires just keep coming off, but I think I may have done a bad soldering job, because when I soldered em back on and gunned the throttle with my finger on the FETs...they got really hot, I almost burned my finger! But no smoke came from them, so I think the FETs may be ok. I can only hope! :(\r\n\r\nHowever, I have some Xmod motors, when I\'m not feeling lazy, then I\'ll get a candle/lighter, heat the pinions and pop em off, and try those out. :D \r\n\r\nI have to start working a bit harder around the house, but when I get 20 dollars, I\'m getting a ball diff, and some more FETs just in case (and if ph2t keeps selling his Woah nelly turbos, I\'ll eventually buy one) and hopefully I\'ll be back in business.');
