INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (49232, '6ea074ed79', '', 'Well Jackd got back, and he loves the bus. He said:\r\n[quote:6ea074ed79]I am really impressed with the paint job too. The pictures on the site do not do it justice. I was really impressed with the finish and smoothness of your work. [/quote:6ea074ed79]\r\n\r\nWhich bring me to the point of my post.\r\n\r\nI\'m really frustrated, DT sent me some of his excellent work to finish up. I wanted it to be some of my best work, and instead the clear coat reacted with the windows.\r\n\r\nIt\'s not as bad as picturtes make it look, but check this out:\r\n\r\n[img:6ea074ed79]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/collab2.jpg[/img:6ea074ed79]\r\n[img:6ea074ed79]http://crazybydesign.net/crazycars/collab3.jpg[/img:6ea074ed79]\r\n\r\n\r\nI have tried to fix it by sanding with 1000 grit and clear coating again,but the same thing happened. So I sanded, and rubbed it out. Now the surface is smooth, but apparently the deformation is under the surface.\r\n\r\nI want to keep sanding and rubbing on it, but I\'m afraid if I get carried away I might ruin the area around it.\r\n\r\nMy wife seems to think it\'s hardly noticeable, and the work me and DT have put into it over rides the windows, but if I\'m gonna sell something, I want it to be perfect. I want to get the kind of response I got from Jack, for all my work. I\'m representin\', you know.\r\n\r\nSo what do you think, should I keep trying to fix it, or should I leave well enough alone?');
