INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50138, '62cfa28738', '', 'I gotta have the Corvette set, but I\'m dying of curiosity over what year the past body is, but that\'s ok, there\'s so many good ones, \'57, \'58, \'63, \'68, \'69 Stingray...and then it ends about there for me, if it\'s one of them fat fendered late \'70s Vettes, I will make a special trip just to beat someone\'s ass.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50139, '74d3c267ee', '', '[quote:74d3c267ee="Sdog"]Dude...I say go for another Chevelle. Why get the same car? I don\'t think the body shell or color has anything to do with it. I like the black Chevelle body way better than the red.[/quote:74d3c267ee]\r\n\r\nWhy get the same car? Call me superstitious, but the 1st Orange GTO I got was stutter-free, and lo-and-behold when I got home tonight with my 2nd Orange GTO it was everybit as stutter-free. I highly doubt the body shell or color has anything to do with it either...But I think the part # might be an indicator...\r\n\r\nThe Pontiac GTO Judge has the highest (newest?) numbering of the SEs. The original 1st gen Initial-D has a part number of 60-7026, the Chevelle is 7038, Starsky &amp; Hutch is 7037...But the GTOs are 7040\r\n\r\nI\'m thinking they updated their PCB production line as of the 7040 SEs and any new kits put together afterwards (whether the Chevelle or even the old Initial-D kits) has the new PCBs (this makes sense because some people are reporting buying Initial-D kits with no stutter.\r\n\r\nAll that said, I\'d rather be sure of getting a fixed board by getting a 7040 (can\'t explain the shitbag blue GTO I got though).');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50140, '65f8e785b4', '', 'Oh, I forgot, sdog...Where\'s the details on that Wide Tire Kit? Is that an actual kit from RadioShack?\r\n\r\nThanks.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50141, '1cf14a3d54', '', 'You know me, I am always into what you have cookin.  Only thing tho is this is really a thread intended for the Custom Jobs section.  Keep us posted (course I know ya will anyhow) 8-)');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50142, '138c7f744d', '', 'If I were you I would extend a standard Zips Cassis to fit and at the very leaste dual cell it.  To find out about how to do both I would suggest a search seeing that personally I have not bothered with either (although I will be stretching a clone chassis very soon).  \r\n\r\nAs far as  how pimps feel about Noobs here...  Well basically we are firm believers in earning street cred.  Show us what you can do, be able to take a joke, obey our simple rules, and enjoy the site while ya develop into a better modder.  That\'s what I did bro and like I have said before click my gallery to see how far I have gotten all due to the pimps here.');
