INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50291, 'f23efebdcc', '', 'i worked in a chocolate shop specialising in wedding cakes for a while, making flowers is labour intensive shit! we used to make "plastic chocolate" for ours. just melt 1/3 cup of glucose syrup with a cup of compound choc. once melted and incorporated it turns to a thick stodgey goo. then you gotta get blobs of it and squeeze it til the fat is removed. then you just heat it slightly in a microwave to use. really pliable stuff, much better option than that marzipan shit :hurl:');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50292, '128eed57bd', '', '[quote:128eed57bd="Son_Gokou"]Ahh5hit, I\'m beginning to wonder, do you just buy these things to paint and make us jealous (lol), or do you actually race and have fun with these things?[/quote:128eed57bd]\r\nTrust me, I don\'t spend this much money for shelf pieces. I do have one for outdoors, one for inside, and my showpiece plus different bodies. They get plenty of run time, but I have just as much fun tinkering with them too.');
INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50293, '2489fb593d', '', '[quote:2489fb593d="hue35"]Yeah, which reminds me that I have few discs to get in the mail! I\'ll get those and the idler gear in the mail next week... I\'m a fuckin\' slacker.[/quote:2489fb593d]That\'s ok, I\'m a slacker too, I got stuff I ripped for you, that I have put to disc yet, so maybe I need to get off my ass too. :lol: \r\n\r\n\r\n[quote:2489fb593d="cabowabo"]I have a love hate relationship with that F150. \r\nfirst off, I hate fords. [/quote:2489fb593d]Yeah, so do I really, but when it come to little toy cars I figure they\'re all the same on the inside, so RS gave us a F150, and I\'m like ahh well, close enough. \r\n\r\nI also think it\'s kinda fun, because there is a billion and 1 Ford trucks riding on dubs around here, so to me this truck screams \'West Side\'.\r\n\r\n[quote:2489fb593d]already dig the lowering, even though I hate lowered trucks in real life - this mofo demands it.[/quote:2489fb593d] Oh I just love all trucks, tall trucks, short trucks, it don\'t matter. Street trucks are cool, because with more and more muscle cars ending up pampered in the garage, you can always pick up a late 70\'s Silverado with a 454, for pretty cheap. Warm that bitch over, and change the gearing in the diff, and you got\'s a screamer.');
