INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50325, '9aa8c65f19', 'rose', 'well here is the south i have tried the marzipan for doing decorations, the only thing is that its so humid and the shelf life is about half a day until its all tacky, now this rose above is made with a sugar substitute, its called isomalt. \r\nIsomalt is produced by enzymatic rearrangement of sucrose in two stages. It is an odourless, white crystalline and low hygroscopic substance. Spun sugar and any other sugar art from made with ISOMALT can stand up for long periods of time – no need for plastic boxes, no need for silica gel – isomalt also resists humidity.\r\n\r\nIt took me about an hour and a half to make this one above, it was the cake topper, there were 12 others without the base that were put around the cake.\r\n\r\nI made a rubber mold of a leaf and used it to press the rose leaves, thats why i had the molding materials available for my rc bodies. cool huh.\r\n\r\n I also dabble with some chocolate, below was a cake i did two weeks ago for a five year old girl. \r\n   the picture in the center of the cake was made with white chocolate, and the girls are chocolate as well, meaning it was not screened on the chocolate, i colored white chocolate to what ever color i needed then scribed the details into the chocolate and then i layed the colored chocolate into the scribed line or area , wait for it to set up and the shave it back down and what you are left with is the image in color, its hard to describe.\r\n\r\nnone the less, this is what i do at work, its monotiness at times and i am sick of desserts.  :-( \r\n\r\n[img:9aa8c65f19]http://img27.photobucket.com/albums/v82/superpieboy/chocolate.jpg[/img:9aa8c65f19]\r\n\r\njmays');
