INSERT INTO phpbb_posts_text VALUES (50385, '8755e5b8f7', '', '[quote:8755e5b8f7="crazydave"][quote:8755e5b8f7]The Orange GTO Judge works great, basically zero stutter. I returned the blue GTO Judge and exchanged for a Chevelle, the Chevelle stutters (nowhere near as bad as my old 1st gen SE, but nowhere as good as the Orange Judge either) [/quote:8755e5b8f7]My Chevelle works great. Hog got a jittery S&amp;H car, but I\'ve got Cabo\'s here, and it\'s fine.\r\n\r\nSince all these newer ones have the same pcb, I have to say the problem is in the set up. I\'ve noticed that if the steering is trying to center between steps, it jitters worse. It\'s like it can\'t decide which step to fall on.\r\n\r\nTry this. Take the front end apart. With the gear removed, center the steering on the controller, and on the chassis. Replace gear, and reassemble. You\'ll have to make slight adjustments to the chassis center adjustment.\r\n\r\nThat would drastically reduce jitter on the first generation SEs, so maybe it will help on the newer ones that still jitter.[/quote:8755e5b8f7]\r\n\r\nDid you take photos while you were doing that by any chance?');
